window.FWN_LEGEND_OF_SWORDSMAN_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_LEGEND_OF_SWORDSMAN_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":6301,"title":"Chapter 6301: Mangshan County","paragraphs":["Chapter 6301: Mangshan County","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Although the current imperial son-in-law was weeping bitterly, showing no pretense or shrewdness, Jian Wushuang knew that such a person, capable of great patience and tenacity, was not even afraid of death.","Once he calmed down, he would surely consider Jian Wushuang’s identity, background, and purpose.","Therefore, Jian Wushuang needed to prepare in advance and subtly convey that he was unfamiliar with the Tang Dynasty and had come here to overcome certain barriers in his cultivation.","He also exaggerated his cultivation level.","Invincible in the Golden Core stage.","He had come here to break through his cultivation and advance to the Nascent Soul stage.","A cultivator at the Golden Core stage was already considered a significant figure, although not much in the grand scheme of the Eastern Tang Dynasty, but to an imperial son-in-law, he was like an immortal. Moreover, Jian Wushuang presented himself as a master with a perfected Golden Core, coming here to break through to the Nascent Soul stage.","Chen Yuan was slow to realize it at first, feeling the pain of Ah Zi’s death, and then focused on revenge.","The two conversed more and more amicably under the peach blossom tree.","“You seem harmless on the outside, yet your methods are so ruthless. Even I didn’t expect it. I initially thought capturing those beasts and executing them publicly would be the end of it. But listening to you, it seems you’re planning to eradicate their entire clan!” Jian Wushuang feigned surprise.","Chen Yuan, however, felt that wasn’t enough and coldly replied, “Those beasts deserve to die. I will ensure they experience utter despair while alive. I’ll leverage all my connections to dismantle several noble families in the Shanhai County. I want them to disappear from this world as if they never existed!”","Seeing Chen Yuan consumed by hatred, Jian Wushuang felt like patting his shoulder and saying, “Young man, anger harms the body!”","Yet he didn’t voice this, instead nodding in agreement, “Revenge, to me, is just about satisfaction. I originally planned to kill those scumbags directly. However, since you’re Ah Zi’s beloved, I’ll leave the revenge up to you. If you need any assistance, you can find me.”","Hearing this, Chen Yuan quickly persuaded, “Why don’t you stay in the mansion, senior? The City Guards are strict in their patrols, and my status makes it troublesome for us to meet!”","“Haha, just some minor City Guards. Apart from their commander, who else could be my match?” Jian Wushuang stood with arrogance, but then changed his tone, saying, “I think this courtyard is nice. I’ll stay here for now. Once Ah Zi’s matter is resolved, I’ll focus on my cultivation.”","After mentioning this a few times, Chen Yuan remembered it in his heart. Although he didn’t say it, he had already decided on how to repay him.","Although he didn’t express it, Jian Wushuang could easily see what he was thinking. This couldn’t be hidden from him.","“Alright, you should go back now. Although I’m free in Tai’an City, you’re different. You are the imperial son-in-law now!” Jian Wushuang intentionally spoke in a teasing tone.","Chen Yuan thought he was angry and complained, “I only have a nominal relationship with the princess. She mingles with her lovers all day, and we haven’t even seen each other in days. Even if she discovers I’m not in my room at night, she wouldn’t care!”","Jian Wushuang was naturally aware of this situation. With a mere thought, he could detect the hundreds of people within the princess’s residence.","“Heh!”","With a flicker, he vanished from sight.","Having witnessed such divine techniques before, Chen Yuan wasn’t surprised. He tidied himself up, picked up a lantern, and walked out of the courtyard.","As dawn broke, the red tide from the east swept in, pushing back the darkness.","The heavy rain also ceased at this moment.","In the morning, as all things lifted their heads, Tai’an City buzzed with life once again.","It was as if nothing had happened the previous night.","The City Guards also withdrew one by one, but the city gates remained tightly guarded.","Tai’an City had four main gates.","The first was the palace gate, the second the royal gate, the third the official gate, and the fourth the city gate.","Each level was more stringent than the last.","This was all because of the commotion Jian Wushuang caused last night, which kept the Zhanxian Guards constantly on edge.","Outside the Zhanxian Tower, Yang Xiao rubbed his eyes as he walked out.","“So tiring, playing chess with the Commander-in-Chief is more exhausting than patrolling outside!”","Dragging his weary body, Yang Xiao led his horse toward the palace gates.","At this moment, he happened to encounter the various officials leaving court.","They merely exchanged glances, each with a darkened expression.","“Hmph, this useless group of Zhanxian Guards still hasn’t figured out the matter of the Jiang Kingdom’s downfall. They are truly useless, only strong in their own territory!”","“Isn’t that right? If it weren’t for the Prince Consort reporting it today, we wouldn’t have known that the nobles of Jiang Kingdom had fled to the Shanhai County. Fortunately, it was just fleeing nobles. If it were an invading army, wouldn’t it have delayed our military response?”","The officials spoke more severely, wishing they could execute Yang Xiao on the spot.","In the past, Yang Xiao would have surely made sarcastic remarks, but now he found himself unable to speak.","He could only ignore them, and once outside the palace gates, he spurred his horse and left.","On the way, his anger grew.","“Have we retreated all the way to Tai’an City from monitoring the four directions?”","Yang Xiao couldn’t help but lament. The once renowned Zhanxian Guards in the capital not only supervised all officials, but also had a strong grip on curfews and control over Tai’an City. They were well-versed in everything happening in the Eastern Lands, with overseers even in the Southern Heaven Realm and the Northern Glaciers.","But now?","The Jiang Kingdom of the Southern Heaven Realm was destroyed, and they knew nothing, nor did they send anyone to investigate.","They had no choice but to swallow their pride in the face of ridicule.","The sects across the Eastern Lands were trampling over them, and they turned a blind eye, even as they watched His Majesty employ people from the demonic cult.","It was disheartening!!!","“Why is His Majesty doing this? The Commander’s heart is fully devoted to you!”","The more Yang Xiao thought about it, the angrier he became, but he had nowhere to vent.","However, the counterattack was about to begin. Last night, while playing chess with the Commander-in-Chief, he received a special mission.","To investigate the external actions of the Holy Cult.","This was a signal, a signal of an impending counterattack.","Over the years, the demonic cult had run rampant, relying on the court to commit countless misdeeds, and now it was time for them to pay the price.","Moreover, this matter was being orchestrated by the Commander-in-Chief behind the scenes, so even His Majesty couldn’t protect them.","Yang Xiao furrowed his brows and sneered coldly, heading straight out of Tai’an City.","Once outside the city gates, he abandoned his horse and traveled on foot.","A cultivator at the Golden Core stage could travel a thousand miles in a day, let alone Yang Xiao, who was one of the best among them. By noon, he had reached Mangshan County, a thousand miles away.","This place was the first major county outside the capital, permanently garrisoned to guard against the great demons and barbarians of the Northern Region.","Small-scale wars often broke out, and deaths were common occurrences.","“What a strong aura of death!”","As soon as Yang Xiao entered Mangshan County, he sensed a powerful aura of death.","That aura of death was so strong that it moved him, something not seen even after years of continuous warfare.","Moreover, it was mixed with a sense of resentment.","The deeper he ventured into Mangshan County, the stronger Yang Xiao felt this sensation."]},{"number":6302,"title":"Chapter 6302: Surrounded","paragraphs":["Chapter 6302: Surrounded","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Yang Xiao wandered, stopping and going for two days, circling Mangshan County, yet he hadn’t seen a single person.","Following the trace of death energy, he eventually entered Mangshan County City.","It was dusk.","Outside Mangshan City, there was a bustling scene.","Many vendors and peddlers hurried into the city.","Numerous northern barbarians were also driving their beasts to carry goods into the city. Although there were frequent conflicts, trade continued uninterrupted. Sometimes, even when both sides fought fiercely, business went on as usual.","The Tang Dynasty sold military weapons, while the northern barbarians sold cattle, sheep, and iron ore.","Both sides had a tacit understanding not to attack the caravans.","Yang Xiao, as a Six-Coin Immortal Slayer Guard, found this unsurprising, especially since he had come for the demonic cult.","“The Chiyang Sect”","Publicly declared as the Sacred Fire Sect.","But everyone knew it was a completely demonic cult.","The headquarters of the Chiyang Sect was unknown, but several branches were set up in counties surrounding the Tang Dynasty.","That’s why Yang Xiao entered the city.","Initially, he planned to find some clues before entering the city, but he hadn’t seen a single person.","Those villages were desolate, as if uninhabited for a long time.","This was a county close to the capital, once home to millions, now nearly deserted.","Yang Xiao felt a sense of unease growing within him.","The closer he got to the city gates, the more intense the death energy became.","“Hurry up and get inside! The gates will close after an incense stick’s time, and you’ll have to wait outside until tomorrow!” The soldier guarding the gate kept urging.","Yet the caravans remained indifferent, and even the lone travelers were the same, walking with heads down, ignoring the warnings as if they hadn’t heard.","Yang Xiao, being alert, immediately sensed something was wrong.","Caravans feared bandits and demons outside at night, let alone the lone travelers.","Under normal circumstances, if a gatekeeper yelled like this, people would rush inside.","But here, they were indifferent.","Moreover, the yelling soldier seemed unaware that his words had no effect, standing aside with a silly grin.","Yang Xiao frowned deeply, stopping in his tracks. He muttered a spell and traced his fingers over his eyes, causing a golden light to flash.","“Heaven’s Eye!”","“Open!”","Buzz!","His eyes turned golden, scanning everything before him.","“What?”","Despite being well-informed, Yang Xiao couldn’t help but exclaim.","Outside the city gates, there were no living beings; everything he saw before was walking corpses. Each had a large hole in their chest, their faces already decayed, eyeballs hanging at the corners of their mouths, eyes dark and hollow.","The gatekeeping soldiers were skeletons, clad only in armor.","“Could it be that the entire Mangshan County is like this?” Yang Xiao felt a chill in his heart. If this were true, the entire Tang Dynasty might not fare any better.","This was the foremost county outside the capital!","While Yang Xiao was in shock, a row of people in black robes appeared on the city wall.","The leader wore a black robe with a hood, obscuring his features, but his chest bore the mark of fire.","There was no need to ask; it was someone from the Chiyang Sect.","“You still found out!” The man in the black robe sighed.","However, Yang Xiao remained unfazed, raising his head to look at the black-robed figure, sneering, “A simple illusion? Are you trying to fool a ghost?”","“Yes, I’m fooling you, this ghost!”","As the voice fell, nine black-robed figures on the city wall simultaneously made their move.","Each one was at the late stage of the Golden Core realm.","Every one of them had strength comparable to Yang Xiao.","These were the nine strongest individuals in Mang Mountain County and the only late-stage Golden Core experts of the Chiyang Sect in the county.","The nine of them joined forces, intending to kill Yang Xiao.","But Yang Xiao was calm because he was fearless!","He feared no one of the same level.","Even against Master Fengjue of Baoguang Temple, he had the strength to fight, let alone these mere demonic cult members.","Though they were at the late stage of the Golden Core realm, they all practiced side-door demonic arts, which were cultivation techniques that merely elevated their realm without being suitable for combat.","Yang Xiao raised his long spear, drawing a full circle.","His terrifying combat power forced three black-robed figures to retreat in shock.","“This Yang Xiao is indeed formidable, truly comparable to the strong of Jinwu Guard!”","“Hmph, even so, he won’t leave Mang Mountain County alive today!”","“Kill!!!”","The nine closed in again, each using different techniques, trying to trap and kill Yang Xiao on the spot.","The battle outside the city startled the birds and beasts in the forest. A crow perched on a branch cawed a few times, its red eyes glinting as it watched the fight below, then flapped its wings and flew away.","In Tai’an City, within the Zhanxian Tower of the palace.","On the top floor, the Grand Commander remained a silhouette with his back turned.","The originally silent top floor was disturbed as a gentle breeze swirled, and a black mist condensed into a humanoid shape, its voice hoarse, “Master, Yang Xiao is fighting with the Chiyang Sect people. He might perish!”","“Mm!”","The Grand Commander standing by the window kept his hands within his cloak, merely giving a slight acknowledgment, as if he had anticipated this outcome.","“Should we save him?” The shadow in the black mist asked cautiously.","The Grand Commander slightly tilted his head and calmly said, “Our Majesty dislikes being at a disadvantage. If we want to eliminate his Chiyang Sect, we must sacrifice some manpower, so he feels balanced.”","“I understand!” The black mist slowly dissipated.","In the palace, outside the Yangxin Hall.","Lord Han was not inside today; instead, he stood guard outside.","Because tonight, a distinguished guest had come to the hall.","Even he had to stand humbly outside the door.","“Hmm?” Lord Han frowned, sensing someone approaching, and asked in a hoarse voice, “What brings you here personally?”","Whoosh!","An elderly man in a black robe suddenly appeared in front of the hall. His eyes were waxy white, his face ashen, expressionless, and his voice was like a puppet, “The matter in Mang Mountain County can’t be contained!”","“What?”","Lord Han, usually composed, widened his eyes, frowning, “Didn’t your Chiyang Sect arrange nine late-stage Golden Core cultivators? Can Yang Xiao escape? Besides, there’s still a...”","“Yang Xiao concealed his strength; his current power is no less than Fengjue’s!” The white-eyed old man finished, turning to look inside the hall, muttering, “Hurry and notify His Majesty; the Zhanxian Guard is not easy to fool!”","With that, the white-eyed old man turned and left.","Lord Han watched him leave, gritting his teeth, but could only turn back into the hall.","In the dimly lit hall, two figures sat opposite each other.","“I’m aware of the situation. You must visit the Zhanxian Tower personally. Ask that old guy what he wants. As long as I can shut his mouth, I’ll give it!”","Lord Han withdrew upon hearing this.","“Sigh!” The Tang Emperor, dressed in a Daoist robe, sighed, his face obscured in the shadows.","The person sitting opposite him had a faint smile, saying, “What’s wrong? Can’t you control your own subordinates? Should I help you get rid of him?”","“Hmph, do you think this is child’s play? Wanting someone dead and they’re dead?” The Tang Emperor’s face shifted, his voice deep, “That old guy was a close minister of the late emperor, with forces spread across the entire East Land. Even though I’ve clipped many of his wings over the years, I can’t take him down. Three years ago, I might have acted against him, but the lesson from three years ago, I won’t forget!”"]},{"number":6303,"title":"Chapter 6303: Material Crystal","paragraphs":["Chapter 6303: Material Crystal","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“It seems her death has indeed drastically changed your temperament!”","The figure on the opposite side slowly rose and walked to the window, where he paused before smiling faintly. “The current progress is still too slow. You need to hurry up, or even when the Great Luo descends, it won’t meet your requirements!”","“The branches of the Chiyang Sect are constantly converging, and soon they will be gathered. There will be a batch of celestial energy tonight. I must trouble the Celestial Master later!”","At this moment, Tang Huang actually bowed respectfully to that person, his expression filled with utmost reverence.","...","At the Zhanxian Tower.","Chang Feng brought Han Gong to the top floor. After glancing at the Grand Commander, he wisely retreated.","“The matter of Yang Xiao is not my concern. I can’t handle it, nor do I want to. If you have the ability, go outside the city and kill him yourself. I won’t stop you!”","Han Gong’s expression changed. He hadn’t even stated his conditions, yet this domineering Grand Commander of the Zhanxian Guards had already relented.","For a moment, Han Gong was at a loss and uncertain. “Really?”","“Have I ever lied?” The Grand Commander sneered.","The two of them had nothing more to discuss. Having received the answer he wanted, Han Gong immediately vanished from the Zhanxian Tower.","His figure dashed towards the outskirts of the city.","Intercept and kill Yang Xiao!","Yet, deep down, he couldn’t understand why the Grand Commander would do such a thing. What benefit did it bring him?","This opportunity, even if it didn’t bring down the entire Chiyang Sect, at least a few eyesores could be eliminated. Yet, without any conditions, he had agreed directly.","The more Han Gong thought about it, the more puzzled he became. But just as he passed through the third city gate, he sensed a team of Chiyang Sect cultivators and immediately understood.","“Not good!”","At this moment, nine teams of Chiyang Sect cultivators entered the imperial city in succession.","But as soon as they stepped into the city, hundreds of presences appeared around them, all of whom were Golden Core stage cultivators.","Additionally, two squads of Jinwu Guards personally intervened.","“Haha, I’ve been waiting for you!”","Chang Feng descended from the sky, squinting as he scanned the Chiyang Sect members and roared, “Capture them all! Anyone who dares resist, kill them on the spot!”","“Yes, sir!”","Hundreds of Golden Serpent Guards and dozens of Jinwu Guards immediately took action.","By the time the belated Han Gong rushed back, it was already too late.","This battle had alarmed many.","It also left Han Gong astonished at the Grand Commander’s tactics and his ability to conceal so many Zhanxian Guard presences.","The person seated across from him smiled faintly. “What now? Can’t even control your own subordinates? Want me to eliminate him for you?”","“Hmph, do you think this is a game? Killing whoever you want?” Tang Huang’s expression shifted, and he said in a deep voice, “That old man was a close confidant of the former emperor, and his influence is entrenched across the entire Eastern Land. Even though I’ve clipped his wings over the years, I can’t bring him down yet. If this were three years ago, I might have acted against him, but I can’t forget the lesson I learned three years ago!”","The wind and rain tonight grew even stronger!","Within the Princess’s mansion, however, there was a scene of song and dance.","The hidden back garden where Jian Wushuang resided remained pitch black, but he was already quite satisfied. Being able to settle in Tai’an City and incidentally using Chen Yuan to resolve matters in the Eastern Land’s cultivation world meant that obtaining treasures in the future would naturally follow.","At this moment, he was playing with a black square object.","“A crystallized material, could it be left from when that cultivation world shattered back then?” Jian Wushuang wondered in his heart.","This was something he had found on the body of a Xian Guard.","Two days had passed since then, and those two Xian Guards had been thrown onto the street by him. He originally thought that the Princess’s mansion would have been searched by now, but after waiting for two days, no one came.","Just now, he sensed the turmoil outside again, indicating that Tai’an City was indeed unstable, so no one paid attention to him.","Therefore, he turned his attention back to studying the crystallized material.","The thought power he had burned last time had already recovered, so he was no longer afraid of being probed by any Nascent Soul experts, which was why he could act so fearlessly.","“The power within this crystallized material is indeed substantial, enough to bring me to the Golden Core perfection stage. However, just the power within the material alone can’t help me reach the Nascent Soul stage!”","Jian Wushuang’s heart stirred as he gripped the crystal in one hand, unabashedly devouring the violent power within.","The power of the material world was indeed formidable. Just this small piece, weighing two to three jin, was enough to bring him to the Golden Core perfection stage.","If he could obtain one hundred thousand jin, he would be invincible in the human realm.","Moreover, this method of devouring was something only he could accomplish. Others simply couldn’t do it, not even Xiang Yang.","“A small Xian Guard actually possessed such a precious item, and it was merely used to conceal his aura? What a waste of a treasure!” Jian Wushuang was quite satisfied as he held the now fully absorbed crystallized material.","Where there’s one, there might be two. Perhaps others also had such crystallized materials on them.","This was far more useful than any of those natural treasures.","“Brother Wushuang, you’ve really struck it rich this time, directly reaching the Golden Core perfection stage. When will you get me a piece to absorb as well?” Xiang Yang’s eyes gleamed with greed as he stared at the absorbed crystallized material, his eyes almost popping out of his head.","He had personally witnessed Jian Wushuang’s aura surge significantly in the short time it took to burn a stick of incense, and he was immensely envious.","Jian Wushuang casually tossed the crystal over and said indifferently, “You can’t absorb it. This is a unique secret technique I created back then. Although my power is gone, I still remember the principles clearly. If I can get two more pieces like this, I can reach the Nascent Soul stage. By then, no one in the Tang Dynasty will be able to stop me, and natural treasures will be yours to choose as you please!”","“That’s true. If you’re invincible, that means I’m invincible too. Haha, I have to admit, I’m really looking forward to the day you regain all your strength!” Xiang Yang said with a face full of envy.","He had seen how powerful Jian Wushuang was at his peak.","Unfortunately, what he saw wasn’t Jian Wushuang’s true form.","If Jian Wushuang’s true form appeared, this world wouldn’t be able to withstand it, and it would have been shattered by a single sword long ago.","Jian Wushuang also smiled and, in the calmest tone, said the most domineering words, “When I regain my peak strength, I will make this world regret being created!”","The next day, at dawn.","Outside the Princess’s mansion, a carriage had already been prepared.","The consort attended court daily, and although he lived in the imperial city, it was still more than ten miles away, so naturally, he needed to take a carriage.","Chen Yuan walked out of the mansion, adjusted his clothes, and boarded the carriage.","Sitting inside the luxurious carriage, he mentally rehearsed the matters he would report during the morning court session.","In recent days, he had repeatedly impeached the Shanhai Prefecture several times.","Moreover, it had already yielded significant results. A court commissioner had been sent to receive the refugees from the Jiang Kingdom.","Everyone knew that those who crossed thousands of miles of the sea weren’t mere refugees; it was essentially a luxurious fleet.","Each of them carried gold and silver treasures.","Anyone who went could gain benefits. The advantages that originally could only be taken by the local aristocratic families of Shanhai Prefecture had now been directly taken over by the court due to Chen Yuan’s actions.","This was only the first step, far from enough.","But court affairs couldn’t be rushed; they had to be tackled step by step.","Outside the palace gates, dozens of court officials were slowly gathering, heading to court together.","Chen Yuan, as the consort, held the rank of a third-grade censor, a prestigious position. Though it was a subordinate third grade, in the outside world, it would make him a top official, far surpassing the status of a local governor.","“Consort, you’re quite early today!”","“In recent days, the consort has been in the spotlight. Shanhai Prefecture is going to experience an earthquake this time!”","The group of officials made remarks, some teasing, some flattering."]},{"number":6304,"title":"Chapter 6304: Pavilion Elder","paragraphs":["Chapter 6304: Pavilion Elder","Because the prince consort knew how to conduct himself and how to be a good official, all the ministers in the court had high hopes for him. After all, the princess was the current","emperor’s own sister-his full-blooded sister!","With such a status, Chen Yuan was seen as having the potential to become the Chief Minister.","“You all overpraise me, my lords. This is merely my duty,” Chen Yuan responded modestly, though he concealed his true intentions.","Today, he had a significant scheme to reveal!","“Hmph, just wait! If today’s plan succeeds, it’ll be like grabbing them by the throat.”","On the surface, the prince consort appeared harmless, but beneath that facade, murderous intent surged within him.","As he entered the grand hall, the officials had already taken their seats.","Even the ever-mysterious and unpredictable Grand Commander of the Immortal-Slaying Tower had arrived early.","His presence puzzled many.","In the eyes of the court officials, this man was the guarantor of imperial power and a close confidant of the emperor. He rarely attended court sessions, usually reporting directly to the Tang Emperor if there was any issue. For him to attend court so early today clearly indicated that something significant was happening.","“Why is he here?”","Chen Yuan silently cursed in his heart. When he looked at the Grand Commander, there was hatred in his eyes, but also fear.","Many in the court harbored grudges against the Immortal-Slaying Tower.","The Immortal-Slaying Tower was not only a formidable force within the cultivation world but also had the authority to oversee the entire court. Even the prince consort feared them, not to mention the other officials. If the Immortal-Slaying Tower targeted someone, that person would be in for a rough time, if not facing death itself.","“Lord Yan, is the Grand Commander here today because of the matters in Shanhai County?”","Among the civil officials, all were on edge.","Lord Yan, who led them, raised an eyebrow and sneered, “Why should we concern ourselves with a eunuch? As for Shanhai County, it’s one of the most important coastal cities of the Tang Empire. If there were to be an investigation, it would be the task of the imperial inspectors, not the Immortal-Slaying Guards!”","Yan Zhong!","A central figure of power within the Tang Empire, head of the Six Ministries, and the Chief Minister of the Imperial Cabinet-he was second only to the emperor.","Only he would not fear the Immortal-Slaying Guards.","After all, he too was a close confidant of the Tang Emperor, perhaps even closer than the Grand Commander of the Immortal-Slaying Tower. He had no worries about the Guards trying to frame him. With the emperor’s protection, he could act with impunity.","Of course, he had to possess sufficient power, not only in his official capacity but also with the backing of his family.","The Yan family hailed from Changshui County in Mangshan Prefecture. Their ancestors had followed Emperor Wuzong six hundred years ago. Though originally military men, the family transformed into a prestigious civil service family thanks to Yan Zhong’s father.","In just a few decades, the Yan family became a renowned noble house in the Tang Empire. When Yan Zhong became the Chief Minister, the family reached its zenith.","In the court, both civil and military officials looked to this Chief Minister for leadership.","As for the emperor, he had been preoccupied with cultivation, leaving the heavy responsibility of the empire to Lord Yan.","The Imperial Cabinet was established because of him, reflecting the Tang Emperor’s trust in him.","Yan Zhong’s father had served under three emperors, and Yan Zhong himself had served two, even being entrusted with the care of the late emperor’s son. Thus, the current emperor trusted him enough to hand over much of the power to the Imperial Cabinet.","It reached the point where the emperor often skipped court sessions, leaving the Chief Minister to preside.","However, recent days had seen the entire court shaken by a single document from the prince consort.","The reason for the upheaval was interesting.","The prince consort’s main objective was revenge!","Meanwhile, the court officials sought to tarnish the reputation of the Immortal-Slaying Guards, as the details of the destruction of the Jiang Kingdom were still unclear. Even the fishermen of Shanhai County knew more than the court officials.","In this way, the officials had successfully outmaneuvered the Zhanxian Guards while also aiding the Imperial Son-in-Law.","Naturally, the two sides came together.","Though the Imperial Son-in-Law was merely a son-in-law, he was backed by the entire noble faction.","Today, their collaboration would undoubtedly strip the Zhanxian Guards of their power.","Now that the Grand Commander of the Zhanxian Guards had arrived, they assumed it was due to this matter.","Once they achieved their objective, they would become ravenous wolves, ready to crush the Zhanxian Guards or replace them with their own people.","This was the nature of court struggles; in an instant, they could tear the flesh from their","opponents.","A single misstep could lead to the confiscation of property and the execution of entire","families.","Such conflicts were akin to a dance of swords.","In the entire court, there was only one observer, the Emperor.","As the bell rang, a middle-aged man dressed in a black dragon-patterned robe appeared above the grand hall. His expression was resolute, and an indescribable aura of nobility surrounded him, overshadowing the immortal energy emanating from the cultivators.","He was the Emperor of the Great Tang Restoration, “Li Miao.”","“Morning court session!”","With the eunuch’s sharp voice, the morning court officially began.","Today’s topic was the Imperial Son-in-Law’s furious criticism of Shanhai Prefecture, with","the aim of targeting the Zhanxian Pavilion.","Of course, the main topic wouldn’t be brought up too quickly; there needed to be some","prelude.","It started with trivial matters, all of which were addressed by Elder Yan Zhong. Emperor Tang didn’t even listen, keeping his eyes closed and frowning the entire time.","This puzzled Yan Zhong, as this Emperor had always been a calm and thoughtful person. Why","was he frowning today?","Officials were masters of reading expressions.","Noticing the Emperor’s displeasure, Yan Zhong signaled for the Imperial Son-in-Law to","speak, introducing today’s main topic.","This matter had been discussed with the Emperor the day before.","The advantage of the inner cabinet was that they could report directly to the Emperor in","person.","In fact, many issues had already been communicated to the Emperor or the inner cabinet before they were brought up in the morning court. It wasn’t a place where one could speak","freely.","Time was limited!","Upon receiving Elder Yan’s approval, the Imperial Son-in-Law, Chen Yuan, stepped forward with a serious expression and solemnly said, “Your Majesty, Shanhai Prefecture has been massively accepting refugees from Jiang State, among whom are many influential figures from Jiang. These individuals not only brought gold and silver but also military equipment and armor. Such a significant matter has been concealed by Shanhai Prefecture for several months. Their intentions are undoubtedly malicious, harboring thoughts of rebellion!”","Rebellion?","This word was highly sensitive in court, as it implicated not just an individual but an entire group-a matter that could result in the collective loss of heads.","Upon hearing the Imperial Son-in-Law’s report, the Restoration Emperor immediately opened his eyes and looked directly at Chen Yuan, his brother-in-law.","“Elder Yan, regarding the Jiang State issue, why have I never heard of it?” Emperor Tang turned his gaze to Yan Zhong.","It seemed like a question about mismanagement, but in reality, the target was the Grand Commander of the Zhanxian Guards.","However, it wasn’t appropriate for him to confront the Grand Commander directly, and this was where Yan Zhong stepped in to relieve the burden.","“Your Majesty!” Yan Zhong cupped his hands and replied, “The Jiang State issue was brought to our attention a year ago through intelligence from the Zhanxian Guards, and it has been under investigation ever since. The Zhanxian Guards have always had the responsibility of monitoring the realm, regularly sending intelligence to the Ministry of War for analysis. However, this investigation abruptly stopped six months ago. As I am stationed in the capital and focused on my primary duties, I was powerless to continue. I humbly request Your","Majesty’s punishment!”","With those words, Yan Zhong spoke flawlessly.","He first praised the Zhanxian Guards, then clarified each party’s role.","One side monitored the realm, while the other governed it."]},{"number":6305,"title":"Chapter 6305: Your Servant, Willing to Die for His Advice","paragraphs":["Chapter 6305: Your Servant, Willing to Die for His Advice","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","One glance, one move.","Everyone performed their duties.","When the Zhanxian Guard received intelligence, they did everything they were supposed to do and kept following up on matters related to the Jiang Kingdom.","However, the reason they hadn’t followed up now was that they no longer had any intelligence from the Zhanxian Guard.","Yet, Yan Zhong took full responsibility and pleaded guilty to His Majesty.","But any intelligent person could see that this was all due to the intelligence issue with the Zhanxian Guard and had nothing to do with the Grand Elder.","Before the Tang Emperor could speak, the civil and military officials all began to persuade him.","“Your Majesty, the Grand Elder manages the cabinet and oversees the affairs of the world. This failure of supervision doesn’t fall under the jurisdiction of the cabinet!”","“Please, Your Majesty, be discerning!”","“Your Majesty!”","A series of pleas followed, but no one directly blamed the Zhanxian Guard.","They were all wise enough to know that even if His Majesty punished the Zhanxian Guard, he wouldn’t completely dismantle them. At most, there would be some penalties to maintain balance between the sides.","If they offended the Zhanxian Guard too severely, they’d surely face retaliation in the future, which wouldn’t be pleasant.","Grand Elder Yan had foreseen this long ago. For every person who feared them, there were those who did not.","Like those who had been wronged by the Zhanxian Guard.","Among the officials, a frail, white-haired old man slowly stepped forward. His hands trembled as he bowed, and though he appeared to be in his twilight years, his voice thundered like a storm.","“Your servant, willing to die for his advice!”","“The Zhanxian Guard has colluded with the remnants of the Jiang Kingdom and failed to report it, harboring sinister intentions. They are a blight on our Tang Empire. I beg Your Majesty to abolish the Zhanxian Tower!”","His words shocked the entire hall.","Yan Zhong took a deep breath and solemnly said, “Prince Yu!”","The other officials dared not utter a word.","The weight of those words was too heavy.","To die for advice—such a statement could indeed lead to death, especially when it involved the Zhanxian Guard, with their Grand Commander present in the hall!","Many secretly glanced at the Grand Commander of the Zhanxian Guard, wondering how this eunuch would retaliate.","Outsiders believed that the Zhanxian Guard only knew how to kill, but they didn’t realize that this Grand Commander had once wielded power to suppress the entire court.","If it hadn’t been for the Tang Emperor’s efforts to maintain balance by leaning toward the cabinet, the officials in the hall wouldn’t have dared to act so boldly.","“Uncle, why are you doing this...” The Tang Emperor seemed a bit surprised.","Not only was the Emperor taken aback, but so was the Imperial Son-in-Law.","He hadn’t expected things to escalate so quickly. Having only recently become the Imperial Son-in-Law, he lacked experience in court matters and couldn’t discern the true intentions of these old foxes.","Especially the one seated on the dragon throne.","“Let them stir things up, the more chaotic, the better. This way, the Shanhai Commandery will be turned upside down!” The Imperial Son-in-Law steeled his heart, deciding to watch how the situation unfolded.","Prince Yu, the leader of the meritorious nobles, had pledged his life for his advice. The other nobles understood that this time, they had to go all out.","After some hesitation, they too began to advise, advocating for the abolition of the Zhanxian Tower.","At this moment, the Grand Elder Yan Zhong stood aside, helping no one.","His role was to ignite the flames; the rest was no longer his concern.","As for Imperial Son-in-Law Chen Yuan, he was merely the one who had struck the match.","For a moment, the court was filled with passionate debate.","Emperor Guangfu furrowed his brows, remaining silent for a long while. His gaze occasionally drifted toward the Grand Commander, but internally, he was delighted.","The Zhanxian Tower had been a thorn in his side. In the past, he had chosen to endure certain things, but after last night’s incident, he could no longer tolerate it.","If he continued to endure, it would only jeopardize his plans sooner or later.","However, the Zhanxian Tower had grown too large to control. Despite several attempts to curtail its influence, the highest authority in the tower remained the Grand Commander—a loyal minister who had once served the late emperor.","Defeating it in one blow was impossible.","Moreover, balance was necessary.","Seeing that the situation had reached a critical point, Emperor Guangfu rubbed his temples, his voice weary. “Commander Wei, do you have anything to explain to me?”","A way out!","Upon hearing these words, the officials below were all startled, realizing that the emperor intended to protect Zhanxian Tower once again.","The emperor had now provided Commander Wei with an escape route. All it would take was a few flattering words and an admission of guilt, perhaps forfeiting some salary for a year or so, and the matter would be resolved.","All their efforts just now would have been in vain.","The elderly King Yu almost fainted at the sight, having waited many years for this opportunity.","“Wei Jiuxian!” King Yu ground his teeth in hatred.","Years ago, in an attempt to secure his eldest son’s path to becoming an immortal, King Yu had secretly divided spiritual mines within his fief. However, the Zhanxian Guard had discovered his actions, killing his son on the spot and confiscating the entire mine.","How could he not hate them?","He didn’t dare to hate the emperor, but he had no qualms about hating this eunuch—and his hatred was immense!","“Your Majesty, our Eastern Tang Empire spans a million miles of fertile land and governs countless millions of citizens. We cannot allow a eunuch to place the Tang Empire in jeopardy. Otherwise, I would be ashamed to face our ancestors!” After speaking, King Yu kowtowed again.","Emperor Guangfu’s eyelids twitched as he listened, his frown deepening. This time, the words struck a chord.","With the court now silent, everyone waited for the emperor’s response.","“Sigh!” Emperor Guangfu let out a long sigh and slowly stood up. His gaze swept across the court as he spoke in a restrained but angry tone, “Minister Wei, this matter started with the Zhanxian Guard. Do you have an explanation?”","In the end, the focus shifted back to Wei Jiuxian, just as initially planned.","Using today’s events to offset yesterday’s mistakes—such was the emperor’s strategy.","Reaching this point as emperor left Emperor Guangfu feeling somewhat helpless, but for the sake of...","In the court, Wei Jiuxian finally raised his head after hearing the emperor speak.","He slowly turned around, surveying everyone before fixing his gaze on Emperor Guangfu. In a solemn tone, he said, “I have no explanation to offer, Your Majesty. However, I must report that the situation in Mangshan County has already affected the capital. The demonic cult has ravaged the Eastern Tang region, leaving the southeastern nine counties empty of people. This is the critical issue for the Tang Empire, far more serious than any border conflict!”","As soon as he finished speaking, the entire court was shocked!","Empty of people?","The southeastern nine counties?","The officials who had lived in the capital all their lives had no idea of the actual situation outside. All they had received were reports filtered through layers of approval.","Now hearing Wei Jiuxian say that the southeastern nine counties were so devastated that not a single living person could be found, how could they not be shocked?","Senior Grand Secretary Yan Zhong was the first to stand up and angrily rebuke, “Absurd, utterly absurd! The southeastern nine counties have a population of tens of millions. How could they be empty? Over the past few years, the Tang Empire has enjoyed favorable weather, with no wars, plagues, or famines. How could so many people have perished?”","“Minister Yan!” Wei Jiuxian’s gaze turned cold as he responded, “I said it was due to the demonic cult’s ravages!”","His words directly targeted Emperor Guangfu.","Everyone in the court knew that in recent years, Emperor Guangfu had considered establishing the Chiyang Sect as the state religion. Yet, Chiyang Sect was nothing more than a demonic cult. Three years ago, they had been allowed to participate in the court, but they should never have been accepted into the imperial hall.","To the civil and military officials, the Chiyang Sect had behaved with restraint over the years, with no egregious actions. The idea of establishing it as a state religion seemed acceptable.","But now, hearing that the Chiyang Sect had committed such atrocities, their confidence wavered."]},{"number":6306,"title":"Chapter 6306: Guangfu Emperor \"Li Miao\"","paragraphs":["Chapter 6306: Guangfu Emperor “Li Miao”","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“It’s impossible! Just a few days ago, I received a memorial from the Southeastern Nine Counties. That’s from my disciple!” The Minister of Revenue was filled with surprise.","The Minister of Personnel also objected, saying, “Every year, hundreds of officials are dispatched to the Southeastern Nine Counties, and they return at the end of the year to submit memorials. If such a major incident had occurred, how could they have kept it a secret?”","For a moment, the entire court was full of doubts and objections.","Wei Jiuxian, however, smiled calmly. With a flick of his fingers, he produced a spark, which instantly transformed into a human figure.","“Desire King!”","Everyone was shocked!","A spark turned into the Desire King, looking exactly like him.","Then, with a few more transformations, it evolved into several high-ranking officials in the court.","Everyone watching was amazed.","“They’re all fake!”","After saying this, Wei Jiuxian put away this small trick.","Such illusions could deceive the civil and military officials, but not the Immortal Slayer Guard.","Since the Chiyang Sect had started working for the Restoration Emperor, he had discovered this issue.","It all began when a member of the Immortal Slayer Pavilion was killed, only to reappear later. Upon investigation, they learned that the later one was a puppet.","Because of this, he questioned the Tang Emperor, who subtly told him, “To keep the land but lose the people is not losing the land, but to lose the land means losing the people.”","The meaning was clear: for the sake of the eternal prosperity of the Tang Dynasty, the people would have to endure some hardship.","As a eunuch, as a court official living off the Emperor’s provisions, it was his duty to relieve His Majesty’s worries.","This was the most natural thing in the world.","But Wei Jiuxian couldn’t accept it!","“Your Majesty, please see clearly!” Wei Jiuxian bowed deeply!","Even if he lost his position today, he had to expose the truth about the Southeastern Nine Counties.","Because both the witnesses and evidence were there.","No one could overturn this case.","For a moment, the court fell into a terrifying silence.","Even the Desire King, who hated Wei Jiuxian to the bone, remained silent. His personal grievances paled in comparison to the foundation of the Tang Dynasty. If the Tang Dynasty no longer bore the surname Li, he would not have his current wealth and power.","The Restoration Emperor furrowed his brows, taking several deep breaths, and in his heart, he cursed, “Wei Jiuxian, I’ve given you opportunities, many opportunities. Why must you oppose me? You, a mere eunuch, dare to teach me how to govern the world!”","His eyes were filled with endless fury.","The roar within his heart was like a prehistoric beast howling, and black mist began to emanate from the center of his brows.","“If I am not strong, how can the Tang Dynasty prosper?” he consoled himself. The Restoration Emperor’s expression gradually calmed down.","After all, this was the morning court session, and he needed to summarize the day’s issues and make decisions.","On the surface, everything had to look proper and beautiful, while in private, nothing could go wrong.","“I am deeply grieved!” The Restoration Emperor, “Li Miao,” clutched his chest, his gaze complex, his tone heavy as he said, “The events of three years ago are still vivid in my memory. Where were all of you back then? If not for the Chiyang Sect’s assistance, how could I have restored the Tang Dynasty?”","These words indeed struck a nerve.","Especially for the civil and military officials; they truly felt useless.","In the past, there were two great contributors: one was the Immortal Slayer Guard, and the other was the Chiyang Sect.","Now, being scolded was something they couldn’t avoid.","“Of course, I must also thank Minister Wei and all the immortals within the Immortal Slayer Guard. Without them, I would never have made it out of Tai’an City. However, gratitude is one thing, but mistakes are still mistakes!”","The Emperor of Restoration’s tone shifted as he continued, “The Immortal Slayer Guard failed in overseeing the Shanhai Prefecture. As a result, the destruction of the Jiang Kingdom went unnoticed, with no intelligence reaching the cabinet. I have decided to remove Wei Jiuxian from his position as the Grand Commander, and let the Nanshan Protector take over. Minister Wei, you will temporarily oversee the southern city defenses!”","Wei Jiuxian, who was present in the court, wasn’t surprised. This was the price he paid for tearing through the heavens today. He had long said that this Emperor never made a losing deal.","“As for the matter of the nine southeastern prefectures, let the Ministry of Justice and the Dali Temple investigate together. As for the personnel selection for the inspection, let Chen Yuan lead the Immortal Slayer Guard to the nine prefectures and uncover everything!”","What seemed like a major matter was actually handled with a light touch.","Who didn’t know that Chen Yuan was the Emperor Tang’s brother-in-law, one of his own people?","What could possibly be discovered in the nine prefectures?","The light in Wei Jiuxian’s eyes completely dimmed.","Even Yan Zhong of the cabinet couldn’t help but frown. He was deeply dissatisfied with this, not because of the significant events in the nine prefectures, but because the Emperor was overly partial to the Chiyang Sect.","A demonic sect from the cultivation world, if not for its merit in following the dragon, would never have been allowed into the court. Yet now, it was being protected by the Emperor so openly, how could this not dishearten people?","“Dismissed!”","But with the court dismissed, what more could they say?","Wei Jiuxian closed his eyes slightly, took a deep breath, and walked out of the grand hall alone, his figure full of desolation.","The hatred that had once burned so fiercely in his heart could no longer be summoned at this moment.","This was the sentiment buried deep in the hearts of the court officials.","Chen Yuan, however, clenched his teeth in hatred. He hated Wei Jiuxian. If it weren’t for the massive issue Wei had exposed, today’s appointment would have made him the governor of Shanhai Prefecture!","Now, he had to inspect the Mangshan Prefecture of the nine southeastern prefectures.","His heart seethed with resentment!","The court session dispersed.","The Emperor of Restoration returned to the Hall of Mental Cultivation, but his heart was far from calm.","“Damn it, damn it, Wei Jiuxian!!!!”","The Emperor of Restoration could no longer maintain his composure, and his eyes were filled with dark mist.","Ever since he became a Nascent Soul stage cultivator, no one in the Tang Dynasty had dared to defy him. Yet last night, Wei Jiuxian had the audacity to withhold the Immortal Fate that he had ordered the Chiyang Sect to collect. How could he not be filled with hatred?","That Immortal Fate had taken the Chiyang Sect an entire year to gather.","Once he refined it, he would be able to rapidly advance to the late Nascent Soul stage.","Immortal Fate was a precious thing.","The reason he had broken through from an ordinary Golden Core cultivator to Nascent Soul was precisely because of the Immortal Fate refined by the Chiyang Sect. In just a few months, he had advanced to Nascent Soul and swept through the different kings.","Three years had passed, and no outsider could have imagined that he was already in the mid-Nascent Soul stage. At such a speed, there were few in the entire cultivation world who could match him.","If it weren’t for Wei Jiuxian ruining his plans, he would now be ready to break through to the peak of the Nascent Soul stage.","The Emperor of Restoration, Li Miao, grew angrier the more he thought about it, gnashing his teeth. His hands gripped the desk, causing it to crack and creak.","At this moment, a mist drifted into the hall, transforming into a figure in white robes.","“Already losing your composure?” The person who came spoke calmly, not at all concerned that the mighty Emperor was in a rage.","Li Miao’s response surprised people even more. He actually replied with respect, “I lost my focus and disappointed the Immortal Master!”","“It’s just a year’s worth of Immortal Fate. If you let it go, you can have the Chiyang Sect collect Immortal Fate from the thirty-six northern provinces. I’ve already shielded that area from heavenly sight. As long as you have enough manpower, within half a year, you can gather enough Immortal Fate to reach the peak of Nascent Soul!” The white-robed Immortal Master spoke with a calm tone.","However, the Emperor of Restoration hesitated, his expression revealing his inner conflict. He said, “The matter of the nine southeastern prefectures has already been exposed, and those thirty-six provinces...”","“What? Have you grown soft?” The Immortal Master showed no concern, floating closer and patting Li Miao’s shoulder, reassuring him, “To accomplish great things, one must be ruthless. What you hold in your hands is the greatest opportunity in the entire cultivation world. Once you succeed, the entire cultivation world will remember your name, not just this small Tang Dynasty!”"]},{"number":6307,"title":"Chapter 6307: Night Meeting","paragraphs":["Chapter 6307: Night Meeting","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Name!","The emperors of past generations all vied for fame!","Take Emperor Wuzong, for example. When he reclaimed the thirty-six northern provinces, his name was etched into history, becoming a source of pride for his lineage.","Li Miao not only wanted his name to be recorded in history, but he also wanted to leave a mark in the cultivation world, earning the reverence of billions.","“Alright, let’s do as the Immortal Master says!”","After only a moment of hesitation, Li Miao made his decision.","As he watched the mist surrounding the Immortal Master dissipate, he comforted himself in his heart, thinking, “Once I achieve great success, the entire cultivation world will belong to the Tang Dynasty. By then, they should be grateful to me, grateful for the prosperous era I will have created for their descendants!”","But he never considered—would those people even have descendants left?","In the imperial palace, at the Zhanxian Tower.","Wei Jiuxian walked alone to the gate, only to be stopped by guards.","“Wei Protector, Lord Nanshan has instructed you to go directly to the southern city wall. There’s no need to come to the Zhanxian Tower anymore!”","The two guards at the gate were new faces.","Wei Jiuxian, his body hunched, didn’t argue. He turned to leave, but before he did, he paused and, without turning his head, said calmly, “Tell Nanshan not to damage my chessboard!”","After that, he left directly.","In the southern city.","At the division of the Zhanxian Guards.","“Commander, are you just going to let that scoundrel Nanshan do whatever he pleases? He’s actually sending me to Shanhai County to oversee the refugees from the Jiang Kingdom. If I leave, Tai’an City will truly be under his control!”","Chang Feng’s face was full of frustration.","As the second-in-command of the Zhanxian Tower, he had always only followed Wei Jiuxian’s orders. Now that Nanshan was in charge, it was hard for him to accept.","Moreover, sending him to Shanhai County was clearly a move to sideline Wei Jiuxian.","Wei Jiuxian, with a calm demeanor, poured a cup of tea and pushed it towards Chang Feng, saying nonchalantly, “Then you should go to Shanhai County.”","“But...” Chang Feng hesitated, but when he saw Wei Jiuxian’s relaxed expression, he seemed to understand something. Lowering his voice, he said, “Commander...”","“My arrangements are not to be questioned. Even if you guess the plan, do not speak of it. Just do as instructed!” Wei Jiuxian handed a brocade pouch to Chang Feng.","After receiving the pouch, Chang Feng nodded heavily. He had always trusted the commander’s strategies. After finishing his tea, he accepted the order and left.","It was only after returning to his residence that he opened the brocade pouch.","Inside was just a short line of words, but after reading them, he was left utterly puzzled.","“Chen Yuan...”","He casually crumpled the paper, closing his eyes in contemplation.","Many things had happened in the court today, creating an air of uncertainty that even permeated the city.","That night.","At the Zhanxian Tower.","The powerful members of the Chiyang Sect, who had been captured by Wei Jiuxian, were released, though they no longer possessed the immortal fortunes they had brought with them.","There was no need to ask—Wei Jiuxian had taken those.","“Tonight, the northern gate will be left open for you. Follow this route to leave the city. Once you’re outside, someone will guide you!” Nanshan, sitting on a rattan chair, waved his hand dismissively. “Go now!”","...","At the Princess’s Mansion.","Tonight, the halls were filled with esteemed guests, the atmosphere bright and vibrant!","Chen Yuan was about to be appointed as the Inspector, heading to the nine southeastern counties.","This was an imperial envoy, essentially a promotion. Upon his return, he would likely be elevated at least two ranks. Moreover, heading to Mangshan County, Chen Yuan would hold substantial regional power as a high-ranking official.","Naturally, many came to offer their congratulations and bid him farewell.","Tonight, Chen Yuan truly experienced the glory of being surrounded by esteemed guests.","Some were friends, while others were colleagues or superiors.","For example, some of the officials from the Six Ministries held positions higher than his, which showed how much face they were giving him.","The banquet lasted until late at night. Chen Yuan, slightly tipsy, saw the guests off one by one at the door. Of course, he did not involve the princess in this task.","After all, she was of noble birth.","Moreover, the relationship between Chen Yuan and the princess was more like a partnership; they didn’t interfere with each other’s affairs, and each took care of themselves.","After the guests were gone, Chen Yuan let out a long breath, the smile on his face fading away as he walked alone towards his study.","He usually stayed in the East Courtyard, while the princess resided in the West Courtyard. They each had their own separate areas of activity.","In the West Courtyard, there were many small courtyards where male companions were kept, as well as some pavilions for entertainment, making it a lively place.","The East Courtyard was much simpler, with only a small bamboo grove and a few scattered courtyards.","Within the bamboo grove stood a pavilion, which was Chen Yuan’s study. This place was his sanctuary, and he had ordered the servants not to enter.","Familiar with the path, he pushed open the door, but his brows furrowed.","Someone was sitting in the main seat of his study.","The figure was shrouded in darkness, making it difficult to see their face.","However, Chen Yuan recognized the person at a glance. Either they were too familiar, or this person had left a deep impression on him.","“What are you doing here?” Chen Yuan’s tone was laced with impatience.","Seeing this person made his heart feel uneasy.","The shadowed figure scoffed, mocking him, “Now that you’ve become a prince consort, have you forgotten your old brother?”","“Hmph, don’t pretend to be close to me. We settled our scores long ago. If there’s nothing important, get lost!”","“Tsk tsk, how heartless!” The figure in the shadows shook their head, then cut straight to the point, “I’m here on orders. There’s something I need your help with.”","Upon hearing that they were on orders, Chen Yuan’s frown deepened. He turned to close the door and lowered his voice, “Is it about the Mangshan County affair?”","“Yes.” The shadowy figure nodded before continuing, “The selection for the journey to Mangshan County has been made. You will be accompanied by a team of imperial guards and a squad of Immortal-Slaying Guards. What you need to do is...”","After finishing the instructions, the shadowy figure revealed a sinister smile.","“Brother Chen Yuan, if you handle this well, your future path will be much smoother!”","As the voice faded, the shadowy figure also disappeared.","Chen Yuan was left alone in the pavilion.","It took him a while to recover, but before he could sit down, another shadow entered the pavilion.","“The Princess’s residence is quite lively today!”","The newcomer was masked and sat in the same spot where the shadowy figure had just been, startling Chen Yuan.","“Who are you to dare trespass in the Princess’s residence!” Chen Yuan immediately shouted in anger.","The masked person playfully responded, “What can a little Princess’s residence do to me? If I can come in, I can kill you. Do you understand?”","This was a blatant threat. Chen Yuan hesitated for a moment, then his breath immediately calmed down.","“I knew this time wouldn’t be peaceful.”","Feeling helpless, Chen Yuan smiled bitterly and said, “Alright, tell me, which great deity are you, and what instructions do you have?”","“Straightforward!” The masked person clapped their hands and said bluntly, “First, ensure Yang Xiao’s life is protected. Second, once you reach Mangshan County, do not interfere with Yang Xiao’s actions!”","“Was it Wei Jiuxian who sent you?” Chen Yuan immediately guessed the origin of the visitor, then sneered, “Your information is really fast. I just found out that Yang Xiao would be joining the team, and here you are right after.”","Now that he had guessed the identity of the visitor, Chen Yuan was no longer afraid. After all, he was now a government inspector and didn’t believe Wei Jiuxian would dare kill him."]},{"number":6308,"title":"Chapter 6308: Selfless","paragraphs":["Chapter 6308: Selfless","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Unfortunately, he had guessed right earlier but made the wrong gamble later.","Wei Jiuxian truly dared to kill him, and there would be no consequences to worry about.","Heading to Mang Mountain for inspection was already unfavorable for the Tang Emperor. If he were to die before even going for the inspection, the focus would shift, and they would start investigating the death of the Prince Consort.","This matter, like the death of Imperial Concubine Yi back then, would become an unsolved mystery. But because of the death of the concubine, the world’s attention shifted from why the different king rebelled to the death of the concubine!","It was a simple matter, and Wei Jiuxian would certainly know that.","If he really sent someone to kill Chen Yuan, then he would have fallen into the trap. The Tang Emperor would likely reinstate his official position and have him investigate the death of the Prince Consort.","In other words, killing the Prince Consort would be like turning back. If that were the case, why would Wei Jiuxian need to cause such a ruckus?","So, even if he could kill, he wouldn’t.","This was an open strategy.","“I cannot avoid answering this question. I’ll ask you just one thing: will you help or not?” The man in black spoke calmly, without any anger.","Chen Yuan, however, remained fearless and sneered, “Then is this a public matter or a private one?”","“Haha, breaking into the Princess’s residence in the middle of the night—what do you think, public or private?”","“So, it’s a private matter, right?” Chen Yuan shrugged.","The man in black nodded, “Correct!”","“Hmph!” Chen Yuan snorted coldly, defiantly saying, “Go back and tell Wei Jiuxian that I, Chen Yuan, have no private matters to discuss with him. If it’s public, he can go to the cabinet and find Elder Yan. If the Elder has any instructions, I will naturally not refuse!”","At that moment, Chen Yuan seemed like a mighty lord of the skies.","But the man in black looked at him as if he were a fool.","“You really aren’t afraid of death, huh!” The man in black shook his head and suddenly drew a dagger, swiftly thrusting it forward.","Yet, just as the dagger was about to reach Chen Yuan’s neck, it stopped abruptly. Chen Yuan, realizing it too late, broke into a cold sweat from fear.","He immediately shouted, “Senior, save me!”","“Hmm?” The man in black was slightly surprised. He was only trying to scare this Prince Consort, so why did the other party call for help?","Moreover, to dare to call for help in front of him, the other party must be highly skilled, capable of stopping him at such a close distance.","Sure enough.","In the next moment, the dagger in the black-clad man’s hand flew out, shooting straight through the window and stopping only after severing the roots of a bamboo tree outside.","A figure in a green robe slowly descended from outside the window and stood on the windowsill. The figure spoke, “He had no intent to kill, just wanted to scare you. But his heart deserves punishment. Do you want me to finish him off for you?”","“Finish me off?” The black-clad figure sneered, “Don’t you think you’re speaking a bit too boldly?”","“You can try!”","The figure in the green robe smiled indifferently, not taking the other person seriously at all.","Just a mere Golden Core perfectionist.","Even if that Grandmaster Feng Jue, who was invincible in the Golden Core stage, came, he could cut him down with a wave of his hand.","The figure in the green robe was none other than Jian Wushuang, who had been hiding in the Princess’s residence.","Since absorbing the spatial crystal, he had reached the pinnacle of the Golden Core stage. In fact, he had long been ready to break through to the next realm, but he still lacked the necessary treasure for the breakthrough.","He only needed one more of those spatial crystals to successfully advance. Unfortunately, he had no idea where to find another one. Moreover, after his breakthrough, his Thought power had greatly increased, allowing him to sense several powerful presences in Tai’an City that could pose a threat to him. Thus, he chose to keep a low profile and remained hidden in the Princess’s residence, waiting for the right opportunity to act.","Just last night, he had sensed a great battle taking place. However, he couldn’t seize the opportunity amidst the chaos, as a powerful expert at the Nascent Soul stage had been present.","If he had known that taking a risk last night might have given him the chance to break through to the Nascent Soul stage, he might have ventured out to try. But with Jian Wushuang’s keen insight, he knew that the events of last night would undoubtedly stir up a storm in Tai’an City. Coupled with the grand banquet the Princess’s consort was hosting tonight, he had already gathered a rough understanding of the situation.","That evening, he used his Thought power to cover the bamboo forest, and sure enough, he discovered someone arriving. He quietly listened outside.","As a result, he heard Chen Yuan’s cry for help and realized he could no longer stay hidden, so he revealed himself.","Moreover, he could guess that the other party belonged to the Zhanxian Guard, and they must have discovered that a formidable expert was hiding within the Princess’s residence. Otherwise, the earlier disappearance of those two Zhanxian Guards would surely have been investigated. However, with the Zhanxian Guard now facing its own troubles, they had no time to deal with such minor matters.","“Did you kill Jiang Jiu and Jiang Qi?” The man in black asked, breaking the tense silence as he stared at Jian Wushuang.","Jian Wushuang saw no need to conceal the truth and calmly admitted it.","“As expected, the Princess’s residence was indeed hiding a master. But who exactly is he? Could he be from the demonic sect?” The man in black speculated inwardly, yet he dared not make a move.","After all, anyone capable of killing two Golden Snake Guards under their noses was no ordinary person. The terrifying power that had just controlled his dagger further confirmed that the opponent was far beyond the Golden Core stage, though he didn’t exude the usual violent aura of a Nascent Soul cultivator. Either the other party had achieved mastery in controlling their power, or he was not a Nascent Soul cultivator.","The man in black was inclined to believe the former.","“With such strength, you must be no ordinary figure. Why are you hiding in this small Princess’s residence?” he probed further.","Jian Wushuang responded with a hint of menace, “Some things are better left unknown. It won’t do you any good to pry.”","The man in black, having been rebuffed, dared not press further. He decided to be straightforward instead, saying, “In that case, I won’t ask. But there is one matter I cannot let go. It concerns the lives of billions of people in the Great Tang. To you, billions of lives may have nothing to do with your cultivation, but please, do not interfere in this matter.”","Interfere?","Jian Wushuang had never intended to interfere. He was only interested in obtaining more treasures to enhance his strength.","As for the common people, the fate of the world—they no longer concerned him.","To him, mortal lives, with their mere century-long lifespans, were too short.","Even if billions of people perished, a hundred years later, billions more would be born.","This was why the human race spread across the entire Starry Sky.","Unlike those powerful races or special beings, who found it difficult or even impossible to reproduce, relying on the universe or even time and space to nurture them.","“This has nothing to do with me,” Jian Wushuang said, shaking his head, his expression still cold.","Seeing this, the man in black frowned slightly. It was as he expected—those with extraordinary power no longer cared about the lives of ordinary people.","Just as he was considering how to extricate himself from the situation, Jian Wushuang suddenly changed the subject and said, “However, I can help you with your previous request regarding Chen Yuan, but not through Chen Yuan.”","He didn’t want Chen Yuan to risk helping the Zhanxian Guard, so he intended to assist Yang Xiao himself.","Yang Xiao!","He had once been to the Kingdom of Jiang and might know about Jiang Shang’s mother.","Helping him while inquiring about the past events in Jiang Kingdom was a simple matter for Jian Wushuang.","This was an exchange.","There was no need to inform the man in black or Chen Yuan about it."]},{"number":6309,"title":"Chapter 6309: Guesses","paragraphs":["Chapter 6309: Guesses","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Is Senior really serious about this?” The man in black was a bit stunned.","Just moments ago, it seemed like there was no room for negotiation. Why had things suddenly changed?","Jian Wushuang’s tone was unfathomable as he said, “Indeed, and I will ensure he returns safely to the capital!”","“Then...” The man in black wanted to ask why but swallowed his words, recalling what Jian Wushuang had said earlier.","Although the truth couldn’t be spoken, Jian Wushuang could easily come up with a plausible excuse.","“Go back and tell Wei Jiuxian that when he sends people to the Shanhai County, I want them to kill a few individuals for me...”","...","At the southern city tower.","Wei Jiuxian sat by the chessboard, holding a piece in his hand, not placing it down for a long time.","“He wants me to help him kill a few noble families?”","“Yes!” Chang Feng respectfully replied, “According to Number One, these people are connected to Chen Yuan, and this time Chen Yuan went to Shanhai County because of them!”","“Heh, who would’ve thought, because of these nobles, I lost so much!” Wei Jiuxian stood up, gripping the chess piece with a sinister tone, “It’s time to clear out some small fry!”","Playing with the chess piece in his hand, Wei Jiuxian looked out beyond the city, replaying the events of the past few days in his mind.","“The tavern, the demon sect, and the suspected transformation into a baby...”","These events had all occurred within a matter of days.","When he connected the dots, two words surfaced in his mind.","“Jiang Kingdom!”","And since it was related to Shanhai County, it must have come from Jiang Kingdom.","“Chang Feng, do you remember the time when His Majesty ascended the throne and sent people to the Jiang Kingdom?”","“I remember, sir. It caused quite a stir back then. They were searching for a female cultivator, but when they couldn’t find her, the matter was left unresolved,” Chang Feng answered truthfully.","Wei Jiuxian nodded, “Among those sent to Jiang Kingdom, the leader seemed to be... Yang Xiao!”","“That’s right!” Chang Feng’s eyes immediately lit up.","Now, everything seemed to make sense.","Back then, the Guangfu Emperor had been concerned about a female cultivator who went to Jiang Kingdom and later sent the Zhanxian Guard to search for her.","When this female cultivator disappeared, the Guangfu Emperor had been troubled by it for a long time, but later, he suddenly let it go.","“Consort Yi!”","It was her appearance that made the current emperor forget about that female cultivator.","And the fight in the tavern was between a mysterious expert and a demon cultivator from the Chiyang Sect.","If it had been something aboveboard, the Guangfu Emperor wouldn’t have needed the Chiyang Sect to take action. He could have just sent the Zhanxian Guard.","But the Guangfu Emperor didn’t do that.","Instead, he sent a team of cultivators from the Chiyang Sect to deal with the mysterious cultivator.","There must be some unspeakable secret behind this.","This matter was likely only known to the Guangfu Emperor.","Even Jian Wushuang, who was involved, was unaware.","Thinking this, Wei Jiuxian’s gaze deepened. He had always felt that a shadow loomed over the Tang Empire these past years.","He couldn’t shake off the feeling no matter how hard he tried.","“Wasn’t there information that the mysterious cultivator went to investigate at the First Floor? Bring me the file; I want to review it again!”","Wei Jiuxian decided to conduct a thorough investigation from the beginning. Perhaps he could uncover some clues, exposing the plot of the Light Restoration Emperor.","...","At the Princess’s residence.","In the bamboo pavilion.","“Thank you, Senior, for your assistance just now!” Chen Yuan bowed slightly, but when he looked up, his eyes were red, and his voice was hoarse as he said, “Senior, it’s my fault. I’ve been planning for so many days, yet I couldn’t personally exact revenge. In the end, I still needed your help!”","Chen Yuan was deeply convinced by Jian Wushuang’s pretext.","From his perspective, Jian Wushuang seemed to be a reclusive expert who always kept his word.","To help an ordinary person seek revenge, he even collaborated with Zhanxian Tower, risking a great deal.","“This was something I intended to do from the beginning; you don’t need to worry about it!” Jian Wushuang patted him on the shoulder and continued, “We depart tomorrow. I will conceal myself within the Zhanxian Guards, but I will arrange for two friends to protect you openly. As for Yang Xiao, you must keep it a secret!”","Chen Yuan immediately knelt on one knee, speaking with a serious tone, “Please rest assured, Senior. I will take this secret to my grave. Even if someone cuts open my belly, I won’t reveal a single word!”","“Live well!”","After Jian Wushuang finished speaking, his figure disappeared from where he stood.","...","The next morning.","Outside the Princess’s residence, a group of people and horses had already assembled.","With the Princess seeing him off, Chen Yuan boarded the carriage, waving goodbye to her.","On the surface, both of them kept up appearances, ensuring there was no awkwardness.","Once Chen Yuan pulled down the carriage curtain, his expression turned cold.","This time, he was heading to Mangshan County with a mission.","Aside from Yang Xiao’s matter, he had other tasks to complete.","That task was to stall!","When he reached Mangshan County, the truth wouldn’t matter; what was important was how to smooth over the situation.","While he might not have been able to discern the nuances of yesterday’s battle, someone had pointed out to him that the more thoroughly this matter was investigated, the worse it would be for His Majesty.","And Yang Xiao was precisely the one investigating this matter, but Chen Yuan had no intention of dealing with Yang Xiao.","He had already thought of an excuse—what could an ordinary person like him do?","After all, Yang Xiao was a powerful cultivator at the peak of the Golden Core stage.","This time, though there were many experts accompanying the team, none of them could take down Yang Xiao without being noticed.","On the surface, the hundred Imperial Guards were all battle-hardened elite cavalry, led by Captain Dong Biao, a powerful innate-stage cultivator.","Individually, they might not be much, but their combined strength was formidable.","The hundred elite troops he commanded could surround and kill a Golden Core cultivator.","In addition to them, there was also a squad of Zhanxian Guards.","Two of them were Jinwu Guards, both late-stage Golden Core cultivators.","And this didn’t even include Yang Xiao.","Besides the Jinwu Guards, there were ten Jinshe Guards.","With the strength they showed openly, it would be easy to sweep through some minor sects.","Secretly, there was also a Seven-Qian Zhanxian Guard.","He had been assigned to eliminate Yang Xiao.","Chen Yuan couldn’t command him since he wasn’t on the official escort list.","Apart from the hidden experts from Zhanxian Tower, there was also a cultivator from Chiyang Sect, whose strength rivaled that of Yang Xiao.","They had made thorough preparations, determined to ensure Yang Xiao perished on the way to Mangshan County.","Beyond these overt and covert forces, there was also a man and a woman traveling under the guise of being the Princess’s retainers. They were Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang.","Initially, Chen Yuan hadn’t wanted to bring them along on this journey, but considering that Tai’an City wasn’t exactly peaceful at the moment, it was better to have them along.","As for Jian Wushuang himself, no one knew his whereabouts except for him.","He had intended to conceal himself within the convoy, but later Jian Wushuang realized there was no need for that.","His thought power extended outwards, already covering a fifty-mile radius.","At the speed of the convoy, it would take an hour to cover fifty miles, while Jian Wushuang only needed the time it took to burn a stick of incense.","So, he moved along, stopping occasionally to survey the surroundings.","He could clearly see every person within fifty miles, whether in the open or hidden, yet no one could detect his presence.","Such formidable thought power had already surpassed that of a Nascent Soul cultivator—this was Jian Wushuang’s confidence.","Relying on his thought power, he constantly monitored the situation within the convoy.","Those openly visible weren’t a concern to him.","However, the two hidden experts were somewhat troublesome."]},{"number":6310,"title":"Chapter 6310: Shopkeeper, Waiter, Chef","paragraphs":["Chapter 6310: Shopkeeper, Waiter, Chef","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Two figures stood before them, one of whom was a Seven Coin Zhanxian Guard, while the other exuded a towering demonic aura, likely the Supreme Elder of the Chiyang Sect, whose strength had reached the Nascent Soul stage.","However, it was neither a true nor a false Nascent Soul, but rather a Dead Nascent Soul cultivator.","Cultivating this kind of Nascent Soul naturally led to overwhelming demonic flames, as such Dead Nascent Soul cultivators required countless living infants as nourishment.","Living infants, of course, referred to babies who were still alive.","Although Jian Wushuang had seen much in his time, encountering this demonic cultivator in this mortal world still surprised him.","The peculiarity of the cultivation technique, combined with the reckless behavior of the cultivation world here, was a rarity.","In the mortal cultivation world outside, such a demonic figure would likely be hunted down by the righteous path, with no rest until one of them perished.","The righteous and demonic paths were irreconcilable, always clashing, all for the sake of upholding a single principle of the Dao.","Where there were those who pursued the righteous path, there would inevitably be those who fell into the demonic path.","But this world lacked such a balance.","Perhaps it was due to the rule of the Tang Emperor, or perhaps because the sects within the cultivation world had grown too desolate.","For instance, in the entire Eastern Land’s cultivation world, sects had withered, long gone was their former prosperity, and even a complete inheritance had not been passed down for ages.","Most sect cultivators could only reach the Golden Core stage at best.","Those few who managed to become Nascent Soul stage cultivators had either encountered ancient fortuitous events or possessed exceptional talent.","Unfortunately, the spiritual energy in this world had dimmed, and the Dao of Heaven was sealed, making ascension impossible, which meant that for many years, no strong experts had emerged from the Divine Aspect Realm.","In Jian Wushuang’s view, it wouldn’t take many more years before this mortal world would completely transform into a peaceful land, with no more cultivators remaining.","Given the current situation, there was still hope for advancing to the Divine Aspect Realm in the next century, but beyond that, the prospects looked bleak.","The Divine Aspect Realm was a critical threshold—manifesting one’s Dharma Form, that was the true realm for displaying divine abilities.","Even with Jian Wushuang’s powerful thought power, if he were targeted by a Divine Aspect Realm cultivator, he would be captured by their spatial shrinking abilities.","Therefore, the absence of Divine Aspect Realm experts was fortunate for him.","Whoosh!","Standing atop the branches of a bush, Jian Wushuang exhaled a breath, and his figure flashed as he continued on his journey, always staying ahead of the group.","The speed of the convoy couldn’t compare to that of cultivators; after traveling for most of the day, they had just barely left the vicinity of Tai’an City.","By dusk, they finally reached the border of Mangshan County, still some distance away from Mangshan City.","The captain of the imperial guards glanced at the sky, slowing the pace and approaching the carriage. He called out loudly, “Lord Chen, I suggest we find an inn to rest for the night, and head straight for Mangshan City first thing tomorrow!”","“Very well, you handle the arrangements!” Chen Yuan accepted the suggestion.","He had come this time only to follow orders. Whether or not the mission succeeded didn’t matter, but he had to heed the advice.","Even if he did nothing at all, returning to the capital would bring no punishment.","He was simply being cautious, fearful of any unforeseen incidents.","If this Dong Biao turned out to be someone under the Emperor’s orders, aiming to eliminate Yang Xiao, then he would have to obey, or else face questioning and punishment upon returning to the capital.","However, he had no concern for Yang Xiao’s safety.","Because Jian Wushuang was watching in secret.","At this moment, Jian Wushuang stood atop a tree thirty miles away, his figure concealed in the shadows of dusk.","His thought power expanded, and every word spoken by Dong Biao reached his ears clearly.","“This Dong Biao, there’s something off about him!”","Jian Wushuang’s brow twitched. Just ten miles away, there was an inn, but it appeared brand new, almost as if it had been prepared specifically for their rest.","Inside, there were only three people.","A shopkeeper, a waiter, and a cook.","Three people!","Yet none of them emitted any aura.","This was what surprised Jian Wushuang.","He knew that his Thought Power was now several times stronger than that of the perfect Nascent Soul stage, comparable to the Divine Appearance stage.","Yet, he couldn’t sense any aura from the three of them.","“It’s impossible that all three are at the Divine Appearance stage!” Jian Wushuang shook his head, dismissing such a ridiculous thought.","No aura, and even their eyes were void of any soul.","There was only one possibility: “Puppets!”","“Who would have thought that this world actually possesses puppet techniques? This is considered top-tier divine power in an ordinary cultivation world. It must be an ancient inheritance from the Northern Region Glacier!”","He didn’t believe that the cultivators of this world, whether at the Golden Core or Nascent Soul stage, could create puppets.","After all, this was the lowest level of the cultivation world.","They didn’t even have enough resources, companions, or land to support the crafting of puppets.","The Tao of the cultivation world differed greatly.","Take, for example, the Greenfire World from back then, which was a top-tier cultivation world.","Later, the Divine Power Universe appeared, which was no longer just a cultivation world; it divided the entire material realm into upper and lower worlds.","To put it simply:","The construction of the world had five levels.","These were the five major layers, and within each, there could be many subdivisions, though Jian Wushuang didn’t delve too deeply into them.","He categorized the world he had emerged from.","The earliest continents were considered the second-layer world, which also included the later Greenfire World.","The first layer was the entirely mundane world, a paradise where there was no survival of the fittest. The Heavenly Dao was relatively fair, and everyone faced birth, aging, sickness, and death, along with the exhaustion of lifespan.","The second-layer world was where the Heavenly Dao allowed some extremely gifted individuals to defy the natural order, entering the path of cultivation and mastering the laws of creation and destruction.","The third-layer world encompassed universes like the Divine Power Universe and the Void Power Universe, which included countless material worlds that merged to form a universe.","Such a universe was a product of the Heavenly Dao.","At its peak were the Ancestral Gods.","No matter how much one defied the heavens, there was only so much one could achieve.","Only by going to the Great Yan Huanyu and entering the original universe birthed by time and space could one advance further.","This was the formidable nature of the fourth-layer world.","In the universe born from primal forces, even the Dao could be controlled. Both the universe and time-space could be governed.","This included the Realm God Continent as well.","However, the Realm God Continent was the pinnacle of the fourth-layer world.","It existed between the starry sky and time-space.","One could become a Universe God at its peak.","As for the Time-Space Gods, Jian Wushuang wasn’t entirely sure.","Since entering this world, he believed that the so-called Universe Gods and Time-Space Gods didn’t differ in terms of realms but in a specific type of power.","Back then, Miesheng was still considered a Starry Sky God!","He didn’t think Miesheng’s strength was particularly formidable. If he could return to his peak, dealing with ten peak Mieshengs wouldn’t be a problem.","Universe Gods, Time-Space Gods, Starry Sky Gods—these were merely titles.","For example, Universe Gods didn’t have levels; they were distinguished by the strength of their power.","Those with strong power were Nine-Star Universe Gods, while the weak ones were One-Star Universe Gods.","A powerful Universe God could certainly kill a Time-Space God or even a Starry Sky God.","It all depended on divine power.","The divine power of the universe and that of time-space were undoubtedly different.","Perhaps only after crossing the Divine Tribulation and heading into the starry sky would one understand.","But that was still a long way off for him, just a fleeting thought in his mind.","He then swiftly moved toward the strange inn.","A distance of ten miles was covered in just a few leaps, and he arrived at the inn’s entrance.","“Waiter, I’d like a room!”"]},{"number":6311,"title":"Chapter 6311: The Level of the World","paragraphs":["Chapter 6311: The Level of the World","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang wore a cloak, his face obscured, but from his attire, he resembled a martial arts master.","Carrying a sword on his back, he looked like a wandering swordsman, his face hidden as he journeyed far.","The waiter appeared dull-eyed, but his hands and feet were quick, and his tone carried the air of the common folk. He eagerly welcomed Jian Wushuang inside.","“Would you prefer an upper room or a middle room?” The waiter bent over, bowing his head with a smile.","Jian Wushuang took out a money pouch from his waist and slammed it onto the table, declaring loudly, “An upper room, and bring me two jars of good wine, a pound of cooked beef, and a plate of peanuts!”","“Right away, sir! Please wait a moment; I’ll arrange it immediately!”","His arrangement was merely shouting back to the kitchen and then retrieving a key from the innkeeper, which he respectfully handed to Jian Wushuang.","Taking the key, Jian Wushuang pulled out a piece of silver from his pouch and casually tossed it to the waiter, saying generously, “This is for you!”","With that, he headed straight upstairs.","After a short while, the waiter enthusiastically knocked on the door and entered, placing the wine on the table before respectfully retreating.","Jian Wushuang sat cross-legged on the bed, not touching the wine. His thought power spread out, enveloping a fifty-mile radius, always keeping an eye on the convoy.","He wanted to be thorough in his actions, not letting the presence of this strange inn make him think he knew everything. He continued to watch the convoy and kept his focus on Yang Xiao.","He needed to ensure that Yang Xiao remained safe.","Then, he would find an opportunity to ask about matters related to the Jiang Kingdom.","Especially regarding Jiang Shang.","“Jiang Shang!” Jian Wushuang’s thoughts triggered memories from years ago.","The events of that time could not be severed!","Because of his helpless actions, Hui Qing’s Dao Heart had wavered several times. This was all cause and effect!","If it hadn’t been for the coercion of the White King...","“Sigh!”","Jian Wushuang let out a long sigh.","To speak of this matter, one must blame Zhen Ling. If Zhen Ling hadn’t brought Demon Sound Mountain to the Heavenly Realm, he wouldn’t have gone there to receive the legacy of the physical trials.","Without that legacy, he wouldn’t have entered the Heavenly Realm early, and thus wouldn’t have been captured by the White King.","This led to him being coerced by the deities and the White King, forced into a blood sacrifice.","Inadvertently, he had killed Jiang Shang’s brother during his mortal period.","This had caused such a mess.","He had thought this matter was long past, but upon entering this vast world, he unexpectedly found traces of Jiang Shang once more.","“Could it be that she has been reincarnated?” Jian Wushuang raised an eyebrow but quickly dismissed the thought.","A Universe Master who had fallen in the long river of time and space would not come to the Realm God Continent!","Nor would they enter this world.","There must be a reason behind it.","He could only explore it slowly.","But no matter what, this time, he wouldn’t make the same mistake.","He would not repeat the same error twice.","“No matter if you are the Jiang Shang of old, I will safely bring you to Hui Qing!”","...","Outside the inn.","The previously peaceful street suddenly bustled with activity.","A group of wild-looking foreigners from the north, driving beast-drawn carriages, collided head-on with Chen Yuan’s convoy coming from the south.","The two sides began arguing outside over the stables.","As a captain of the imperial guard, Dong Biao had fought on the battlefield and battled these wild foreigners before. Seeing them now made his eyes burn with rage. Although relations with the foreigners had eased in recent years, with both sides engaging in trade, they still wouldn’t show each other any kindness.","“Damned foreigners!” Dong Biao cursed inwardly. However, this time, they had important matters to attend to, and there were strong individuals among these foreigners as well. Not wanting to cause unnecessary trouble, he scowled and reprimanded, “You savages, don’t you prefer living in the wild? Why are you staying in an inn?”","His words were harsh, but they were already the most polite he could muster.","Otherwise, he would have simply told them to get lost!","The foreigners didn’t back down either. One of them, a seductive woman with bronze skin adorned with various ornaments, glared at him and retorted angrily, “Hmph! Aren’t you Central Plains people always boasting about being a land of etiquette? According to your sages’ teachings, shouldn’t you be treating your guests with respect?”","Her words stunned Dong Biao. He hadn’t expected her to be so familiar with the Tang Dynasty.","“Now it seems that you’ve ignored the words of your sages, only picking the parts that benefit you. How hypocritical!” The seductive woman sneered at Dong Biao.","For a moment, Dong Biao didn’t know how to respond. He had never been humiliated like this before. If this were a battlefield, he would have already drawn his blade and cursed his enemy.","“Courting death!” Dong Biao roared in fury, drawing his sword.","A hundred Imperial Guards immediately drew their weapons as well, tightening their reins, ready to charge at any moment!","However, Chen Yuan, who had been observing from the carriage, stopped Dong Biao at this critical moment.","“Wait!”","Chen Yuan lifted the curtain and stepped out, his gaze falling on the seductive woman from the Cang Clan.","This matter could be handled either lightly or seriously. It wouldn’t be wise to kill this foreign merchant caravan over a verbal dispute; that would be inviting trouble.","As the officer in charge, he would have to take responsibility if something went wrong, but he also needed to handle the situation effectively.","If he didn’t, it would undermine his subordinates’ authority, which would in turn undermine his own.","Although he hadn’t spent many years in officialdom, he had learned plenty of techniques for managing subordinates.","He first signaled Dong Biao to sheath his sword, then dismounted and approached the Cang Clan’s merchant caravan. The Zhanxian Guards followed closely behind.","Among the ten Zhanxian Guards were elite Jinwu Guards, whose imposing presence alone could crush the caravan.","Even the sharp-tongued seductive woman couldn’t help but take a half-step back.","It wasn’t until an old man behind her gently placed his hand on her shoulder that she regained her composure.","“Those are Jinwu Guards from the Zhanxian Guard. It’s best not to act recklessly,” a voice warned in her mind. The seductive woman’s expression changed slightly, but she responded with a subtle nod.","Seeing that his message had been received, Chen Yuan raised his hand and instructed, “Show some respect!”","Only then did the Jinwu Guards retract their overwhelming aura, allowing the foreigners to breathe freely again. They gasped for air, as if a weight had been lifted from their chests.","“These people in battle gear must all be Great Immortals. Who is this man?” Some beast tamers in the caravan, despite their shock, couldn’t help but marvel at the power of the Tang Dynasty, where ten Great Immortals were protecting a mere mortal.","The man must be one of the highest-ranking individuals in the Tang Dynasty.","Otherwise, there wouldn’t be so many Great Immortals guarding him.","In the wild regions, the Cang Clan referred to cultivators at the Golden Core stage as Great Immortals.","Just like how the eastern lands called them Immortals, it was merely a title.","Chen Yuan glanced at the people who had been subdued and softened his expression, speaking kindly, “Young lady, you mentioned the way of hospitality earlier. Indeed, that is a tradition of the Tang Dynasty. ‘Isn’t it delightful to have friends come from afar?’ Of course, we should show hospitality, and we should offer the best.”","These words immediately won over many members of the foreign merchant caravan. After all, standing before them was a harmless-looking scholar, surrounded by a group of intimidating Great Immortals. It was only natural for them to develop a favorable impression of him. Moreover, in their eyes, it was astonishing that someone of such high status would speak so courteously to them."]},{"number":6312,"title":"Chapter 6312: Saint’s Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 6312: Saint’s Dao","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“This... does this mean you intend to give the stable to us?” The seductive woman’s voice was sharp, her alluring gaze fixed on Chen Yuan as she waited for his response.","Chen Yuan smiled faintly, but his tone quickly shifted to one of seriousness as he said, “We will give it, of course. But before we do, I need to make you understand the essence of the Great Tang’s etiquette. Just because you are guests doesn’t mean you can act recklessly!”","As soon as he finished speaking, his aura became imposing, and the once frail scholar appeared as if he had transformed into a saint.","“The concession of etiquette is the host’s choice, not something the guest demands. I hope you remember that what this official gives you is yours; what is not given cannot be asked for, and certainly cannot be taken by force!”","After speaking, Chen Yuan paid no attention to their shocked expressions. With a wave of his hand, he loudly commanded, “Captain Dong, lead the imperial guards to rest in the nearby woods. Let them have the stable. The rest of you, follow me to the inn for some rest!”","After giving his orders, he smiled slightly, cupped his hands toward the foreign caravan, and then turned to lead his men into the inn.","Dong Biao, his eyes burning with admiration, felt deeply satisfied by the words he had just heard.","He found it even more satisfying than giving the other party a beating and now held a newfound respect and reverence for Chen Yuan.","The Zhanxian Guards, however, who had seen much in their time, felt it was nothing special. They remained silent, showing no particular reaction as they continued to follow Chen Yuan.","Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang, who trailed behind Chen Yuan, each had their own thoughts and did not give the matter much consideration.","Upstairs, Jian Wushuang’s lips curled into a faint smile.","It was nothing more than a petty trick.","He then withdrew his thought power until it covered only a three-mile radius, then stopped.","An invisible force swept through the entire inn, monitoring everyone present.","Including the foreigners.","Both groups entered the inn one after the other. Due to the number of people, they all sat down in the first-floor hall.","Having learned from the earlier encounter, these foreigners no longer dared to provoke anyone. They obediently drank their wine and ate their meat.","Chen Yuan, having ridden all day, had little appetite. He drank only a bowl of clear water before calling the innkeeper to prepare a room upstairs for him to rest.","The Zhanxian Guards, tasked with his protection, were not interested in feasting downstairs either. They rose and took up rooms next to Chen Yuan’s. With their Golden Core cultivation, their thought power was more than enough to cover the entire inn, ensuring Chen Yuan’s safety.","The sky grew completely dark.","The inn, however, remained brightly lit.","In the first-floor hall, besides the dozen or so foreigners from the caravan, there was also Dong Biao and his imperial guards.","The guards, being numerous, had chosen to eat in shifts.","As for resting, they had no choice but to use the sky as their blanket and the ground as their bed.","Both groups were boisterous by nature, and soon enough, they had all ended up at the same table.","Particularly, a few burly men from the caravan struck up a conversation with Dong Biao, and the more they talked, the more animated they became. The seductive woman was by their side, urging them to drink.","Despite having been ordered not to drink, Dong Biao, under the pressure of their hospitality, took a sip to be polite.","But with alcohol, once you have the first sip, the second follows.","And once one person drinks, others do as well—otherwise, it would be seen as unfair treatment.","Before long, everyone was getting along like old friends, drinking one jar of wine after another.","The innkeeper, however, did not even raise an eyebrow. He showed no sign of being pleased by the sudden influx of business; instead, there was a glint of murderous intent in his eyes as he glanced at Dong Biao.","“Add something to their wine. Let’s send these fools on their way sooner rather than later.”","The innkeeper’s assistant, grinning slyly, was not at all surprised. He even called out loudly, “Sure thing! Ten more jars of good wine coming right up!”","With that, he headed to the wine cabinet, grabbed the jars, and brought them over.","But this time, the wine was different.","Within the time it took to drink a cup of tea, the burly foreigners and the imperial guards, including Captain Dong Biao, were all flushed and unsteady on their feet.","“To... tonight ends here. Next time, next time when we reach Tai’an City, I’ll treat you to the best wine!” Dong Biao mumbled as he staggered toward the door.","He had no idea that everyone else had already collapsed on the tables, unable to get up.","Fortunately, his strength was formidable enough to allow him to walk out steadily.","Once he was far enough away, the assistant’s smile faded. After shutting the door, his tone and demeanor changed as he scanned the foreigners and glanced at the innkeeper.","“Get ready to move!”","The shopkeeper nodded and clapped his hands. A chef with a plump figure emerged from the kitchen.","The three of them made no sound or movement detectable by even those in the Nascent Soul stage.","But they couldn’t escape the keen eye and thought power of Jian Wushuang.","Just as the three were about to make their move, several powerful beings within the caravan suddenly stood up without warning. The drunken haze in their eyes vanished, replaced by a fierce and violent energy.","Even the alluring woman among them revealed her true power. All five of them were cultivators at the Golden Core stage.","Three of them were in the late Golden Core stage, while the alluring woman was in the mid-stage. However, a red centipede slowly crawled out from her arm, growing larger by the second until it reached the thickness of a water barrel and stretched several meters long.","“Heavenly Centipede!!!”","The shop assistant exclaimed, “You’re not from the Cang Clan caravan! You’re sorcerers from the Thousand Legs Tribe!”","The Thousand Legs Tribe was a savage tribe near the northern glaciers, with only a few thousand people. Yet, their strength was incredibly formidable.","Many children were born as innate beings, and even those with poor talent could become innate warriors as adults.","In this tribe of a few thousand people, dozens of Golden Core cultivators could emerge.","But that wasn’t the most terrifying part. The Thousand Legs Tribe had a powerful lineage of sorcerers who could control centipedes.","The tribe was named after their totem—the centipede. The ferocious centipedes they raised were unmatched in the world, causing significant losses to the Tang Dynasty multiple times.","The alluring woman shifted her body and looked at the shop assistant with an eerie gaze. “Even you puppets know about the Heavenly Centipede? Then let it send you on your way!”","“Heh, even if it’s a Heavenly Centipede, it’s still just flesh!” The shop assistant tore off his shirt, revealing a body as black as ink, crafted from a unique crystalline material. Not only was it incredibly hard, but it also blocked any aura.","The shopkeeper and the chef, on the other hand, had silver bodies, clearly made from different materials.","The three of them had no aura, making it impossible to gauge their true strength.","However, as the two sides clashed, the hall was instantly destroyed.","Despite the fierce battle below, there was no movement from upstairs.","Even if they were blind, they certainly weren’t deaf.","Everyone knew a fight had broken out below, but the identities of those involved remained unclear. The reason behind the conflict, however, likely had something to do with Yang Xiao within the group.","Chen Yuan stood at the door, peeking through a crack and frowning deeply.","“Damn it, I should’ve known better and camped outside!” Chen Yuan muttered in frustration.","If they had stayed in the wilderness, it would have been easier for Jian Wushuang to remain hidden. Even if the Zhanxian Guards attacked, Jian Wushuang could have easily escaped.","“Let’s hope everything goes smoothly!”"]},{"number":6313,"title":"Chapter 6313: Ecstatic Joy","paragraphs":["Chapter 6313: Ecstatic Joy","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Next door, ten Zhanxian Guards gathered together, all observing the battle.","Yang Xiao, on the other hand, was alone in his room, also watching the fight.","“The Great Commander is truly a divine person, to have anticipated that we would stay at the inn and even encounter a mysterious expert’s attack!” he thought, his heart filled with admiration.","Before leaving Tai’an City, the Great Commander had instructed him that if he encountered foreign races at the inn, he could choose to trust them.","However, he was not to act rashly.","Because the Great Commander had a backup plan, and that plan was Jian Wushuang.","After all, if there was help available, there was no need for Yang Xiao to take risks.","At this moment, however, Yang Xiao was feeling a bit restless. Ever since he had taken on nine opponents in Mangshan County, his strength had advanced once more. Within the Zhanxian Guards, he had received complete inheritance and had been granted treasures. Now, all he lacked was an opportunity. Perhaps a great battle could help him find the breakthrough to the Nascent Soul stage.","......","“I wonder if Senior Wushuang is here. In this situation, should we just keep watching?” Jiang Shang was a bit worried.","The battle below was causing quite a commotion.","Especially that centipede—its aura was even stronger than someone at the peak of the Golden Core stage. Under the control of the alluring woman, its combat power was nearly comparable to someone at the Nascent Soul stage.","Yet, when it encountered the three puppets, it couldn’t even inflict damage.","Their defense was astonishing!","It could be said that they were invincible within the Golden Core stage.","Xiang Yang stood with his arms crossed, also watching the battle, but his expression remained calm. He said, “Don’t worry, these people are likely here for Yang Xiao. Since Brother Wushuang arranged for us to protect Chen Yuan, there’s no need to intervene. Just watch.”","“Okay!” Jiang Shang nodded slightly.","The reason she was a bit anxious was that Jian Wushuang had told her that Yang Xiao might know something about her mother. Therefore, she was worried that Yang Xiao might be killed.","However, she trusted Jian Wushuang’s abilities even more.","Since the plan was already in place, it was surely foolproof. She had witnessed this firsthand when Jian Wushuang and Xiang Yang, in just half a year, had led over a hundred thousand rebels out of Jiang Nation. This demonstrated his incredible planning ability.","If Jian Wushuang knew how much confidence Jiang Shang had in him, he might feel embarrassed.","At this moment, Jian Wushuang stood at the doorway, also watching the battle.","His expression was filled with excitement, even his body trembled.","“Spatial Crystals!!!!”","The shop assistant’s body material was space crystal, which was why Jian Wushuang hadn’t noticed him earlier despite being so close—it was due to the unique properties of space crystals.","Now that he saw it with his own eyes, he finally recognized it.","“Such a large space crystal! If I could obtain it, it would be enough to advance to the Nascent Soul stage!” Jian Wushuang’s heart trembled with excitement.","He even forgot to speculate about the experts of the Centipede Tribe.","Because, to him, that was unimportant.","The inn had been prepared for Yang Xiao, and these three puppets had also come to kill Yang Xiao.","The Centipede Tribe’s experts intervened, clearly intending to protect Yang Xiao.","There was probably some scheme by Wei Jiuxian involved, but Jian Wushuang wasn’t particularly interested in that.","Right now, he only wanted to obtain the space crystal.","The three puppets had no consciousness; they were being controlled by someone.","To burn thought power and kill them, he had to target the thought power left on the puppets by their controller.","But killing them from such a distance was too difficult.","Even though Jian Wushuang’s thought power was strong, he couldn’t accomplish that.","Unless he found the mastermind hidden within the group who was controlling the puppets.","“I can’t detect them!”","At first, he thought it was Dong Biao, but upon closer inspection, he didn’t see anything suspicious about Dong Biao. Even his thought power was a mess, which didn’t match the characteristics of someone remotely controlling puppets.","If it wasn’t Dong Biao as he had initially suspected, then who could it be?","Could it be that the other person wasn’t hiding within the group but, like him, had been secretly following the convoy all along?","Jian Wushuang frowned slightly. Unless the other person was in the Divine Appearance Realm, or their thought power was somehow being shielded.","He ruled out the possibility of the Divine Appearance Realm first. Based on his deductions, if the other person could refine a puppet’s body using space crystals, they likely had more space crystals and had crafted a treasure to shield their aura.","That was probably the case. As long as their strength wasn’t a threat to Jian Wushuang, he wasn’t worried.","After all, the puppets couldn’t escape.","With the situation right before his eyes, the priority now was to find the mastermind controlling the puppets.","“Who is it?” Jian Wushuang’s eyes flashed with killing intent.","He swept his thought power over everyone.","If he truly couldn’t find them, he wouldn’t hesitate to kill them all.","Especially those Golden Crow Guards—after all, they were against him anyway.","If they wanted to protect Yang Xiao, sooner or later, there would be a conflict with them.","He might as well strike first.","Jian Wushuang gripped his sword sheath, his gaze rising to the sky. His divine sense condensed into a phantom figure in midair, looking down at the inn below.","Wait.","Wait a little longer.","But Jian Wushuang’s patience had its limits.","At this moment, he had to take some action.","“Yang Xiao, you wouldn’t want to surrender without a fight, would you?”","In the guest room, Yang Xiao was startled, knowing that it was a transmitted message. Immediately, a thought rose in his mind, and he responded through the transmission, “Are you not planning to make a move?”","“It seems Wei Jiuxian has already informed you, so I won’t waste words. Right now, I suspect there’s another hidden expert controlling the puppets. Their strength shouldn’t be weak. To control three puppets so skillfully, they’re likely at least a pseudo-Nascent Soul stage cultivator. I need to keep an eye on this person. You go down and help, and later, someone will assist you. All you need to do is cooperate with the Centipede Tribe’s experts and take down that puppet covered in black. Once that’s done, I can lock onto the mastermind’s position!”","Jian Wushuang told a small, well-intentioned lie, forcing Yang Xiao to take action.","After all, there were still two strong experts watching from the shadows. The logic of striking first didn’t need Jian Wushuang’s reminder.","“Alright!”","Yang Xiao agreed readily. He kicked open the door and shouted, “Enemy attack! Everyone, protect the inspector and retreat! I’ll hold them off here!”","With that shout, Chen Yuan could no longer pretend to be dead in his room.","At the same time, Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang received Jian Wushuang’s message, instructing them to assist.","“Master Chen, stay here and don’t go out. I’m going to help Yang Xiao!” Xiang Yang cupped his hands, then immediately led Jiang Shang downstairs.","The scene instantly became lively.","Seeing these two figures, Yang Xiao wasn’t surprised, but he was a bit troubled. Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang’s strength was too weak.","Forget about helping; they might even become a burden.","Xiang Yang noticed Yang Xiao’s odd look and nodded, saying, “You go ahead and fight; don’t worry about us!”","Their strength might not be impressive, but they still had their methods.","Jiang Shang might be ordinary, but Xiang Yang, who was once a Universe Master, still had some tricks up his sleeve. Although his combat power wasn’t great, since the opponent was just a puppet, he could still interfere and restrain them.","Otherwise, he’d be nothing more than dead weight, and all those years of cultivation would have been wasted.","“Alright!” Yang Xiao no longer hesitated and shouted to the nearby Centipede Tribe experts, “What are you waiting for? Attack!”"]},{"number":6314,"title":"Chapter 6314: Guardian Tong Shan","paragraphs":["Chapter 6314: Guardian Tong Shan","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Well, well, didn’t your Master Chen say earlier that you shouldn’t force things?” The seductive woman teased before commanding the Tianzu Centipede to attack the shop assistant again.","This time, everyone focused on a single puppet, completely ignoring the shopkeeper and the chubby chef.","The puppet’s defense was astonishing, but its strength was still manageable, allowing it to hold out for a while.","“Exterminate Evil Sword!”","Yang Xiao roared, and in an instant, a long sword with a wine gourd attached to it unsheathed.","This sword, named Exterminate Evil, embodied the essence of Yang Xiao’s swordsmanship.","With a single strike, the ancient iron sword surrounded by black crystals pushed the shop assistant back.","Although it couldn’t harm the puppet, it was enough to repel it.","The others unleashed their fiercest moves as well, especially the Tianzu Centipede, which took the opportunity to wrap itself around the shop assistant and spew venom.","The intense corrosion, however, failed to damage the puppet in the slightest and only managed to bind it.","Jian Wushuang had been observing the battle, but he hadn’t been idle.","While searching for suspicious individuals, he kept a close watch on the two experts lurking in the shadows.","Neither the demonic cultivator, the Death Infant, nor the Seven Coin Zhanxian Guard had made a move.","If Jian Wushuang acted now and the person controlling the puppet joined forces with them, he might meet his end here today.","At this moment, all those behind the scenes were engaged in a battle of patience.","It was as if the fighters below were merely their pawns, and even if they were injured or fell, they remained indifferent.","“Hmph, you hide well, but let’s force you out!” Jian Wushuang chuckled softly.","A burst of intangible thought power shot from the ceiling above.","The Seven Coin Zhanxian Guard, who had been hiding, felt a strong wave of thought power and was instantly exposed.","The thought power wasn’t meant to attack but was a friendly reminder.","A reminder that Jian Wushuang knew exactly where they were hiding!","He intended to force them to reveal themselves.","Crash!","Fragments of wood fell from the ceiling, and a figure dropped down.","Though they wore plain clothes and even a bamboo hat, Yang Xiao, as a Six Coin Zhanxian Guard, recognized them at a glance.","“Guardian Tongshan, since you’re here, why not lend a hand?”","Yang Xiao had long known that a powerful figure was lurking in the shadows, but he hadn’t expected it to be Guardian Tongshan of the Zhanxian Guards.","Guardian Tongshan, aligned with Guardian Nanshan, had likely been hiding in the dark to eliminate him. Now that he had revealed himself, Yang Xiao was uncertain of his intentions. However, he had no choice but to expose Tongshan’s identity, ensuring that Tongshan wouldn’t pose a threat to him.","Yang Xiao didn’t believe that Tongshan would dare to attack him in front of so many people.","The Zhanxian Guards were forbidden from killing each other, a crime punishable by death, with no exceptions.","The Guardian, Tong Shan, who had just appeared, was grinding his teeth in frustration. He yanked off his bamboo hat, glancing around before finally fixing his gaze on Yang Xiao. With resentment, he said, “I am only responsible for protecting the Imperial Inspector. These small fry aren’t worth my effort!”","He wasn’t foolish. At this moment, he couldn’t make a move against Yang Xiao, but he also wouldn’t lend him a hand.","These puppets were clearly here to kill Yang Xiao, so he absolutely wouldn’t help.","Even if it meant exposing his identity, he stood at a distance with an air of indifference, coldly watching the events unfold.","“Tong Shan, have you forgotten who gave you a meal back then?” Yang Xiao’s face twisted with rage.","Initially, he hadn’t wanted to bother with him, but the more he thought about it, the angrier he became.","Tong Shan had originally been a mere wanderer in the martial world, quite ordinary and not even an innate talent. When he first arrived in the capital, he clashed with a young noble, and the noble’s guards had severely injured him. If it hadn’t been for Wei Jiu-Xian’s intervention, Tong Shan would have frozen to death on the streets.","But what happened later?","After joining the Jinwu Guard, Tong Shan grew closer to Nanshan, eventually becoming estranged from Wei Jiu-Xian.","Now, he was repaying kindness with betrayal!","With Yang Xiao’s straightforward temperament, how could he not be enraged?","“Hmph! You grew up within the Zhanxian Guard, so how would you understand my struggles!” Tong Shan’s expression was ugly. Although he retorted, he guiltily turned his head away, avoiding Yang Xiao, who was fiercely battling the puppets.","He appeared disdainful, but his eyes couldn’t hide the truth.","There was a trace of reminiscence in his eyes—memories of when he first joined the Zhanxian Guard.","He hadn’t forgotten the past. He knew who his benefactor was and who had helped him reach this point.","However, everything he did now was to avoid returning to his former miserable state.","He believed he wasn’t wrong!","“I’m not wrong. It’s you all who have been too fortunate!” Tong Shan inwardly defended himself, his thoughts gradually calming.","He began analyzing the current situation.","As one of the four Guardians of the Zhanxian Guard, he had both the capability and strength.","From Yang Xiao’s active participation, he could infer that there were others backing him in Wei Jiu-Xian’s scheme.","“The two guests from the Princess’s mansion are also suspicious!” Tong Shan’s eyes flickered.","Initially, he thought these two were Wei Jiu-Xian’s plants within the Princess’s residence, but he hadn’t expected them to be so formidable.","Although they appeared to be ordinary Golden Core cultivators, they managed to survive against the puppets and even entangled them, clearly possessing extraordinary skills beyond that of regular Golden Core cultivators.","“Interesting. Let’s see what other tricks you have up your sleeve!”","Tong Shan wasn’t worried at all. He knew that a strong expert from the Chiyang Sect was still lurking in the shadows.","Though he looked down on demonic cultivators, he couldn’t deny their strength, especially a Nascent Infant expert.","Their power was on par with his. If they acted now, they could definitely turn the tide and perhaps even kill Yang Xiao on the spot, making the inspection of Mangshan County a failure.","However, he didn’t know that the Nascent Infant expert in the shadows was also under the watchful eye of Jian Wushuang.","“You’re really good at being patient!”","Jian Wushuang’s thought power drifted through the night like a ghost, always focused on that Nascent Infant cultivator.","Since he couldn’t find the person secretly controlling the puppets, he could only keep an eye on this demonic sect elder.","This person’s strength was formidable; even if Jian Wushuang launched a sneak attack, he couldn’t guarantee a one-hit kill.","He had initially brought Tong Shan out to force him to help, but now that Tong Shan refused to act, Jian Wushuang had no choice.","As for the demonic sect’s Supreme Elder, without any constraints, if Jian Wushuang exposed him, he would likely retaliate by attacking Yang Xiao directly.","So, the more patient this person was, the more advantageous it was for Jian Wushuang. He only needed to keep an eye on him with his thought power while focusing most of his energy on finding the mastermind controlling the puppets.","“Where are they?”","Jian Wushuang opened his eyes, no longer sweeping the area with his thought power.","He couldn’t detect the person’s aura with thought power alone; there must be a space crystal concealing them.","Now, he could only rely on his deductions to find them.","When they first spotted the inn, Chen Yuan’s team was still thirty miles away. At that time, the puppets were stiff and their eyes were lifeless.","But as the team drew closer, the puppets became more animated.","Especially after Jian Wushuang entered the inn, the innkeeper moved like a normal person.","“It seems I exposed myself too early!” Jian Wushuang felt a bit frustrated.","He had been too careless. He shouldn’t have revealed himself so soon. Instead, he should have found a place to hide or even concealed himself within the team."]},{"number":6315,"title":"Chapter 6315: Luring the Tiger Out of the Mountain","paragraphs":["Chapter 6315: Luring the Tiger Out of the Mountain","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","In the end, they startled the snake in the grass, and the other party never showed up.","“Ten Golden Crow Guards, each with a powerful aura, all of them are cultivators at the Golden Core stage. This can’t be wrong!” He began to speculate one by one.","There weren’t too many people present.","Simply put, there were only four types of people.","One group consisted of their own people: Xiang Yang, Jiang Shang, and then Chen Yuan.","Yang Xiao and the powerful warriors from the Thousand Foot Tribe were currently in the same camp. As for their reason, he didn’t know, but it seemed to be to protect Yang Xiao’s life for the time being.","The second group had more people, including three puppets and the person controlling them from behind the scenes, followed by Guardian Tongshan, the Supreme Elder of the Demon Sect, and then those Golden Crow Guards inside the house—all here to kill Yang Xiao.","The third group, Jian Wushuang’s side, was caught in the middle, and even Chen Yuan was in the same situation.","The fourth group consisted of the Imperial Guards!","One hundred elite martial soldiers at the peak of the Houtian realm, plus one martial artist at the peak of the Houtian realm.","Was this team redundant?","Every time the court dispatched an inspector, they would indeed send the Imperial Guards. Normally, it wouldn’t be excessive.","But this time, Jian Wushuang found it a bit odd.","Because Dong Biao himself was problematic.","However, he was just a martial artist at the peak of the Xiantian realm. Although he was responsible for leading the team, he couldn’t do much more.","Yang Xiao alone could overturn the entire Imperial Guard.","What made Jian Wushuang most suspicious was that Dong Biao clearly knew the inside story, yet at such a critical moment, he dared to drink with those powerful warriors from the Thousand Foot Tribe.","And he drank until he was unconscious!","“A smokescreen!”","Jian Wushuang saw the crux of the problem, his eyes swirling with colors, and the corner of his mouth revealed a trace of contempt as he thought to himself, “Dong Biao, a mere warrior, couldn’t be this clever. This drunken act must be guided by someone behind the scenes!”","Moreover, the fact that Dong Biao knew the tavern had issues and deliberately got drunk to avoid being forced to take action during the fight was telling. Although Dong Biao wasn’t strong, if the Imperial Guards intervened, it would represent the court.","That would change things. Once Dong Biao made a move, the Golden Crow Guards would also be forced to act.","“It seems I need to meet this Lieutenant Dong!”","Jian Wushuang stood up, crossed the windowsill, and his figure disappeared in an instant.","When he reappeared, he was already at the camp where the Imperial Guards were stationed.","At this moment, the camp was pitch-black, with no one on duty, and the soldiers lay sprawled on the ground.","Some had been drugged, but most had been affected by a spell that made them sleep even more soundly.","“Rosemary!”","Jian Wushuang walked closer and immediately noticed the subtle signs.","“No wonder my Thought Power couldn’t detect any issues. Such a simple method, I truly hadn’t paid much attention to it!” He touched his nose and called out toward Dong Biao’s tent, “Lieutenant Dong, will you come out and meet me yourself, or will you have the person behind you come out to meet me?”","Dong Biao himself had only minor issues, but from the details, it was clear that everything was connected to him.","Although Dong Biao’s aura seemed fine, he always managed to make quick decisions, suggesting that the person controlling the puppets must be right by his side.","Gazing at the tent, Jian Wushuang casually snapped his fingers, and the torches stuck in the ground around him instantly lit up.","“Hiding won’t do you any good!” Seeing that no one came out, Jian Wushuang made a hand seal with one hand, and a Wind Control Spell immediately swept through, tearing the tent open in an instant.","He didn’t hold back and rushed forward, intending to resolve the situation quickly.","“Hmm?”","As he got closer, he realized that the three people inside the tent no longer had heartbeats.","The aura that his Thought Power had detected came from a token on the chest of each person.","“An ancient token!”","Jian Wushuang raised an eyebrow. He recognized the token, and he even had one on him, which he had obtained from a spirit creature in the Jiang Kingdom’s royal palace long ago.","He had originally intended to study it but found that the power on the token was peculiar and impossible to activate, so he had given up on it.","Unexpectedly, he encountered it here.","Holding three tokens, the top bore a white eye.","The one he had obtained earlier had a black eye.","Clearly, there was a difference in status between the two.","While he was still in shock, the fight inside the tavern suddenly changed.","“Not good!” Jian Wushuang’s heart sank, realizing he had fallen into a diversion trap.","He hurriedly tried to rush back to the tavern, but as soon as he took a step forward, he found himself back at his original spot.","A barrier rose around him.","It was a formation.","But the formation contained a divine power that was quite common in the mundane world.","“Shrinking the Ground into an Inch!”","For Jian Wushuang, this was indeed a common technique, but in this small world, it was rare.","Only a high-level cultivator at the Divine Aspect stage could possess such divine power. Even setting up a formation that shrinks the ground would require someone at the Divine Aspect stage.","Jian Wushuang’s brow twitched instantly.","This time, his plan had been manipulated, and there were significant flaws in his calculations regarding his opponent.","A puppet crafted from space crystals could not possibly be an ordinary cultivator.","Even a Nascent Soul cultivator couldn’t do it; it was likely someone at the Divine Aspect stage.","However, one thing puzzled him. Why would someone at the Divine Aspect stage need to set up a formation? Why not just kill directly?","“No, at my peak strength, I was still a Ninth Star Universe God, wasn’t I? Now, I’m also calculating every move in this broken place just to recover my strength!”","At this thought, he understood.","“If we’re all in the same boat, then let’s see who has the stronger skills!”","He didn’t take this formation seriously, only considering that the person who set it up was probably at the Divine Aspect stage. But now that he understood, he no longer worried.","Buzz!","A surge of thought power erupted from him, like a dragon in the night, tearing towards the hidden demon god in the darkness.","Jian Wushuang stood motionless, his eyes shining brightly. The battle of thought power was swift, and in an instant, he had torn open a gap in the formation.","“Hold on!”","His figure shot out in an instant, dashing towards the tavern at the fastest speed.","It was a diversion.","What would come next would undoubtedly be a lethal attack.","If he were even a moment late, he might not see Yang Xiao in person. But that wasn’t the most important thing; if Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang died, there would be no one left to reason with.","These two were his dearest loved ones; they absolutely couldn’t die.","Xiang Yang had connections to Xing Luo, and Jiang Shang was Jiang Shang’s daughter.","They couldn’t die, no matter what.","Although he didn’t know how the other party had managed to produce this daughter, or if this Jiang Shang was the same Jiang Shang he knew, taking her out would surely surprise Hu Qing. If Hu Qing was delighted, his mood might naturally round out, and he might even break through directly.","So, they absolutely couldn’t die!","Boom!","In his haste to reach the inn as quickly as possible, he didn’t even bother with the door and crashed straight through.","Crash!","The shattered wooden boards flew out instantly.","As the dust settled, Jian Wushuang appeared inside the inn.","“Thank goodness, they’re all alive!”","When he rushed in, he hadn’t dared to use his thought power to check their auras.","Seeing his arrival, Chen Yuan on the upper floor let out a sigh of relief."]},{"number":6316,"title":"Chapter 6316: Immortal Jiu Chen","paragraphs":["Chapter 6316: Immortal Jiu Chen","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Just moments ago, Yang Xiao and his group were about to capture the innkeeper, but then a mysterious expert appeared and severely injured everyone with a single strike.","If it weren’t for that Skyfoot Centipede, Yang Xiao and the others would have been slain by the mysterious expert by now.","“Brother Wushuang, you’re finally here!” Xiang Yang’s breath was unstable, clearly having just survived a life-threatening situation. He was still filled with lingering fear as he hurriedly pulled Jian Wushuang behind him, feeling a bit safer only after standing in his shadow.","Jian Wushuang, however, didn’t seem too afraid of death. His eyes remained cold, his head held high with pride, and his voice sharp as he said, “Senior Wushuang, it was that black-clad expert who struck just now. With a single palm, he severely injured everyone. He must be a powerful cultivator in the Nascent Soul stage!”","Jian Wushuang glanced at the calm and composed Jian Shang, feeling satisfied. This reminded him of the Jian Shang from back in Qishen Temple, who remained cool-headed even when being hunted down, displaying both courage and wisdom in the face of his pursuers.","“Senior Wushuang?” Jian Shang felt uneasy under the constant gaze, his small face blushing slightly as he lowered his eyes and softened his voice.","“Ahem!” Jian Wushuang quickly averted his gaze, coughing lightly to cover his embarrassment before turning to look at the mysterious black-clad elder.","The elder had a head full of silver hair and wore black robes, exuding a vigorous aura.","This wasn’t the demonic expert from the Dark Sect.","It was a formidable figure he had never sensed or discovered before.","Even now, standing face to face, Jian Wushuang couldn’t detect the elder’s presence.","“Your formation is much more troublesome than any puppet!” Jian Wushuang took a step forward, his figure suddenly rising as he met the elder’s gaze head-on.","The black-clad elder, standing on the shattered beam, looked astonished. Forcing himself to remain calm, he asked, “How did you break the grand array I set up?”","“Simple!” Jian Wushuang thought to himself, and a surge of illusory power rose within him—this was the power of thought manifested into consciousness.","It could even create a consciousness avatar.","If he were to burn this power, he could kill even a Nascent Soul stage cultivator.","“So strong!” The black-clad elder trembled inwardly.","Then, as if realizing something, he exclaimed in shock, “Are you a cultivator from the Upper Realm?”","He could see that Jian Wushuang’s aura was only at the Golden Core stage since Jian Wushuang hadn’t concealed his presence. But that powerful thought power was already comparable to the Divine Appearance stage.","That’s why he instinctively mentioned the Upper Realm.","“Upper Realm?” Jian Wushuang’s heart stirred. Although he knew of the Upper Realm, he didn’t understand much about it. In fact, he hadn’t even fully grasped the nature of this small world, with its figures like the True Immortal of the Tang Dynasty or the creator of the Princess Tomb.","At that moment, someone happened to clarify things for him, so he pretended to be calm and said, “Everyone’s the same, what’s there to be surprised about?”","“Oh, do you think I’m also a strong practitioner from the Upper Realm?” The black-clad elder’s previously tense expression relaxed slightly.","Both were schemers, their minds working faster than ordinary people. With just one sentence, he deduced that Jian Wushuang wasn’t from the Upper Realm.","Since the black-clad elder himself wasn’t a strong practitioner from the Upper Realm, he had assumed Jian Wushuang was one based on the other’s thought power. But now that Jian Wushuang claimed to be from the Upper Realm as well, it made his words seem less credible.","The black-clad elder wasn’t from the Upper Realm but was instead a powerful practitioner native to this world.","The method of distinguishing between the Upper and Lower Realms was through power.","The power systems of the Upper Realm and the Lower Realm were completely different. Although the black-clad elder had never been to the Upper Realm, he had glimpsed the divine techniques and secret methods of the Upper Realm through his inheritance, which differed greatly from those of the Lower Realm.","“I haven’t asked for your name yet, sir?”","“Jian Wushuang!”","The moment Jian Wushuang announced his name, his brow furrowed slightly, realizing he had just misspoken. Now, the black-clad elder had begun to shift the topic.","It was clear that the elder would no longer believe anything he said.","“I miscalculated. If the other party had come from the Upper Realm, he would have recognized the space crystal and wouldn’t have used such a treasure to refine a puppet. Instead, he would have restored his own strength. Obviously, he doesn’t recognize the space crystal, which is why he used it to make a puppet!” Jian Wushuang sighed inwardly.","In just one encounter, he had already made two missteps.","The opponent certainly possessed a mind as sharp as a seven-orifice exquisite heart.","Although this was a mundane world, one couldn’t underestimate the wisdom of ordinary people.","When they found their path of cultivation blocked, some would choose to walk the path of the Dao, the heart, or the kidneys.","It was evident that this opponent had chosen the heart.","His mental state was very strong. When faced with challenges, he remained calm and could unravel lies with just a few words, subtly shifting the topic and diverting attention.","In this way, Jian Wushuang found himself completely at a disadvantage.","After exchanging names, Jian Wushuang became cautious with his words and instead began to deduce the elder’s identity through his name.","Jiu Chen Immortal!","That was the elder’s Dao name.","The ability to refine puppets meant he had surely obtained secret divine techniques from the Upper Realm. It wasn’t surprising that he knew about the Upper Realm’s powerful practitioners.","In terms of cultivation, he might have once been a practitioner at the Divine Form level but had somehow fallen to the Nascent Soul stage. He was likely in a cooperative relationship with the Tang Emperor now.","After all, such a powerful figure in the mundane world wouldn’t be subservient to imperial power.","Cooperation!","Following this train of thought, Jian Wushuang spoke up.","“Daoist Jiu Chen, since we’ve laid everything out, why don’t we be more straightforward? This time, give me some face and spare Yang Xiao’s life. Whatever you need, just name it!”","Jian Wushuang lowered his stance. He couldn’t gauge the elder’s strength, but the elder was at least a mid-Nascent Soul stage practitioner. If it came to a fight, Jian Wushuang had no problem with it, but there were so many people present.","If Yang Xiao died, it would be troublesome.","He regretted not asking Yang Xiao about the matters of the Jiang Kingdom earlier, which had led to this situation.","Jiu Chen Immortal gently stroked his beard and smiled faintly. “In the mundane world, there’s a saying that I’ve always appreciated. Let me share it with you, Daoist.”","“Please,” Jian Wushuang gestured.","“The one who eats the lord’s salary must serve the lord and relieve the lord’s worries.”","After Jiu Chen Immortal finished speaking, his demeanor remained calm and indifferent.","However, Jian Wushuang’s expression darkened.","The elder gave no face at all. The message was simple: since he had received benefits, he must fulfill his obligations. Yang Xiao’s life couldn’t be saved.","Since that was the case, there was nothing more to discuss with the elder.","“Xiang Yang, take Jiang Shang upstairs and stay with Chen Yuan. When the time is right, take Chen Yuan and leave!”","He silently transmitted his voice, and his thought power surged to its peak.","“Today, no one shall escape from my hands!” Jiu Chen Immortal raised his hand, summoning a golden light.","Buzz!","The dazzling golden light was so bright that no one could keep their eyes open.","Even Jian Wushuang felt his eyes stinging, but fortunately, his thought power enveloped the surroundings, so he wasn’t completely blinded.","However, the others weren’t as fortunate. They all clutched their eyes in pain, curling up into balls.","Only four people remained standing.","Besides Jian Wushuang and Jiu Chen, there were the Guardian Tong Shan and Xiang Yang."]},{"number":6317,"title":"Chapter 6317: Nine Prison Pagoda","paragraphs":["Chapter 6317: Nine Prison Pagoda","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Regarding the powerful infant from the Demon Sect, it directly revealed its true form. Countless black gases erupted from its body, seemingly on the verge of tearing its entire form apart.","“This person can actually remain unaffected!” The Immortal Jiuchen was astonished deep down, and his gaze also turned toward Xiang Yang.","Because only this person was beyond his expectations.","As for Jian Wushuang, there was no need to say more—if he couldn’t withstand even this little bit of light, he wouldn’t be worth risking everything for. The Guardian Tong Shan, on the other hand, was protected by a treasure bestowed by Zhanxian Tower. Since he followed the righteous path, the treasure matched well with his abilities, so he wouldn’t be intimidated.","But Xiang Yang, just an ordinary Golden Core stage cultivator—how was he managing this?","Bang!!!","Jiuchen immediately made a move, attempting to stop Xiang Yang, who was dragging Jiang Shang away.","A beam of golden light pierced through the wooden pavilion, shooting straight toward Xiang Yang.","Jian Wushuang had already spread his Thought power across the area, so how could he stand by and watch the opponent take action? In a flash, he blocked the golden light, and with a single grip of his hand, a force of nothingness emerged. The nothingness burned and transformed into power, directly dispersing the golden light.","The entire inn was instantly shattered, and the terrifying destructive force caused several Golden Core cultivators who were already severely injured to fall unconscious.","“Run!”","This time, Jian Wushuang didn’t use his voice transmission technique; he shouted directly.","He finally understood the situation—his opponent probably intended to kill everyone to silence them.","There was no consideration for anyone nearby.","Yang Xiao would die, the Zhanxian Guards would also die, and Chen Yuan wouldn’t survive either.","Sensing the intense explosions, Tong Shan, who was protecting Chen Yuan, hesitated for a moment. Without concern for anyone else, he immediately fled with Chen Yuan.","His orders were to kill Yang Xiao and quickly bring Chen Yuan back to Tai’an City. As for the matters in Mangshan County, he was not to intervene or investigate further.","Acting on orders was the principle of the Zhanxian Guards, leaving no room for personal emotions. Even with the sudden appearances of the Immortal Jiuchen and Jian Wushuang, he didn’t bother to ask any questions—his only focus was on leaving.","Because in his view, Yang Xiao’s death was inevitable today.","The inn was instantly destroyed.","Even the Imperial Guards stationed in the distance were obliterated in an instant.","Yet, the golden light and the burning force of nothingness continued to clash.","Jian Wushuang gritted his teeth, and his entire Thought power surged once again. Gathering in the palm of his right hand, he once more condensed the consciousness of nothingness.","“Burn!”","Buzz!","The power of void that had ignited grew ten times stronger, forcing back the golden light that had been blasting out.","“Not bad, but still far from enough!”","Faced with the overwhelming golden light that could crush one’s spirit, the Immortal Jiu Chen conjured a nine-story pagoda in his hand.","“Absorb!”","The golden light, which had been reflected back by Jian Wushuang, was completely drawn into the nine-story pagoda.","“Take a good look, this is the Supreme Treasure, the Nine Prison Pagoda. Dying by the hand of a Supreme Treasure is an honor!” The Immortal Jiu Chen’s white hair fluttered as the nine-story pagoda in his hand spun upwards, preparing to suppress Jian Wushuang.","The terrifying gravitational force made it impossible for Jian Wushuang to stand firm. The wooden debris around him was instantly sucked into the pagoda, along with the severely injured cultivators who had no time to escape, all of them being drawn into the Nine Prison Pagoda.","“A Supreme Treasure?”","Jian Wushuang gritted his teeth and let out a cold laugh, though blood trickled from the corner of his mouth.","It was clear that he was struggling to resist and had already been injured.","“I underestimated him!” He felt a slight tremor in his heart, yet he also realized the determination of the Tang Emperor.","He had indeed prepared to kill them all.","What puzzled Jian Wushuang the most was why a cultivator with such divine abilities would willingly work for the Tang Emperor.","There were likely many reasons behind this that he didn’t know.","But now was not the time to think about it.","With his current strength alone, he was no match for the Immortal Jiu Chen. He had no choice but to burn his Thought power again.","Moreover, he had to burn all of his Thought power if he hoped to kill his opponent.","However, the Immortal Jiu Chen was no fool. He wouldn’t just stand there and let himself be killed. Jian Wushuang had to find the right opportunity.","Crack!","The floor shattered, and his figure slowly rose.","“I’ll take the risk!”","Jian Wushuang made up his mind, and his figure began to move closer to the Nine Prison Pagoda.","To kill his opponent with a single strike using his Thought power, he had to get closer.","Fortunately, his opponent also wanted to suppress him with the Nine Prison Pagoda, giving Jian Wushuang the opportunity to approach and deliver a fatal blow.","But there was also a downside. If Jian Wushuang’s Thought power burned out, with his current strength, without the support of Thought power, he would likely be instantly sucked into the Nine Prison Pagoda.","At that point, even if his opponent died, the instant power of the Nine Prison Pagoda would be enough to shatter Jian Wushuang’s body.","He had entered this world with nothing more than a mortal body.","Even after becoming a cultivator in the Golden Core stage, his body hadn’t undergone any significant transformation. Without the protection of power, even a mortal body could be shattered by ordinary weapons, let alone the crushing force of the Nine Prison Pagoda.","But at this moment, he had no better choice.","Escape?","If he fled now, it could be many years before he had another opportunity like this.","Besides, escaping was not his style.","Even if his body was destroyed, as long as his soul remained, that would be enough.","The soul couldn’t be altered. His Thought power was so strong, even because of his soul.","Even if this world had an underworld, it wouldn’t be able to control his soul. Even if his soul couldn’t return to his original body, he could still find another one in this world.","“Let’s do this!”","After calculating everything, Jian Wushuang spat blood and clutched his chest, feigning an appearance of being unable to hold on any longer.","A sinister grin spread across the Immortal Jiu Chen’s face, “Haha, a powerful figure from the upper realm, you are about to fall. Everything you have will belong to me, including your soul. The fear and inheritance hidden within you will all be mine!”","“Nine Prison Demon Suppression!!!”","Buzz!","Jian Wushuang and the Nine Prison Pagoda rushed toward each other.","But just as he was about to be suppressed, everything around him seemed to freeze. Wooden debris and shattered wine jars floated in the air, and amidst the chaos, a terrifying eye flickered.","“Candle Dragon’s Eye!”","Jian Wushuang roared as a red light burst from the center of his forehead. The massive eye instantly transformed into a Starry Sky.","Although he didn’t have a Supreme Treasure on him, the Candle Dragon’s Eye, part of the Beast God’s arsenal, was the first treasure he had obtained. He was well acquainted with it, and even without the treasure itself, he could still use its secret techniques.","Relying on his burning Thought power, he awakened the power to control the Candle Dragon’s Eye. The beam of light that shot out was enough to obliterate an ordinary God Manifestation realm cultivator.","The Immortal Jiu Chen didn’t even have time to react before the light in his eyes dimmed.","The three puppets below also fell silent.","The Immortal Jiu Chen’s body, without a single wound, fell straight from the sky.","At that moment, everything around him resumed its movement.","The suppressive force of the Nine Prison Pagoda surged forth.","In just a moment, its power swallowed Jian Wushuang, along with the Immortal Jiu Chen’s corpse and the three puppets, all into the Nine Prison Pagoda.","As the power dissipated, the Nine Prison Pagoda fell heavily to the ground, its golden light fading, and darkness once again descended."]},{"number":6318,"title":"Chapter 6318: Explanation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6318: Explanation","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The surrounding area had already been flattened.","After a long while, Chen Yuan and the others, who had escaped the danger zone, cautiously returned, only to see a nine-story small tower standing on the ground, about the height of a person.","“Where is Senior Wushuang?” Jiang Shang asked in confusion.","Xiang Yang approached the nine-story pagoda, circling around it with a strange tone, “The aura from this pagoda is stronger than that of a treasure. It should be a supreme treasure. Given Brother Wushuang’s current strength, I’m afraid things don’t look good for him!”","“What are you talking about? Aren’t you all friends of Senior Wushuang? Why aren’t you rescuing him right away?” Chen Yuan stood anxiously on the side.","“Rescue?” Xiang Yang sighed, “What do you expect me to use for a rescue?”","His strength wasn’t even on par with Jian Wushuang’s. Although his thought power was strong, without the divine arts from burning secret methods, he could at best rival some late-stage Golden Core cultivators.","And what lay before them was a supreme treasure.","A treasure that even an immortal like Yinxian could use, and no one in this world could fully activate it.","The divine arts that the Nine Dust Immortal used likely only involved one of the levels within the nine-story pagoda.","Moreover, its full power hadn’t been unleashed. If all the power of the first level were controlled, it would be enough to destroy this world.","“But what do we do now!” Chen Yuan was worried and helpless.","At this moment, the Left Guardian Tong Shan, who had been protecting him, said, “With such a significant incident, I suggest Young Master Chen return to Tai’an City with me first. I believe His Majesty will send someone to investigate the aftermath, as this situation has already exceeded our limits. Continuing further will likely yield no results!”","After this battle, Tong Shan was also somewhat terrified. If he hadn’t run fast enough just now, he would have been sucked into the Nine Prison Tower and instantly torn apart.","“Leaving already?”","A voice suddenly rang out from behind, and everyone couldn’t help but turn their heads to look.","It was the alluring Saintess of the Centipede Tribe.","This time, all the powerful members of the Centipede Tribe, including the giant centipede controlled by the Saintess, had perished, leaving only her alive.","But she was also injured at this moment.","Tong Shan looked down on her and sneered, “You’re just a minor Golden Core cultivator. Do you think you can stop me?”","Although he had suffered significant injuries, dealing with an injured Golden Core cultivator was still a piece of cake.","However, in his mind, if he could avoid fighting, he would. Who knew if there were any hidden tricks left, and if he were to fall here, it would be a huge loss.","“I may be just a minor Golden Core cultivator, but I still have this!” The Centipede Saintess shook a cloth bag in her hand, with the Centipede Totem marked on it.","As she spoke, she squeezed the bag and slowly approached, her tone filled with menace, “You may be able to kill a Golden Core cultivator now, but can you escape from a Nascent Soul Centipede?”","“Impossible! Absolutely impossible! Your life-bound centipede has already self-destructed! The Saintess of the Centipede Tribe can only cultivate one life-bound centipede. The rest can’t compare to the life-bound centipede. You must be bluffing!” Tong Shan’s face changed dramatically as he backed away.","“Even if it’s not as powerful as a life-bound centipede, as long as it has the strength of a late-stage Golden Core, we can still keep you here!”","At this moment, Yang Xiao also stepped forward.","Everyone else had died.","Among those remaining, apart from the Left Guardian Tong Shan, the targets were almost the same, and Chen Yuan wasn’t important.","So, as long as they killed the Left Guardian Tong Shan, they could still take Chen Yuan to Mangshan County City.","“Yang Xiao, I am the Left Guardian of the Zhanxian Guard. I am taking Chen Yuan back to Tai’an City. Do you dare defy orders?” Tong Shan no longer had the courage to rely on his strength and could only try to suppress Yang Xiao with his official position.","Yang Xiao, however, remained indifferent. He casually took out the Zhanxian Guard’s token from his waist and threw it directly to Tong Shan, saying nonchalantly, “Then I’ll quit right now. As a commoner, I’ll kill you, this court lackey!”","“You’re rebelling? Aren’t you afraid of causing trouble for Wei Jiuxian?” Tong Shan was now utterly panicked.","Apart from Chen Yuan, there were two other formidable figures on the scene. If these people joined forces to attack him, he would be doomed.","He definitely didn’t want to die here.","After finally climbing to the rank of a pseudo-Infant stage cultivator and becoming a superpower, it had been his lifelong dream. For this dream, he was willing to give up everything.","Loyalty, righteousness, and reason—all could be abandoned.","The only thing he cherished was his own life.","Sensing the situation had turned against him, he immediately began to soften his stance.","“Yang Xiao, no matter what, we are still fellow disciples. Do we really need to reach this point? Let’s take a step back—I can pretend nothing happened!”","“You sure know how to back down quickly, but it’s too late!” Xiang Yang drew his sword and made his move.","The saintess of the Qianzu tribe also untied her bag, and a blood-red centipede flew out.","This wasn’t a Tianzu Centipede; it was a mutated blood centipede far more powerful than the Tianzu Centipede, already possessing combat power at the Infant stage.","Even if Tong Shan were at his peak, he wouldn’t stand a chance against it. However, with his current injuries and being surrounded by so many people, escape was impossible.","Faced with Xiang Yang’s bizarre swordsmanship, Tong Shan made a single mistake, and his legs were instantly severed.","“Ah!”","Tong Shan fell to the ground, completely losing his combat abilities. He gritted his teeth to endure the pain of his severed legs, his eyes filled with hatred.","“Yang Xiao, you have a grudge against him, so I’ll leave him to you!”","Xiang Yang sheathed his sword and stepped aside, not delivering the final blow.","In his mind, this was an opportunity to strengthen his relationship with Yang Xiao.","Before Jian Wushuang went into battle, he had sent a message to Xiang Yang. If the Nine Prison Tower became ownerless, Xiang Yang should take the tower and leave, waiting for Jian Wushuang to emerge from it before making further plans. He was also instructed to take the black puppet among the three puppets.","Moreover, he was told to win over Yang Xiao.","This man knew some things about the Jiang Kingdom, so he must be brought along. He couldn’t be allowed to leave, nor could he be offended.","“Forget it!” Yang Xiao closed his eyes slightly and shook his head. “He’s already crippled; there’s no need for more killing.”","He still couldn’t bring himself to deliver the killing blow, feeling that Tong Shan was just doing his duty. Besides, he hadn’t actually attacked him yet, though he had the intention. Actions should be judged, not intentions.","Xiang Yang secretly shook his head. “Naive. Trying to reform a Dao-seeker? Unless you turn into an elixir for him to consume!”","He had lived through hundreds of eras and understood human nature far better than these mortals.","Those who pursued strength, also known as Dao-seekers, often resorted to any means necessary. Although they could distinguish right from wrong, they would abandon all principles to become stronger.","This was the ruthlessness of Dao-seekers.","Calling them demons wasn’t inaccurate, but they wouldn’t look twice at useless mortals and wouldn’t bully the weak without reason.","However, if the weak held treasures they needed, they would kill them without hesitation to seize those treasures.","Dao-seeking was simple—only for the sake of becoming stronger!","Although Xiang Yang secretly disdained Yang Xiao’s attitude, he didn’t argue with him, hoping to win him over.","Leaving behind the crippled Guardian Tong Shan, Xiang Yang carried the Nine Prison Tower on his back and led the group away from the place."]},{"number":6319,"title":"Chapter 6319: The Final Plan","paragraphs":["Chapter 6319: The Final Plan","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","One hour later.","In the distant sky, a blood cloud approached, thick with dense blood mist.","“Immortal Master, the Nine Prison Pagoda is gone!”","The blood cloud paused briefly before returning the way it came.","As for Tong Shan, the Guardian on the ground, he didn’t even glance back.","In Tai’an City, within the Palace of Mental Cultivation.","Emperor Li Miao sat cross-legged on a prayer mat. Opposite him was a faint, ethereal figure. If one looked closely, they could discern the figure’s outline and facial features.","If Jian Wushuang were present, he would have immediately recognized the figure as the very Nine Dust Immortal he had previously killed with his Thought power.","Yet now, it had transformed into a wisp of a soul, sustained by Thought power to maintain its consciousness.","“The Nine Prison Pagoda is gone!!!” the ethereal figure trembled and stammered, “You’re saying the Nine Prison Pagoda disappeared from its place?”","Emperor Tang nodded and reassured him, “Immortal Master, there’s no need to worry. I’ve already sent people to chase after it. Moreover, the Nine Prison Pagoda is so unique that those people surely won’t be able to activate it!”","“Hmph, what do you know!” the ethereal Nine Dust suppressed his anger and shouted, “Do you think they’re just ordinary cultivators? If they were ordinary cultivators, my physical body wouldn’t have been destroyed. The power I’ve accumulated for a thousand years scattered in an instant is a minor issue, but if they manage to control the Nine Prison Pagoda, they will undoubtedly discover the secret hidden within the Northern Region Glacier. Do you understand?”","Emperor Tang showed no anger at being reprimanded, and his expression didn’t change. He calmly replied, “Then we can only initiate the final plan ahead of schedule. Everything has been arranged, just waiting for Immortal Master to personally direct it!”","“There’s no other way!” Nine Dust closed his eyes slightly, though unwillingly.","Those so-called plans in his heart paled in comparison to the importance of the Nine Prison Pagoda.","As long as the Nine Prison Pagoda was in his possession, even if he ascended to the higher realms, he could still dominate across the world.","...","Tai’an City, South Tower!","At that moment, Wei Jiuxian was draped in a coarse black robe, standing on the tower and gazing at the darkened Tai’an City, his mind swirling with countless thoughts.","After a moment, a mist descended, forming into a black-clad figure who knelt on one knee and respectfully reported, “Commander, Yang Xiao and his people have completely disappeared, along with the mysterious cultivator who had been hiding in the shadows!”","“Hmm, continue searching!”","Wei Jiuxian didn’t even turn his head, his tone remained calm.","This development was expected, yet it also surprised him.","The original plan was for Chen Yuan to be brought back.","But then, an unexpected variable appeared.","The mysterious immortal by His Majesty’s side.","This simple situation had suddenly become complicated.","The mysterious cultivators of the Jiang Kingdom, the ancient mysterious cultivators, all were unpredictable factors.","“There aren’t many people who could force him to silence, but he ended up being silenced himself. How amusing. But it works out well; it saves me the trouble of slowly leading you to madness!” Wei Jiuxian clasped his hands behind his back and turned to shout towards the stairs, “Someone, deliver a message to the Desire King for me!”","...","Nine Prison Pagoda.","Though it was only human-sized at the moment, the internal world, just the first level alone, far surpassed this mundane world.","Such was the power of a supreme treasure.","In the past, an item like this would have been mere trash to Jian Wushuang.","A simple supreme treasure would drive an ordinary Yan Immortal mad, but a slightly wealthier Great Yan Immortal wouldn’t care for it.","Yet, this treasure shouldn’t have appeared in such a mundane world.","To Jian Wushuang, Yan Immortals and Great Yan Immortals were merely transcendents who had escaped the lower-level universes.","In the vastness of space, even in the original universe, Great Yan Immortals were not considered powerful.","But comparing that level of the universe to the present was like comparing the distance between here and the Starry Sky.","It was indeed odd that such a supreme treasure, which could only be nurtured in the original universe, was hidden in a small mundane world.","It was akin to a cultivator at the Divine Aspect Realm facing a Great Yan Immortal.","In the vast first level, the surroundings were as bright as day, with abundant light, yet nothing could be seen.","This was the law of light.","What appeared to be a field of light was actually the greatest darkness.","There was no difference between pitch-blackness and blinding light.","“Hoo!”","In the white world, the first breath was exhaled, and a phantom figure floated in the air, aimless, as if lost.","“Is this inside the Nine Prison Pagoda?”","The consciousness suddenly opened its eyes, Thought power controlling the soul, causing the figure to hover in mid-air.","It was Jian Wushuang!","At this moment, his soul aura had undergone a vast transformation compared to when he was in the outside world. If any living beings from the outside saw him, they would be too shocked to speak.","Because a black mist swirled around him, constantly devouring and collapsing, and every bright point of light around him represented a star.","“My soul power has actually increased here?”","Jian Wushuang was equally astonished. He hadn’t expected that after entering the Nine Prison Pagoda, his soul power would recover significantly.","Before entering this world, he had only been an avatar, with strength equivalent to a quasi-Seven Star level.","But now, his soul power had already reached the level of a Dao Lord.","If he wanted to break open this supreme treasure, it wouldn’t be a problem at all.","Once he left the treasure, if he could maintain this level of soul power, he could ascend directly in broad daylight, heading to a greater world.","He could even condense a powerful physical body, comparable to a Dao Lord’s combat power.","However, there was one thing that worried him.","What if his soul power decreased after leaving the Nine Prison Pagoda?","If his soul power were reduced again, returning to the level of Divine Aspect Realm Thought power, it wouldn’t be able to last long. Moreover, in that small world outside, it would be extremely difficult to condense a matching physical body. Otherwise, no one would have reached the level of ascension for so many years.","After some hesitation, Jian Wushuang decided to search the place first. He still remembered that when he was swallowed in, three puppets had come along with him.","He wasn’t interested in the other two puppets, but the one refined from space crystals could be of great help to him.","Perhaps he could use that puppet to separate a portion of his soul power from this place.","The rest of his soul power could then explore this supreme treasure and possibly take control of it, using it to restore his soul power.","He knew the Nine Prison Pagoda had nine levels. Even the Nine Dust Immortal could only control the first level, and they hadn’t fully understood it. The subsequent levels might hold even more surprises.","With his current Dao Lord-level soul power, he could quickly comprehend the first level.","Having made up his mind, Jian Wushuang spread out his Thought power, beginning to search for the puppet.","But as his Thought power expanded, his eyes filled with disbelief.","“Even with my powerful Thought power, I can’t fully explore the first level. This supreme treasure is extraordinary, at least a peak-level supreme treasure!”","Jian Wushuang’s heart stirred, and his soul split apart.","His realm was high; as long as the power was there, all the secret techniques within his consciousness could be used.","At this moment, he performed a splitting technique of the Devouring Dao.","His body instantly split into countless avatars, each with the strength of a Nine Revolution Great Yan Immortal."]},{"number":6320,"title":"Chapter 6320: The Strength of Space","paragraphs":["Chapter 6320: The Strength of Space","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Thousands of clones dispersed, each flying in different directions.","The speed of the clones was incredible, covering tens of thousands of miles with every breath.","Meanwhile, his Thought power could cover a distance of approximately a hundred million miles.","The various clones flew for an entire day, and their connected Thought power spanned an area comparable to a great world, yet they still hadn’t reached the boundary.","“Fortunately, I found that puppet!” Jian Wushuang breathed a sigh of relief. Thousands of clones continued to spread out in search of the boundary, while the clone that retrieved the puppet remained in place, preparing to divide the soul force.","At this moment, that puppet had already been reduced to fragments.","Though Nine Prison Pagoda was in the hands of the Immortal Jiu Chen, and only a minor secret technique from the first level was employed, it was still enough to easily destroy a puppet crafted from spatial crystals.","Fortunately, the spatial crystals had turned into powdery fluid, which could still be reformed into a humanoid shape, and the spatial power within remained intact.","This was sufficient for Jian Wushuang’s needs.","Moreover, he even considered refining the spatial crystals anew, using the methods of the Immortal Jiu Chen to craft a body that embodied the laws of space.","The puppet crafted by the Immortal Jiu Chen only utilized the hardness of the spatial crystals, failing to tap into their full potential. However, for a practitioner at the Divine Aspect Realm, this was already pushing the limits.","But for Jian Wushuang, this was far from enough.","In his eyes, the hardness of spatial crystals wasn’t their most significant strength.","The space of a world was, in fact, not the most stable, often less so than time.","When Jian Wushuang had first become a Universe Master, he could tear through the void within an endless world. Later, when he reached the Realm God Continent, he, as a Universe God, was able to tear through space-time, even shattering it.","The seemingly formidable space of the Realm God Continent was like thin paper in the eyes of the powerful.","However, the upper limit of strength nurtured by the Realm God Continent was that of a Ninth Tribulation Universe God or even a God of Time and Space.","Yet, its spatial laws could only support Universe Masters below the level of Universe Gods.","A slightly stronger Universe God could tear through space, but some Universe Gods couldn’t alter the flow of time. Only the most powerful Universe Gods could achieve this.","Thus, space, within a world, was relatively easy to break through.","This is why most lower realm experts ascended by shattering the void.","For ordinary mortals who couldn’t ascend, breaking the void was already a great feat. But for a super-powerful being like Jian Wushuang, it was child’s play.","Shattering the void was purely a matter of strength.","To obtain even greater power, one had to rely on laws and the blessings of the world’s Dao.","It was like how the Emperor had refined a great world and became its controller, using the power of that world to rise as a supreme expert among Emperors.","Beyond that, one could control an entire universe.","Or create a universe and become a Universe Master. While this seemed to transcend the laws, it was still dependent on the power of laws.","The same applied to Universe Gods, who internalized the laws of the universe and could even resist the suppression of supreme rules.","But where did the power they wield come from?","Time?","Starry Sky?","This question was beyond what Jian Wushuang could fully comprehend at the moment, but based on his knowledge and deductions, he could infer that this power likely originated from the being who first created the Starry Sky.","The power of the Twelve Star Spirits was just a part of the Starry Sky. The Starry Sky couldn’t bear such immense power, so it dispersed it among the cultivators.","That was why so many powerful beings, governed by the highest rules, emerged, but in essence, they couldn’t escape the laws of the Starry Sky.","And the laws of the Starry Sky were created by that Starry Sky Creator.","Or rather... the Realm Beast.","Swish!","While guiding the space crystal, Jian Wushuang pondered over the path ahead.","Restoring his strength was just a minor detour, perhaps costing him tens of thousands of years at most. The road ahead was still the Divine Tribulation.","That was what mattered most to him.","After crossing the Divine Tribulation, whether he became a Universe God or a Time and Space God, he would be invincible on the Realm God Continent.","Whether to head to the Starry Sky or remain here would be a decision he could make on a whim.","He could stay to search for the whereabouts of the Prophet, who had once forged a Beast God’s weapon for him and then disappeared, as if they had never existed on the Realm God Continent.","The Prophet’s mystery reminded him of his teacher, Xuan Yi.","And this world he currently resided in—he had once dreamed of the Prophet’s silhouette.","That dream of the Prophet’s silhouette had occurred without any warning.","He had been groping for clues, hoping to see the Prophet again.","But he had never succeeded; he still needed to explore step by step.","“Prophet? Teacher Xuan Yi?” Jian Wushuang gently shook his head. “What exactly are you plotting? Back then, you guided me from a small world, gave me treasures and secret techniques, helped me step by step to leave the small world, to reach the Primordial Universe of the Great Yan Domain, encounter the Qishen Temple, venture into the Nine Great Time Spaces, and eventually arrive at the Realm God Continent. What is your plan behind all of this?”","Even today, he still couldn’t fully comprehend it.","In fact, he had almost given up back then, but then he encountered that Sword Immortal, Ding Baiyi, who drew him into the Great Yan Domain, and afterward, it was one step at a time of guidance.","Just like today, it was still a form of guidance.","“I already possess the combat strength of a Ninth Star Universe God. Can I still not meet Teacher Xuan Yi? Can I still not help him?” Jian Wushuang slowly closed his eyes.","Although he didn’t know how far away the so-called future was, he knew that time was already close.","Sitting cross-legged, a strand of his soul power merged with the space crystal.","The first attempt, failed!","Because his soul was too powerful, and those space crystals were merely the space crystals of this small world, their capacity too weak.","They could, at most, bear a soul power one level above the Divine Appearance Realm.","As for what that soul power level one level above the Divine Appearance Realm was, he wasn’t entirely sure. If he calculated it according to the cultivation system of the small world and the unified cultivation system of the outside world, it should still be the Dao Foundation realm.","In the unified cultivation system of the outside world, the stages were Postnatal, Innate, Dao Foundation, Primordial Spirit, Great Completion, Immortal, and Emperor.","Postnatal encompassed all postnatal creatures, while Innate was for special life forms, though special life forms could also be transformed. For instance, Jian Wushuang was a postnatal special life form.","However, in the context of the highest laws, he wasn’t considered a special life form, as his perspective was relatively narrow back then.","The difference between Postnatal and Innate was significant, but the realms were the same.","The first step on the cultivation path was still the Dao Foundation, which included many things.","Take the current small world as an example: all cultivation realms within it belonged to the Dao Foundation.","They all cultivated the basics.","Above the Dao Foundation was the Myriad Phenomena stage, which included even more.","Among them, there were tens of thousands of laws, and the differences between those at the same realm could be vast.","A faint memory of his weaker days flashed through Jian Wushuang’s mind as his soul power split again.","After continuous divisions, he finally retained a trace of soul power that entered the space crystal.","Whoosh!","The space crystal, which had already turned to dust, transformed from black to transparent, circling Jian Wushuang like a stream."]},{"number":6321,"title":"Chapter 6321: Jian Wushuang’s Surprise","paragraphs":["Chapter 6321: Jian Wushuang’s Surprise","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Although I lack divine power, my mastery of the laws has reached the foundational level. Not bad. Once I absorb the power of the spatial crystal, I should reach the limits of this world’s combat strength!” Jian Wushuang felt quite satisfied.","This was the advantage of having a supreme treasure, of course, provided that the treasure was unique enough.","If it were an ordinary treasure, no matter how much one of the deities from this world’s Divine Aspect Realm tried, they wouldn’t be able to attain it.","However, the Nine Prison Pagoda was different. It allowed even a small cultivator who had fallen from the Divine Aspect Realm to control it and utilize its inherent power. This was truly extraordinary.","But this alone wasn’t enough to surprise Jian Wushuang.","Now, he had been inside the Nine Prison Pagoda for a day, and his countless avatars had already spread out in all directions.","Each avatar’s Thought power covered a range of a billion miles. With ten thousand avatars, they covered a trillion miles, yet they still couldn’t find the boundary of the first layer. This place seemed like a world without borders.","Jian Wushuang had no choice but to send some weaker avatars to search for the boundary, while his main avatar remained in place.","His physical body had also almost finished refining, looking exactly like him—bronzed skin and sharp, chiseled features, all exuding a fierce aura.","“Now, let’s try controlling the Nine Prison Pagoda and send out the physical body. I wonder how Xiang Yang and the others are doing!”","Jian Wushuang wasn’t sure if the flow of time within the Nine Prison Pagoda differed from that of the outside world, which made him worried.","He was concerned about Jiang Shang’s safety.","Buzz!","As the thought arose, he began to comprehend the laws of the first layer of this world.","According to his calculations, a cultivator of the Divine Aspect Realm could control it, so with his current soul power, it should be effortless.","However, after comprehending several laws, his soul still couldn’t control the Nine Prison Pagoda!","“What’s going on?”","Jian Wushuang frowned.","He had already comprehended several laws, and by all accounts, he should have become the master of these laws. Moreover, the laws here weren’t simple; they were comparable to those of the Qinghuo Realm in the past.","Yet, he still couldn’t control the Nine Prison Pagoda!","He didn’t need much—just to master the first layer would be enough.","“Interesting. I underestimated this Nine Prison Pagoda. Its difficulty exceeds my expectations. Its range is comparable to a high-level world, and I still haven’t found the boundary. However, the further I go, the weaker the spatial power becomes. Its limit is probably only about the size of the Human Realm in the Four Great Secret Realms of the past, but the laws here are much stronger than those of a typical original universe. They’ve already touched the level of time and space. How did Immortal Jiu Chen inherit this Nine Prison Pagoda in the first place?”","The more Jian Wushuang thought about it, the more perplexed he became. He could only find out by asking Immortal Jiu Chen directly.","However, at this moment, he still believed that Jiu Chen had already fallen, which left him utterly puzzled.","“Forget it. Since I can’t master the first layer in a short time, I’ll break open a small hole at the edge and send my physical body out. When I scour everything, I’m sure I’ll find some clues!”","Jian Wushuang did not delve deeper into the matter. His main avatar, along with his physical body, began to head toward a weak spot in the space. Even if he couldn’t fully control the Nine Prison Pagoda, he could use burning thought power to break through the first layer of weak space and send his physical body out.","As long as his physical body could leave, the remaining main avatar would stay behind to continue comprehending, ensuring that nothing would be delayed.","“Yes, I’ll choose this spot!” Jian Wushuang halted his movements.","From the outside, this place didn’t seem much different from any other, but the space here was indeed weaker.","He only needed to burn a bit of soul power to pierce through.","“Soul burning!”","“Ha!”","Jian Wushuang formed his hand into a claw. Even though it wasn’t divine power he was burning, the fierce claw technique still caused the surrounding space to tremble instantly.","With a single tear, the sky-shattering claw broke the space apart, but it didn’t shatter the external space. However, it did leave a claw mark behind.","Within the deep, crisscrossing claw marks, a few specks of starlight could be seen.","That was light from the outside world.","“Go!”","In an instant, Jian Wushuang’s physical body transformed into a clear, crystalline stream of water. Following those tiny stars, he left the Nine Prison Pagoda in an instant.","Outside.","Xiang Yang, who was carrying the Nine Prison Pagoda, suddenly felt a chill down his spine. He quickly threw down the pagoda and retreated in a hurry.","This action confused the others, who turned to look at the Nine Prison Pagoda, only to find their mouths gaping open in shock.","Except for Xiang Yang, who had initially been the most worried, but now that he saw the water stream surging out, his face lit up with joy.","The others, who had lived their whole lives in this mundane world, were powerful beings themselves, referred to as upper Immortals, but their vision was much more limited.","Such divine techniques weren’t even recorded in ancient legacies.","The water stream shot out and instantly condensed into the appearance of Jian Wushuang, identical to the person they had seen before.","However, they stared at him in disbelief, their faces filled with fear.","It was Xiang Yang who broke the silence, hurrying forward to ask, “Brother Wushuang, have you regained your strength?”","Such a transformation of form at least required one to reach the Immortal stage.","This stage encompassed both the Yan Immortal and Great Yan Immortal, as well as the Dao Lords.","Xiang Yang assumed Jian Wushuang had regained his strength to the Immortal level, which meant he could take him along for the ride.","In fact, his assumption wasn’t wrong. Jian Wushuang had indeed reached the Immortal stage, but unfortunately, only his soul power had reached that level.","However, without a suitable physical body, it was impossible to bear the soul power of the Immortal stage.","The growth of the physical body couldn’t be separated from law, wealth, companions, and land, bringing him back to square one.","“Everyone, don’t you recognize me?”","Jian Wushuang’s lips curled into a smile, and his aura spread out in an instant. However, it didn’t target the crowd but instead swept through all the surrounding life forms, checking if anyone was watching them.","This time, his thought power coverage could extend to a limit of five hundred miles, a tenfold increase.","The only unfortunate part was that when his physical body left the Nine Prison Pagoda, it had absorbed quite a few space crystals from the fissures, preventing him from reaching the peak of the Nascent Soul stage or even the Divine Form stage. Instead, he remained in the middle of the Nascent Soul stage.","This was somewhat disappointing, as he had initially planned to come out and immediately take control of this world.","However, it wasn’t a significant issue. The soul power within his current physical body had already surpassed the Divine Form stage. Burning divine power was enough to rival a cultivator of the Divine Form stage, and this world posed no substantial threat to him.","Moreover, his main avatar was still inside the Nine Prison Pagoda. Even if he burned soul power, he could instantly replenish it.","With this, he could burn soul power at will.","“This soul-burning secret technique is really useful. Once I regain my strength, I must study this soul-burning technique!” Jian Wushuang pondered in his heart.","Outwardly, he spoke to the others about his experiences. Since their knowledge was limited, he didn’t go into too much detail, only mentioning that he had been trapped in the Nine Prison Pagoda and had obtained an ancient legacy, eventually breaking through to the middle of the Nascent Soul stage and successfully escaping the Nine Prison Pagoda.","He wasn’t deceiving them. If he said too much, they wouldn’t understand anyway.","As for Xiang Yang, Jian Wushuang didn’t hide much from him, only sending him a brief transmission, indicating that he was now invincible in the mortal realm and could roam freely as he pleased."]},{"number":6322,"title":"Chapter 6322: Questioning","paragraphs":["Chapter 6322: Questioning","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Even if they went straight to Tai’an City now, there would be no concerns.","However, when he mentioned returning to Tai’an City, everyone unanimously opposed it.","Even Xiang Yang expressed that there was no need to return now.","At this moment, Chen Yuan stepped forward to explain, “Senior Wushuang, you may not know this since you just came out. A few days ago, we captured a dying cultivator from the Chiyang Sect. From him, we learned that there is an altar hidden underground in Mangshan County, containing a great secret!”","“Oh, is that so?” Jian Wushuang looked doubtful.","It wasn’t that he didn’t believe Chen Yuan, but rather that he didn’t trust certain people.","For example, the Holy Maiden of the Centipede Tribe.","Ever since she learned that he had reached the mid-Nascent Soul stage, her gaze had been evasive, clearly indicating that there were things she hadn’t told Chen Yuan, and she was likely conspiring with Yang Xiao.","However, Jian Wushuang could tell that Yang Xiao didn’t know as much as the Holy Maiden.","His gaze turned to the Holy Maiden of the Centipede Tribe, and in an uncompromising tone, he said, “I don’t care what relationship or cooperation you have with Wei Jiuxian. I just want to know what your goal is!”","“This...” Yang Xiao was the first to step forward and plead, “Senior, you and the Commander must also have some sort of cooperative relationship, right? Since we’re all on the same side, we all have our own secrets. Why push for answers?”","“Heh!” Jian Wushuang turned his head to look at Yang Xiao, amused. “Yang Xiao, are you really unaware of the Centipede Tribe’s affairs?”","In truth, he didn’t know either; he was merely trying to bluff the other party. After all, the situation with the Jiang Kingdom wasn’t yet clear, and he didn’t want to burn bridges at this time.","Yang Xiao was obviously stunned by this statement, but then he resolutely said, “The Centipede Holy Maiden saved my life, and she cooperates with the Commander. I don’t want to know more than that!”","“She saved your life?”","At this moment, Xiang Yang sneered, “Yang Xiao, don’t forget that it was Brother Wushuang who saved your life. He saved everyone!”","These words naturally solidified their stance.","Chen Yuan was the same; he was a middleman, and his journey to Mangshan County was related to a matter that concerned him. However, everyone else was focused on the Holy Maiden of the Centipede Tribe’s goal.","Everyone, that is, except for the oblivious Yang Xiao, who thought that she had saved his life and was eager to repay her.","“If I don’t tell you, will you take action, Senior?” The Centipede Holy Maiden asked angrily.","Jian Wushuang simply shook his head and calmly replied, “Whatever you did to that demon sect cultivator earlier, I will do to you.”","Soul Search!","This technique was far too simple.","Once a Soul Search was performed, all secrets would be revealed.","Previously, Jian Wushuang’s strength hadn’t been enough, and with powerful figures watching them from the shadows, he hadn’t intended to search Yang Xiao’s soul.","But now things were different. He had the strength, and there were no prying eyes around. He could freely search souls.","He would uncover the truth about the Jiang Kingdom, and he would also learn the Centipede Holy Maiden’s purpose in Mangshan County.","He was just pondering whether to act so ruthlessly in front of Jiang Shang.","If she obediently confessed, he was willing to believe her.","For a moment, the situation was at an impasse.","Jiang Shang’s gaze was clear, and he tried several times to speak, but the words never left his lips.","Upon witnessing this scene, Jian Wushuang’s heart softened, and he spoke calmly, “I’ll give you a chance. Tell me what’s inside the altar beneath Mangshan County. I won’t concern myself with anything else. This benefits everyone.”","Except for the Centipede Saintess.","Among everyone present, only the Centipede Saintess knew what lay within the altar.","This time, Yang Xiao didn’t insist on protecting her. Instead, he tried to persuade her, “Saintess, this matter concerns the billions of people in the Tang Dynasty. Please, reveal it. It will also allow Senior Wushuang and the others to prepare in advance!”","“Even if I told you, you wouldn’t understand!” The Centipede Saintess responded with a bitter smile, her eyes even carrying a trace of mockery.","It was as if she were looking at a group of monkeys.","“What do you mean?” Jian Wushuang didn’t immediately grasp her meaning, for it had been too long since anyone dared speak to him this way.","Could it be that this Centipede Saintess was an illegitimate child of a Star Spirit?","If that were the case, she might indeed know more than Jian Wushuang.","But the likelihood of this happening was as slim as Jian Wushuang being a failure. How could a failure possibly cultivate to possess the battle power of a Nine-Star Universe God?","Clearly, this wasn’t possible!","“Just speak. Whether we understand or not is none of your concern, and you don’t have to worry about whether I believe you. My Thought power is strong; you should have witnessed this. Thought power reflects mental strength, so you can’t lie to me!” Jian Wushuang remained unhurried. After giving her some reassurance, he casually shrank the Nine Prison Pagoda and began playing with it in his hand.","Although he couldn’t control its interior, he could still manipulate its exterior with ease; he just couldn’t store it within himself.","Fortunately, his current physical body was a type of spatial special life form. Even a single drop of his blood contained a small space, albeit not large. However, placing a small nine-tiered pagoda inside was quite simple.","The Centipede Saintess cast a deep glance at everyone present.","This irritated Xiang Yang, who was impatient by nature. Just as he was about to lose his temper, Jian Wushuang held him back.","Yang Xiao and Jiang Shang believed that what she was about to reveal involved secrets of ancient cultivators. Although they were anxious, they patiently waited for her to speak.","Only Chen Yuan seemed utterly indifferent.","He wasn’t a cultivator and had no interest in the secrets of cultivators. However, he did harbor a secret of his own, one so significant that it could shock the entire Tang Dynasty. To him, whatever the Centipede Saintess said, no matter how earth-shattering, paled in comparison to his own secret.","“This matter needs to be traced back to ancient times!” The Centipede Saintess sighed deeply.","Her eyes showed no nostalgia, only a sense of melancholy.","From her words, everyone learned the name of this world.","“Red-Eyed Realm!”","This world was called the Red-Eyed Realm.","Upon hearing this name, everyone felt a sense of astonishment.","Jian Wushuang, however, was calculating whether this Red-Eyed Realm had any connection to the Red Sun Sect.","Xiang Yang felt no surprise; instead, he was full of disdain. He couldn’t care less about the name of such a small world.","The Centipede Saintess, with mockery and pride in her eyes, continued, “You might not know much about the realms between worlds. Let me explain it this way: the Red-Eyed Realm is one of the weakest worlds. Do you know where those who have shattered the void go?”","“The Upper Realm!” Yang Xiao answered honestly.","This was something the Immortal Jiu Chen had mentioned earlier. Repeating it now didn’t make him seem ignorant.","However, his answer only provoked a bout of laughter from the Centipede Saintess. “Even a three-year-old knows there is an Upper Realm. But do you know what the Upper Realm is called? What races live there? What kinds of cultivators exist, and how powerful they are? You don’t know!”","Without waiting for a rebuttal, she immediately dismissed everyone’s understanding.","No wonder she was so arrogant.","It seemed she truly knew some secrets.","“The Upper Realm consists of seventy-two ancient domains. Each domain is countless times larger than the Red-Eyed Realm. Even a cultivator at the Divine Form Realm, relying on flight alone, would never be able to cross a single ancient domain, not even if they lived their entire lifespan. You should know that in the lower realms, a cultivator at the Divine Form Realm can live for several thousand years. In the Upper Realm, they live even longer. Yet, crossing the Red-Eyed Realm for a Divine Form Realm cultivator only takes a month. Can you now grasp how vast the ancient domains are?” The Centipede Saintess smiled smugly, her bronze-colored eyebrows arched high."]},{"number":6323,"title":"Chapter 6323: Dead Water and Flowing Water","paragraphs":["Chapter 6323: Dead Water and Flowing Water","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Good heavens!”","Chen Yuan was utterly stunned.","As a mere scholar, he had always believed that this world was vast enough. In his understanding, there was no higher realm; he thought such tales were deceitful.","Even if a higher realm did exist, he assumed it wouldn’t be much stronger than the Red Eyes Realm.","Yang Xiao felt the same, his eyes widening with a strong sense of longing.","His path of cultivation was both peculiar and extreme. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have been able to escape from the hands of nine Golden Core experts and even kill several of them.","Jiang Shang, still young and with limited knowledge, was equally astonished. She felt as if she had been viewing the sky from the bottom of a well.","She never imagined that the upper realm could be so magnificent.","She had been following in her mother’s footsteps, searching for her mother’s whereabouts, though after all this time, she had only managed to gather a few clues.","Her entire cultivation path had been guided by her mother. She had never once pondered the wonders of the cultivation world on her own.","Now, hearing about the grandeur of the upper realm, her thoughts began to stir. She envisioned a scene where she would find her mother, and the two of them would ascend together.","Jian Wushuang stood there, his face filled with melancholy. He remained silent, showing little expression.","Only Xiang Yang sat on the ground, his usual carefree demeanor intact, still holding his stomach.","“Brother Wushuang, aren’t you overwhelmed by the vastness of this world?” Xiang Yang stifled a laugh, looking at Jian Wushuang with a serious expression as he asked, “In such a massive world, there must be Universe Masters, right? It’s simply terrifying!”","Jian Wushuang took a deep breath and interrupted, “Enough, stop messing around!”","“But this has nothing to do with Mangshan County. Grand narratives, anyone can tell them. I could even talk about the Realm God Continent!” Xiang Yang shouted, raising his voice.","Indeed, grand narratives were something anyone could speak of.","In their understanding, even the Realm God Continent wasn’t much.","Then there was the Starry Sky, which was even larger.","So vast that it made mortals despair.","But what did that matter?","That world had already left them far behind.","Jian Wushuang felt this way as well, which was why he seemed so melancholic.","They once had that splendid world.","Xiang Yang paused for a moment, the mockery in his eyes slowly turning into reminiscence.","“What are these two whispering about?” The Thousand-Legged Saintess glanced at Xiang Yang curiously.","The others, however, were somewhat confused, as Xiang Yang’s recent words made even less sense to them.","At least the Thousand-Legged Saintess’s narration had explanations and comparisons that allowed them to directly feel the power of the Upper Realm.","Yang Xiao, feeling a bit excited, gently urged, “Saintess, please continue. Brother Xiang Yang is a recluse; it’s normal for him to say some odd things after being surprised!”","This remark deeply hurt Xiang Yang’s heart. Just as he was about to retort, Jian Wushuang interrupted him.","“There’s no need. You are a Universe Master!”","After explaining the structure of the Upper Realm, the Thousand-Legged Saintess began talking about a legend.","This was all a prelude.","It was said that the Upper Realm once had 108 Ancient Domains, of which 36 were shattered, transforming into countless small worlds.","The Crimson Eye Domain was one of them.","Upon hearing this, everyone except Jian Wushuang and Xiang Yang revealed astonished expressions.","This time, no one interrupted, and the Thousand-Legged Saintess continued, “After the Ancient Domains shattered, they became countless worlds. The Crimson Eye Domain emerged from this, but as the Ancient Domains broke, their power slowly dwindled. The more cultivators there are, the less power this world has!”","“I see!” Yang Xiao and Jiang Shang revealed identical expressions.","This matter wasn’t exactly a big secret, and many should already know.","Jian Wushuang and Xiang Yang had long been aware that the power of this world was waning. In no time, it would turn into a purely mundane world.","But even mundane worlds have long lifespans. Perhaps after a hundred thousand or a million years, when the power of life is exhausted, even mortals will vanish.","Even the plants and beasts would perish, the world collapsing into the void.","The world would be destroyed.","But for mortals, that was far too distant.","“This matter had already spread during ancient times. Back then, cultivators were obsessed with cultivation, even giving rise to many demon sects. They slaughtered each other, reducing competition to achieve ascension.”","“During that era, a crimson eye appeared, changing everything!”","An eye!","Upon hearing those two words, Jian Wushuang thought of the ancient token.","But he didn’t ask directly.","This time, he truly listened.","The more he listened, the more astonished he became. A small cultivator in a mundane world telling a legend could shock a super powerhouse with the strength of a Nine-Star Universe God.","Xiang Yang thought he was going mad.","“Substance is the foundation. The foundation is this world. What encompasses this world? It’s a bigger world. Beyond the bigger world, there are even bigger worlds, but the essence is the Starry Sky. That’s the power of the Starry Sky!” Jian Wushuang muttered, making Xiang Yang think he had gone mad.","But Jian Wushuang just smiled indifferently.","The Thousand-Legged Saintess on the other side wasn’t lying; he could see that.","Whether the legend was true or not, he needed to verify it himself.","“Brother Wushuang, what did you hear that surprised you so much?” Xiang Yang couldn’t help but ask through a voice transmission.","Jian Wushuang, however, spoke directly, “What the Thousand-Legged Saintess just mentioned, the Divine Eye Secret Technique, which allows one to enhance strength and realm without absorbing the power of the Crimson Eye Domain, I find it very interesting. Why not share your thoughts as well?”","“A world is like a pool of water. The Crimson Eye Domain is clearly a stagnant pool, while the 72 Ancient Domains of the Upper Realm are like a river. Even if the people living by the river drink as they please, they can’t finish it, because the water just flows by their doorstep.”","His analogy was apt.","This time, Xiang Yang finally understood.","He exclaimed in shock, “This inheritance secret technique is truly defying the heavens, going against fate!”","“You can’t say that. As far as I know, although the Crimson Eye Domain is a stagnant pool, what if a strong person is willing to add water?” Jian Wushuang speculated.","Xiang Yang first nodded seriously, then shook his head. “Impossible. If water could be added, the power of those cultivators who died in the mutual slaughter would have returned to the pool. But according to what the Thousand-Legged Saintess said, the power of those cultivators who were killed did not return. They only killed to prevent their opponents from continuing to absorb the power of the Crimson Eye Domain!”","“You’re right, but those people were too weak!” Jian Wushuang shook his head.","If he hadn’t obtained the Nine Prison Pagoda, he might have believed it.","Moreover, when he first entered this place, he encountered those demonic creatures, all of whom were Universe Gods with the combat strength of six or seven stars.","The upper limit of this world was far from as simple as Xiang Yang imagined.","Besides, he had also dreamed of the Prophet, a person who could vanish from others’ memories.","A Universe Master could already create a universe. Activating a universe was also easy, though the probability was low.","Aside from the Divine Eye Secret Technique mentioned by the Thousand-Legged Saintess, the Crimson Eye Domain had nothing special.","If one came for the secret technique, it was indeed possible.","But this kind of secret technique was for mundane cultivators. Even if it were taken by an Emperor or even a Universe Master, what use would it be?","Could they really create a heaven-defying secret technique?","If they could create it, allowing them to skip over a river and absorb the power of an ocean, wouldn’t that be redundant?"]},{"number":6324,"title":"Chapter 6324: Ancestor of the Qianzu Tribe","paragraphs":["Chapter 6324: Ancestor of the Qianzu Tribe","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The power absorbed ultimately belonged to the Starry Sky.","Although it wasn’t of much use, the person who created this secret technique intrigued Jian Wushuang. If possible, once he regained all his strength, he would reverse time and space to witness firsthand how that person crafted such a technique.","As he pondered this, Jian Wushuang recalled that his original task was related to the underground altar in the Mangshan County.","Could this have something to do with the God Eye Secret Technique?","After all, given how long this had been building up, if there was no connection, it would be quite absurd. It would be a waste of time!","The Centipede Saintess spoke again, but this time, she had lost much of her earlier arrogance. Jian Wushuang’s earlier analogy and hypothesis were indeed things she had never heard before.","“Let me put it this way: The reason the Red Eye Realm is called the Red Eye Realm is because of the God Eye Secret Technique. However, the God Eye Secret Technique originated from the God Eye Clan, and it not only appears in the Red Eye Realm but also exists in the Upper Realm. However, in ancient inheritances, only the matters related to the God Eye Secret Technique are recorded, and there is little mention of the God Eye Clan itself.”","“However, the Red Eye Realm is different. The inheritance of the God Eye in the Red Eye Realm is unlike any other world, or rather, it is more powerful. It is even stronger than the ancient domains of the Upper Realm. According to the records, the inheritance of the God Eye Secret Technique is divided into seven levels. The first level is the simplest—one only needs to be innately gifted to obtain a black-pupil God Eye token. With this token, one can go to the Northern Region Glacier and pass the first level of the test to receive the inheritance!”","At this point, Xiang Yang couldn’t help but urge, “You should get to the point about Mangshan County. If you keep going off-topic, you’ll just be wasting everyone’s time!”","“It’s fine. Just speak at your own pace. No need to rush!” Jian Wushuang interjected, causing Xiang Yang to fall silent once more.","The others were also not in a hurry. After all, it was like listening to a story—they naturally wanted to know more details; otherwise, where was the appeal?","Unfortunately, the story had already reached its end.","The Centipede Saintess spoke with a tone of regret: “Many years ago, an ancestor of our clan obtained a fourth-level token and passed the test set by the God Eye Clan. He successfully received the inheritance. With this inheritance, he quickly reached the peak of the Divine Image Realm. Just as the ancestor was about to make a breakthrough and ascend to the Upper Realm, he was ambushed by a despicable person who used a secret technique to seize his body. However, the ancestor had a contingency plan in place. Using the Heaven’s Foot Blood Shield, he fought the attacker to a draw, with both losing their physical bodies and power. The power lost could not dissipate on its own due to the nature of the God Eye Secret Technique. But because that power was so immense, others could not absorb it either. In the end, the clan’s strongmen sealed it, hoping to wait for the ancestor to recover and reclaim his lost power. Yet, unexpectedly, the ancestor ultimately couldn’t hold on...”","Although this event had taken place a millennium ago, the Qianzu Saintess still felt sorrowful, as her tribe had almost produced an ascendant. What a great honor that would have been!","Everyone present began to realize the significance of what she had just said.","“You mean to say that the altar beneath Mangshan County holds the power sealed by your ancestors?”","“That’s right. This time, I’ve come to reclaim that sealed power. I forgot to mention, it was the ancestor of the Tang Dynasty who sealed this power a thousand years ago!” the Qianzu Saintess added.","This statement sparked a chain of thoughts in Jian Wushuang’s mind.","The Tang Dynasty ancestor?","Wasn’t that the monk from Baoguang Temple?","He had sealed the power of the Thousand-foot tribe’s ancestor, and now, due to the current Tang Emperor, it was reappearing in Mangshan County.","There was a conspiracy behind this.","Jian Wushuang couldn’t fully comprehend it yet. He glanced at Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang, then said, “In that case, let’s not hesitate any longer. We’ll head straight to Mangshan County!”","“Better to be cautious. I’ve already informed the elders of my tribe. They will arrive outside Mangshan County soon, and it won’t be too late to enter the city together then,” the Qianzu Saintess expressed her concern.","Meanwhile, Yang Xiao was fiddling with a token by his side. It was obvious he was summoning reinforcements.","He reported everything to the Chief Commander and then dispatched people for support.","The power at the peak of the Divine Phase was enough to drive all cultivators mad.","The Thousand-foot tribe had collaborated with Wei Jiuxian precisely to reclaim this power, allowing the tribe’s experts to break through to the peak of the Divine Phase.","They hoped that with the last bit of power in the world, they could shatter the void and ascend to immortality.","Most people would think this way.","But Jian Wushuang was a strategist—he always planned before acting!","The planning had already begun. When the Qianzu Saintess revealed this secret, he started pondering why this power had been sealed in the first place.","The ancestor of the Tang Dynasty, though a man of deep emotions, was believed to have no hope of ascending.","However, hearing that he could seal the power of a Divine Phase peak expert, Jian Wushuang realized that he was likely a super expert on the verge of ascension.","Why didn’t such a person absorb that power and ascend directly?","Either he had no interest in ascension, or there was a problem with that power, making him too afraid to absorb it. Hence, he sealed it.","But now, the current Tang Emperor had discovered it and wanted to try absorbing that power for ascension.","To Jian Wushuang, regardless of the secrets hidden within that power, he needed to obtain it!","So he had to move quickly.","As for the others, if they went along, they would only compete with him. Why wait?","Yang Xiao wanted to wait for Wei Jiuxian, and the Qianzu Saintess wanted to wait for her tribe’s experts.","Jian Wushuang had no reason to wait.","“Since this power is now sealed within the altar, everyone can rely on their own abilities!” Jian Wushuang’s words left the group stunned.","Recalling Jian Wushuang’s previous god-like strength, they couldn’t help but worry that he might decide to eliminate them all at this moment.","“Don’t worry, I have no intention of attacking you. Whether you’re from the Zhanxian Guard or the Thousand-foot tribe, you can choose to wait or go now. We’ll rely on our own abilities, and I won’t strike against you first!”","Jian Wushuang had enough magnanimity to say this. To him, that power was already within his grasp.","With his current strength and the burning of his Thought power, even a Divine Phase expert would not be his match. He might not be invincible, but he dared to fight.","“Join me, or wait here—it’s your choice!”","The Qianzu Saintess and Yang Xiao hesitated no longer and replied, “We’ll go!”","“Good!”","Jian Wushuang enveloped the group with his Thought power, and with a powerful surge of energy, they instantly soared into the sky.","Without holding back, they flew straight toward Mangshan County.","Their speed reached the peak of the Infant Transformation Phase.","This was even with others in tow—without them, they would have been faster.","While they made a grand entrance toward Mangshan County, they were unaware that a heavy guard had already been stationed outside the county.","The Tang Emperor had initiated the final plan, gathering all the experts from the Chiyang Sect and the Zhanxian Guard, sending them to Mangshan County.","Such a large-scale mobilization could not escape Wei Jiuxian’s notice. He immediately recalled Chang Feng and led half of the Zhanxian Guard to Mangshan County as well.","Besides the Tang Dynasty of the Eastern Land, ancient inheritors from the Northern Glacier and tribes from the Barbarian Wilderness had also received word. The cultivators from the entire Red Eye Realm seemed to converge, all heading toward Mangshan County at once."]},{"number":6325,"title":"Chapter 6325: Clouds Move","paragraphs":["Chapter 6325: Clouds Move","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The winds stirred, and the clouds trembled!","Outside Mangshan County...","Eight hundred miles from the city of Mangshan County, a group of savage men riding ferocious beasts halted at the foot of the mountains. Among them, an elderly man clad in clothes sewn from animal hides slowly stepped forward. Tears glistened in his eyes as he gazed in the direction of Mangshan County. His voice quivered as he said, “Our great ancestor, soon our Qianzu Tribe will be able to bring you home!”","“Bring the great ancestor home!” echoed a middle-aged man behind the elder, whose appearance bore a striking resemblance to him.","Instantly, the entire valley resounded with a thunderous uproar. From a higher vantage point, the entire valley was filled with barbarian warriors mounted on beasts.","The Qianzu Tribe merely took the lead, but all the tribes of the wilderness had mobilized their entire forces as well!","They were doing this for their great ancestor, and also to overthrow the Tang Dynasty.","In the western part of Mangshan County...","This area bordered the vast desert, and deep within the desert lay the connection to the northern glaciers.","There, ancient relics could be found, a sacred land for ancient Qi Refiners.","Almost all the cultivators of the Scarlet Eye Realm yearned to reach this sacred land to receive the inheritance of the Divine Eye.","However, very few managed to pass the inheritance.","But those who did were able to establish sects in the northern glaciers.","In the past thousand years, sects in the northern glaciers had dwindled, but a few super sects remained. Now, they had all gathered outside Mangshan County.","The leader of these sects wore a Daoist robe, his face as handsome as jade. Though he appeared to be a youth of seventeen or eighteen, he had lived for over a thousand years, and his strength was unfathomable.","He was the Daoist Leader of the northern glaciers, having once passed the fourth level of the Divine Eye inheritance.","With this inheritance, he had cultivated to the peak, yet he was still a step away from shattering the void.","If he could obtain that sealed power, he was confident he could ascend.","“I have waited a thousand years, and finally, the seal is breaking. I wonder which high expert has been plotting behind the scenes!” The young Daoist Leader stood with his hands behind his back, treading the void between the valleys. His steps reverberated through the air.","The surrounding space rippled.","Behind him, countless majestic warships sailed against the wind, moving through the high skies.","On the decks, rows of cultivators stood, all of them in the Golden Core stage.","There were over a thousand people in total.","Such a powerful force was enough to rival the entire Eastern Tang of the Great Tang.","One had to know that since the Dao Realm had shattered, the entire cultivation world had been in decline.","The cultivators of the Southern Heaven Realm no longer resembled true cultivators, indulging in wealth and the pleasures of the mortal world.","The Northern Ice Region, on the other hand, was too cold and heartless, resembling a traditional cultivation sect.","Only the Great Tang retained a trace of human warmth.","Thus, the most cultivators were born there, and in fact, many of the cultivators in the Northern Ice Region originally hailed from Eastern Tang of the Great Tang.","The only pity was that now, everyone had their own duties.","Though they came from the Great Tang, they had to fight for their own opportunities.","Moreover, this Tang was no longer their Tang.","It was the Tang of the imperial Li clan.","No one cared about their identity as Tang cultivators anymore.","At the same time, high above the coast of the Eastern Region, a group of cultivators in luxurious robes also stepped across the sea.","Their display was grand, and their numbers were many. Besides the Golden Core cultivators, they had even brought innate cultivators, significantly outnumbering the barbarian tribes.","Anyone unaware of the situation might have thought they were here to attack the Great Tang!","But that wasn’t the case. These cultivators came from the Southern Heaven Realm, from various sects worshipped by the Seven Southern Nations.","Their sects were scattered, without a core structure, a loose collection that looked grand but was actually hollow.","The seventy-six warships in the lead rose from the sea, hovering in mid-air, creating a spectacular sight.","But behind it all were Golden Core stage cultivators silently contributing their strength.","Especially the massive warship in the lead, which was over a hundred meters long and wide. To keep it suspended in mid-air required a force far beyond the Nascent Soul stage.","However, the Southern Heaven Realm was the weakest, and Nascent Soul stage cultivators would never waste their strength on appearances.","Thus, the burden fell on the Golden Core cultivators operating the warships.","“Those people from Tianyang Sect are truly shameless. The three of us do all the hard work, and they bask in the glory outside. I’m not happy about it!” In the control room, a burly man grumbled as he channeled energy into the warship.","Beside him, two others were using the same methods to control the massive ship.","The thin elder in charge tried to comfort him, saying, “Enough, they paid us too much. It’s not a big deal to swallow our pride for a bit. Stop complaining, and once we get the ship over there, we’ll slip away!”","“But what if there’s a benefit?” asked a young cultivator with sharp features, unable to resist.","This time, the Southern Heaven Realm had put in such effort, not just for a show, but because they had received news—a piece of information that could change the entire cultivation world.","However, the three of them were only in the late Golden Core stage and weren’t qualified to know such secrets. They only knew that a great opportunity awaited, but what exactly it was, they had no idea.","The thin elder’s brow furrowed at his companion’s question, and he scolded, “Just get to work! For people like us, Tianyang Sect’s reward is already a great opportunity!”","Buzz!","Seventy-two warships simultaneously sailed towards the Great Tang’s coast, with a clear target—Mangshan County City.","In just a few days, the events in Mangshan County City had spread like wildfire, gathering cultivators from the entire Scarlet Eye Realm.","No one knew who had leaked the information.","No one cared to investigate the source either; they all chose to believe it.","That was the strangest part of it all.",".....","In Tai’an City, within the imperial palace.","In the rear garden, Emperor Guangfu Li Miao walked barefoot on the muddy ground scattered with flower petals, enjoying the cold sensation. The Great Tang emperor found it quite pleasurable.","“Lord Wei, I’m glad you came to see me today, but your earlier words have put me in a difficult position!” Li Miao spoke casually, strolling through the soft soil, admiring the flowers and occasionally picking one to sniff.","Wei Jiuxian stood by the corridor at the edge of the garden, head held high, completely ignoring the emperor’s subtle reprimand.","His expression grew increasingly grim.","“Your Majesty, I care not about the people of the Northern Ice Region, but the barbarian tribes have entered Mangshan County with one hundred thousand troops, and those from the Southern Heaven Realm have gathered tens of thousands of warships on the sea. Even the mortals have come. Why is this? What does it mean? Surely Your Majesty knows better than I do!” Wei Jiuxian’s tone was neither humble nor arrogant.","He valued the Great Tang more than the emperor before him.","For the Great Tang, he would defy the emperor and even give up his position as the commander of the Zhanxian Guard. Now, with enemies invading from all sides, how could he not be anxious, even if it meant offending the sovereign?","“You’ve worked tirelessly for the Great Tang, and I’ve taken note,” Emperor Guangfu slowly turned his head, his tone softening as he gazed at this elder statesman. He recalled the time when he had just ascended the throne, and Wei Jiuxian had stood by his side. Later, when the Rebel King attacked, it was Wei Jiuxian who protected him, allowing him to reclaim his throne. It wasn’t just the Chiyang Sect’s support; it was also the assistance of this commander."]},{"number":6326,"title":"Chapter 6326: Are You Laughing at Us?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6326: Are You Laughing at Us?","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","He had been intelligent since childhood, surpassing the former emperor in the art of ruling.","How could he not discern who among the court officials were loyal ministers and who were traitorous ones?","“But the things I must do are equally important. The events of three years ago will not repeat themselves. This empire will not perish because of me; it will exist because of me. Do you understand?”","After saying this, the Guangfu Emperor’s dragon robe fluttered behind him, and his entire aura surged.","Born with the appearance of a dragon, once he reached the Divine Image Realm, he could unleash the power of the Dragon Image, becoming a supreme powerhouse within the realm.","Yet, Wei Jiuxian found it laughable. He even laughed out loud.","“Is this still the same little brat who was kicked off the dragon throne three years ago?”","Three years had passed, and too many people had changed.","The young emperor who had been kicked off the dragon throne back then now dared to utter such words as “exist because of me.”","Perhaps that ancient figure from a thousand years ago could have said this.","But a thousand years later, even the one from Baoguang Temple could not.","“Are you mocking me?” The Guangfu Emperor’s expression twisted, both deranged and furious, as he shouted, “Wei Jiuxian, the bond between us has reached its limit. Don’t push me. Now, you just need to stand quietly atop the southern city gate and watch—watch me complete my grand plan. Afterward, you can do whatever you want with the empire!”","Wei Jiuxian shook his head and said firmly, “Too late. It’s time for a new emperor in this Tang dynasty!”","“How dare you!”","The Guangfu Emperor’s face changed. Although he had long expected Wei Jiuxian to join forces with the Desire King to force his abdication, he had not anticipated that Wei would still dare to tear off the mask after witnessing his strength.","He had just displayed his power to let Wei know that he was no longer the little emperor who could be easily kicked aside three years ago.","“Why wouldn’t I dare!” Wei Jiuxian knocked off his official hat, and from his sleeve slid out a Nine-Ridge Long Whip.","“The King’s Whip?” The Guangfu Emperor was shocked.","This was the King’s Whip passed down from their ancestors, used to strike corrupt rulers and rebellious ministers.","It had fallen into the hands of the Desire King in this generation.","The two had originally been mortal enemies, but the nobles valued the empire above all.","It didn’t matter who the emperor was, as long as the empire remained and the one on the throne bore the surname Li.","As for the current emperor, naturally, someone had to lead the charge to overthrow him.","Just as Wei Jiuxian made his move, outside the imperial palace, the Desire King and a hundred princes and dukes from the Xiangzong Mansion entered the court.","The Empress Dowager issued a decree, and its contents were simple.","It was the truth about Mangshan County.","“The current emperor is foolish, favoring the demonic cult and indulging in slaughter. For his own selfish desires, he has ruined the empire left by the ancestors. Today, we advise him to abdicate!”","Persuade!","But not against.","After all, the Tang Dynasty was still the Tang Dynasty.","The Desire King and his group didn’t care whether the Restoration Emperor had been taken down by Wei Jiuxian. They had already started drafting a second imperial decree to select a new emperor.","As for the confidants of the Restoration Emperor, they had all headed to Mangshan Country. Whether it was the Chiyang Sect or the Zhanxian Guards led by the Guardians of Nanshan, they were all gathering in Mangshan Country.","There wasn’t a single confidant of the Restoration Emperor left within Tai’an City.","Adding to this, Wei Jiuxian acted cleanly and efficiently, quickly allowing the Desire King to gain control of the situation.","Meanwhile, the battle between Wei Jiuxian and Emperor Li Miao also came to an end!","Their struggle lasted only the time it took for an incense stick to burn.","This made Li Miao, who had been so confident, unable to believe that he had actually lost to Wei Jiuxian.","He had just broken through to become a late-stage Nascent Soul cultivator!","“You’ve been hiding your strength all along?” Li Miao’s face was full of shock.","Wei Jiuxian remained calm and said indifferently, “I was never too focused on cultivation, but after what happened three years ago, I could no longer remain indifferent.”","“Hmph!” Li Miao sneered, shaking his head. He casually threw his dragon robe to the ground and bitterly smiled, “I underestimated you. Reaching Nascent Soul completion... truly remarkable!”","As he spoke, he began to walk towards the door.","This place no longer belonged to him, and he had never intended to be an emperor for life.","Once one embarked on the path of cultivation, all worldly matters would gradually be forgotten.","So he dared to go against all public opinion, slaughtering common people to gather blood pills for his cultivation.","This was also the reason why he and Wei Jiuxian had parted ways.","“Your Majesty...” Wei Jiuxian said softly, “Back then, when she entrusted the imperial consort to you, you should have kept your promise.”","Whoosh!","Hearing these words, Li Miao stopped in his tracks, his body trembling uncontrollably.","“Enough, I’ve given you the entire Tang Dynasty. What more do you want?” Li Miao impatiently shouted, venting the frustration in his heart.","In truth, his heart was filled with more fear than anyone else’s.","That promise from years ago?","An image flashed through his mind.","A delicate woman leaned against him, while he knelt on the ground.","At that time, he had not yet ascended to the throne; he was just the crown prince.","In that image, he knelt before a woman dressed in pure white, as spotless as snow.","That woman was like a beacon in the darkness, pure and flawless.","She was the embodiment of all light.","“You wronged the imperial consort, and you wronged the Celestial Maiden who brought her back to life!”","At this moment, Wei Jiuxian’s words shattered his light.","Celestial Maiden?","That title caused Li Miao’s entire body to tremble. After a long moment, he suddenly turned around and sneered at Wei Jiuxian, “She was just an ancient cultivator sealed in the northern glacier. She was never a Celestial Maiden! If she were a Celestial Maiden, how could she have fallen in love with a monk? It’s utterly laughable!”","“Is that so? And who do you think orchestrated your downfall today?” Wei Jiuxian sneered.","Li Miao grew even more terrified, losing all the pride and composure he once had.","This was the deepest fear buried in his heart.","The Princess’s Tomb!","The most mysterious imperial mausoleum of the Tang Dynasty, and also an immensely terrifying force.","“Impossible! How could she be connected to the Princess’s Tomb? Besides, she said she would ascend soon. How could she still be in the Red Eyes Realm?” Li Miao was already somewhat hysterical.","Wei Jiuxian continued to provoke him, “You’re right, she is no longer in this world. But the Princess’s Tomb remains, as does the Baoguang Temple. When your ancestors sealed that power, they foresaw this day. That’s why someone has come to break the seal!”","“Are you talking about those few people from Jiang Kingdom?” Li Miao took a deep breath.","He had many spies throughout the world, and the First Pavilion of the World was one of them.","When Jian Wushuang and his companions had just entered Tai’an City, they were immediately watched. Those cultivators from the Jiang Kingdom—combined with the destruction of the Jiang royal family and the absence of bodies—had raised Li Miao’s suspicions. He had then sent the experts from the Chiyang Sect to assassinate Jian Wushuang and the others.","It was initially a probe, but the group suddenly disappeared from Tai’an City.","Now, in hindsight, they were probably hidden by Wei Jiuxian.","“Wei Jiuxian, you truly had your own agenda. When I sent people to the Jiang Kingdom to search for the Celestial Maiden, you obstructed me at every turn, secretly opposing me. Now it seems that the Celestial Maiden indeed left something behind. If I’m not mistaken, she must be that woman in plain clothing who visited the Baoguang Temple earlier!” At this moment, Li Miao’s expression became calm, as if everything had returned to his control."]},{"number":6327,"title":"Chapter 6327: The Past of the Jiang Kingdom","paragraphs":["Chapter 6327: The Past of the Jiang Kingdom","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The conversation between the two seemed completely aimless, yet it inadvertently revealed a shocking secret.","...","Mangshan Country, the Rift Sky Canyon.","Jian Wushuang, along with his group, arrived at the canyon outside Mangshan City at the first possible moment. As soon as they landed, they sensed countless auras flashing around them, indicating that powerful beings had already arrived in advance.","This surprised the group, and they exchanged glances, each harboring suspicions in their hearts.","After all, the Qianzu Saintess had just revealed the hidden secret beneath Mangshan Country, and they had rushed over immediately, only to find that others had arrived even earlier.","This inevitably made them wonder if someone had tipped them off in advance.","Yang Xiao had indeed sent a message, but he had only informed Wei Jiuxian, a disgraced eunuch. How could such a person have the ability to gather so many powerful figures?","There was clearly more to this than they knew.","Taking advantage of this opportunity, Jian Wushuang began to question Yang Xiao.","He first inquired about the situation on Wei Jiuxian’s side, then brought up the matter of the Jiang Kingdom, which they had long wanted to understand.","At the mention of this, Yang Xiao’s expression turned grim.","Jiang Shang, on the other hand, eagerly awaited the answer he had dreamed of for so long.","“This matter... I shouldn’t be talking about it, but since you all come from the Jiang Kingdom, I knew I couldn’t hide it from you!” Yang Xiao forced a bitter smile.","At that moment, he finally understood why Jian Wushuang and the others had been protecting him. It was all because he had once visited the Jiang Kingdom and completed a top-secret mission.","Very few people knew about this.","As for his trip to the Jiang Kingdom, only a few within the Zhanxian Guard knew about it, and the mission’s content was known to only three people.","One was his direct superior, Wei Jiuxian, and another was the Emperor of the Tang Restoration, Li Miao.","To this day, no one else knew about it.","Because it involved a shocking secret.","“Yang Xiao, I have two ways of finding out about this. You should understand what I mean!” Jian Wushuang’s tone carried a hint of threat.","He could search his soul or have him speak.","But the former was too extreme. If Yang Xiao willingly spoke, things would be much easier.","Yang Xiao was the kind of person who responded better to gentle persuasion, but at this moment, he knew better than to resist.","Especially since this earth-shattering secret was related to the Jiang Kingdom.","He also knew that Jian Wushuang and the others came from the Jiang Kingdom.","In the end, he chose not to resist anymore. After all, revealing it wouldn’t harm Wei Jiuxian, and as for that Emperor, he had long ceased to recognize him.","Mangshan Country had been slaughtered entirely by the current Emperor. Such a rebellious act would not be unjustified, even if the Emperor himself were executed. Why would he still have any desire to protect the Emperor’s secret?","“I can tell you, but everyone else needs to step aside!” Yang Xiao glanced at the Qianzu Saintess and Chen Yuan.","Jian Wushuang raised his hand and formed a barrier.","This barrier, created by thought power, isolated sound and movement. Even those who could read lips wouldn’t be able to discern what Yang Xiao was saying.","If Jian Wushuang had more power, he could have isolated time and space directly, but he deemed such precautions unnecessary for a mundane world’s small secret.","Once everything was arranged, Jiang Shang, the most excited of the group, couldn’t help but urge, “Why did you go to the Jiang Kingdom back then? Was it because of a woman in white?”","“So you do know her!” Yang Xiao’s eyes narrowed slightly. The more he looked at the woman in front of him, the more she resembled the woman in white from the painting the Emperor of Tang had given him.","Jian Wushuang turned his head to glance at Jiang Shang, then looked at Yang Xiao, frowning as he said, “Just say it directly, no need to beat around the bush!”","He could only guess so much, and simply listening to the other person riddling wouldn’t help. Even if he had a mind as sharp as a seven-orifice exquisite heart, he wouldn’t be able to figure it out!","And it was exhausting!","“This matter... I don’t know much about it, but I do know that it’s related to Qishen Temple and the Princess’s Tomb,” Yang Xiao said, his gaze tinged with recollection. He continued, “Not long after the Tang Emperor’s restoration, he suddenly summoned me and Duke Wei. They handed me a portrait and instructed me to go to the Jiang Kingdom to find the person in the painting. However, on the day I was about to depart, Duke Wei privately found me and told me to bypass the Jiang Kingdom, take a detour over the sea, and return without conducting any investigation in Jiang.”","Yang Xiao remembered the scene clearly.","In addition to advising him not to go to the Jiang Kingdom, Duke Wei also revealed the identity of the woman in the portrait.","“A Celestial Maiden.”","The woman in the portrait was an ancient Celestial Maiden.","This title left Jiang Shang somewhat puzzled, while Xiang Yang listened as if it were just a story.","Only Jian Wushuang was left standing frozen in place.","“It really is her!”","There couldn’t be such a coincidence in the world.","A Celestial Maiden!","The Maiden of the Nine Heavens, Jiang Shang!","At that moment, he recalled the deity statue enshrined in Qishen Temple. His voice trembled as he asked, “What is the connection between the deity statue in Qishen Temple and the Celestial Maiden?”","“I’m not too sure about that, but the records in the Zhanxian Guard’s archives state that the deity statue was brought to the Tang Dynasty by an ancestor a thousand years ago. It was said to be called ‘Chanji,'” Yang Xiao replied, somewhat puzzled as to why Jian Wushuang would ask such an unrelated question.","Weren’t they talking about the Celestial Maiden just now?","Moreover, he could tell that Jiang Shang was likely the descendant left behind by the Celestial Maiden.","What intrigued him was who could have been responsible for the Celestial Maiden having a descendant.","Although Yang Xiao didn’t fully understand the identity of the Celestial Maiden, he could guess that she had the power to ascend at the time. No one in the entire world would have been worthy enough for her to leave a child behind.","It all seemed unsolvable.","But Jian Wushuang had found the answer in his heart.","The deity statue might have been the remnant left behind when Huiqing played chess with the Celestial Maiden in the Gu Yue Space-Time and later somehow fell into the Realm God Continent.","He had figured out the reason; the only mystery remaining was why it had appeared in this world.","And why he had encountered it by chance.","Glancing at Jiang Shang, Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but reach out and touch her head, a smile forming at the corner of his eyes.","Jiang Shang didn’t shy away, instead curiously asking, “Senior, do you know my mother?”","She wasn’t foolish and could tell that Jian Wushuang’s expression had drastically changed after hearing her mother’s name.","Of course, this was because Jian Wushuang hadn’t hidden his reaction.","He nodded, not denying it, and calmly said, “I knew her, a long time ago.”","Xiang Yang, standing nearby, silently complained about Jian Wushuang in his heart.","“You know everyone, huh? You’ve only been here a few days, and I’m embarrassed to expose you!”","In his view, Jian Wushuang was definitely pretending to be mysterious with no good intentions.","Whoosh!","Jian Wushuang took a deep breath and casually lifted the barrier, saying, “Everyone, the chance for ascension is right before us. It’s all up to your own abilities now!”","Everyone nodded in a daze, not knowing what he was thinking.","...","Tai’an City.","The Restored Emperor staggered out of the imperial palace, having shed his dragon robe and donned a coarse Taoist robe, with a trace of malevolence at the tip of his brow.","“Everyone in the world thinks this palace is a treasure, but they don’t realize it’s a cage. Today, I’ve escaped from this cage, and I shall no longer be the Emperor trapped inside!” Li Miao said, his figure flickering as he disappeared from the palace gate."]},{"number":6328,"title":"Chapter 6328: \"Sweep\" the World","paragraphs":["Chapter 6328: “Sweep” the World","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","When he reappeared, he had already arrived at the Imperial Tombs.","The largest tomb among them wasn’t for an emperor, but for a princess.","This princess’s tomb had become the ancestral tomb that every former emperor had to worship.","This was because, back then, when the prince from a small foreign nation married into the Tang Dynasty, it was naturally impossible for him to worship someone from another country.","Even if that person had founded the Baoguang Temple.","Li Miao walked along the path of the Imperial Tombs, heading towards the deepest part, where a towering ancient palace stood.","At this moment, a figure in black appeared in front of the ancient palace. Judging by the posture, it was a woman, seemingly young, yet with a commanding presence.","“Li Miao, what are you doing here?”","Few would dare to speak to the recently abdicated emperor in such a tone.","Li Miao didn’t get angry. Instead, he calmly replied, “Even though I am no longer the emperor of the Tang Dynasty, the princess’s tomb is still the ancestral tomb of my Li family. I am here to pay my respects. Do I need to report to you?”","Seeing the other person momentarily speechless, he no longer paid her any attention and walked straight into the hall.","The hall was simply furnished, with statues and altars.","He first lit three incense sticks, respectfully bowed several times, and then turned to head to the rear hall.","It was dark and damp here, with occasional water droplets falling, creating a pleasant sound.","“Guardian of the Tomb, may I have the honor of meeting you?” Li Miao called out.","But there was no response.","The woman from outside the hall followed him in and said, “Li Miao, my master has gone to Mangshan Country. She said that if you want to take Sister Yi away, you’ll have to get through me first!”","“Hehe...” Li Miao let out a strange laugh and slowly turned his head.","At this moment, his face had changed to a new one—a withered face with black blood flowing across it. Countless venomous insects crawled upon it. His face had no features, only wriggling insects.","The woman, who had been so confident with her sword moments before, turned pale with fright. Before she could react, she realized that Li Miao’s body had suddenly disintegrated into countless blood-red insects, like a blood mist, instantly engulfing her flesh.","...","In just one day, changes unfolded in various places, one after another.","Especially in Tai’an City, the situation had become incredibly complex.","But for Wei Jiuxian, everything was calm.","He finally had a moment to sweep the snow from his front door.","“Pass down the order: leave thirty thousand Imperial Guards to defend the imperial city. Six captains will be assigned to ensure the safety of the city walls and the interior. The rest will assemble outside the city!”","“Inform Desire King that the new emperor’s enthronement cannot be delayed!”","“Order Chang Feng to lead the vanguard troops to Mangshan Country to rendezvous with Number Ten. Someone there will tell him what to do!”","Standing at the threshold, Wei Jiuxian issued command after command. The dark figures behind him gradually disappeared.","Until only he remained.","By then, the sky had darkened.","Yet, in his eyes, there was light.","“For the sake of the Emperor...”","“For the Tang Dynasty, for the countless citizens, this world needs to be cleaned up!”","Buzz!","At that moment, Wei Jiuxian appeared like a heavenly deity descending to earth, radiating light. With a single move, he pushed back the darkness and strode towards Mangshan Country, bathed in brilliance.","As for Tai’an City, if they lost this battle, there would be no need for its continued existence. But if they won, it would shine even brighter.","At the same time, in Baoguang Temple, the three Buddha statues erupted with a burst of light.","Master Mingjue, who had been silently reciting Buddhist scriptures, suddenly opened his eyes.","“They’re here!”","He quickly stood up and walked straight towards the rear hall. Bowing respectfully to two of the statues within, he said, “Disciple Mingjue greets the Arhats Eradication and Annihilation!”","“Mingjue, why are you the only one here to greet us? Where are the others?” The two Arhats glared angrily, their expressions fierce and menacing.","This was in line with the Arhat status they had attained.","With hands clasped together, Mingjue explained, “All the warrior monks of Baoguang Temple have been borrowed by Wei Jiuxian. He is a key figure in this Tribulation, and the True Immortal has instructed that, aside from Patriarch Fanxin, everyone is to obey Wei Jiuxian’s commands!”","“Humph, the so-called True Immortal? He’s just someone who failed in his ascension. How dare he challenge Patriarch Fanxin?”","The two Arhats were full of disdain.","“You two don’t seem to respect my senior brother much!”","At that moment, another figure spoke. She had thick, green hair, and within her eyes lay a deep, indescribable killing intent.","In her presence, the two battle-hardened Arhats lost their luster.","Even Mingjue felt a deep unease. Compared to facing the two Arhats, he was more afraid of the green-haired woman before him.","She was the true master of slaughter.","“Immortal Fu Qingjian!”","In ancient times, she was a peerless sword immortal, renowned for her incredible might. She had slain over ten thousand gods in her time.","She hailed from the Upper Realm.","A supreme power from an ancient domain in the Upper Realm, she descended to this world because of the Divine Eye secret technique.","But once she descended to a lower world like this, her strength would be suppressed, and she would be bound by the laws of the heavens. Ascension would be nearly impossible unless a great opportunity presented itself.","Clearly, this sword immortal from the Upper Realm had missed the grand opportunity of ancient times, which was why she remained in the Red-Eyed World.","In this era of dwindling power, she chose to enter a deep slumber, only to be awakened by Patriarch Fanxin from the Northern Glacier and brought back to the Great Tang.","Her presence silenced the two battle-hardened Arhats.","Patriarch Fanxin was their master’s master, yet the ruthless woman before them was even more powerful than their master.","Seeing the two Arhats fall silent, Fu Qing continued, “It wasn’t my senior brother who awakened me; it must have been Fanxin. Where is he?”","“Master left Baoguang Temple in a hurry after meeting with two cultivators from the Jiang Kingdom. He mentioned that something significant would happen in Mangshan County soon and instructed me to assist Wei Jiuxian, along with the two Arhats, the True Immortal, and you, Immortal Fu Qingjian!”","Fu Qingjian frowned slightly. Her power was already limited, and every bit she used would deplete her reserves. She wouldn’t have chosen to awaken unless it was absolutely necessary.","Now that Fanxin wasn’t even here, and she had been summoned by a junior, she felt a surge of irritation.","She asked, “Where is Senior Brother Xinghai?”","“True Immortal Xinghai went to Mangshan County!” Mingjue answered truthfully.","Throughout the conversation, Mangshan County kept coming up.","Clearly, all the answers lay there!","Ignoring the others, Fu Qingjian clenched her hand, and her ethereal form solidified. She now wore the same white and green robe as her spiritual form, with a divine sword strapped to her back. Her aura was even more menacing than before.","Without wasting any words, she broke through the void, flying into the sky, identified her direction, and headed straight for Mangshan County.","The three remaining individuals looked at each other. Eradication Arhat was about to say something to regain some dignity when he sensed a disturbance coming from the Northern Glacier.","“That far away, and I can still sense it?” Eradication Arhat muttered. “Are those demon cultists doing...”","Before he could finish, he remembered that Patriarch Fanxin seemed to be at the Northern Glacier too, and his expression immediately became serious.","“Mingjue, you are responsible for guarding Baoguang Temple. Annihilation and I will head to Mangshan County!” With that, he solidified his form and broke through the void, leaving swiftly."]},{"number":6329,"title":"Chapter 6329: Gathering of Three","paragraphs":["Chapter 6329: Gathering of Three","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Mingjue stood before the temple gate, letting out a soft sigh.","His strength wasn’t sufficient. Although he was formidable among the Jindan cultivators, even achieving an invincible level within his rank, he still lacked the qualifications to participate in this great tribulation without reaching the Nascent Soul stage.","The winds of change were upon them.","Experts within Tai’an City began to move in a frenzy, rushing towards Mangshan County.","Even the common folk in the city sensed that something was amiss, as the army guarding the capital had already mobilized.","When immortals fight, it’s not just the immortals who suffer.","Although Mangshan County no longer housed mortals, the land still belonged to the Tang Empire.","So it had to be defended.","Even if immortals were battling there, they had to go.","After all, many from the Barbarian Lands and the Southern Seven Kingdoms had also gone, eager to annex the Tang Empire in one swift move.","Among the major forces, only the Barbarian Lands and the Southern Seven Kingdoms harbored such ambitions.","The ancient cultivators of the Northern Glacier, known to the Tang Empire as demon cultivators, had no interest in seizing territory. Most of them originated from the Tang Empire, and after accepting the inheritance of the Divine Eye, they remained in the Northern Glacier to cultivate.","By now, night had fully fallen. Mangshan County was engulfed in darkness, without a single light, resembling a primordial beast lurking outside the canyon.","Yet, deep within the canyon, the area was ablaze with light, as bright as day.","In the southeast direction, seventy-two warships hovered in mid-air above the mountain ridges, resembling a vast constellation, illuminating the peaks.","The two large factions, with their numerous members, were positioned very close to each other, and the atmosphere was thick with tension.","The lower-ranking experts were ready, their fists clenched, waiting for the command.","What they didn’t know was that the top experts from all the major forces had already gathered at the summit of the mountains.","A figure clad in luxurious robes, exuding a powerful aura and bearing a stern expression that commanded respect, stood at the forefront and spoke loudly, “Nantian Realm, Tianyang Sect Master, Hua Xuejian!”","“I, Zhang Xiansheng, represent the Northern Glacier!” The young man in a yellow Daoist robe merely raised his head slightly, appearing very modest.","With the leaders of the two great cultivation realms having spoken, a representative from the Barbarian Lands forces also stepped forward.","“Barbarian Lands, Qianzu Leader, Miao Renfeng,” the white-haired man, though appearing old, had a robust physique, with his chest bare and clad in beast skins that gave him a wild look. However, his tone was surprisingly gentle.","Strictly speaking, the Barbarian Lands didn’t count as part of the cultivation world. Their isolationist ways and refusal to acknowledge the practices of ancient Qi cultivators meant they were never truly part of the same path. Over time, as they abandoned ancient inheritances, their power gradually waned, leading to their exclusion to the Barbarian Lands territories. Most of them lived on the borders between the Eastern Lands and the Northern Glacier.","In ordinary times, orthodox cultivators would look down on these people.","But now, with everyone gathered together to face the entire Eastern Lands cultivation world, they naturally came together.","There was no idle chit-chat. They went straight to the point.","How to enter Mangshan County?","In truth, they had already arrived.","But no one had taken the first step into Mangshan County’s city, fearing an ambush.","Here is the translation:","—","An empty city!","No guards, no presence of any kind.","This surprised them greatly.","If it were just one faction coming, they might have taken the risk, but with three parties gathered together, who would take the lead became the critical question.","As the saying goes, “When three people walk together, one can be my teacher!”","This saying wasn’t wrong, and it had spread widely among many mortal worlds for a reason.","When people gathered, power formed!","Just like now, with three factions converging, each had its own calculations. And since the matter was of great importance, some had even waited for a thousand years.","At such a crucial moment, the first to bear the brunt of the attack would affect their chances in the subsequent struggle for the opportunity.","Thus, they were all conserving their strength, trying to manipulate the others into taking the lead.","However, the leaders of the three great factions had different thoughts.","They were the most anxious because it concerned their greatest interests.","What opportunities could those in the middle and lower ranks find here?","They were nothing more than cannon fodder.","But now, the three leaders had to make some symbolic gestures. If they recklessly charged in and only let one side’s subordinates die, they would lose face.","The most anxious were still the three leaders, so they gathered together to perform this public show.","Such things were most evident among mortals, but even among cultivators, while the effect was somewhat diminished, it still persisted.","Even if only one faction came, there would still be internal factions and conflicts.","In the end, everyone was fighting for themselves.","If there were a few hot-headed individuals, it would be a rare occurrence.","“Everyone, time is of the essence. We need to come up with a strategy quickly. Don’t forget, this is the Eastern Lands, this is the Great Tang, the strongest cultivation world in the Scarlet Eye Realm. I’m sure many of you come from the Great Tang and understand just how powerful its foundation is. The True Immortal from Baoguang Temple is rumored to be a peak Nascent Soul cultivator, and the guardian of Princess Tomb has always been a Nascent Soul stage cultivator!” Hua Xuejian from the Southern Heaven Realm spoke first.","He felt he should take the lead, after all, among the three factions, it was the Southern Heaven Realm that had the most to boast about.","Although the Northern Territory Glacier was an ancient relic, and its cultivators were known as inheritors, in the eyes of those from the Southern Heaven Realm and the Eastern Lands, they were nothing more than a group of demonic cultivator disciples.","Because ancient inheritance didn’t only mean the God Eye inheritance.","The God Eye inheritance was extremely harsh; many cultivators couldn’t even pass the most basic Black Eye inheritance. So, many who went to the Northern Territory Glacier, after losing hope, would go to other relics to try their luck.","The main focus of the ancient inheritance was the God Eye inheritance, but those who became super-powerful through it would leave behind their own inheritance grounds before ascending.","In its heyday, thousands of immortals ascended.","Their inheritances fell into the Northern Territory Glacier like raindrops.","Therefore, many cultivators inherited from the ancient cultivators and became known as inheritors.","But among these inheritances, demonic cultivators were the most numerous.","Because the requirements were low, many accepted the inheritance of demonic cultivators.","That’s why they were called demonic cultivator disciples by the outside world.","Calling them disciples was even a compliment; in such a grand setting, being polite meant referring to them as cultivators of the Holy Sect.","If things turned ugly or they were mentioned behind their backs, they would be cursed as demonic cultivators.","Of course, even the proud geniuses who could accept the God Eye inheritance were also cursed, but those who reached such heights didn’t care about the opinions of the outside world.","Now, with Hua Xuejian from the Southern Heaven Realm speaking up and showcasing the righteousness of his sect, it was a normal move.","As for Miao Renfeng from the Savage Barbarians, he was hardly worth mentioning, so naturally, he had nothing to say. Instead, he was eager to hear what this righteous leader from the Southern Heaven Realm had in mind.","In his understanding, the more righteous a cultivator claimed to be, the more devious their schemes, and they could still speak with great righteousness.","Zhang Xiansheng from the Northern Territory Glacier, on the other hand, was more pragmatic. He didn’t care about Hua Xuejian’s leadership demeanor; what mattered to him was how things would proceed now.","So after hearing Hua Xuejian’s empty words, he immediately retorted, “Baoguang Temple and Princess Tomb won’t easily involve themselves. Even if they do, these two can’t stop the forces of our three factions!”"]},{"number":6330,"title":"Chapter 6330: The Light of Righteousness","paragraphs":["Chapter 6330: The Light of Righteousness","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“You’re right!”","Hua Xuejian waved his hand and then arrogantly declared, “In Baoguang Temple, it’s nothing more than a Luohan, or perhaps a true immortal, or maybe just the spirit keeper of the Princess Tomb. These are all minor issues. Besides, this time we’ve come to uphold the righteous path.","Within Mangshan County lies a vast amount of death energy, so much so that even ordinary people can sense the endless resentment hidden within it. Clearly, demonic cultivators have emerged within the Tang Empire. It is our duty to eradicate these demonic cultivators. Even if the entire Tang Empire falls into demonic ways, I, Hua Xuejian, will wipe out the entire Tang Empire if I must!”","This lengthy speech was delivered with such passion that Hua Xuejian almost painted himself as a saint.","Miao Renfeng could hardly suppress his laughter. Wasn’t the most infamous demonic cult in the outside world the one from the Northern Region’s glacier?","He glanced at Zhang Xiansheng, whose expression remained unchanged, though a trace of anxiety still lingered between his brows.","Hua Xuejian began to employ the tactics he used in the Southern Sky Realm, starting by addressing Zhang Xiansheng. “I’m glad that the Northern Region’s glacier could join us this time. I’ve thoroughly investigated that demonic cult; it has some connections with your Northern Region’s glacier. So this time, you might consider it as cleaning up your own house.","I’m someone who values boundaries and usually doesn’t interfere in others’ affairs. But this time, the Chiyang Sect’s actions have been too egregious. Rumor has it that the Chiyang Sect harbors a devastating weapon capable of threatening the entire cultivation world. We, the Southern Sky Realm, must intervene and eliminate this sect!”","“Ahem, ahem! Alliance Master Hua, you’re most righteous. With the three of us united, eliminating the Chiyang Sect is certainly not an issue. The key point is that this is their territory. On the surface, everything seems calm, but who knows what dangers lie within? The most pressing matter now is to gather the strongest from all three sides and storm Mangshan County’s capital together!”","Miao Renfeng couldn’t bear the conversation’s direction any longer. If they kept talking, they wouldn’t reach a conclusion before dawn, so he redirected the discussion back on track.","Seeing the conversation finally hit the critical point, Zhang Xiansheng nodded and said, “Indeed, given the current situation, relying on one side alone isn’t enough. We need to unite and first enter Mangshan County to investigate.”","Noticing the anxious expressions on their faces, Hua Xuejian first showed a trace of worry, then looked at the two of them and asked, “Do you two have any brilliant ideas?”","The sudden shift in attitude caught Zhang Xiansheng and Miao Renfeng off guard. However, since the discussion was finally moving forward, they didn’t dwell on it and quickly presented a comprehensive strategy.","The strategy was simple.","Each of the three factions would send five late-stage Golden Core cultivators to lead the charge!","The second wave would consist of a Nascent Soul cultivator from each faction to reinforce the frontlines.","The third wave would involve dispatching thirty Golden Core cultivators and three hundred innate martial artists from each side.","Since the Northern Region’s glacier didn’t bring any innate martial artists, they would compensate by sending more Golden Core cultivators, with each counting as ten innate martial artists.","This plan was straightforward and wouldn’t cause any dissatisfaction among the three factions.","But internally, things weren’t so clear-cut.","Each faction had its own complex internal issues, and if they got entangled, resolving them could take a long time.","Replicating this plan perfectly would be impossible.","For example, among the many tribes in the wildlands, some only had two or three Golden Core cultivators, while others had dozens.","How should that be calculated?","Should the smaller tribes send one person, and the larger ones send two?","Surely, someone would be unhappy. This was where a strong and capable leader was needed to mediate the situation!","Miao Renfeng had no issues with the plan, especially since much of it was his own suggestion. Now, he was more concerned about the internal problems.","So, after the three of them finalized the decision, they each returned to notify their respective tribes or sects and discuss sending out powerful individuals.","In the canyon, on the way back, Miao Renfeng glanced at Hua Xuejian and wondered to himself, “This person loves the spotlight so much, yet he didn’t say a word about the plan?”","His curiosity quickly faded, and now he had to worry about how to explain this to his own people.","In the sky, aboard the largest warship.","Hua Xuejian returned to the grand hall inside, feeling quite satisfied.","He was very pleased with the three-way discussion that had just taken place.","On the surface, he had taken charge, but he intentionally held back when it came to the plan, not participating at all.","The reason was simple—this was something even a child could come up with. Why should he be the one to state it?","It wouldn’t benefit him in any way and might make others think he was simple-minded.","So, he deliberately let Zhang Xiansheng and Miao Renfeng present the idea.","That way, he could avoid internal issues.","Since the plan came from them, if anyone had complaints, they could go to Zhang Xiansheng and Miao Renfeng. It had nothing to do with him!","Most importantly, being labeled as someone who sends others to die on dangerous missions wasn’t a reputation he wanted. He wasn’t going to wear that hat.","Sure, he could dress up the idea of sending people to their deaths in grand, noble language, but deep down, who knows how others might be cursing him!","So, he avoided doing anything that was thankless and unrewarding.","He then revealed everything, streamlining what he had said earlier, and presented the plan proposed by Miao Renfeng and Zhang Xiansheng.","The hall immediately fell silent.","In the Southern Heaven Realm, there were nine sects, large and small.","Among them, Tianyang Sect, where Zhang Xianzong was from, was the most powerful, with over a hundred Golden Core cultivators and three Nascent Soul cultivators, including Zhang himself.","The other sects were somewhat weaker.","The only one that could compare to Tianyang Sect was Giant Sword Sect, which had two Nascent Soul cultivators. One of them, known as “Giant Sword King Lan,” was reputed to be the second strongest cultivator in the Southern Heaven.","His strength had reached the peak of the Nascent Soul mid-stage.","He was a powerhouse who could even challenge late-stage Nascent Soul cultivators.","Aside from that, each of the other seven sects had only one Nascent Soul cultivator, and their Golden Core disciples numbered only in the dozens, with the smallest sects having just over ten.","The combined strength of the nine sects wasn’t much, and in terms of quality, they couldn’t compare with the Northern Territory Glaciers. Their combat power might not even match that of the Barbarian Tribes.","“Since the alliance leader has brought back a plan, let’s discuss it!” Wang Lan, who was always blunt, spoke up first, his words tinged with mockery toward Hua Xuejian.","He raised an eyebrow slightly, glanced at everyone present, and said, “Actually, there’s not much to discuss. I think this plan is quite good; it suits me well. Since each of the three factions will send out cultivators, the number from our Southern Heaven Realm isn’t that many. I have a suggestion that everyone can consider.","For the first tier, five Golden Core cultivators: three from the nine sects and two from the unaffiliated cultivators. For the second tier, I’ll personally take command. For the third tier, the nine sects will send twenty Golden Core cultivators, and the unaffiliated cultivators will send ten. As for the remaining innate martial artists, I don’t think it’s necessary to divide them. We have enough people this time, so we can draw lots to decide. Who agrees? Who opposes?”","As soon as he finished speaking, the powerful cultivators of the nine sects all nodded in agreement.","However, the unaffiliated cultivators were put in a difficult position.","Resources in the Southern Heaven Realm were tightly controlled, and the path of an unaffiliated cultivator was already hard enough."]},{"number":6331,"title":"Chapter 6331: Cultivators of Our Generation Should Be Self-Strong","paragraphs":["Chapter 6331: Cultivators of Our Generation Should Be Self-Strong","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The entire group of rogue cultivators didn’t have a single cultivator at the Infant Transformation stage, so they were all overlooked. Good opportunities never came their way, but trouble always found them first.","The worst part was that they had no right to object.","Inside the hall, there were thirteen chairs.","Twelve of them were occupied by Infant Transformation stage cultivators, while the last one seated a Golden Core Perfection cultivator, the rogue cultivator representative, Chu Xiu.","Although he frowned, deep down, he was willing to accept this arrangement.","Since he was a rogue cultivator and also their representative, naturally, he wouldn’t go himself. He only needed to struggle a bit to secure some benefits for his group.","Many rogue cultivators relied on him, and he, in turn, relied on those behind him.","It was a cooperative relationship.","Now that the difficult decision was upon him, he wouldn’t bear the burden alone.","With a thought, he began discussing strategies with several dozen Golden Core stage rogue cultivators.","In the end, they chose to draw lots.","Chu Xiu naturally wouldn’t participate in the drawing, but he still had to set an example. He decided to personally lead the third group.","The two unlucky ones who drew the first group were both early Golden Core stage cultivators, weak with no treasures. Their faces were grim, but there was also a hint of excitement—if there was a great opportunity inside, they would be the first to benefit.","The rogue cultivator camp had already selected their participants in batches.","Now, it was the turn of the nine great sects.","Deciding how to allocate the slots was far more complicated than it had been for the rogue cultivators.","In the end, following Hua Xuejian’s suggestion, each sect sent the same number of people.","No one could complain about being at a disadvantage; they could only blame their sect’s lack of strong cultivators.","The Giant Sword Sect didn’t send any Golden Core stage cultivators because Wang Lan was in the second group, and that was already risky enough.","No one dared to raise any objections—after all, the life of an Infant Transformation stage cultivator was worth a hundred times more than that of a Golden Core stage cultivator.","Among the nine great sects, seven had only one Infant Transformation stage cultivator, and none of them dared to take this risk.","But the exceptionally powerful Wang Lan dared to take the risk!","He was only one step away from reaching the late stage of the Infant Transformation, and more importantly, he had once obtained the Black Eye inheritance from the God Eye lineage. His combat strength among peers was formidable. Once he stepped into the late stage of the Infant Transformation, he would be no weaker than Hua Xuejian. Therefore, he wanted to take a gamble, especially since the danger wasn’t that great.","The greatest danger lay in the first group.","Among the selected cultivators, no one dared to take the first group.","As for the sects, as long as one person volunteered for the first group, they could choose not to send anyone for the third group.","Faced with this temptation, several weaker sects ultimately pushed forward a few Golden Core stage cultivators who were unafraid of death.","These three were all strong and shared one common trait—they had been stuck at the Golden Core stage for too long.","“Since the participants have been chosen, let’s set off!” Hua Xuejian’s tone was serious as he glanced at the group. “This time, you represent the Southern Sky Realm. Make sure you give your best effort. Don’t be afraid when you face danger. Remember, you still have your sects and families to protect. It is our duty as cultivators to exterminate demons and uphold the Dao!”","“Exterminate evil, uphold the Dao!”","Hua Xuejian nodded in satisfaction. With a flick of her elegant robe, she gathered everyone and left the warship.","When she reappeared, the other two factions had already selected their members.","The internal workings of the Northern Domain Glacier were not complicated. They were all pure cultivators. They could take risks as long as the rewards were plentiful, without much concern for other matters.","It was unlike the cultivators of the Southern Heavenly Realm, who had concerns about their sects, disciples, families, and clans.","They no longer resembled cultivators but rather a privileged class.","As for the Barbarian Lands, things were much simpler. Although there were many internal tribes, the plan provided by Miaoren Peak left no room for dissent. It was the simplest method—drawing lots.","Everyone drew lots, and whoever drew the short straw went.","Of course, some reckless souls who feared nothing fought for the first wave, making the process even simpler.","“Everyone is here, so let’s begin!”","The three of them simultaneously nodded in agreement and signaled their subordinates to secretly implement the predetermined plan.","The first wave consisted of fifteen Golden Core cultivators. Using treasures that masked their auras, they silently advanced towards Mangshan County City.","The second wave consisted of three Nascent Soul cultivators. They also used similar treasures to conceal their auras, following closely behind the first wave.","The third wave wasn’t as fortunate. However, they didn’t face much danger either, so they didn’t bother hiding their auras. They simply kept a fifty-mile distance from Mangshan County City.","Mangshan County City.","The entire city was eerily silent, without a single sound.","But as soon as the fifteen Golden Core cultivators entered, the colossal beast that lay dormant in the darkness seemed to awaken!","“Heh heh...”","“These fools sent only a few Golden Core cultivators to their deaths!” A figure on the city wall chuckled bitterly and shook his head.","Behind him stood several others.","One of them, a woman from a different tribe, asked anxiously, “These are the strong warriors of our Barbarian Lands. Why are there so few of them?”","“Just over a dozen Golden Core cultivators—is this supposed to represent the entire strength of the cultivation world?”","“No, these people are merely here to test the waters. But they’re in for a miserable fate!”","These people were none other than Jian Wushuang and his companions.","They had arrived in Mangshan County City long ago and had already entered the city.","With Jian Wushuang’s Thought power masking their presence, it was difficult even for a God Appearance Realm expert to detect them.","So they didn’t have many concerns.","When they first entered the city, just as Yang Xiao had described, the city was empty. During the day, they scoured the entire Mangshan County City but couldn’t find the so-called altar.","They had been told it was an underground altar, but they couldn’t exactly dig up the entire city!","Just as they grew anxious, night fell.","It was then that they discovered the entire city was filled with vengeful spirits, malevolent ghosts formed from resentment.","These spirits were not weak either. They devoured each other, gradually growing stronger.","They even encountered a ghost cultivator at the Nascent Soul stage, one that had developed intelligence.","Witnessing this scene, Jian Wushuang decided to act during the night. He realized that these malevolent ghosts kept emerging, likely tied to the altar. Perhaps the altar’s deathly aura had transformed into these evil spirits, allowing them to continually spawn.","But after searching for a long time, they still couldn’t find the altar. They eventually went to the city wall to closely observe the transformation of the ghosts into ghost cultivators. It was during this observation that Jian Wushuang noticed something peculiar.","“These malevolent ghosts and spirits devour each other and evolve, eventually becoming ghost cultivators. Starting from the Golden Core stage, they evolve further. Based on the current number of ghost cultivators in the city, three Nascent Soul peak ghost commanders could emerge!”","This term, ghost commander, was coined due to the mark on the ghost cultivators’ chests.","Innate martial artists corresponded to ghost soldiers.","Golden Core cultivators corresponded to ghost generals.","Nascent Soul cultivators corresponded to ghost commanders.","As for the malevolent and evil spirits that hadn’t evolved, they were at the postnatal level.","However, postnatal martial artists were powerless against such malevolent ghosts. The ultimate attack against them was a soul-destroying strike, which manifested as a mental assault.","In higher-level terms, it was a soul attack.","Therefore, dealing with these malevolent ghosts and ghost cultivators required at least an innate martial artist.","And consciousness and thought power were Jian Wushuang’s strengths at the moment.","So he wasn’t in a hurry, but the cultivators outside were in for a terrible time."]},{"number":6332,"title":"Chapter 6332: Death of the Imperial Consort","paragraphs":["Chapter 6332: Death of the Imperial Consort","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang remained vigilant, observing the situation unfolding before him. In each of the five regions within the city—southeast, southwest, northeast, northwest, and central—there were Ghost Commanders. The Ghost Generals were even more numerous, with each region having hundreds of them.","Sending just a dozen Golden Core stage cultivators would be futile. Once they entered, they would be overwhelmed in no time.","Jian Wushuang did not consider the people outside as true opponents. His concern lay in understanding why this situation had arisen in the first place.","The underground altar was sealed with power from a thousand years ago, belonging to the Divine Image Realm.","And these fierce ghosts appeared to be a part of a blood sacrifice!","He recalled their journey toward Tai’an City, where they encountered numerous corpses, and in the fishing village, he had personally witnessed the dark cultivators performing blood sacrifices on mortals.","This was undoubtedly the work of the Chiyang Sect, and the mastermind behind it was none other than the Tang Emperor.","Jian Wushuang was unaware that the current Tang Emperor had already been exiled by the Li family. If not for preserving the royal family’s reputation, he would have been executed long ago.","“The underground altar... it’s probably not as simple as it seems!”","With his vast knowledge, Jian Wushuang could tell that these evolved fierce ghosts were likely being cultivated to form a perfect Three Souls and Six Spirits.","Once perfected, just a sliver of thought power would be needed to control this flawless soul. If combined with a strong physical body, it would result in a perfect resurrection!","However, such a resurrection required a trace of thought power from the one being revived.","There were countless methods to preserve thought power, and Jian Wushuang knew of over ten thousand of them. However, only a few could manifest in the mortal world.","It wasn’t surprising that in the Crimson Eye Realm, there might be treasures or secret techniques capable of preserving thought power.","“Are they trying to resurrect someone? Or are they intending to devour the perfect soul to enhance their own?”","The latter seemed too wasteful, while the former seemed more plausible.","But who would they want to resurrect?","The Empress?","A thought flashed through Jian Wushuang’s mind, recalling the imperial decree he had heard about during his visit to the First Pavilion.","As he pondered this, he glanced over at Chen Yuan, intending to ask if he knew anything about the matter.","However, when Jian Wushuang looked at him, he noticed that Chen Yuan seemed lost in thought, with a tear streaking down his cheek.","This surprised Jian Wushuang. The last time he had seen Chen Yuan cry was when he had told him about A’Zi.","Who could he be grieving for now?","Jian Wushuang walked over and patted Chen Yuan’s shoulder, asking with concern, “What’s wrong?”","“Ah, it’s nothing!” Chen Yuan’s body trembled slightly, and he forced himself to suppress his emotions. As he replied, he even managed to muster a faint smile.","Anyone with keen eyes could see that Chen Yuan was troubled, and it seemed to be related to the malevolent spirits within the city.","However, Jian Wushuang was more interested in knowing whether the Empress had any connection to this place. Thus, he didn’t dwell too much on why Chen Yuan seemed so sorrowful.","Hearing Jian Wushuang’s question, Chen Yuan’s face turned pale.","“If it’s hard for you to talk about, I can block them out,” Jian Wushuang offered, his tone appearing concerned, but also making it clear that Chen Yuan needed to say something.","Chen Yuan was deeply conflicted because this matter had become a heart demon for him, just like the death of A’Zi.","However, when he saw the city full of vengeful spirits, he thought, what did his heart demon matter compared to the lives of billions?","“No need to hide it; this can’t be kept a secret for long anyway,” Chen Yuan said with a bitter smile, shaking his head.","When the others heard this, they all perked up and looked at him with curious eyes.","Xiang Yang squinted his eyes and teased, “What is it? Don’t tell me all the vengeful spirits in this city are your doing?”","“Almost,” Chen Yuan responded calmly, and everyone gasped in shock.","Even Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but frown, using his Thought power to carefully observe Chen Yuan again and again, only to find that the other man had no demonic aura, not even a trace of evil energy.","There was only a faint aura of karma.","“What nonsense are you talking about?”","Chen Yuan, however, shook his head and said, “I’m not lying. Everything here is because of me. In fact, A’Zi’s death is also entirely my fault. It’s my retribution!”","As he spoke, he suddenly spat out a mouthful of blood. Jian Wushuang feared he might die from sudden shock, so he quickly used his power to clear Chen Yuan’s meridians.","“I shouldn’t have been so greedy, I shouldn’t have been so greedy!” Chen Yuan steadied himself, but tears streamed down his face.","This scene left everyone utterly bewildered.","But once Chen Yuan revealed the truth, they suddenly understood.","Yet some were driven to fury because of it.","Yang Xiao was one of them.","He charged directly at Chen Yuan, grabbing him by the collar and roaring in anger, “It was you who killed Empress Yi! How dare you commit such a treasonous act!!!”","“It’s not his fault!” Jian Wushuang waved his hand, using Thought power to separate the two of them.","If anyone was to blame, it was Emperor Tang, Li Miao.","Empress Yi was merely a pawn being used.","But this was a knot in Chen Yuan’s heart, as well as a knot in the hearts of the Zhanxian Guards.","The former number one beauty of the Tang Dynasty had perished because of an attack by the Yi King.","The Zhanxian Guards had borne three years of infamy.","Failing to protect the Empress was also a source of deep guilt for the loyal Zhanxian Guards like Yang Xiao, who were devoted to the Tang Dynasty.","Now, Chen Yuan was telling them that he had been the one to kill Empress Yi.","This story was a long one.","It was the tale of a scholar who had failed the imperial exam and had no face to return home.","Chen Yuan had not become the top scholar at all. After arriving in the capital, he failed the very first exam, but he was unwilling to give up. Even though he had no money, he stayed in Tai’an City, living alone in a ruined temple outside the city.","Then came a turning point.","The Yi King launched an attack, and Emperor Tang fled from Tai’an City.","Along the way, they unexpectedly ended up seeking refuge in the ruined temple.","That night, only four people knew what happened in the temple.","Emperor Tang, Duke Han, Chen Yuan, and Empress Yi.","The so-called attack by the Yi King was nothing more than an earth-shattering conspiracy.","The Yi King did not seek the throne but rather the Empress.","As for why he desired the Empress, Chen Yuan did not know.","However, at the time, the Yi King was very powerful, with a terrifying force by his side that could suppress the Zhanxian Guards.","Emperor Tang could only flee.","He was afraid.","Afraid that the Yi King would take the Empress, yet he could not bring himself to kill her.","At that moment, he encountered the poor scholar, Chen Yuan, and hinted that he should kill Empress Yi, letting the Yi King bear the infamy.","If he did the deed, he would enjoy all the riches and honors.","At this point, Jian Wushuang’s eyes lit up.","Chen Yuan was just a poor scholar with no background whatsoever.","If he had killed Empress Yi, he would surely have been silenced—how could they have allowed Chen Yuan, who knew the truth, to live?","It made sense to spare Duke Han, as he was an old eunuch who had served the Tang Emperors loyally for hundreds of years and was unlikely to be silenced. Moreover, Emperor Tang had no power to silence him, as he himself was barely surviving at that time.","But killing someone like Chen Yuan would have been as easy as blowing out a candle. Why hadn’t they silenced him?","This led to the involvement of a certain secret method.","Chen Yuan had killed Empress Yi, but Emperor Tang had prepared in advance, preserving a trace of the Empress’s Thought power.","Even if her physical body was gone and her soul had scattered, with that trace of Thought power, a particular memory of the Empress could be revived.","As for her physical body, as long as it was well-preserved, it could still be used for three years.","However, this method of resurrection had one requirement..."]},{"number":6333,"title":"Chapter 6333: What a Ruthless Heart","paragraphs":["Chapter 6333: What a Ruthless Heart","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang gradually understood everything, and the corners of his mouth slightly curled up. He didn’t hide anything and directly revealed the true intentions of Emperor Tang, Li Miao.","It wasn’t just about comforting Chen Yuan; it was about making them understand that the entire city filled with vengeful spirits was for the sake of the empress alone.","Jian Wushuang didn’t believe that Li Miao went to such great lengths simply to resurrect the empress. The empress, if revived, must have a greater purpose, which made him spare no effort to bring her back.","Everyone was shocked by his speculation!","“What a ruthless mind, what cruel methods!” Yang Xiao’s face showed fear.","This was the first time he was truly scared!","Even more so than when he was being hunted by nine late-stage Golden Core cultivators.","Xiang Yang couldn’t help but frown, trembling as he spoke, “To calculate everything so precisely, even predicting that Chen Yuan would appear in Mangshan County—this might not just be the emperor’s doing, right?”","“Your Tang Empire’s emperors, none of them are good people!” Qianzu Saintess didn’t miss the chance to mock.","She usually didn’t care much about the internal affairs of the Tang Empire, but after hearing such a terrifying scheme, she couldn’t help but feel a chill down her spine.","Jian Wushuang remained calm. To him, it was merely a method to grow stronger.","In the mundane world, such tactics were considered brilliant, a normal approach for a skilled strategist.","In terms of advanced methods, he had seen far too many to be surprised, only curious about what made the empress so special.","Could it be that she could help someone ascend?","In the Crimson Eyes Realm, that might be the only thing that could fascinate people so much!","“News just came in from Zhanxian Tower—something major has happened in Tai’an City, the Tang Emperor has been deposed!!!!”","Yang Xiao received the internal news from the Zhanxian Guard and exclaimed in shock.","But this matter was no longer important.","Whether deposed or not, the other side was still a Nascent Soul stage cultivator.","Moreover, there were powerful figures with great abilities behind him, assisting with the planning and schemes.","“Has Wei Jiuxian arrived as well?”","Yang Xiao nodded, saying, “The Grand Commander personally led the army and has already reached Mangshan County; they are not far from the county city!”","“Tell him not to send mortals to their deaths. He should come alone!” Jian Wushuang warned.","Wei Jiuxian certainly knew more, and Jian Wushuang wanted to gather some information from him.","“No, the Grand Commander will not come to the County City!” Yang Xiao shook his head and sighed. “The Grand Commander is leading the army, most likely to intimidate the Barbarian Lands and the cultivators of the Southern Sky Realm!”","“Is he really not interested in this place at all?” Xiang Yang asked in surprise.","Yang Xiao nodded. “Yes, the Grand Commander is concerned with the welfare of the world. He has no interest in ascension, which is also why the Tang Emperor targets him!”","“What a pity!” Jian Wushuang sighed slightly.","Insignificant characters didn’t matter whether they came or not.","For now, finding the altar was the most pressing matter.","While they were conversing, the second wave of forces from the three factions entered the County City.","The first group had almost all perished, encountering a Ghost Commander within less than a hundred feet of the city. Unfortunately, it was a mid-stage Ghost Commander, which spelled bad luck for them.","They leisurely stood on the city walls, watching the battle.","The rest were not so fortunate.","The three Nascent Soul cultivators of the second wave were dumbfounded by the scene before them as soon as they entered the city.","Even Wang Lan was no exception.","Penetrating deep into the County City seemed impossible unless all three factions entered together, paving a path of blood. Otherwise, relying solely on individual strength would only allow those at the Divine Aspect level to move freely in and out.","“Retreat!”","Wang Lan had no intention of delving deeper. As for the cultivators of the first wave, he couldn’t be bothered with them. Since they weren’t from his sect, he turned around and left.","The other two Nascent Soul cultivators shared the same sentiment. Staying would serve no purpose and could lead to being dragged down by the powerful ghost cultivators.","They immediately withdrew from the County City.","They also called back the third wave, as sending them in would only mean certain death.","They had gathered some information about the situation inside Mangshan County City.","Fifty miles away, in a massive ancient fortress, the Nascent Soul cultivators of the three major alliances had gathered, along with a few Golden Core cultivators.","“Is the entire County City filled with ghost cultivators?”","Upon hearing this news, everyone’s first reaction was disbelief.","They hadn’t sensed anything from outside the city, which explained why the first wave had been so silent.","It must have been a barrier that blocked everything.","“This is going to be difficult. A city full of ghost cultivators, with quite a few at the Nascent Soul level. If we risk entering, the losses will be incalculable!”","The first to feel the headache was Miao Renfeng. His forces from the Barbarian Lands were numerous, and most of the powerful cultivators had gathered outside Mangshan County City. Even in the Southern Sky Realm, many innate experts were outside Mangshan County.","If a siege occurred, they would be at a disadvantage.","“Ghost cultivators?” He muttered to himself and quickly came up with an idea. He immediately suggested, “Since they’re ghost cultivators, ordinary innate warriors won’t be of any use. I suggest gathering all cultivators above the Golden Core stage to storm the city. We may not be able to kill all the ghost cultivators, but at least we can find the main hall of the Chiyang Sect. Once we kill the key figures, the remaining ghost cultivators can be dealt with at our leisure.”","He had grasped the essence of Hua Xuejian’s plan, speaking without leaving any loopholes.","Hua Xuejian wasn’t upset that his idea had been taken. Instead, he smiled and said, “Chief Miao’s suggestion is excellent. The most important thing now is to find the main hall of the Demon Sect so we can eliminate them in one fell swoop. Since they are ghost cultivators, only Golden Core stage cultivators and above can deal with them. I support this proposal!”","With two of them in agreement, it was down to Zhang Xiansheng.","He had no reason to refuse.","Charging in together was the best option, saving them from internal strife.","“I agree as well!”","With all three in accord, the message was spread.","An incense stick later, all the strong cultivators gathered to storm the city together!","The call: Eliminate demons and protect the Dao!","The barbarian war horns sounded, signaling the charge. Over a thousand Golden Core cultivators gathered in three groups, advancing in unison.","Such a vast force of cultivators was the last remnant of ancient glory.","Dozens of Nascent Soul cultivators also gathered.","Over a thousand Golden Core cultivators moved together toward Mangshan County City.","As they entered, another horn echoed.","Wei Jiuxian had arrived!","He led his thousand-strong army into battle.","Besides Wei Jiuxian, Chang Feng led another army to the coastal Southern Sky County.","With the powerful cultivators on both sides absent, it was a slaughter feast.","Blood stained the ground red.","Although the warriors of the Barbarian Lands were brave and skilled in battle, they couldn’t withstand the precision strikes of the Zhanxian Guards.","Any innate warrior with significant strength was instantly killed.","The rest were trampled by the overwhelming tide of the army."]},{"number":6334,"title":"Chapter 6334: One for One","paragraphs":["Chapter 6334: One for One","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Together with the war beasts, they were ground into a pulp.","This battle had no suspense; it was won decisively, fought with precision, and retreated swiftly.","Wei Jiuxian stayed behind with the Zhanxian Guards.","Inside the ancient fortress where the three forces had gathered earlier.","“Commander, the situation by the coast has also been resolved. Lord Changfeng will be here shortly!”","Dressed in spotless white, Wei Jiuxian sat in the seat where Hua Xuejian had previously been. He nodded calmly, as if the earlier slaughter had not stirred him in the slightest.","“Have the Ten Attendants been gathered?”","A shadowy figure replied truthfully, “Number Ten is with Lord Changfeng, and the others are outside waiting for orders!”","“Good, very good!”","Wei Jiuxian nodded in satisfaction.","Today’s battle had pleased him greatly.","He had taken the opportunity to eliminate the threats from the Southern Heavenly Realm and the Barbarian Lands.","As for Mangshan County, that place was a slaughterhouse!","No matter how many people were sent, it would never be enough.","Now, they could only wait—for the true mastermind to reveal themselves.","His task was already half done.","He had defended the Tang Empire, as he was supposed to.","The remaining half involved cleaning up internal affairs.","At that moment, a report came from outside: a powerful presence was approaching.","Before the words had even been fully spoken, that presence had already arrived.","It was a woman dressed in white and green robes, exuding an incredibly cold aura. On her back was a divine sword brimming with immense power.","Wei Jiuxian was slightly surprised when he saw her.","He didn’t know this person!","But judging by her aura, she was far stronger than the Nascent Soul cultivators he had encountered before.","She was most likely a grand cultivator at the Divine Transformation level.","Yet, Wei Jiuxian remained calm, showing no fear.","He asked plainly, “What brings you here?”","“You are quite powerful. Despite seeing me, you have managed to remain calm. That’s rare!” The cold woman unexpectedly praised Wei Jiuxian as she spoke.","This left Wei Jiuxian even more perplexed. After pondering, he thought of Baoguang Temple.","If there were two most mysterious places in the Chimu Realm, the first would be the Northern Glacier, and the second would be Baoguang Temple.","Because Baoguang Temple had a true immortal!","Furthermore, it was widely rumored that the master who founded Baoguang Temple, Fanxin, was a Huaying stage cultivator. But in Wei Jiuxian’s view, this was not the case; the other party was definitely a Shenxiang stage cultivator.","Otherwise, how could he have sealed another Shenxiang stage great cultivator over a thousand years ago?","Moreover, the sealed Shenxiang stage cultivator came from the Qianzu tribe, with strength that had already reached the peak of the Shenxiang stage, just one step away from shattering the void.","Being able to seal such a person meant that this Tang Dynasty son-in-law likely already possessed the strength to shatter the void.","And the woman before him probably knew that master, Fanxin.","“Your praise is too much!” Wei Jiuxian responded with a faint smile.","The cold woman, however, rarely smiled and said, “You remind me of someone I once knew. I was going to search your soul, but now I’ve changed my mind!”","“Oh?” Wei Jiuxian’s lips curved into a smile as he said, “Although I haven’t reached the Shenxiang stage, I have some confidence. Below Shenxiang, I am invincible; above Shenxiang, it’s a one-for-one exchange!”","“Now that you’ve said that, you resemble him even more!” The cold woman finished speaking, her eyes suddenly flashing, and a sharp sword gaze burst forth.","The sudden and terrifying sword energy didn’t make Wei Jiuxian panic. He simply waved his hand, dispersing the sword energy.","Yet in his heart, he was deeply shocked. Just a glance had made his arm numb.","If they truly fought, he might not last three moves under her hand.","However, he had a trump card, and the one-for-one exchange at the Shenxiang stage was not just empty talk.","But this trump card wasn’t something he could easily use.","“Your strength is impressive, but you’re still a bit short of trading lives with a Shenxiang stage cultivator!” The cold woman finished speaking and turned to leave.","At that moment, Wei Jiuxian stood up and asked, “May I know your name?”","“Fu Qing!”","The cold woman spoke her name, then directly broke through the air and headed straight for Mangshan County.","Wei Jiuxian chased to the entrance of the ancient castle, looking toward Mangshan County, when two more powerful auras flashed across the sky.","“The two Arhats have arrived!”","He wasn’t surprised by this, as he had expected it.","The Tang Dynasty still had some trump cards, and he intended to make good use of them.","One person alone couldn’t sweep away this ancient snow.","“Fanxin, you should be arriving soon!” Wei Jiuxian’s eyes flashed as he gazed northward.","Northern Glacier!","The wind was biting, and this place was extremely unsuitable for mortal habitation, but it was a paradise for cultivators!","Because ancient glory was buried here.","The scene of ten thousand immortals ascending seemed like it happened just yesterday.","The perpetual snow had buried that glory beneath the glacier.","In this white world, a black-clad figure stood out sharply. His face was haggard, but his eyes shone with a piercing light.","“More than a thousand years... It’s enough. It’s worth it!”","He took a step forward, directly ascending the ten-thousand-feet ice mountain.","This was the extreme north of the Northern Glacier, the highest point in the world.","From here, he looked down upon the entire Red Eyes Realm.","“Fanxin, worldly desires be gone!”","The haggard monk clasped his hands together, silently reciting a Buddhist scripture. Golden light burst forth behind him.","A surge of power erupted from the mountaintop, and countless rays of golden light shot into the white glacier.","As the light pierced the glacier, it caused a massive tremor.","Under the illumination of the Buddha’s light, the silence of ten thousand years in this place was shattered.","Countless cave dwellings collapsed within the glacier, and many cultivators in seclusion were startled awake. They hurriedly left their crumbling abodes and soared into the sky. Upon seeing the scene below, they all showed expressions of terror.","“Who is it? Who dares to destroy the Heavenly Mountain? Are they tired of living?”","“Damn it! I’ve been in seclusion for a thousand years, just grasping the mystery of breaking through to the Shenxiang stage. Who disturbed me?”","Most of these wandering cultivators, who had been in seclusion for many years, didn’t head to Mangshan County. There weren’t many of them, but their strength wasn’t weak. Each one was a Huaying stage cultivator.","At that moment, they all looked toward the towering ice mountain and the golden light!","“Look, it’s Buddha’s light!”","Above the sky, the black-clad monk paid no attention to the wandering cultivators of the Northern Glacier. Instead, he silently closed his eyes.","In the moment before closing his eyes, he took one last look at this world, recalling everything he had experienced.","Once his eyes closed, the paths of man and ghost diverged, and heaven and earth were separated.","This man was none other than the Tang Dynasty’s son-in-law, the founder of Baoguang Temple.","If Jian Wushuang had seen him, he would have been astonished, for this man was none other than Fanchen, who had welcomed them into Baoguang Temple!","Known as Fanchen, also called Fanxin.","Now that Fanxin and Fanchen were understood, his end had come.","When he passed away, the world grew still, and the Buddha’s light vanished.","His life force drained away in an instant.","The wandering cultivators of the Northern Glacier were stunned. Did he just die like that?","They couldn’t comprehend it.","If it had been a powerful force from the Heavenly Mountain, there should have been some movement. Yet, there was none, and the man simply perished.","An inexplicable fear began to rise in their hearts.","“I feel a great terror!”"]},{"number":6335,"title":"Chapter 6335: Ancient Demon Revival","paragraphs":["Chapter 6335: Ancient Demon Revival","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“I feel it too... it’s as if it’s right beneath the glacier!”","At that moment, someone recognized who Fancheng was and exclaimed, “He is Fanxin from a thousand years ago, now reborn as Fancheng!”","“Isn’t he the lovestruck monk from the Tang Dynasty?”","“That’s right!”","Everyone seemed to understand in a daze.","A thousand years ago, that lucky young man had received a legacy within the glacier, and his strength skyrocketed. Not only did he establish the prosperity of the Tang Dynasty, but he also once sealed a top-tier divine warrior.","Yet now, he had fallen silently.","It was evidently related to the legacy he had once received.","As waves of shock rippled through their hearts, Tianshan suddenly trembled, and a terrifying aura erupted from the depths of the earth.","Everyone swallowed hard.","“There’s something down there... that aura is the source of the terror!” A Nascent Soul stage cultivator stared in horror at the crack in Tianshan.","At this moment, a beam of white light appeared in the distance, revealing a man dressed in white with a tall crown. When he saw Fancheng’s corpse, he couldn’t help but sigh.","“I’m too late!” This man was Zhen Xian from Baoguang Temple, a close friend of Fancheng.","Moreover, he had another identity—an upper realm cultivator.","He was known as Zhen Xian because in the upper realm, he truly was an Immortal!","“You shouldn’t have fallen like this. Your talent far surpassed mine. If I had asked my master to descend, he would have certainly taken you away! Why did you insist on repaying a favor to an ancient demon?” He sighed deeply.","This was something he couldn’t understand, perhaps because he came from the upper realm.","Mortals valued karma, and cultivators also placed importance on it. However, no matter how great the karma, it shouldn’t block one’s path to cultivation.","Yet Fancheng was willing to die to fulfill his karma.","In the eyes of true cultivators, this was a foolish act.","Years ago, Fancheng had benefited from the ancient demon and promised to release the demon after deciphering the secret technique.","But he had one condition: not to harm mortals.","The ancient demon could slaughter cultivators across the world, but it had to leave a path for mortals.","Both sides verbally agreed.","Fancheng repaid his debt, but the ancient demon might not honor its promise.","Therefore, Zhen Xian believed Fancheng was too foolish and naive.","Now that the ancient demon had awakened, who knew if peace would still reign in this world.","“Sigh, I hope you don’t go too far!”","Zhen Xian sighed, glanced at the terrifying ancient demon about to break free from the ice, and then turned to leave.","He needed to return to the upper realm. Besides seeking help from the experts in his sect, he could also shatter the void and leave on his own—though the power required was immense.","Initially, he had intended for Fancheng to help, but Fancheng had been determined to die.","Now, he had to rely on himself.","However, the area around Mangshan County was a viable option.","Besides, his junior sister had already gone there.","It was time for him to return and clean up the mess, to obtain that power and rise again!","Zhen Xian left lightly, but the scattered cultivators of the Northern Glacier were in a dire situation.","It was too late to escape now. The ancient demon shattered the glacier, and a sharp claw extended out, instantly crushing a Nascent Soul stage cultivator.","“Roar!”","The fresh blood made the ancient demon incredibly excited. It let out a howl and freed its entire body from Tianshan.","“Curse the Divine Eye Clan!”","The ancient demon broke free from the ice mountain, fully revealing itself between heaven and earth.","It stood a hundred zhang tall, with nine heads, eight arms, and six legs.","Each head was grotesque, but none had eyes—only a large, bloody mouth.","The ancient demon’s eyes were located on its chest.","It was a blood-red pupil, like a giant fireball.","Blindingly bright.","It gazed at the cultivators who had inherited the Divine Eye’s legacy, and the blood-red eye immediately shot out a beam of light. The cultivators struck by it were instantly reduced to dust.","The ancient demon absorbed both the strength and blood of its prey, leaving behind only a pile of ashes that had once been a body.","“Heh, hahaha, the taste of blood—I haven’t savored it in so long. The living beings of this world shall all become my nourishment!” the ancient demon cackled.","It rampaged across the entire Northern Region Glacier, madly hunting down cultivators. Despite its massive frame, its speed was anything but slow. With each stride, it covered a hundred miles.","The Nascent Soul cultivators scattered in all directions, trying to escape, but ninety percent of them still perished. Only a lucky few managed to survive.","But they knew that peace would no longer exist in this world. Even if they escaped now, once the ancient demon set its sights on them, there would be no hiding within the Red Eyes Realm. The demon would traverse the entire realm in no time, and eventually, it would hunt down every last cultivator.","Despite the overwhelming despair, as long as there was even a sliver of hope, they would fight for it.","“The Dao Leader is in the Eastern Land of the Tang Dynasty! We must quickly join forces with him. The ancient demon shouldn’t head to the Tang Dynasty right away!”","“Everyone, scatter and flee! We’ll regroup in the Tang Dynasty!”","“Agreed!”","The surviving Nascent Soul cultivators nodded in unison before dispersing in different directions, each fleeing with all their might.","As expected, the ancient demon didn’t immediately chase after them. Instead, it turned its destructive focus on the Northern Region Glacier. The millennia-old profound ice was shattered to pieces by the demon’s eight arms. With its blood-red eyes, the demon transformed the entire glacier into a vast ocean.","This was the true power of the ancient demon, far beyond what could be achieved by merely shattering space.","The demon now possessed strength that surpassed even the Divine Manifestation Realm.","“Divine Eye Inheritance?” The ancient demon wrapped its eight arms around a colorful grand hall, lifting it straight from the ocean’s depths.","“So, this is the inheritance of the third sequence. No wonder I was sealed in this place. Among the 108 ancient domains, 108 gods and demons were born. 72 of them were slain, and the remaining ones must have been sealed by the Divine Eye Clan!”","The ancient demon was highly intelligent. It had once been a powerful being from the Upper Realm, part of the oldest batch of innate creatures. These special lifeforms had genes far superior to those of acquired creatures. Their innate divine power was a thousand times stronger than that of ordinary people.","When the world first formed, each ancient demon had access to limitless resources and quickly cultivated to great heights.","But as the human race’s numbers grew and their comprehension abilities increased, they rose up despite lacking the divine power of the ancient demons. Their rise was so rapid that the ancient demons didn’t even have time to react.","One must understand that each time an ancient demon slumbered, it was for tens of thousands of years or even longer. They never considered humans a threat, treating them like livestock to be raised.","But by the time they realized what was happening, humanity had already produced superpowers that could rival them. And their numbers continued to grow.","When the ancient demons tried to suppress them, the humans banded together and established the Heavenly Court.","Back then, the Heavenly Court was ruled by those who inherited the Divine Eye.","These inheritors possessed heaven-defying strength. Not only did they catch up to the ancient demons, but they quickly surpassed them.","In just tens of thousands of years, the era of the ancient demons crumbled.","One by one, the ancient demons were slain, and the ancient domains fell into human hands.","In the end, the last thirty-six ancient demons fought desperately. Even though they lost, they shattered their ancient domains, refusing to leave them for the human cultivators.","Thus, the ancient domains were broken.","For the ancient demons, the destruction of their domains was akin to self-destruction."]},{"number":6336,"title":"Chapter 6336: Shattering the Nine Heavens","paragraphs":["Chapter 6336: Shattering the Nine Heavens","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","After the destruction of the Ancient Domain, his strength significantly declined. Eventually, he was suppressed one by one, or slain and refined into magical artifacts.","The Ancient Demon’s entire body was considered a treasure.","Especially his blood.","This was the reason why the humans later launched a frenzied attack on the Ancient Demons.","Fortunately, at that time, internal problems also arose within the Heavenly Court. A strong expert of the Divine Eye Clan suddenly fell, and much of the Divine Eye inheritance was reclaimed. This finally halted the siege of the Ancient Demons.","The reason he survived was due to the later suppression.","He was suppressed by an unparalleled Sword Immortal in the Crimson Eye Realm. The artifact used to suppress him was none other than the third-sequence Divine Eye Inheritance Hall.","He harbored deep hatred for this hall. After all, the rise of the humans back then was due to the inheritance of the Divine Eye Clan.","Later, his own suppression was also due to the Divine Eye Clan, so he despised the Divine Eye Inheritance.","He yearned to shatter this Divine Eye Inheritance Hall.","However, when he realized it was the third-sequence inheritance hall, he gave up.","Even in the higher realms, this third-sequence inheritance hall was the top-level Divine Eye inheritance, one he couldn’t possibly break. Even the one who suppressed him back then couldn’t break it.","Otherwise, that person wouldn’t have used this hall to suppress him.","“Hmph, if I can’t destroy it, I’ll use you to obliterate the entire Crimson Eye Realm!”","The Ancient Demon let out a sinister laugh, completely unconcerned about the promise he made to the mortal world.","After all, it was just an exchange. Without his help, the mortals back then would have perished long ago, and there would have been no glory for the Tang Dynasty.","In fact, the glory of the Tang Dynasty was all his doing.","“Hmm?”","The Ancient Demon’s massive eyes shifted, and his Thought power spread over ten thousand miles, sensing that those fleeing cultivators were all heading towards the Tang Dynasty.","From the direction of the Eastern Lands, he felt a familiar aura, one that also came from the Ancient Demon’s bloodline.","“Could there still be members of my clan in the Crimson Eye Realm?”","The Ancient Demon was initially stunned, but then he was delighted to discover that the presence with an aura similar to his own no longer had any life force—it was clearly a dead thing.","“Who would have thought my luck would be this good? As long as I absorb that power, I can restore my peak strength. Even without the Innate Ancient Domain, I could still head to the Upper Realm and seize another ancient domain. Then, I’ll settle the score with the Divine Eye Clan and those inheritors!”","Having made up his mind, he lifted the entire Divine Eye Inheritance Hall and flew up toward the Nine Heavens.","“Let’s start with some interest!”","The Ancient Demon raised the Inheritance Hall and smashed it directly onto the Chaos Realm in the Nine Heavens.","That space was the hardest within the entire Crimson Eye Realm. Back in the day, not a single deity who ascended by shattering the void had been able to break through the Chaos Void; they all ascended by breaking through the space below the Nine Heavens. Among them, the best could only shatter the First Heaven or, at most, the Second Heaven.","It was rumored that someone who had received the complete Divine Eye inheritance managed to break through the Ninth Heaven’s space.","However, the Ninth Heaven’s space ultimately still belonged to the Crimson Eye Realm, while the Chaos Void did not. It belonged to a higher-level world.","Once shattered, the ascendant might not even reach the Seventy-Two Ancient Domains.","Of course, this was only speculation.","But now, he intended to make it a reality.","By shattering the Chaos Void and introducing chaotic energy, he would turn the Crimson Eye Realm into a dead world.","“Smash it for me!”","Boom!","The Ancient Demon lifted the Divine Eye Inheritance Hall and struck the Chaos Realm with force.","Instantly, the entire world trembled.","Not just the Northern Region but the entire Crimson Eye Realm quaked.","“Hmm?”","The Ancient Demon looked at the Chaos Realm, slightly surprised to find that not a single crack had appeared.","That strike should have been powerful enough to shatter the Nine Heavens.","Yet, it hadn’t left even the slightest mark on the Chaos Realm.","“Damn it, my strength is being too heavily suppressed. If it weren’t for the suppression of the Heavenly Dao, I could have shattered this Chaos Realm with just a casual strike!”","The Ancient Demon struck the Chaos Realm several more times but still failed to break through. Frustrated, he gave up.","“If I can’t break the Chaos Realm, then I’ll shatter the Nine Heavens. From now on, there will be no more ascendants from this world!” The Ancient Demon let out a wicked laugh, descended into the Nine Heavens, and smashed the Divine Eye Inheritance Hall directly into them.","Rumble!","This time, the impact was even greater.","The entire Crimson Eye Realm trembled for the time it took an incense stick to burn, causing flat lands to suddenly give rise to mountain ranges, while places that had been mountains became deep chasms.","This great supernatural power that altered the landscape led to countless deaths among mortals.","But the most terrifying part was yet to come. The shattered Nine Heavens turned into fragments of space, falling from the sky.","Countless black spatial crystals rained down on the world.","With the Nine Heavens shattered, the fragments of space fused with the human world, making what had been a fragile space several times stronger.","As a result, all cultivators lost the hope of shattering the void and ascending.","From then on, ascension became a distant dream.","Yet, the people deep within Mangshan County’s city were completely unaware of the changes outside.","However, one immortal who exuded an aura of true divinity ground his teeth as he watched the black rain droplets fall from the sky, angrily declaring, “Just wait! If you dare go to the Upper Realm, I’ll be sure to cut you down!”","His anger wasn’t over the shattering of the Nine Heavens or the fact that the Crimson Eye Realm could no longer produce ascendants.","What enraged him was that the third-sequence Inheritance Hall had been fused into the shattered Nine Heavens.","As a result, it would be much harder for him to enter the third-sequence Divine Eye Inheritance Hall.","He had come to the Crimson Eye Realm precisely for that Inheritance Hall!","And now, that foolish Ancient Demon had tossed it into the fragmented space. Although it appeared to be floating in the sky, entering it now would require matching space fragments.","But those fragments had already fused with the ground’s space.","Finding matching fragments would be as difficult as climbing to the heavens.","“This is a big problem!”","The Immortal and his junior sister, Fu Qing, stood guard outside the ancient fortress.","Wei Jiuxian also looked up at the falling raindrops, but his expression showed no fear.","It was as if everything had been within his expectations.","Seeing his expression, the Immortal seemed to have guessed something and asked, “Did Fancheng leave you a backup plan?”","“Just a small trick!” Wei Jiuxian replied calmly.","The Immortal sighed, “Then don’t do anything unnecessary. Use whatever tricks you have left and flee quickly! That Ancient Demon once ruled an Ancient Domain. His strength is beyond comparison with you mortals.”","“How would I know if I don’t try?” Wei Jiuxian’s tone was firm.","The Immortal and Fu Qing exchanged a glance, both showing a hint of pride in their eyes—a disdain for mortals.","They came from the Upper Realm and knew more. In the entire Crimson Eye Realm, they only acknowledged Fancheng.","The Upper Realm’s power was not as simple as those legends made it out to be; it was so powerful that mortals couldn’t even begin to imagine it.","The Upper Realm now was no longer the era of the Ancient Demon. Most of the records in the legends belonged to the time when humanity united to fight against the Ancient Demon, a time long past.","Though it was now countless times stronger, their power was still suppressed in the Lower Realm.","While the Ancient Demon’s strength was also suppressed by the Heavenly Dao, his base power was a thousand times that of the human race—they were still no match for him."]},{"number":6337,"title":"Chapter 6337: If You Can’t Beat Him, Call Someone","paragraphs":["Chapter 6337: If You Can’t Beat Him, Call Someone","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","To win, they had to pay a price. That price might lead to their downfall.","“If it comes to it, I’ll crush the token my master gave me. With his power, descending to this realm would be effortless, and he could easily kill the ancient demon and obtain the inheritance hall!” Zhen Xian steeled his resolve.","But unless absolutely necessary, he wouldn’t crush the token.","Because it concerned his standing within the sect.","Moreover, this kind of assistance token, he only had one.","Once used, it would be gone. Who knew when he would get another?","If he needed his master’s help even in the mortal world, he wouldn’t be able to hold his head high among his peers.","“Senior brother, it seems there’s some movement in the city!” Fu Qing frowned as he looked toward the city.","Zhen Xian also turned his gaze.","With a thought, he sensed that the soul power within the city was rapidly increasing.","His eyes immediately froze, and he exclaimed in surprise, “What’s going on? Why is the soul power of those cultivators who entered Mangshan County City increasing so rapidly!”","With his Thought power, he pierced through the barrier that isolated Mangshan County and sensed that the soul power of the cultivators within the city was growing at a staggering rate. Several of the cultivators in the Nascent Soul stage had already reached the God Aspect level in terms of soul power.","This development shocked him even more than the ancient demon he had seen earlier!","Because the increase in soul power was permanent.","“I never imagined that such a secret method existed in the mortal world. Junior sister, let’s hurry inside!” Zhen Xian was ecstatic.","He had realized that after those cultivators killed the ghost cultivators, they automatically absorbed the ghost cultivators’ soul power, which was the reason for their rapid increase in soul power.","And the cause of all this was the barrier around Mangshan County.","Though it was called a barrier, it was more like a grand formation.","The ghost cultivators devoured each other, creating stronger ghost cultivators, all because of this formation.","After Zhen Xian finished speaking, Fu Qing’s expression also changed.","Soul cultivation methods were the most mysterious of all cultivation methods. Even in the upper realms, they were top-tier secret techniques, and neither of them had ever practiced a complete soul cultivation method.","Therefore, their soul power was only one level higher than their current realm.","It wasn’t considered top-tier, but practicing a soul cultivation method could amplify their soul power, allowing them to fully exert the power of their realm.","In their understanding, this was how soul power was used.","However, when one reached the Immortal Emergence stage, soul power would be used differently.","Because Immortal Emergence cultivators could control certain aspects of the Heavenly Dao, which required even higher levels of soul power.","At the level of an Emperor, mastering the Dao and controlling a vast world required even more soul power. Thus, they would all cultivate soul secret techniques to amplify their Thought power, enabling them to control the Dao.","But this amplification wasn’t intrinsic.","It was similar to Jian Wushuang’s Ancient Transformation technique, where the amplification required greater consumption of power, but the actual divine power hadn’t increased.","Only by amplifying one’s own divine power was it truly significant.","Soul power was the same. Only an increase in essence was truly useful.","Once their soul power surpassed their realm by two levels, the two of them could undoubtedly enter the core of their sect and become the Dao successors of their generation, allowing them to practice even more powerful secret techniques.","The only downside was that this was the mortal world.","Therefore, they were even more eager to obtain this formation that raised ghost cultivators. If they acquired it, they wouldn’t need to ask their master to descend; even inviting the strongest expert in their sect would be met with no resistance, and they would even be rewarded.","But there was one thing they needed to ascertain in advance: whether this grand formation had higher-level applications.","If it didn’t, its value would decrease significantly. However, it could still be used to cultivate lower-level disciples, which would be a significant contribution.","In any case, it would rival the value of his token.","That was Zhen Xian’s plan.","Meanwhile, inside the ancient castle, Wei Jiuxian listened in confusion, merely watching the two leave without following them.","He had more important matters to attend to in this place.","...","Inside Mangshan County City.","Jian Wushuang, who hadn’t appeared for a long time, sat cross-legged on the city wall, watching the cultivators and ghost cultivators fighting, but showed no interest.","Because his soul realm was too high.","Within the Nine Prison Pagoda, his soul realm had already reached the Immortal Emergence level.","In the mortal world, it had also reached the peak of the God Aspect realm.","There was no need for him to kill these ghost cultivators to enhance his soul realm.","However, Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang needed it, as did Yang Xiao and Qianzu Saintess. Under his guidance, they had all gone down early to kill ghost cultivators.","In fact, he had discovered this benefit from the start, but he didn’t feel the need to mention it because it had nothing to do with what he wanted.","But now that he couldn’t find the altar, he sent them down to kill ghost cultivators, thinking that if all the ghost cultivators were eliminated, perhaps they would find the answer.","Unfortunately, he could only rely on this clumsy method to explore for now.","Swoosh!!","Two powerful auras soared into the sky, instantly descending upon the county city of Mangshan.","The intensity of these auras far exceeded that of Immortal Jiu Chen earlier.","They were undoubtedly strong experts in the Zhen Xian realm.","“Two more Zhen Xian have appeared, making it four in total. The depths of the Tang Dynasty’s hidden powers are truly astounding!” Jian Wushuang rubbed his temples in surprise.","Earlier, two monks had arrived, both in the early stages of Zhen Xian, with average strength.","But this time, the two Zhen Xian who had arrived were at least in the later stages.","They immediately plunged into the vast group of ghost cultivators and began to fight fiercely.","Their speed in slaying was far faster than those from the three major forces.","Among the three forces, the strongest were only in the early and mid stages of Zhen Xian.","As for the Southern Heaven Realm, they had the grandest display yet the weakest strength, without a single Zhen Xian.","They were undoubtedly the most awkward party.","The three major forces each divided into three areas.","The two Arhats went to another area.","The later arriving Zhen Xian and Fu Qing went to the central area.","But even so, the pace of the siege was still insufficient. To completely annihilate all the ghost cultivators would take at least another hour.","“This won’t do. The demon in the sky won’t give them that much time!” Jian Wushuang sighed inwardly.","He had sensed the demon breaking the seal in the sky earlier.","Although there was a barrier in this place, it couldn’t completely block his detection.","If even Zhen Xian and Fu Qing could feel what was happening within the city from the outside, there was no way Jian Wushuang wouldn’t notice.","He was surprised when he sensed the demon’s emergence.","How could a mortal world bear the existence of a demon?","But upon realizing that the demon’s strength was also suppressed, he felt relieved.","Even he was being suppressed by this world, let alone that demon.","“It seems I’ll have to step in myself!”","Though he didn’t care much for that bit of soul power, he had no choice but to take action now.","As long as he found the altar and obtained that power, he could rapidly absorb it and reach the peak of the Zhen Xian realm.","By then, that demon would no longer be his match.","Despite being in a mortal body, every time his strength grew, he could access tens of thousands more secret techniques and divine abilities, all of which were top-tier."]},{"number":6338,"title":"Chapter 6338: Destroy the City With One Hand","paragraphs":["Chapter 6338: Destroy the City With One Hand","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Slaying a divine demon of the same level was simply effortless.","The difference wasn’t so obvious during the Infant Formation stage, but once one reached the Divine Aspect realm, it was a leap forward.","This was because the secret techniques recorded in his mind were all at least at the Myriad Phenomena level, and with his powerful soul, he could only begin cultivating them at the Divine Aspect realm.","The small techniques he used before weren’t even considered secret techniques in his eyes.","However, burning Thought power didn’t count, as it didn’t depend on the realm or strength, but rather on soul power.","“Chen Yuan, don’t move around here. I’ll be back soon!” Jian Wushuang instructed before he soared into the sky.","He flew directly toward the center of the city.","At this moment, he didn’t bother to hide his aura anymore and openly appeared above the two Divine Aspect realm experts.","Zhen Xian and Fu Qing sensed Jian Wushuang’s aura and only slightly frowned, thinking that Jian Wushuang was being a bit presumptuous for daring to come into their territory to seize ghost cultivators.","They originally intended to teach him a lesson, but in the next moment, a terrifying wave of Thought power descended upon the entire city.","“Burning Thought power!” Jian Wushuang shouted softly.","All his Thought power erupted simultaneously, burning multiple times over, and the terrifying pressure instantly caused all the ghost cultivators in the city to stand dazed and motionless.","“Destroy!”","With one hand, Jian Wushuang struck down, and the giant palm print formed from Thought power descended like a divine weapon from the heavens.","In just one move, he crushed ninety percent of the ghost cultivators.","Among them was even a Ghost Commander who possessed Divine Aspect realm soul power.","Yet, even so, Jian Wushuang easily crushed him to death.","If it were a true Divine Aspect realm expert, it might not have been possible to crush the opponent, but since it was just a spiritual body, he had no difficulty dealing with it.","This move shocked all the cultivators, causing cold sweat to break out on their backs.","At the same time, all eyes turned towards Jian Wushuang in the sky.","Zhen Xian and Fu Qing were no exception, their eyes filled with disbelief.","The suppression from the Thought power just now had shaken them both, extinguishing any thoughts of resistance. It took them several breaths to react.","Such powerful Thought power pressure absolutely surpassed the Divine Aspect realm.","Zhen Xian stared at Jian Wushuang’s figure and exclaimed, “Could he have already reached the Myriad Phenomena realm?”","“Impossible! The heavenly laws of the mortal world absolutely do not allow the existence of the Myriad Phenomena realm. Once someone reaches that level, they would be annihilated unless they became a Transcendent!” Fu Qing retorted.","But the reality was right in front of them, and they had no choice but to believe it.","“Could he already be a Transcendent being?”","However, that aura couldn’t deceive them.","Jian Wushuang’s aura was very weak, only at the Infant Formation stage.","If it weren’t for the lack of time, he could have gone outside to absorb those scattered spatial crystals. But gathering them was too troublesome, unlike the ones he had obtained from Immortal Jiu Chen, which were already refined.","Those large chunks couldn’t be found even if he scoured the entire Mangshan County. Even if he were lucky enough to find spatial crystals similar to the ones before, after absorbing them, he would at most advance to the early Divine Aspect stage, which still wouldn’t be enough to fight against divine demons.","He had to obtain the power within the altar.","But even with such powerful Thought power, he still couldn’t locate the altar, making him more anxious than anyone.","Ignoring the shocked expressions of the others, his Thought power continued to probe the city of Mangshan County.","The remaining ghost cultivators were quickly exterminated by the cultivators. After all, anything that could enhance the soul was something everyone desired.","The vast city, now empty of ghost cultivators, had become much quieter.","The remaining cultivators began searching for the altar.","Some even started destroying houses to search for it.","Zhen Xian and Fu Qing, however, lost interest and prepared to leave.","But before they could, they wanted to probe Jian Wushuang a little.","Yet, before they could make a move, Jian Wushuang unleashed a terrifying burst of Thought power that pushed them back.","“Fools! That divine demon is still watching from outside. If you don’t find the altar quickly, when that demon arrives, you’ll all be doomed!” Jian Wushuang was growing irritated.","He wouldn’t die, nor would Jiang Shang or Xiang Yang.","Because he had the Nine Prison Pagoda, at worst, he could have the soul avatar within the pagoda create an opening and let them take refuge inside the treasure.","With the defensive power of this treasure, not to mention that divine demon outside, even if a Dayan Immortal came, they wouldn’t be able to break it.","But doing so would make shattering the void much more difficult.","He feared they would be trapped for a very, very long time.","He didn’t want to be trapped, especially at this mortal stage.","Because at this stage, he couldn’t enhance his original body’s strength.","If his original body were trapped, he could still cultivate and increase his power to break free, but now that his original body was gone, getting trapped would just waste time, and the strength gained wouldn’t help his original body at all.","Moreover, he wanted to explore this world, not be imprisoned within it.","After being scolded, Zhen Xian and Fu Qing were momentarily stunned, then sneered, “Hmph, it’s just a small altar. Even if it’s found, what can it do? We thought with your strong Thought power, you’d be more knowledgeable. Turns out, you’re just a frog in a well. Do you not recognize an ancient demon? That’s an innate being born from the Ancient Domain. Even if you reach the peak of the Divine Aspect Realm, you won’t be a match. Let me tell you something else—don’t even think about shattering the void. The space on the ground now is even more solid than the Nine Heavens back then. Even if you reach the peak of the Divine Aspect Realm, you still won’t be able to break through the space to leave!”","“A frog in a well!” Jian Wushuang chuckled at himself.","He could tell that the souls and realms of the two before him were suppressed.","They were undoubtedly strong beings from the Upper World. He once thought the Upper World was vast, and even considered it a low-level chaotic world.","But now, it seemed either that world was too weak, or the cultivators there were too foolish, lacking any insight.","The so-called ancient demon was just an innate divine demon, which was the common term in the outside world.","Also, this altar here was far from simple.","If it were merely the power sealed at the peak of the Divine Aspect Realm, how could he not have found it?","The key issue was that this place’s array was special—it allowed ghost cultivators to devour one another and grow.","Such a unique array, nurturing so many ghost cultivators, had not just appeared today.","From the time Yang Xiao noticed something odd about this place, at least ten days had passed.","Judging by Jian Wushuang’s calculations, the ghost commanders who appeared tonight had just advanced.","This meant that the ghost cultivators who had previously advanced had already been taken away.","And the purpose of nurturing so many ghost cultivators was to resurrect the imperial concubine.","So, what was the deal with the altar’s power?","The two didn’t seem to be connected!","But upon deeper consideration, one could deduce that the imperial concubine was just a pawn, and her resurrection was to benefit that Tang Emperor.","The altar’s power had likely already fallen into Tang Emperor’s hands.","That was why he had yet to make an appearance.","Besides all this, Jian Wushuang also sensed a peculiar aura from those ghost cultivators, one that was very similar to that of divine demons."]},{"number":6339,"title":"Chapter 6339: The Array Appears","paragraphs":["Chapter 6339: The Array Appears","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","It was evident that the altar not only sealed divine power but also possibly contained the power of gods and demons.","Once this power was obtained, not just Jian Wushuang, but even if Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang combined their strength, they wouldn’t be able to fully consume it.","Even the cultivators in the city, who had significantly increased their soul strength by killing ghost cultivators, could reach the level of shattering the void if they acquired this power of gods and demons.","Even though space had become more solid than before, it could still be shattered with the power of gods and demons.","However, Jian Wushuang was too lazy to explain these things to the others.","Whether they understood it or not depended on themselves.","He didn’t care if they stayed or left, but if anyone dared to cause trouble, he wouldn’t hesitate to act.","Zhen Xian and Fu Qing coldly snorted but had no intention of leaving. Although they didn’t fully understand the situation, they also chose to search for the altar.","At that moment, in the southern part of the city, after a two-story pavilion was overturned, a wave of death energy surged out.","Simultaneously, a similar event occurred in the southwest.","Jian Wushuang’s thought power instantly gathered.","By focusing on the two locations, he quickly noticed something unusual.","“There’s actually a hidden formation here!” Jian Wushuang’s eyebrows twitched, and he immediately transmitted his thoughts, “Xiang Yang, take Jiang Shang and head to the city wall quickly!”","Both Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang were only cultivators at the Golden Core stage. If they encountered danger, they could easily be killed in an instant. The city wasn’t lacking in Golden Core cultivators, so it would be safer for them to head to the city wall.","Without hesitation, Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang flew directly towards the city wall.","Meanwhile, cellars emitting death energy continued to appear throughout the city.","That death energy quickly spread across the entire county city.","“A death energy formation, ghost cultivators, and the altar!”","Jian Wushuang began to see through the intentions of the mastermind behind this.","It wasn’t just about resurrecting the imperial concubine; it seemed more like a case of possession by borrowing a corpse to return to life!","As for the imperial concubine, she was merely an appetizer.","“One hundred and eight cellars, forming the foundation of this grand formation. The person who set this up is no ordinary figure!” Jian Wushuang calmly remarked.","He wasn’t afraid of the opponent’s methods; what he feared was the opponent hiding and not coming out.","Now that the formation had appeared, it wouldn’t be long before the opponent showed themselves.","The exposure of the formation provided Jian Wushuang with an opportunity.","To Jian Wushuang, formations weren’t overly complicated. The core of this formation wasn’t just the one hundred and eight cellars, but rather the death energy.","That was the key to driving the formation.","As long as he suppressed the death energy, he could stop the formation from operating, and at that point, the opponent would surely emerge to confront him.","However, Jian Wushuang wasn’t planning to do that. He was more interested in seeing what the opponent was up to.","Who was this formation meant to bring back to life through possession?","So, he didn’t rush to take action.","But the other cultivators panicked, starting to suppress the death energy from the cellars.","In groups of three or five, they formed simple battle formations to suppress the cellars.","Unfortunately, there weren’t enough people, and they could only suppress a dozen or so cellars at most.","This merely slowed down the formation’s operation but couldn’t stop it.","Neither Zhen Xian nor Fu Qing took action to suppress the formation; they remained silent.","Everyone wanted to wait.","Jian Wushuang returned to the city wall, observing the scene within the city, his thought power constantly monitoring the cultivators throughout the city.","“Wushuang, this formation seems strange, especially that death energy. Why do I feel like it’s similar to when we first entered this place?” Xiang Yang gazed at the surging death energy, revealing a puzzled expression.","The death energy was indeed similar to the one that erupted when they first entered, but back then, it was far more intense than what was present here.","The most important difference was that the death energy back then contained a special aura.","It was somewhat different from the death energy here.","“It’s somewhat similar, but it’s not a big deal!” Jian Wushuang explained to Xiang Yang, “Do you remember those demons we encountered before entering this place? If I’m not mistaken, those demons were tricked and slaughtered in life, and many of them were killed, which is why so much death energy gathered!”","“Ambushed and killed? But those creatures included Universe Gods at the Six-Star level!” Xiang Yang exclaimed in shock, momentarily forgetting to communicate through thought transmission.","Yang Xiao and the others were stunned when they heard the term “Universe God.”","The Qianzu Saintess hadn’t followed Miao Renfeng’s Barbarian Lands tribe, believing that sticking with Jian Wushuang might reveal more useful information.","However, what she heard now left her completely baffled.","Universe Gods?","What kind of existence was that?","These people might have lived their entire lives without even hearing of the universe, let alone understanding the immense power of a Universe God.","Jian Wushuang ignored their confusion and calmly explained, “The ghosts here can devour and evolve, so it’s likely the same principle applies to those creatures as well.”","“Ah, that makes sense. But even so, the one who ambushed and killed those creatures must have been a Universe God. Otherwise, how could they have subdued such beings?” Xiang Yang still seemed worried.","Although he hadn’t yet regained much of his strength, he was concerned about the future.","If there truly were incomparably powerful Universe Gods in this world, he wouldn’t stand a chance.","At his peak, he had only reached the Ninth Tribulation as a Universe Master.","His power as a Demigod had already reached its limit.","As for Universe Gods above Six-Star level, he didn’t even dare to imagine confronting such beings.","“There’s no need to overthink. If this world really is filled with powerful Universe Gods, it wouldn’t make much difference whether you leave or stay,” Jian Wushuang reassured him.","Indeed, Xiang Yang was merely a Ninth Tribulation Universe Master. If this world contained super-powerful Universe Gods, his cultivation here would be no different from training in the outside world.","Besides, the Xiang family had already perished, and leaving might only lead to his enemies pursuing him for revenge.","If there were better opportunities here, staying and cultivating in this world could be a more viable option.","Just like Xing Luo, who, despite having access to a larger world, chose to return here. Likely due to a certain legacy that couldn’t be further enhanced in the outside world, it was better to return and continue strengthening himself in this realm.","Xiang Yang might as well cling to this opportunity; staying here and becoming a son-in-law might be a hundred times better than leaving.","Of course, he didn’t voice this thought.","After chatting with Xiang Yang for a while, Jian Wushuang continued to observe Mangshan County.","Unlike Xiang Yang, Jian Wushuang’s true self was incredibly powerful, already at the peak of the Nine-Star Universe God level.","Once he regained his strength, not only this world but even the Realm God Continent couldn’t hold him back.","The most crucial point was that entering this world seemed to be part of someone’s plan.","The Prophet!","This mighty figure could erase some people’s memories, but not his.","The Prophet had helped him several times, and this time, entering this place was also connected to that person.","For example, the strong figure who destroyed the Eastern True Immortal Realm was also known as the Prophet, and Jian Wushuang had even dreamed of the Prophet.","Now that he had obtained the Nine Prison Pagoda, he was even more certain that entering this world was no mere coincidence.","The Prophet must have been scheming something.","The Crimson Eye Realm was just the first challenge. What he needed to do was find a way to gain benefits that would strengthen his true self.","At the very least, the Nine Prison Pagoda was no ordinary treasure; it was far more than it seemed."]},{"number":6340,"title":"Chapter 6340: Ghost Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6340: Ghost Emperor","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Obtaining this treasure was likely part of the Prophet’s plan all along.","Now, with all the cultivators of the Red-Eyed Realm gathered here, and one ancient legend after another emerging, it was clear that a hidden hand was orchestrating everything.","But he still wondered if he was the protagonist of this story.","Buzz!","While his mind was swirling with countless thoughts, a sudden change occurred within the city.","The deathly aura that filled the sky began to coalesce, and a powerful force erupted from it.","“What is that?” Jian Wushuang looked up at the clouds within the city and immediately sensed a strong spiritual force emanating from within.","Swish!","Countless soul bodies suddenly shot out from the underground chambers, surging into the clouds along with the deathly aura.","These soul bodies were different from the ghostly cultivators previously in the city; they were more complete.","They were no longer at the level of ghost commanders, for a “king” character was etched upon their chests.","“Are these Ghost Kings?”","From 108 underground chambers, 108 Ghost Kings emerged, each one a soul at the level of a divine general.","Combined with the soul force already present in the clouds, the fusion unleashed an unprecedented spiritual power.","Witnessing this, Jian Wushuang, Zhen Xian, and Fu Qing knew they couldn’t stand idly by. This grand formation could very well give birth to a peerless existence.","One that might rival the ancient demon.","In an instant, they couldn’t afford to hold back any longer, each of them making their move to intercept the fusing souls.","Zhen Xian began with the Kunlun Divine Form. A towering, majestic mountain suddenly crashed down from the sky, and just as the ethereal immortal energy spread, it was obliterated by the Heavenly Dao. Yet even so, this towering mountain had already reached the peak of divine form combat power.","“Shake the Kunlun!”","Zhen Xian roared, forming hand seals, and the towering mountain smashed into the clouds.","Numerous secret techniques were employed by various Nascent Soul cultivators and even some divine form cultivators.","But these techniques were not enough to shake the deathly cloud.","Even when the towering mountain struck it, it didn’t stir a single ripple.","This made everyone anxious.","The soul force within the clouds grew stronger.","A pair of blood-red eyes gradually formed within the clouds.","“Sister, don’t hold back! Strike now and suppress that soul force! Whatever you do, don’t let it fully manifest—I have a feeling that once it forms, it might break free from the Heavenly Dao!” Zhen Xian was extremely worried.","That pressure beyond the Heavenly Dao was all too familiar to him. He had been following their master for a long time, and he was well aware of this aura.","Hearing her senior brother’s words, Fu Qing no longer hesitated. She drew the divine sword from her back, battle intent rising between her brows.","“Heaven-Splitting Sword Art!”","With a soft cry, her divine sword unleashed a power capable of shattering the void. In an instant, ten thousand sword lights burst forth.","As the sword lights shot out, they quickly converged into a colossal, tangible divine sword, a hundred meters long, thrusting fiercely towards the clouds.","The previous wave of attacks couldn’t compare to the power of this single strike.","Even Jian Wushuang, standing on the city walls, was a bit surprised by the sharpness of this woman’s sword technique. It carried a similar intensity to his own in the past—she was a remarkable sword prodigy.","But unfortunately, it still wasn’t enough to deal with the deathly cloud. Although the sword managed to pierce the cloud, the battle intent was instantly consumed by Thought power upon entering.","Without the battle intent, the Heaven-Splitting Sword was like a blade without an edge.","It lost its sword essence.","It immediately shattered and disintegrated, yet the deathly cloud felt the threat and began absorbing the Ghost Kings even faster.","Soon, the cloud transformed into a humanoid figure.","This was a massive soul body, ten thousand meters tall, and in its hand, a Soul Summoning Banner appeared!","“I am the Ghost Emperor!” the soul body declared, waving the Soul Summoning Banner. The moment it was swung, the banner released countless ghostly wails, and an attack that pierced the soul instantly rendered all the Nascent Soul cultivators present powerless, leaving them standing dazed and immobile.","Jian Wushuang’s Thought power easily blocked the crude soul attack. His Thought power shield even extended to protect several Golden Core stage cultivators. Observing the scene before him, Jian Wushuang remained calm and composed.","When he first sensed something was amiss, he anticipated that the deathly cloud might give birth to a terrifying entity. However, he hadn’t expected that the Ghost Emperor it formed would be capable of launching a soul attack.","But it made sense; after all, the Ghost Emperor was a soul entity, and its only means of attack would be through soul attacks, which happened to be its specialty.","The intense soul attack swept across a large number of cultivators. If it weren’t for the soul power boost Jian Wushuang gained from slaying the ghost cultivators earlier, even Nascent Soul stage cultivators would have perished en masse.","Even so, the attack wiped out the souls of all cultivators below the Nascent Soul stage, claiming their lives. Not even those at the peak of the Golden Core stage were spared.","This wide-range attack was somewhat similar to Jian Wushuang’s previous Thought power burn, but there was one key difference—the opponent couldn’t compare to Jian Wushuang. After all, Jian Wushuang had the power to annihilate even a Ghost Commander at the Nascent Soul stage.","This was because Jian Wushuang’s soul techniques were far superior, and with the reverse-heaven technique of burning his soul, there was no comparison between this world and his.","“Interesting. This Ghost Emperor’s soul attack likely stems from its inherent characteristics, a natural secret technique!” Jian Wushuang’s heart stirred as he realized that this Ghost Emperor’s consciousness had only just formed.","For a newly formed consciousness to already wield soul attacks, it must indeed be a natural secret technique. This Ghost Emperor could be considered an innate being.","But to be born so powerful—wasn’t the one who set all this up afraid that the Ghost Emperor would become uncontrollable?","Just as this thought crossed Jian Wushuang’s mind, he sensed a familiar aura within the range of his Thought power. His figure vanished from the city wall in an instant, and he transmitted a message to Xiang Yang, instructing them to leave the city and find Wei Jiuxian outside. That place was much safer than Mangshan County’s city.","Furthermore, he had just discovered that the slain cultivators, even after their souls were destroyed, left behind intact bodies. But as soon as that familiar aura appeared, those bodies instantly turned into blood water.","The blood water flowed through the cracks in the ground, seeping into the earth.","“Found you!”","Jian Wushuang moved swiftly, a smile tugging at the corners of his lips.","In a dilapidated house in the southern part of the city, he dove into the courtyard well.","The aura emanated from that location.","Even the two peak God Phase experts above hadn’t noticed it, as the aura was masked by the Ghost Emperor. It would be hard for an ordinary person to detect, but Jian Wushuang had meticulously burned his Thought power to cover every corner of the city, waiting for this moment.","Sure enough, the opponent had exposed a flaw after the Ghost Emperor appeared.","With a splash, he plunged into the well, following the aura as he descended deeper and deeper.","He could detect the opponent, but the opponent had no idea of his presence.","“Thought power burn!”","Jian Wushuang burned his Thought power once again, completely concealing his aura."]},{"number":6341,"title":"Chapter 6341: Evasion","paragraphs":["Chapter 6341: Evasion","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","At this moment, almost no one in this world could detect his presence.","“Hmm?”","Jian Wushuang, who was continuously sinking, noticed that the deeper he went, the larger the space below became.","After descending several hundred feet, the water temperature also began to rise.","He cautiously used his thought power to probe the direction of that peculiar aura. Once he pinpointed the exact location, he began to quietly move towards it.","The closer he got to the source of the aura, the faster his heart began to beat.","An unsettled heart?","Ever since he had entered this world, his physical body was gone, and his soul had been reduced to the level of a mortal. However, his state of mind remained untouched.","Yet now, something in that direction was disturbing his inner peace.","This was beyond his expectations.","“What could be hidden there that can affect my state of mind? Could it be something beyond the level of a Universe God?”","This thought quickly flashed through his mind, but he dismissed it immediately—it was simply impossible.","He then considered that his current physical body, formed from spatial crystals, might be particularly sensitive to space, which could explain why his heartbeat was so rapid, causing his state of mind to become slightly unstable.","Without dwelling on it further, he calmed his heartbeat and swiftly moved towards the location.","The reason he had been so cautious earlier wasn’t that he feared the opponent’s strength surpassing his own, but rather that he was concerned that being discovered by the opponent might have adverse effects.","It would be troublesome if his plans were ruined.","After swimming for the time it takes for an incense stick to burn, a cave mansion appeared in the depths of the dark water.","The entrance to the cave was small, barely wide enough for two people to enter side by side. This time, Jian Wushuang was exceptionally cautious. He disassembled his physical body, just as he had done when he emerged from the Nine Prison Pagoda, transforming into a stream of water that seeped into the cave mansion, clinging to the cave walls. This way, even with the naked eye, it would be difficult for anyone to detect his presence.","Once inside the cave mansion, he realized that its internal structure resembled that of a well—the deeper he went, the larger the space became.","“Almost there!” Jian Wushuang’s eyes gleamed with excitement. He could even hear the breathing of the person inside, though he had not yet seen them.","However, he quickly discerned that there were three distinct auras within the cave mansion.","Or rather, three and a half.","One person was barely alive, with only a trace of breath remaining.","Among the three, there was one he was very familiar with. It was this aura that had led him to this place.","“Immortal Jiu Chen!”","After reaching the depths of the cave mansion, Jian Wushuang finally saw the person clearly. As he had sensed, it was indeed Immortal Jiu Chen.","The original owner of the Nine Prison Pagoda.","He had thought that Immortal Jiu Chen might have perished, but unexpectedly, he was still alive and had orchestrated such a grand scheme.","Not only had he slaughtered all the Golden Core stage cultivators of the three major forces, but he had also created a being like the Ghost Emperor.","And there was also the Soul Ascension Array.","This made Jian Wushuang view Immortal Jiu Chen in a new light. He had once thought of him as a frog at the bottom of a well, but now it seemed that he truly possessed some remarkable abilities.","Otherwise, he would never have obtained such a mysterious treasure as the Nine Prison Pagoda.","That was a treasure that could drive even the most powerful of Great Immortals mad.","And now, even though he had not unlocked the first layer, the world within the first layer alone could rival a medium-sized world.","It was far from an ordinary treasure.","Some of the most heaven-defying treasures in the universe could nurture cosmic secret realms.","While the space within the first layer of the Nine Prison Pagoda was vast, it was still a far cry from a cosmic secret realm. However, with eight more layers remaining, he couldn’t make a definitive conclusion yet.","If his true self were here, he could forcibly unlock it and fully understand the true power of the Nine Prison Pagoda.","He moved along the wall, carefully observing the three people inside the cave and the woman in white lying on the stone bed.","The old man with white hair was Immortal Jiu Chen. Although his physical body had changed, his aura remained the same as before.","There was also a middle-aged man in a black robe, who should be none other than Emperor Li Miao of the Tang Dynasty. His strength was only at the mid-stage of the Nascent Soul.","However, it was Immortal Jiu Chen’s power that startled him. He had reached the pinnacle of the Divine Aspect realm, comparable to the Zhen Xian within the city.","No wonder he was able to plot so deeply.","He must have some method of control, which is why he wasn’t worried about the Ghost Emperor outside.","Aside from these two whose identities had been revealed, there was also a stern-faced middle-aged woman. He had neither seen nor heard of her before, but her strength was extraordinary, already at the mid-stage of the Divine Aspect realm.","Next, he cautiously used Thought Power to probe the woman in white on the stone bed.","There was no need to ask; this was undoubtedly the Empress Yi.","Her body still harbored a wisp of soul energy.","This was not surprising. He had previously calculated that she must have used a secret method to preserve Thought Power, and now it seemed she had stored it in the Empress’s body, keeping this wisp of soul energy intact.","“This physical body?” When he used Thought Power to examine her body, his expression changed slightly.","Because within this body, there was a hidden, powerful force of all things, and the source was a force of life.","He was all too familiar with this aura.","In the past, he first mastered the Great Way of All Things and eventually elevated it to the Way of Life, hoping to use it to break through and become a Universe Master.","However, he later found that this path seemed unsuitable for him and instead focused on the Sword Way, creating the Nine Swords.","Even now, he could only unleash the first six swords, but one of them was named after life itself.","It was clear that his mastery of the power of life was second only to the God of Life.","“This force of life is not innate; it was definitely injected by a powerful being capable of refining life force. But in this world, the strongest beings are only at the Divine Aspect realm. How could anyone here condense life force?” Jian Wushuang was puzzled.","If he were to suggest that beings who transcended the Heavenly Dao, such as Ancestors or Great Immortals, had descended here, it didn’t seem plausible. After all, the Empress had only been attacked three years ago, and during these three years, there had been no reports of any super-powerful beings appearing.","Even the Divine Aspect realm was considered extinct at first.","“Wait!” Jian Wushuang’s mind suddenly stirred as he thought of the Wanliu Totem behind Jiang Shang.","Her mother, Jiang Shang, must have mastered a divine ability that allowed her to condense life force. If that was the case, then everything made sense.","The reason the Empress didn’t die back then was because of Jiang Shang.","Moreover, that force of life was very similar to the life force of the Wanliu Divine Tree.","In the past, Dan Bao had saved him many times using the life force of the Wood Way.","As for the life force Jian Wushuang himself had mastered, it was the counterpart to death, pure life force. But such life force could only be controlled by the true God of Life in the Starry Sky.","That was a deity that transcended time and space, a starry sky deity.","To reach that position, he would have to first kill the deity and then inherit their power.","But since even Miesheng couldn’t accomplish that, it was naturally beyond his reach as well.","Therefore, Miesheng had sought to devour the four Starry Sky Gods of Life. If he succeeded in gathering pure life force, he would become the God of Reincarnation, bypassing the Starry Sky’s true God of Life.","The more one saw, the more directions one could analyze.","This was the terrifying power of experience, a rare form of wisdom."]},{"number":6342,"title":"Chapter 6342: Ancestor Destruction","paragraphs":["Chapter 6342: Ancestor Destruction","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","At least now, Jian Wushuang had clearly understood the hidden truth behind it all.","Jiang Shang had indeed appeared in the Great Tang Dynasty and had even saved this imperial consort.","That was just three years ago.","He had been in this world for almost a year now.","Calculating the time, the more he thought about it, the more he wondered if Jiang Shang’s disappearance was related to his arrival.","Perhaps it was possible.","But it was merely speculation.","While he was lost in thought, the three people inside the cave started arguing.","At this moment, Jian Wushuang pricked up his ears.","“No way!”","“Absolutely not!”","A double denial.","It came from Immortal Jiu Chen and Emperor Li Miao of the Tang Dynasty.","These two were clearly on the same side.","The middle-aged woman, however, raised her eyebrows and glared at Li Miao, shouting, “Do you intend to destroy your ancestors?”","“Stop using the ancestors to pressure me! Everything I’m doing now is enough to make the ancestors tear me apart!” Li Miao was not willing to back down either.","When he considered the things he had done, not just the ancestors but even the relatives in Tai’an City wished to kill him.","They simply lacked the strength to do so, which was why they let him go.","Otherwise, Wei Jiuxian wouldn’t have let him go either.","However, the old ancestor of Baoguang Temple had never troubled him over this matter.","This was originally what he feared the most, but with the Immortal Master around, he no longer feared it.","Yet unexpectedly, that old ancestor hadn’t made things difficult for him at all. He had even instructed the Guardian to help preserve the imperial consort’s body.","But now, the Guardian wanted to take the life force from the imperial consort’s body and use it to resurrect the princess from back then.","She was a witness to the glory of the Great Tang Dynasty, and the entire dynasty had changed because of her.","It was also because of her that the Great Tang Dynasty attracted its first imperial son-in-law.","Which led to the flourishing age of the Great Tang.","“No wonder the old ancestor of Baoguang Temple was so kind; it turns out he had his eyes on this life force. Little girl, I advise you to give up this idea. Seeing that you’ve guarded this body for so many years, this old man can help you ascend!” Immortal Jiu Chen sounded quite polite at this moment.","It wasn’t out of kindness; he was just worried that the old ancestor of Baoguang Temple had left some tricks for the Guardian.","Now that the grand plan was nearing completion, he didn’t want any mishaps at this critical juncture.","Because this place was extremely important, and any accident would render all previous efforts futile.","However, the Guardian seemed determined to take that life force, as if she had swallowed an iron weight.","The three of them argued endlessly, and tension gradually filled the air.","“Li Miao, you will regret this decision!” the Guardian sneered, saying no more.","Her words were full of threats, which made both Immortal Jiu Chen and Li Miao very displeased, but they didn’t dare to act rashly at such a crucial moment.","They could only grit their teeth and endure.","“Agree to her terms, but first, revive the imperial consort. After you take the essence from her body, there should still be some life force left. Reviving a mere mortal should be possible!” Immortal Jiu Chen secretly sent a message to Li Miao, choosing not to confront her directly.","Li Miao, upon hearing this, could only nod in agreement. After softening his tone, he said to the Guardian, “I won’t give you all the life force, but I promise to revive the princess. Will that suffice?”","“But the princess must be revived first!” the Guardian’s tone remained firm.","This time, even Immortal Jiu Chen couldn’t hold back. He angrily shouted, “Don’t push your luck! Don’t think that just because you have some cards up your sleeve, you can test my patience!”","As he spoke, he unleashed the full pressure of his divine form at its peak, intending to make the Guardian submit.","But to his surprise, the Guardian remained unaffected and even sneered, “Old fool, don’t think I don’t know your secrets. You’re not even human! Don’t bother trying those petty tricks with me. The trump cards the old ancestor left me are more than enough to kill both of you! The old ancestor instructed me not to act unless absolutely necessary. Do you really think I fear you?”","“Not human?”","Upon hearing these words, Jian Wushuang was stunned. Could it be that Immortal Jiu Chen wasn’t human?","This was something he had never anticipated!","Reflecting on how the other party had been slain before reappearing, and now wielding such immense power, it made sense. But if he wasn’t human, what could he be?","Initially, Jian Wushuang had guessed that the other party was an ancient cultivator who had simply remained in the mortal world. But to think that he wasn’t of the human race?","Yet he possessed a human soul.","At this moment, the debate had not ceased.","“You!”","Li Miao’s face turned ashen, but he managed to suppress his anger. He then turned to Immortal Jiu Chen and directly asked, “Immortal, is there a compromise?”","“Sigh!” Immortal Jiu Chen let out a long sigh, frowning as he said, “Li Miao, ascension doesn’t necessarily require shattering the void. Do you understand what I mean?”","These words indicated that the Immortal might abandon him.","The life force within the Empress’s body had to be kept intact for her resurrection. Only after she was revived could a portion of it be extracted. But before that, it couldn’t be tampered with—if even a trace was removed, the remaining life force would instantly dissipate.","Now, it seemed necessary to give up the Empress and his future!","Jian Wushuang, who had been eavesdropping, also grasped their intentions.","He couldn’t help but feel a pang of regret in his heart: “What a waste, that’s life force! A priceless treasure that can enhance one’s life genes, yet they’re thinking of reviving the Empress and then extracting that bit of essence from her. It’s like dropping a watermelon to pick up a sesame seed!”","Jian Wushuang really wanted to jump out and explain the uniqueness of life force to them, but unfortunately, this was not the right moment. Otherwise, he would have been slapped twice by the other party.","Inside the cave, a brief silence fell.","The Guardian still held his head high, a vague sense of transcendence between his brows.","Immortal Jiu Chen, on the other hand, had his head lowered, appearing harmless.","Li Miao, who had suffered a blow, clenched his fists, and with his eyes slightly closed, he reminisced about his time with the Empress and the beautiful moments they had shared. Tears welled up and fell from the corners of his eyes.","This was his final act of tenderness for her.","“Alright!”","He uttered just one word, then took a deep breath and continued, “The shackles on the Empress have already been unlocked. You can extract that power now!”","A light flickered over the Empress’s body as the seal was lifted.","If it weren’t for this seal, the Guardian would have long since taken the life force.","“Hmph, at least you have some conscience. Once the princess is revived, you can continue to reign as the emperor of the Tang Dynasty!”","After the Guardian spoke, the ring on his finger glowed briefly, and a green stone coffin appeared out of thin air.","Inside lay the princess of the early Tang Dynasty.","Though she was Li Miao’s ancestor, he felt no excitement.","Immortal Jiu Chen, standing silently on the side, had a changed look in his eyes as he gazed at Li Miao.","The Guardian first probed the life force within the Empress’s body before opening the stone coffin.","The lid was lifted, revealing a face of unparalleled beauty.","It was a countenance that could unsettle anyone’s mind at first glance.","Even Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but be astonished. This peerless face could easily rank among the top hundred he had seen in his life."]},{"number":6343,"title":"Chapter 6343: Master-Disciple Relationship","paragraphs":["Chapter 6343: Master-Disciple Relationship","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","One had to understand that the people he had met were more numerous than the meals these people had eaten.","To be ranked within the top hundred in his eyes was an honor that the entire Crimson Eye Realm should be proud of.","If this princess were to be revived, offering incense and kowtowing to him in the future would be only fitting.","Because he was the great Universe God!","But before he could avert his gaze from that face, a streak of black light suddenly shot out.","The black light, sharp as a blade, pierced straight into the Guardian’s chest.","The black mist seeping from above instantly corroded both the Guardian’s soul and body, leaving no time for him to muster his Thought power.","As a result, he couldn’t make a counter move.","“Immortal Jiu Chen, you...” Li Miao was also startled.","There had been no prior signs, and he had already resigned himself to the worst—he was willing to abandon the imperial consort and not affect the grand plan.","He was even prepared to give up his own chance to shatter the void and ascend.","Yet, at this critical moment, Immortal Jiu Chen unexpectedly killed the Guardian, without giving any hint beforehand!","“Stop standing there in a daze. Quickly gather up your ancestor, and let’s get down to business!” Immortal Jiu Chen retracted the black light blade and let out a sigh of relief.","He had only been seventy percent confident in that move.","If he had failed, it would have risked ruining the entire plan.","But this was a risk he was willing to take, and he had no regrets.","Li Miao retrieved the stone coffin and turned to look at Immortal Jiu Chen, his eyes slightly reddened.","“Hey, hey, don’t say anything. We’re just partners; don’t overthink it. I only want you to become stronger so you don’t drag me down in the future!” Immortal Jiu Chen waved his hand dismissively, showing no concern.","Even with a heart of stone, Li Miao silently accepted this great favor at that moment.","The reason he always called the other party “Immortal Master” was because, to him, the other was no different from his own master.","He just hadn’t formally become his disciple, and since the other claimed to be Immortal Jiu Chen, he had continued to address him as Immortal Master.","At this moment, the bond between master and disciple transcended everything.","With just a glance, the two began their plan to resurrect the imperial consort.","The first step was to bring Chen Yuan over, and Li Miao immediately took out a token to issue the command.","Bringing a mortal over naturally didn’t require his personal involvement.","But what he didn’t know was that Chen Yuan was no longer in the city but in a castle outside the city.","Jian Wushuang, who had witnessed all of this, had already made arrangements to capture Chen Yuan, instructing them to find Wei Jiuxian, so he wasn’t worried.","However, the relationship between Li Miao and Immortal Jiu Chen made him think there was more to it than met the eye.","The bond between master and disciple was deep.","This significance wasn’t limited to the righteous path; it applied equally to the demonic path.","Even for those who pursued the Dao, it was the same.","In fact, some masters would willingly sacrifice their lives for their disciples, hoping that they could tread the great path that the masters themselves had never reached.","It was akin to the relationship between a father and son.","If the father couldn’t achieve something, he would hope that his son could. If the son failed, he would be disappointed but wouldn’t lose faith.","But if the son could fulfill his expectations, or even surpass them, the father would be willing to die contentedly.","This was the legacy of Dao seekers.","It was extreme.","Jian Wushuang neither liked it nor hated it.","After observing for so long, he hadn’t heard anything about the altar. Now that they intended to resurrect the imperial concubine, it didn’t concern him much.","However, the life force within the concubine greatly tempted him.","His current body was forged within the Space Realm.","Skipping the process of refining his body, once he regained his mastery of space, he could quickly elevate his physical body to a new level.","But his life force was lacking. If he could obtain that life force at this moment, he could use it to comprehend the Dao and advance his body to master the Dao of All Things ahead of time.","This would greatly help him return to his peak.","But since he hadn’t found the altar yet and hadn’t sensed the sealed power, revealing himself now and seizing the life force would only alert the enemy.","Moreover, there were external threats like the Ghost Emperor and the demons.","Even if he obtained the life force, it would be hard to strengthen himself in a short time.","The risk wasn’t worth it.","Fortunately, after the resurrection of the imperial concubine, that life force wouldn’t vanish. He still had a chance to claim it. But reviving the concubine required Chen Yuan, so he had to make a choice now.","With a thought, Jian Wushuang sent a message to Xiang Yang.","All that remained was to stay hidden carefully.","To observe this human tragedy as a bystander!","But those outside weren’t so lucky.","...","Outside Mangshan County City.","Yang Xiao led Xiang Yang and the others to the ancient castle, where they met Wei Jiuxian.","Qianzu Saintess also followed, discovering that all the strong members of her tribe had died. She collapsed on the spot.","Fortunately, Wei Jiuxian wasn’t a petty person; otherwise, she wouldn’t have survived.","The others were fine.","After all, it wasn’t their people who died.","When Yang Xiao saw Wei Jiuxian, he immediately knelt on one knee and respectfully reported, “Commander, in the city...”","He relayed everything he had witnessed.","Wei Jiuxian merely nodded indifferently and said, “Stay here for now. There’s probably no safer place than this.”","“Oh?” Xiang Yang raised an eyebrow, just about to retort, but when he felt the oppressive force from afar, his expression changed instantly.","He was all too familiar with that power—it was the aura of demons.","“So strong!”","Before he could marvel, he received a message from Jian Wushuang.","The message was simple: send Chen Yuan into Tai’an City.","Even if someone tried to take Chen Yuan, don’t fight back.","Xiang Yang found this odd. Wouldn’t that allow the Tang Emperor to revive the imperial concubine?","Could this somehow benefit Jian Wushuang?","Though he had his doubts, he still followed Jian Wushuang’s instructions.","This time, however, he laid out the consequences for Chen Yuan.","There was no need to deceive a mortal.","Moreover, Chen Yuan had always harbored guilt. When he learned that he was the key to reviving the imperial concubine, he resolutely walked toward Tai’an City.","Wei Jiuxian, of course, knew this and didn’t stop Chen Yuan.","Instead, he curiously sized up Xiang Yang.","At the same time, Chen Yuan rushed toward Tai’an City.","A group of black-clad, masked demonic cultivators also headed his way, reducing a lot of trouble by converging on him.","But they were still detected by Zhen Xian and Fu Qing.","However, both were entangled with the Ghost Emperor.","They couldn’t afford to be careless.","Nor did they have the time to deal with these small fry.","Several Daoists at the Divine Form Realm focused their full attention on besieging the Ghost Emperor.","This bought time for the demonic cultivators of Chiyang Sect.","After binding Chen Yuan tightly, they tossed him into the well where Jian Wushuang had entered.","A force pulled Chen Yuan into an underground palace.","Li Miao watched him calmly and dispelled the restraints with a wave of his hand. He said in a steady voice, “Chen Yuan, you must have known this day would come, right?”","“No,” Chen Yuan shook his head and replied, “But a senior has enlightened me, so I’ve come to terms with it!”"]},{"number":6344,"title":"Chapter 6344: Exposed","paragraphs":["Chapter 6344: Exposed","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Oh? Is that the cultivator from the Jiang Kingdom?” Immortal Jiu Chen suddenly showed interest.","Earlier, when Jian Wushuang had annihilated so many ghost cultivators in one move, Jiu Chen had already noticed him. However, Jian Wushuang had mysteriously disappeared later on. At the time, Jiu Chen had been busy controlling the grand formation and didn’t have the extra energy to pay further attention.","Now, upon hearing the mention of him again, he remembered that there was still a troublesome person who had yet to reveal himself.","Jiu Chen was quite wary of Jian Wushuang, for two reasons: one, Jian Wushuang could burn Thought power; and two, his Nine Prison Pagoda had fallen into Jian Wushuang’s hands.","“My life is only for resurrecting the Empress. Don’t even think about getting anything else out of me!” Chen Yuan, in that moment, exhibited the same righteous spirit as he had when he was a scholar.","Immortal Jiu Chen sneered, “Do you think you can hide it from me?”","With his strength, he could easily perform a soul search.","Asking questions was merely a formality.","If time weren’t pressing, he would have definitely searched Chen Yuan’s soul.","But right now, there was no need to waste time; advancing the plan was of utmost importance.","Even if that troublesome cultivator from the Jiang Kingdom posed some difficulties, once the plan succeeded, it wouldn’t matter anymore.","Li Miao, on the other hand, was quite curious about Jiang Shang.","His appearance and aura closely resembled that of the woman who had once saved Empress Yi many years ago.","“Alright, let’s begin!” Immortal Jiu Chen urged, then started gathering the spiritual bodies within the formation to begin the resurrection ritual for the Empress.","Outside, there was a Ghost Emperor, and here, there was another one.","However, this Ghost Emperor was different from the one outside.","This Ghost Emperor was a simplified version, with a much weaker aura, just right for a mortal.","“Li Miao, inject the soul body into Yi Ren’s body first, and leave the rest to me!” Immortal Jiu Chen handed the soul body to Li Miao, then walked towards Chen Yuan. With a sinister smile, he said calmly, “Young man, don’t worry. What I need is the karma on your body, not your life!”","At this, Li Miao also nodded, indicating that he wouldn’t take Chen Yuan’s life.","There was no need to kill the goose that laid the golden eggs; taking some karma was sufficient.","After all, he was a seeker of the Dao, not a madman who killed for pleasure. He wouldn’t add unnecessary slaughter.","Chen Yuan, however, appeared calm. Even if they intended to take his life, he didn’t care.","The world worked in mysterious ways.","When you were ready to die courageously, your opponent might just spare you one last mercy—not killing you, but instead taking away your final value, leaving you to face a woman full of guilt.","The main reason Chen Yuan wasn’t afraid of death was because he couldn’t face the Empress. The second reason was that he missed A’Zi.","In this world, there were gods and immortals, as well as vengeful spirits and fierce ghosts. Perhaps, if he died, he would be able to see A’Zi again.","But now, he couldn’t die.","Immortal Jiu Chen struck out with a palm. Chen Yuan showed no reaction, but his soul was forced out of his body.","As a soul, Chen Yuan felt an odd sensation in his body. Before he could get accustomed to it, Immortal Jiu Chen’s claw reached towards his forehead, extracting a strand of golden causality.","This was akin to a mundane version of the Causality Tribulation.","“Li Miao, step back!”","Immortal Jiu Chen held the causality thread and pressed it into the forehead of the imperial consort.","The causality thread, soul body, life force, and the remaining wisp of the imperial consort’s soul began to fuse.","Several forces repelled each other but gradually started to merge in Immortal Jiu Chen’s hands.","Once fully integrated, the imperial consort’s consciousness would be restored.","That was the major part.","The next task was to restore the body.","Li Miao was not idle either. The refined blood of cultivators he had collected earlier was intended for the imperial consort’s physical body.","Not only did he want to revive the imperial consort, but he also wanted her to reach the Infant Transformation level after revival, matching his own realm. Only then could he use her refined blood to break through to the Divine Aspect realm.","“Silence!”","Li Miao called softly.","A blood pool gradually manifested in the cave, finally solidifying.","Jian Wushuang, witnessing this scene, suddenly narrowed his eyes, his heart filled with shock. “No wonder my thought power couldn’t detect it. The altar wasn’t in this space!”","He immediately understood where the altar had been summoned from.","It should have come from a spatial rift.","The altar did not exist in this space, or more specifically, in the Scarlet Eye Realm.","If he were to search for it, he wouldn’t have found it, even if he scoured all of Mangshan County.","But how did Qianzu Saintess know about it?","This was a point of suspicion.","As for why several major powers had descended here, it was likely due to information deliberately leaked by Li Miao and Immortal Jiu Chen.","In that case, Qianzu Saintess was probably just a pawn, manipulated by Li Miao and Immortal Jiu Chen.","At this thought, Jian Wushuang felt a chill run down his spine. In an instant, he regained his human form.","Because he had been exposed.","If they could locate the spatial rift and even place the altar within it, then either Immortal Jiu Chen or Li Miao must have had profound knowledge of spatial manipulation. No matter how thoroughly he concealed himself, his presence would be detected, even if his thought power covered everything.","So, he revealed himself immediately.","Since the altar had appeared, his goal had been achieved.","He desired both the life force and the sealed power within the altar.","His sudden appearance did not surprise Li Miao and Immortal Jiu Chen. It was as if everything had been calculated in advance.","As soon as he emerged, the altar emitted a beam of blood-red light, directly shining upon Jian Wushuang.","“Haha, we’ve been waiting for you!” Immortal Jiu Chen formed a hand seal and roared, “Bloodlight Technique, absorb!”","Buzz!","A powerful force pulled Jian Wushuang towards the altar.","Chen Yuan, watching this unfold, was also shocked. He hadn’t expected Jian Wushuang to be here, and from the looks of it, Jian Wushuang had clearly been trapped.","“Thought power, ignite!”","Jian Wushuang was unwilling to be defeated. He had come prepared and wouldn’t be captured so easily.","His burning divine power enveloped his entire body as he desperately resisted the bloodlight’s pull.","He had no intention of becoming nourishment for the altar.","However, Immortal Jiu Chen sneered at this moment. “Jian Wushuang, do you think your thought power can block everything? You underestimate me, Jiu Chen. You won’t be able to withstand it!”","“Moreover, the reason I’m called Jiu Chen is because I’ve experienced nine different worlds and know far more than you can imagine. Don’t think that just because you defeated me once, you can do as you please. This time, you’ll lose everything, including your powerful soul, which will become nourishment for the altar!”","Li Miao didn’t know much about Jian Wushuang and simply watched him coldly.","The overwhelming suction power made it impossible for Jian Wushuang to resist, even though he had pushed his thought power to its limits.","Buzz!","His body and soul had already begun to separate.","This time, he was truly done for.","If his soul entered the altar, it would be annihilated.","He wasn’t too concerned about death.","Trapped in this world, he had thought about what would happen if his soul was extinguished. Would he return to the Realm God Continent, or would he reincarnate in this world?","If he returned to the Realm God Continent, then he would immediately return to his true self.","That would, of course, be the best outcome.","If he entered the reincarnation cycle of this world, then he would reincarnate.","But which world he would be reborn in was uncertain.","However, doing so would waste his time.","And he was unwilling to be outsmarted by mere mortals."]},{"number":6345,"title":"Chapter 6345: Where’s the Nine Prison Pagoda?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6345: Where’s the Nine Prison Pagoda?","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The greatest threat he feared was that if his soul were annihilated, it would neither return to the Realm God Continent nor to the reincarnation of this world.","If that happened, his true self would fall into slumber, and he would truly be doomed.","Even though the possibility was slim, he dared not take the gamble.","Currently, he could not endure the absorption of the blood light. Once he entered the altar, he feared he would have no choice.","Therefore, he decided to self-destruct his soul before entering the altar.","Don’t forget, his soul body within the Nine Prison Pagoda was considered the true self in this world.","However, the Nine Prison Pagoda originally belonged to Immortal Jiu Chen, and he worried that Jiu Chen might have tampered with it. Thus, he wanted to destroy his current soul to prevent Jiu Chen from gaining any leverage over him.","But just as he was about to self-destruct, a burst of blood light flashed, and a guiding force sent him into the altar.","“Haha, success! This guy’s soul power is much stronger than the refined Ghost Emperor. With him as nourishment, I no longer need that Ghost Emperor. I can finally kill that Zhen Xian and Fu Qing! Then, I’ll refine a body for the Ghost Emperor that surpasses the Divine Form Realm, and he’ll have the strength to take revenge!” Immortal Jiu Chen was overjoyed, revealing many things in his excitement.","Li Miao was also happy, feeling pleased for Immortal Jiu Chen.","But before they could celebrate for long, they noticed a change in the Empress’s body.","“Not good, her life force is fading! We need to revive her immediately!” Immortal Jiu Chen exclaimed in shock.","What he didn’t know was that before Jian Wushuang entered the altar, his Thought power had drawn the Empress’s life force into his own soul.","Such a technique was beyond Jiu Chen’s detection.","Now, seeing the Empress’s life force fading, he assumed it was due to the recent delay. He hurriedly performed a secret revival technique to carry out the final resurrection.","Fortunately, the prior fusion was almost complete. Otherwise, if the life force were to fade entirely, there would be no way to reverse it, and the fusion would be impossible.","At least for now, he could save half of her life. The remaining half could be restored using the power of the blood-colored altar’s seal, allowing the Empress to ascend to the same realm as Li Miao.","“This time, nothing will go wrong!”","Immortal Jiu Chen wiped the sweat from his forehead, revealing a satisfied smile. He said, “I will use the altar’s power to restore the Empress’s remaining half of her life while also elevating her to the Infant Formation stage. As for what comes next, I’ll leave it to you!”","“Rest assured, Immortal Master!” Li Miao also smiled.","Despite the twists in the plan, nothing had hindered its progress.","After seeing Chen Yuan’s soul and Jian Wushuang’s body, Immortal Jiu Chen found them a bit of an eyesore and immediately ordered someone to take them away and seal them under the well.","Once everything succeeded, Chen Yuan could live.","But when he stepped forward to inspect Jian Wushuang’s body, his brows furrowed.","“How could it be missing?” Immortal Jiu Chen was stunned.","Li Miao asked with concern, “What’s wrong?”","“The Nine Prison Pagoda isn’t on him!!!” Immortal Jiu Chen immediately flew into a rage. That was a priceless treasure!","He had assumed Jian Wushuang would have stored it within his body, but after searching, it wasn’t there.","He immediately turned to Chen Yuan’s soul, and without waiting for him to speak, he initiated a soul search.","After thoroughly investigating everything related to Jian Wushuang, he was even more puzzled.","“How could this be? The Nine Prison Pagoda was clearly taken by him. How could it be missing?”","This touched upon his blind spot.","The Nine Prison Pagoda was a treasure, and with preliminary control, one could manipulate its size at will.","If fully mastered, it could fuse with one’s body.","But this was no ordinary treasure!","Even those beyond the Ancestral Realm couldn’t recognize it, only a true immortal could.","Yet, even if recognized, it should have merged with the body.","He shouldn’t have been unable to find it.","In his mind, only one possibility remained.","“He must have given the Nine Prison Pagoda to someone else!!” Immortal Jiu Chen gritted his teeth and said, “Forget it. Once we’ve succeeded, I’ll search for it again!”","After all, no one could truly refine the Nine Prisons, so it couldn’t escape his grasp.","He waved his hand, instructing the Chiyang Sect cultivators to take Jian Wushuang’s body and Chen Yuan’s soul away. Then, he sat cross-legged outside the cave, personally guarding the entrance.","...","Mangshan County City.","The Ghost Emperor grew stronger as the battle raged on, continuously unleashing his innate secret techniques. His combat power had already surpassed the peak of the Divine Aspect Realm.","Zhen Xian and Fu Qing could barely hold their ground.","The other Divine Aspect Realm cultivators could only assist from a distance.","As for the Nascent Soul cultivators, they had long been devoured, leaving not even a trace of their bones behind.","“Senior Brother, the Ghost Emperor’s strength is increasing. If this drags on, it won’t be good for us!” Fu Qing exclaimed, worried.","Zhen Xian felt the same, but with all his cards already played, there was no solution in sight.","“Damn it, dealing with one ancient demon was bad enough, but that little emperor had to go and create this monstrosity!”","Though he was anxious, he wasn’t entirely out of options.","Wasn’t there still another ancient demon outside?","The ancient demon that shattered the heavens had been rampaging, draining the blood of the human race to replenish the energy it had lost during years of being sealed.","Its combat power far exceeded that of the Divine Aspect Realm by a thousandfold.","Taking on this Ghost Emperor, who hadn’t fully matured yet, would be more than enough.","With a plan in mind, Zhen Xian suddenly retreated, his gaze locking onto the formation barrier on the city wall. A sinister grin appeared on his face.","...","Boom!","The deafening explosion from Mangshan County City instantly alarmed everyone in the ancient castle.","Wei Jiuxian furrowed his brows and stood up.","He looked directly towards the commotion in the county city, then turned to the sky behind him. A towering divine demon had descended.","The great battle was about to begin!","The ancient demon versus the Ghost Emperor.","Both sides possessed power that surpassed the peak of the Divine Aspect Realm.","This would be a battle for the ages.","The glory of ancient times would be reborn in this battle!","At this moment, the sky darkened as black clouds covered the faint morning light in the east. A heavy rain was imminent, following a gentle drizzle.","But all of this seemed irrelevant to Jian Wushuang.","His physical body was sealed at the bottom of a well.","It was merely a shell, of no use at all.","What mattered was the soul.","To ensure absolute safety, he had entered the blood-colored altar along with the Nine Prison Pagoda, wrapping his soul in layers of protection.","He had also siphoned the life force from the empress’s body as an additional safeguard.","Even so, he had suffered immensely within the blood-colored altar.","Upon entering, the devouring force seemed capable of absorbing his entire soul.","Fortunately, the Nine Prison Pagoda’s original essence continuously replenished his soul power, making it almost limitless.","After all, replenishing a Divine Aspect peak-level soul with an Origin Source at the Immortal level was relatively easy.","If not for the suppression of the Heavenly Dao, he could have elevated his soul power beyond the Divine Aspect Realm.","But even as a peak-level Divine Aspect soul, it was enough to sustain itself against the altar’s endless absorption.","His soul, now transformed into a stream of water, delved deeper into the altar’s core.","Inside, it was like a new world, though everything around him was shrouded in red mist. This mist flowed rapidly, driven by the devouring force."]},{"number":6346,"title":"Chapter 6346: Blood Crystal Passageway","paragraphs":["Chapter 6346: Blood Crystal Passageway","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang’s soul was intertwined within it.","It took him an entire hour just to pass through the blood mist region.","During that hour, his soul power was greatly depleted.","It was equivalent to the soul power of ten peak-stage Universe Masters.","If it had been an ordinary peak-stage Universe Master, their soul would have long been destroyed.","Fortunately, Jian Wushuang could continuously replenish his soul power and maintain his peak condition. Additionally, the burning Thought power acted as a barrier, allowing him to keep his consciousness clear.","He was also able to continually observe the interior of the blood-colored altar.","Passing through the blood mist region had consumed ten times the soul power of a peak-stage Universe Master.","Beyond that, there was a blood crystal passageway.","Originally, he thought that the devouring force here would be even stronger, but upon entering, he discovered that there was no suction force at all. Instead, the passageway had the miraculous effect of nurturing the soul.","However, this benefit wasn’t of much use to him. He was merely curious—wasn’t this altar supposed to seal the bloodline of a god and demon?","As for the former peak-stage Universe Master, they were likely not sealed but rather refined by this altar.","Over a thousand years ago, it was a Prince Consort of the Great Tang who sealed the Qianzu Saintess.","That same person was also the founder of Baoguang Temple.","If it wasn’t a seal but a refinement, then everything made sense.","At that time, the situation must have been that the altar refined the peak-stage Universe Master, and the so-called seal was a lie.","But now, the altar had ended up in the hands of Immortal Jiu Chen.","Before Jian Wushuang entered the altar, Jiu Chen had mentioned that he had experienced nine different worlds.","Yet, Jiu Chen’s realm and strength weren’t particularly exceptional.","He was merely an ordinary peak-stage Universe Master.","“What exactly was hidden back then?” Jian Wushuang pondered, realizing that this small world concealed far too many secrets.","Perhaps those secrets had little to do with him, but he couldn’t help but marvel at how such a small world could have been so intricately planned out, with such a complex web of relationships.","“Maybe the relationship between that Great Tang ancestor and Jiu Chen was similar to the current relationship with Li Miao!”","He didn’t know that the Great Tang ancestor had already fallen, which made him curious why Jiu Chen chose Li Miao.","But these matters had little relevance to him.","What he needed to do now was to figure out the function of this altar.","Judging from the earlier blood mist, this might not be an altar at all; it resembled more of a small cave world.","Typically, such a cave world would be used by cultivators to tame beasts or cultivate herbs.","After all, carrying around a portable world was rare, and turning it into an altar seemed somewhat wasteful.","Altars like this could easily be made into one-time-use items.","He wasn’t particularly experienced in these matters, but he had seen others use them before.","Thus, he was convinced that the purpose of this place wasn’t as simple as an altar, and its true function would require further exploration.","Jian Wushuang ignited his Thought power and began to explore the depths of the passage.","Nothing unusual happened along the way. He even touched the walls of the passage formed by the blood-colored crystals with his hand.","“This was actually infused with the essence blood of gods and demons. What a grand gesture!” He was somewhat surprised, as the essence blood of gods and demons was a hundred times more powerful than ordinary divine blood.","Moreover, it appeared that the essence blood used came from the mental aspect of gods and demons.","In this way, just entering this place could nourish the soul.","The blood mist outside the passage seemed to be transformed by the power emanating from this place. Inside, it nourished the soul, while outside, it devoured souls.","This setup was quite ingenious.","Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but nod in approval.","But back to the main point, what surprised him even more was the level of this god or demon.","Comparing it to the so-called Ancient Demon from the outside world, the owner of this essence blood had a life gene at least five thousand times stronger than that of ordinary gods and demons.","Based on this, his strength could be estimated to reach the level of transcendence, possibly even the level of a Zhen Xian.","If that was the case, then the owner of this altar had a strength that was at least at the level of a Great Zhen Xian.","Moreover, looking at the appearance of the altar, it did not seem to be a supreme treasure but rather a supplementary artifact.","In terms of value, it certainly couldn’t compare to a supreme treasure.","Considering that Immortal Jiu Chen even possessed supreme treasures, having this kind of supplementary artifact seemed normal.","From this perspective, at his peak, the other party was probably quite formidable.","Even if these treasures were all picked up, he would still need the strength to refine some of them.","“Jiu Chen!”","Jian Wushuang caressed the blood crystal, muttering to himself, “His life level is quite ordinary, and his soul level is also ordinary. He’s far inferior to Zhen Xian or that Sword Immortal. Coming from the upper realms, he was naturally not weak at his peak, but compared to transcendents, he still falls short. Not to mention Zhen Xian. Even so, in the mortal world, his power could far surpass that of ordinary gods. How could Jiu Chen be so weak?”","This was his greatest doubt.","With this doubt in mind, his steps quickened.","His Thought power continued to cover a distance of ten miles ahead.","Therefore, he wasn’t worried about danger.","After walking for a short while, he reached the end of the passage.","At this moment, he also sensed a faint consciousness at the end of the passage.","That consciousness was quite peculiar, devoid of any signs of life and lacking the deathly aura that usually accompanied soul bodies.","However, it exuded a certain spiritual charm.","Jian Wushuang’s eyes lit up, and his pace quickened.","This aura felt familiar, reminding him of the true spirit of Qishen Temple.","The two auras were quite similar.","The difference in strength, however, was like comparing billions of times.","Regardless of the disparity in strength, it was at least a conscious spiritual entity!","This was incredibly useful to Jian Wushuang, as it might help him unravel the mysteries of this place.","Following the aura, he burned his divine power, probing while getting closer.","At the end of the passage stood a temple radiating blood-colored power.","“I’ve arrived!”","Jian Wushuang exited the passage and stood in front of the temple.","From a distance, the temple was right in front of him, but when he closed his eyes, it seemed to be deep within a nebula.","All around him were blood-colored light dots.","“Interesting!”","He slightly curled his lips into a smile. There was little he could do about such a small trick right now.","But the spiritual entity was right in front of him, and he could only start with it.","With a thought, he pointed his finger, sending out a strand of green energy.","It was the life force he had obtained from the empress.","What he needed wasn’t the life force itself but the various principles contained within it.","While in the passage, he had comprehended several principles from it, then transmitted them to his main body within the Nine Prison Pagoda, allowing him to grasp the embryonic form of all things.","In this way, the soul of his main body within the Nine Prison Pagoda could extract the internal power of the pagoda to reshape a physical body of all things.","The more power of all things he absorbed, the stronger the physical body would become.","Once the body reached the level of ten thousand times, it would be at the level of Zhen Xian. At that time, his soul would enter the body of all things, allowing him to leave the Nine Prison Pagoda.","This saved him a lot of time, directly returning to the level of an undying Zhen Xian.","That is, Zhen Xian!","The road ahead would then become much easier."]},{"number":6347,"title":"Chapter 6347: Can’t Walk the Old Road","paragraphs":["Chapter 6347: Can’t Walk the Old Road","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Following the path he had walked before would be enough. First, he would start with transforming the universe from all things, then step into the realm of Dayan Immortal, mastering the ultimate swordsmanship, becoming the Ultimate Dao Monarch, and then merging with the Dao.","With the countless experiences of Jian Wushuang, it would take him only a few hundred years to reach the peak of the Emperor level.","By that time, he would have almost cultivated the power of life from All Things, and with that, he could push forward, evolve the universe of life, and with Sword Dao as his core, open up the universe and become a Universe Master.","Tribulations would be as easy as drinking water.","Breaking through all the way to the Ninth Tribulation would be no problem.","At that moment, it seemed that everything had become simple.","Jian Wushuang suddenly shook his head, a sharp glint flashing in his eyes.","He had only channeled a wisp of life force into that spiritual sense, yet he had directly envisioned his own future.","And it seemed so effortless.","But this was not what he wanted.","Not to mention whether the path ahead would go smoothly, even if he reached the level of Universe Master, the tribulations that followed would not be that simple.","His tribulations were not ordinary cosmic Tribulations.","Otherwise, he wouldn’t be so powerful.","There was also his soul’s thought power, which had become so formidable only because he had devoured the Realm Beast Morosa.","Moreover, in the outside world, he had the augmentation of the Beast God Weapon, and the Wanjie Sword, which contained his Dao, had been nurtured for countless years, allowing him to unleash the sixth sword move.","His true body in the outside world had already reached the peak of Nine-Star Universe God.","He possessed countless fortunes.","Just the Eternal Ancient Transformation alone could trap countless people.","Eternal Ancient Transformation was something he had created based on the Ancient Transformation.","It required mastery of the Dao of Transformation, which he probably couldn’t grasp in this world.","Furthermore, entering this world might have been for the purpose of undergoing the Universe God Tribulation in the first place.","How could he still walk the old path?","But within this world, he didn’t even know if there was a suitable Dao for him.","Sword Dao as the core.","That was the foundation, but relying solely on swordsmanship would be too limited.","A mortal could wander the world with a sword, and a cultivator could resolve grudges with a single stroke.","But beyond that, transcending, becoming immortal, merging with the Dao, opening up a universe—these could not be achieved by swordsmanship alone.","Many auxiliary Daos were also needed.","“Will this world have them?”","“No!”","Jian Wushuang’s gaze instantly became resolute, and his state of mind returned to calm.","“The path I want to walk is unique, unrelated to the world I am in. Every Universe God is a being who breaks the supreme Law Rules, and should not be bound by the Daos under those supreme Law Rules!”","At that moment, he seemed to understand everything.","He also realized the significance of entering this world.","Walking his own path had nothing to do with the world he was in.","Simply put, it was like the life of an ordinary mortal family.","In the Crimson Eye Realm, the children of noble families grew up without worries, mastering various ways to make a fortune upon reaching adulthood. However, the children of poor families, when they became adults, might face a dark reality, feeling the unfairness of the world and realizing that not everyone is treated the same.","But even from humble origins, great individuals could emerge.","Chen Yuan was one such person. Although he didn’t achieve fame through examinations, he made the right choices at the right time and soared to new heights.","If it had been someone else, perhaps they wouldn’t have succeeded.","Was this due to the environment?","No!","It was because of his choices.","Now, Jian Wushuang had the right to make his own choices. He could choose to follow the old path, which might not lead him to the peak, but leaving this world wouldn’t be difficult.","But what would happen after he left this world?","Would he return to being the Jian Wushuang with the combat power of a Ninth Tribulation Universe God?","Was this the purpose of his coming to the Tomb of the Gods?","Leaving Huaiqing and the others behind, he came here to undergo the divine Tribulation, didn’t he?","Back when he left the Northern Starry Sky and arrived at the Realm God Continent, after facing numerous challenges, even Wu Zuo had undergone the divine Tribulation. How could he lag behind?","Moreover, his goal had never been to reach the peak of the Realm God Continent.","It was to step into the Starry Sky.","That was the destination.","But not the ultimate destination.","At this moment, his mind was as sharp as a sword.","He was not influenced in the slightest.","He also realized that the force that had just disturbed his thoughts likely came from that temple.","“A temple that can affect my state of mind? Interesting!”","He casually dispelled that spiritual force but did not rush into the temple.","For now, entering was not possible anyway. Although it appeared close, it was actually still far away.","As life force entered the wisp of spiritual consciousness, it quickly stimulated the other party’s spiritual power.","“Whoosh!”","The illusory spirit began to take shape, and a familiar face appeared before him.","“Immortal Jiu Chen!!!”","Jian Wushuang was startled, and the other party was also taken aback.","They stared at each other for a while before simultaneously asking:","“How do you know me?”","“What are you doing here?”","“You go first!” Their synchronization was impeccable.","But then they reached an impasse. However, Jian Wushuang wasn’t in a hurry, while the other party was growing impatient.","From his tone, it was clear that he had been dormant for who knew how many years. Now, seeing a half-living person who recognized his identity filled his heart with joy. He was eager to know what had happened outside.","This made Jian Wushuang realize that although this person looked exactly like Jiu Chen, his identity might not be the same.","There were more deductions and guesses, but those needed to be clarified by the other party.","“I’ve met someone exactly like you in the outside world, but he wasn’t a spirit; he had a physical body!” Jian Wushuang answered the question directly, without holding back.","The spiritual Jiu Chen’s excitement surged instantly, becoming somewhat frenzied as he muttered to himself, “He actually succeeded, he really succeeded!”","Although Jian Wushuang didn’t know exactly what the other party was referring to, he could make an educated guess.","“No wonder Jiu Chen had such a high level of cultivation, vast knowledge, and even the ability to initially control a treasure like the Nine Prison Pagoda. It turns out he wasn’t human after all!”","This was entirely literal.","If Jian Wushuang guessed correctly, Jiu Chen and this spirit were likely one and the same.","Perhaps he was a formation spirit or the spirit of a treasure.","This also explained why the other party was so powerful yet so seemingly ordinary.","So at this moment, Jian Wushuang concocted another lie.","“Are you the one my original self sent here?” Jiu Chen’s spirit asked in surprise, “Could it be that he rebuilt the Heavenly Fire Realm?”","This question made Jian Wushuang sweat a bit because it wasn’t within his calculations.","“The Ancient Realm isn’t that easy to rebuild. Outside, Immortal Jiu Chen established the Crimson Eye Realm!” He continued to bluff, “I inherited Immortal Jiu Chen’s legacy and came here, never expecting you to be Immortal Jiu Chen’s incarnation!”","Upon hearing that he was an incarnation, Jiu Chen’s spirit roared angrily, “What do you know? I am the original! That guy is just a fragment of my consciousness that split off! I can’t believe he gambled right and became an immortal!”","His eyes widened in rage.","Jian Wushuang didn’t expect the other party to be so easily deceived. Fortunately, he had respectfully called him Immortal Jiu Chen, which allowed the other party to realize that Jian Wushuang belonged to Jiu Chen’s side."]},{"number":6348,"title":"Chapter 6348: Fraud","paragraphs":["Chapter 6348: Fraud","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Impossible! Immortal Jiu Chen has already transcended existence, and yet you, with your mere spiritual body, dare to impersonate him?” Jian Wushuang spoke with a tone of feigned anger, as if deeply loyal to Immortal Jiu Chen.","This only made the real Jiu Chen even more furious. He clutched his head and roared, “No! I am the real one! He is just a fragment of my consciousness. He could never surpass me!”","“But you’re very weak right now!” Jian Wushuang raised an eyebrow, intentionally provoking him.","This statement dealt a heavy blow to Jiu Chen’s fragile consciousness, nearly causing him to fall into slumber. Fortunately, with the life force he possessed, Jian Wushuang was able to use his soul power to help nourish Jiu Chen’s spiritual awareness, preventing him from slipping into unconsciousness.","“Hm?” The awakened Jiu Chen finally noticed the strength of Jian Wushuang’s soul and exclaimed in surprise, “You mentioned earlier that you arrived here through the blood mist?”","Jian Wushuang lifted his head proudly and replied calmly, “That’s right. I came here to receive the inheritance.”","As he spoke, he glanced at the distant temple.","That grand hall undoubtedly contained the inheritance. Jiu Chen must have been the true spirit of this inheritance hall. However, this spirit had grown restless and wanted to break free from the temple to become a cultivator.","From Jiu Chen’s earlier words, it was clear that this was indeed the case.","Upon hearing that Jian Wushuang had passed through the blood mist, Jiu Chen’s face lit up with joy, as if he had completely forgotten about the mockery from just moments ago.","“You actually made it through the blood mist! It seems that even if my clone failed to rebuild the Heavenly Fire Domain, it still managed to establish a remarkable power!” Jiu Chen’s excitement grew palpable.","Jian Wushuang narrowed his eyes as he observed Jiu Chen, wondering what the spirit was plotting. Why did he get so excited upon hearing about the blood mist?","The blood mist outside didn’t seem all that powerful. As long as one’s soul power reached about ten times the normal level, it was barely passable.","Reaching ten times the soul power wasn’t that difficult, right?","At least, before transcending, increasing one’s soul power was quite simple.","However, after transcending, it became extremely difficult to enhance soul power, especially after becoming immortal. Raising soul power would be as hard as ascending to the heavens. This was why soul cultivation methods were so rare—few could meet the standards required for practicing such techniques.","Hence, they were considered precious and mysterious!","But that was a matter for after transcendence or immortality.","In the mortal phase, permanently enhancing soul power beyond tenfold was relatively easy.","Jian Wushuang had experienced the mortal world and didn’t find passing through the blood mist to be particularly remarkable.","After all, Jiu Chen’s original world was the Ancient Domain, far larger than the Crimson Eye Realm. Encountering geniuses with tenfold soul power wasn’t uncommon, so why was he so shocked?","While Jian Wushuang pondered this, Jiu Chen suddenly spoke with excitement, “Kid, being able to pass through the blood mist means your thought power has exceeded tenfold. And walking the Path to Heaven means your thought power can withstand a hundredfold! In the Heavenly Fire Domain of yore, such a genius hadn’t appeared in tens of thousands of years. Today, I’ve finally encountered one, and it’s thanks to the dumb luck of my clone that you’re here! My past decisions weren’t wrong after all, hahaha!”","A hundredfold soul power?","Jian Wushuang was stunned. He could hardly believe it and instinctively turned to look at the passageway behind him.","“How could there be a hundredfold soul power...?”","At first, he spoke earnestly, but as he continued, he suddenly realized the truth.","He had been burning his soul power all along, and unknowingly, it had already reached a hundredfold. He simply hadn’t noticed, which was why passing through the blood-colored passage seemed so effortless.","Immortal Jiu Chen’s true form had been slow to react, previously caught up in his own words, which had inadvertently led to confusion. Now, as clarity returned, he finally spoke about this matter.","“A hundredfold soul power—that’s quite challenging!” Jian Wushuang thought to himself.","If it were tenfold soul power, that would be within the realm of normality. However, a hundredfold soul power required an innate talent.","Innate divine abilities were abilities that came naturally to beings born with them.","Innate beings, like ancient demons—also known as divine demons—had life levels that were hundreds or even thousands of times that of ordinary humans. This was considered normal in the eyes of the strong.","However, when it came to soul power, everyone was on equal footing.","Enhancing one’s soul power required diligent effort over time.","But upon reaching a certain level, one could create special beings on their own.","For example, Jian Wushuang’s true form could create special life forms within his own universe, elevating their life levels by tens of thousands of times without issue.","Beyond life levels, it was also possible to create beings with unique souls.","For instance, a newborn might have a soul level ten times that of an ordinary being, and by adulthood, it could reach a hundredfold. This wasn’t a problem.","Life and soul were different concepts.","Life levels could easily reach thousands or even tens of thousands of times higher, but enhancing the soul to such a degree was extraordinarily difficult.","If not for devouring a Boundary Beast, his own mental thought power would never have surpassed that of a Universe God.","Although he was a Universe Master, his soul could rival that of a Time-Space God.","He had surpassed two entire levels.","And it wasn’t just any small leap—it was a monumental one.","If it were a matter of divine power, that would be relatively simple.","As a Universe Master, achieving a combat power comparable to a Time-Space God was something he had nearly accomplished.","But when it came to soul power, without the encounters he had within the Realm King’s divine realm, no matter how much effort or genius he put into it, he wouldn’t have been able to reach this level.","Such was the uniqueness of the soul.","The world within the altar, from the blood mist to the blood-colored passage, all tested one’s soul. It seemed that the requirements of that temple for the soul were extremely high.","His current soul, though still an ordinary soul, could reach a hundredfold strength through burning his soul to enhance his thought power.","“So that’s how it is!”","Jian Wushuang, suddenly understanding, refrained from further provoking Immortal Jiu Chen’s true form.","He needed to enter the temple.","Enhancing his current soul would expedite the recovery of his true soul within the Nine Prison Pagoda.","Inside the Nine Prison Pagoda, whether or not he had a physical body did not affect breaking through the first level.","Therefore, enhancing his soul would help him enter the second level.","Developing a peak-level treasure was the fastest way to boost his strength.","Moreover, he now understood that re-entering the mundane world to cultivate again meant he had to tread a unique path.","He had to abandon everything.","He had to shed his arrogance.","His previous experiences could be used, but not recklessly.","He had to walk the path of cultivation to its true pinnacle.","“Then let’s start with the soul!”","Jian Wushuang’s heart was as firm as a rock!","He conversed with this ancient true spirit, who had slumbered for tens of thousands of years, for a full hour.","Both of them opened up new worldviews.","At that moment, Immortal Jiu Chen’s true form had a vision of a small world connected to the ancient domain in his mind.","The master of this small world was a fragment of his consciousness, known as Immortal Jiu Chen, who had now reached the level of Yan Immortal.","And the young man before him came from a group of geniuses under Immortal Jiu Chen, entering this place to receive the inheritance.","Before him, countless other geniuses had entered, but none had left alive."]},{"number":6349,"title":"Chapter 6349: Sequence Inheritance","paragraphs":["Chapter 6349: Sequence Inheritance","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang was the first to arrive at the temple.","There were many details, and Jian Wushuang explained them in great detail, almost convincing himself of their truth.","Of course, it was all a lie he had fabricated. Whether the other party believed him or not, he didn’t know, but he himself had come to believe it.","In his mind, a world also appeared.","It was an ancient domain before its destruction.","The Upper Realm had 108 ancient domains.","He had heard Qianzu Saintess mention that later, 36 of these ancient domains shattered, forming countless small worlds.","The Crimson Eye Realm was one of them.","Before these 36 ancient domains collapsed, they had also been glorious.","The Heavenly Fire Domain, where Immortal Jiu Chen resided, was one of them.","At that time, the Heavenly Fire Domain was the Origin Source of the Flame Emperor.","This Origin Source was naturally innate. For the acquired to possess an Origin Source, one had to become an Emperor.","Although the Upper Realm was vast, there likely weren’t any Emperor-level figures.","Moreover, from Jiu Chen’s description, Jian Wushuang could deduce that the Flame Emperor was a divine demon.","A special life form of the fire path, born with divine flames.","At that time, besides the Flame Emperor’s Flame Dragon Palace, there was another grand palace in the Heavenly Fire Domain that was equally renowned.","“The Divine Fire Palace!”","It was the grand palace before them.","This palace had been arranged by a supreme being within the Divine Eye Clan.","“The First Sequence Legacy Hall!”","The Divine Eye legacy was divided into five major sequences.","The first sequence was the strongest.","The fifth sequence was the weakest.","However, within the Divine Eye Clan, strength was not the sole determinant.","Some had even cultivated legacies from two different sequences, and their power had surpassed those who had only inherited the first sequence.","Therefore, the initial legacy one accepted wasn’t too important; what mattered was dual cultivation.","To merge all five sequences into one was a heaven-defying feat.","However, even in the 108 ancient domains back then, those who could merge two sequences were as rare as phoenix feathers, and the merging of three sequences was merely a legend.","“Each sequence has 36 types of legacies, and the five major sequences have a total of 108 legacies. To merge other sequences, one must first complete all 36 legacies within the initial sequence. This alone has stumped countless cultivators!” Jiu Chen’s original body shook his head with a bitter smile and said, “Not to mention, just the foundational legacies required for the first sequence—I haven’t encountered a single person capable of mastering them in tens of thousands of years!”","Jian Wushuang took a deep breath and nodded.","He had learned about the uniqueness of the Divine Eye legacy.","At the same time, he admired this clan greatly, and even more so the strong individual who had created the Divine Eye legacy. He wondered just how powerful that person had been.","To create such a heaven-defying legacy, they must have been at least a Universe God.","“So, you’re the true spirit of the Divine Fire Palace? Created by a powerhouse of the Divine Eye Clan back then?”","Jiu Chen nodded and said, “It seems you know quite a lot. At your level, to know this much, you must hold a high position in the Crimson Eye Realm!”","“I’m the current Dao Child. My master has told me many things!” Jian Wushuang lied without even blinking, leaving the other party stunned.","This, too, was a talent, Jian Wushuang thought to himself.","“You don’t even need to say it. If a cultivator like you, with a soul power a hundred times stronger than ordinary people, isn’t a Dao Child, then my clone must be blind!” Jiu Chen was in a good mood, but he didn’t hold back when cursing his own clone.","Jian Wushuang respectfully said, “Senior, since I’ve arrived here, shouldn’t I enter the Divine Fire Palace to receive the legacy?”","He had gathered almost all the information he needed. The only thing he was still puzzled about was why the other party wanted to break free from this palace and transform into a cultivator.","Perhaps it was due to ambition, or maybe the formation within the temple had malfunctioned, causing the True Spirit to lose its restraints.","The final reason could be that the master who established the temple had perished.","This was the most likely possibility.","The formation malfunctioned, and with the restraints gone, the True Spirit developed ambition.","But how could the first-sequence inheritance created by a supreme powerhouse possibly have issues with its formation?","Most likely, that existence had already fallen, and the soul imprint on the True Spirit had been exhausted, allowing it to break free.","The remaining true form was loyal and devoted.","The clone that left was the manifestation of that ambition.","This revealed the cunning wisdom of Qishen back then.","By splitting his consciousness to create the True Spirit, the issue of betrayal never existed.","Since he himself was the True Spirit, how could he betray himself?","Even if he fell, there was nothing to fear.","Upon hearing that Jian Wushuang intended to enter the Divine Fire Temple, Immortal Jiu Chen’s expression instantly became solemn.","“I am the True Spirit of the Divine Fire Temple. Originally, I was supposed to personally guide you in receiving the inheritance, but as you know, my spiritual consciousness is currently too weak to lead you inside. So...” Jiu Chen sighed before continuing, “However, if you nourish me with your soul power for three to five hundred years, once my spiritual consciousness has recovered, I will be able to guide you into the Divine Fire Temple!”","Three to five hundred years?","Jian Wushuang frowned. In the past, even if you added a “ten thousand” after that number, he wouldn’t have batted an eye. But now, he didn’t have time to nourish someone’s soul.","Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang were waiting for him outside!","That ancient demon posed a threat, and Jiu Chen’s clone and Li Miao’s schemes could lead to Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang’s demise.","He had little hope in Xiang Yang now. Even if he found Xingluo, the most he could do was gain some understanding of the world from him.","As for asking for help, he no longer needed it.","His main concern now was Jiang Shang.","She was Jiang Shang’s daughter.","There was no need to elaborate on who Jiang Shang would have a daughter with. When Jian Wushuang saw Hu Qing’s Dao Image, he understood.","This was Hu Qing’s bloodline.","Whether or not he found Jiang Shang wasn’t important anymore. If he could bring little Jiang Shang out, even Hu Qing bowing to him wouldn’t be too much.","He was more than willing to see Hu Qing happy and forgetting the past.","So, he couldn’t let Jiang Shang die.","Even if it meant not receiving the inheritance, he couldn’t let anything happen to Jiang Shang.","Naturally, he couldn’t agree to nourish Jiu Chen’s true form.","With some reluctance, Jian Wushuang asked, “Senior, is it only under your guidance that I can enter the Divine Fire Temple?”","“Of course. Without my guidance, entering the Temple of Inheritance is impossible, unless your strength reaches a level defying the heavens, surpassing the one who created me!” Jiu Chen’s tone was firm.","Forcing entry was possible.","But you’d have to be a level stronger than the one who originally created this Divine Fire Temple.","This was a widely accepted understanding. For example, the inheritance formation set up by a Dao Lord was nearly impossible to break for someone of the same level, unless they were a heaven-defying Dao Lord like Jian Wushuang back then.","If it were an Emperor, breaking it would be much easier.","“Senior, what level was that Eye of God clan expert who created this inheritance?” Jian Wushuang probed.","Jiu Chen squinted his eyes with pride and said, “Your talent is not bad. If you can accept the inheritance of the Divine Fire Temple, you might have a chance to transcend and even become an immortal. However, my master’s realm surpasses that of an Immortal!”"]},{"number":6350,"title":"Chapter 6350: Pretending to Be a Pig to Eat a Tiger","paragraphs":["Chapter 6350: Pretending to Be a Pig to Eat a Tiger","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Surpassing Yan Immortal?","“Could there be realms beyond the Yan Immortal?” Jian Wushuang’s tone showed genuine surprise, as if he had just stumbled upon some earth-shattering secret.","This made Immortal Jiu Chen even more pleased. After all, it had been tens of thousands of years since he had encountered a worthy successor. Now, having met someone as talented as Jian Wushuang, he was more than willing to boast a bit.","Most importantly, he wanted to tempt Jian Wushuang into nurturing his spiritual consciousness. If Jian Wushuang reached the highest level, he could enter the Divine Fire Temple and use its power to fully restore himself.","So, without hesitation, he explained, “Of course, there are higher realms. However, becoming an Undying Immortal is already extremely difficult. Even the Flame Emperor never reached that level. I remember when the Divine Fire Temple entered the Heavenly Fire Realm, there was only one Undying Immortal across all the ancient domains. I’m not sure if there have been any new breakthroughs since then. With your current level, even if you’re a Dao Child, I doubt you know much about it, right?”","“I don’t,” Jian Wushuang shook his head in confusion.","This time, he wasn’t lying. He truly didn’t know how many Undying Immortals existed in the higher realms, nor did he know the limits of cultivation in the numerous ancient domains.","Based on the information he currently had, having a Dao Master was already impressive. If an Emperor appeared, it would be even more extraordinary.","Back in the original universe, the worlds were categorized into three levels.","In lower worlds, it was rare to see Emperors.","In middle worlds, like the Grand Si Domain, there were plenty of Emperors during its golden age.","These middle worlds were far superior to lower worlds in countless ways.","Higher worlds were even more powerful. A fragmented higher world like the Tongtian Buddha Realm could produce dozens of Emperors.","If complete, it could produce hundreds of Emperors.","The world of Shang was incredibly powerful, producing ultimate Emperors, and even reached the peak of the fifth tier.","The 108 ancient domains of the higher realms, even when combined, were not as vast as the lower worlds of the original universe.","Unless these ancient domains were separated by vast voids and distances, they might be comparable to lower worlds.","However, according to Immortal Jiu Chen, powerful beings from other worlds could still be encountered within the ancient domains.","This implied that the higher realms were not limited to just 108 ancient domains.","What they currently considered the higher realms could be collectively referred to as the ancient domains.","Beyond the ancient domains, there were other worlds.","This structure resembled the original universe’s divine hierarchy.","The ancient domains of the higher realms could be likened to the Grand Si Domain, while the other worlds were akin to the Tongtian Buddha Realm or the Great Dream World.","If this were the case, the so-called higher realms might actually be an entire universe.","Of course, this was just speculation.","If it were truly a universe, then there was a possibility of not only having Emperors but even a Universe Master.","After pondering for a moment, Immortal Jiu Chen continued, “The realm beyond the Undying Immortal far surpasses your imagination. They are millions of times stronger than Undying Immortals. Their abilities are beyond your comprehension. For instance, the 108 ancient domains were created effortlessly by a great being. Their Origin Source is fragile and can’t even compare to the great world where my master resided.”","“Created effortlessly? The 108 ancient domains were man-made?” Jian Wushuang exclaimed in shock.","Feigning surprise, he managed to gather some information. The 108 ancient domains were not as special as he initially thought, and being man-made wasn’t unheard of. That person’s power was likely at the Emperor level, possibly even at the peak or beyond.","“Why is that so hard to believe? Those at that level are called Great Emperors!” Immortal Jiu Chen said proudly. “But don’t confuse these Great Emperors with the Flame Emperor. The Flame Emperor isn’t even worthy of comparison. No matter how powerful the Flame Emperor was, he was merely a transcendent being, not even an Undying Immortal. A Great Emperor could kill someone like the Flame Emperor with just a glance!”","This was true. At its peak, the Ancient Demon was nearly invincible below the Undying level due to its high life form level, making it difficult to kill. Combined with its unique strength and robust vitality, it was practically unbeatable at the same level.","However, their bottleneck was also terrifying, as most of them were stuck below immortality.","Becoming an immortal was incredibly rare for special beings, and each one of them was a super powerhouse within their level.","But compared to the ultimate Dao, there was still a significant gap.","Especially for the Ultimate Emperor, who could fight across levels and even slay Emperors.","If this were said aloud, even Immortal Jiu Chen might not believe it.","After all, the world he had experienced was still quite weak, considered the early stages of a cultivation civilization. Even someone like Shenmo could dominate, which showed that the human race had yet to fully demonstrate its advantage in the heavenly Dao.","Once humans broke through in the heavenly Dao, they would become even more powerful.","The so-called ancient demons would become mere legends, or perhaps even pets raised by strong cultivators.","What was once cherished would eventually become commonplace.","The ancient domain had not existed for a long time, and it was unclear what those so-called alternate worlds were like!","But all this seemed to be still far away from him.","Immortal Jiu Chen had laid the groundwork for a while, and finally began to talk about his master.","“You already know a bit about the strength of Emperors, but my master is someone who has surpassed the Emperor level. His power is such that he can create worlds with a flick of his hand. In fact, within my master’s body, there exists a grand world that is countless times larger than the ancient domain!” Immortal Jiu Chen grew more excited as he spoke.","Jian Wushuang was genuinely stunned. “A world within his body?”","Wasn’t that the Origin Source Universe?","A Universe Master!","Immortal Jiu Chen’s master was a Universe Master, and not just any Universe Master, but one who could integrate the universe into his body.","At the very least, he must have reached the Seventh Tribulation level.","Of course, to create the First Sequence of this inheritance temple, even if he hadn’t reached the Eighth Tribulation, he could still absorb the universe into his body.","It was the same when he was in the Ancient Moon Time-Space.","Seeing Jian Wushuang’s astonishment, Immortal Jiu Chen felt quite satisfied.","He began to plot in his mind.","His plan was to entice Jian Wushuang to nurture his soul. Once he recovered, he could guide Jian Wushuang into the Divine Fire Temple. With his help, Jian Wushuang could accept the inheritance of such an existence.","But Jian Wushuang wasn’t falling for it.","While conversing with Immortal Jiu Chen and extracting useful information, he was also pondering how to enter the Divine Fire Temple.","A sequence inheritance created by a Universe Master was indeed extraordinary.","Moreover, this sequence inheritance was not unique.","There were many First Sequence inheritance temples, and several existed within the ancient domain.","Of course, they were all occupied by powerful forces, making it difficult for ordinary people to enter, let alone accept the inheritance.","There were even more Second Sequence temples, and as for the Third Sequence, they were all dominated by powerful factions.","The Fourth and Fifth Sequence inheritances were the ones most commonly accepted.","However, entering these inheritance temples also depended on the token one obtained.","The weakest was the Black Eye Inheritance Token.","There were five types of inheritance tokens: black, white, blue, red, and gold.","Five sequences, five tokens.","As long as one had a token, they could enter the corresponding sequence inheritance.","If they didn’t have a token, they would be forced to accept the strongest inheritance.","That was where the real danger lay."]},{"number":6351,"title":"Chapter 6351: Entering the Divine Fire Temple","paragraphs":["Chapter 6351: Entering the Divine Fire Temple","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang wasn’t worried. A divine eye inheritance left behind by a Universe Master—he had no concerns about whether he could withstand it.","His mental state was steady, his soul intact.","Everything was in place!","“Guidance?” He smirked slightly.","He didn’t need it at all.","Ignoring Immortal Jiu Chen’s constant chatter, he sat cross-legged and stopped nurturing Jiu Chen with his soul power. Instead, he fully immersed himself in his own state of mind.","Seeing Jian Wushuang’s posture, Jiu Chen was momentarily stunned.","“Is this kid out of his mind?” Doubts arose in his heart, but then he sensed Jian Wushuang’s thought power approaching the Divine Fire Temple.","Such behavior seemed utterly absurd to him.","The inheritance token could only be used once inside, and to enter this first sequence of the inheritance hall, Jiu Chen’s guidance was necessary. Yet now, Jian Wushuang seemed to be preparing to guide himself inside.","Jiu Chen thought he had gone mad.","He immediately mocked, “Kid, you’re way too arrogant. I already told you, the existence that opened the inheritance hall isn’t something you can just...”","Before he could finish his sentence, he felt a powerful thought power surge behind him.","That thought power continuously grew stronger.","In an instant, it broke through the Godly Form Realm, surpassing Manifestation, Primordial Spirit, and Great Accomplishment, finally stepping into the realm of immortality.","Jiu Chen quickly turned his head to look—it was Jian Wushuang.","His eyes almost popped out of his head in shock, his voice trembling as he stammered, “You... how did you get here? No, how did your strength suddenly become so powerful?”","This development was beyond his expectations.","Standing before the Divine Fire Temple, Jian Wushuang clasped his hands behind his back, speaking indifferently, “How I got here doesn’t matter. Why I’ve become so powerful? Naturally, it’s because this place is isolated from the Heavenly Dao. Without its suppression, I can naturally return to my peak!”","“What? You said Heavenly Dao suppression?” Jiu Chen suddenly realized—he had been deceived by Jian Wushuang all along.","In the mortal world, suppressed by the Heavenly Dao, his split incarnation had never become a true Immortal and hadn’t opened a small world. Everything had been Jian Wushuang’s fabrication.","The so-called Dao Child wasn’t real. Most likely, his split incarnation had already been destroyed by Jian Wushuang, allowing him to enter this place.","For a moment, Jiu Chen was left speechless.","Jian Wushuang stood there, slightly clenching his fist as powerful thought power swept around him. The long-lost feeling lifted his spirits.","Just now, he had reached the Divine Fire Temple with his thought power.","He quickly discovered that there was no Heavenly Dao suppression here, which made sense—this inheritance hall, created by a Universe Master, naturally isolated itself from the Heavenly Dao.","Therefore, his true soul, trapped within the Nine Prison Pagoda, had been able to emerge.","In the mortal world, powerful beings beneath transcendence could only be maintained at the peak of the Godly Form Realm.","Even a transcendent soul without a physical body would be suppressed.","Thus, he couldn’t leave in the outside world.","But here, he could fully emerge.","With the soul power of an Immortal, Jian Wushuang felt revitalized, his mood improving significantly.","“Senior Jiu Chen, I’ll head in first. If I pass the inheritance, I might consider helping you restore your peak strength, or even help you leave this hall. But on one condition—you must acknowledge me as your master. You can start thinking it over now!” Jian Wushuang teased, then turned and entered the Divine Fire Temple.","Left behind, Jiu Chen’s face flushed with embarrassment as he recalled his earlier boasts in front of Jian Wushuang. Feeling exposed, his anger flared at the suggestion of submitting to him.","Back then, he had split his soul, discarding the part filled with ambition, and refused to leave the Divine Fire Temple. How could he now pledge allegiance to Jian Wushuang?","“Hmph, let’s see if you can survive first!” He snorted coldly and turned his head away.","In his mind, even if Jian Wushuang had reached the Immortal level, he was still no match for his master.","His master was someone beyond the Emperor.","A mere Immortal? Jiu Chen didn’t even consider him a threat. Even without Jian Wushuang’s nurturing, Jiu Chen believed that with a few thousand years of self-recovery, he could re-enter the Divine Fire Temple and guide everything himself.","Fuming, he sat cross-legged before the hall, focusing on restoring his soul power.","...","Jian Wushuang stepped into the Divine Fire Temple and immediately felt a pressure filled with divine power, emanating the essence of fire.","From this pressure alone, he could estimate the strength of the one who wielded this fire’s divine power.","“Divine power of fire... mastered the ultimate path within the Origin Source of fire. The divine power should be at a semi-divine level, around fifty million!”","With just the presence of the pressure, Jian Wushuang could roughly gauge the opponent’s strength.","However, this pressure seemed to have existed for a long time, and it was merely something left behind casually by the Universe Master of the Shenyanzu universe who had opened this place long ago.","The true divine power of the original being likely rivaled that of a Universe God.","But this wasn’t much of a surprise, considering that this world might harbor Universe Gods of six stars or higher.","What surprised him was how quickly he had encountered a legacy on par with the Universe God level.","He had been in this world for less than a year, and this place was still considered a mortal world.","He couldn’t deny that his luck had been extraordinary, stumbling upon such an incredible opportunity.","Even after his reconstruction, his fortune remained astonishing.","This was the destiny of one chosen by fate.","Jian Wushuang continued walking, passing through the long corridor of the main hall and entering the central chamber.","There was no divine statue or altar here.","The setup was simple, with only a few items like an incense burner and a square table.","From the outside, the temple appeared boundless in power, but inside, it was incredibly understated.","Below, there were six meditation cushions. As Jian Wushuang moved closer to investigate, he realized that a barrier surrounded them.","Based on what he had learned from Immortal Jiu Chen earlier, these cushions had been left by those who had already received the inheritance within this temple.","Though Immortal Jiu Chen seemed like someone who had never seen a living person, that was because he had been in slumber for over ten thousand years.","Moreover, his consciousness had split into so many parts that he had forgotten his early experiences.","The Jiu Chen outside was different. Not only had he obtained a treasure like the Nine Prison Pagoda, but he had also claimed to have traversed nine worlds, which was why he named himself Jiu Chen.","Initially, Jian Wushuang had thought these nine worlds referred to ancient domains, but now it seemed they were great worlds.","This made it unsurprising that Jiu Chen had set up an array to advance into a fearsome ghost and might have obtained the Nine Prison Pagoda from the bodies of those who had entered this place before him.","One had to remember that even receiving an inheritance carried risks.","These risks could lead to one’s demise.","And when someone perished, their treasures would naturally fall into Jiu Chen’s hands.","According to Jiu Chen’s true self, the foundation of this inheritance was the soul, and entering the temple would test one’s consciousness.","The earlier pressure test was merely the beginning.","Next, there would be three trials to pass, followed by six rounds of selection, and nine secret methods of inheritance.","What Jian Wushuang lacked now was time. Given the obstacles, he needed to advance quickly.","So, he concealed his soul essence within the Nine Prison Pagoda once more, leaving behind only his spiritual body, still at the level of a divine being.","The inheritance of the Shenyanzu required very little in terms of cultivation level. Even a cultivator at the Jindan stage could enter."]},{"number":6352,"title":"Chapter 6352: Nine Physical Forms","paragraphs":["Chapter 6352: Nine Physical Forms","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The most crucial aspects were the physical body, strength, and Thought power in the first three stages.","Among these, the most important was the spiritual Thought power.","Successfully channeling the physical body’s strength through Thought power to achieve perfection was the key to passing the first three stages.","Jian Wushuang felt confident.","He turned his gaze to the wall on the left front side.","There were three lamps.","The first lamp represented the physical body.","With a thought, his consciousness instantly entered the lamp.","Inside was a micro-space.","Before him, various physical forms were arranged.","The challenge here was not to use one’s own body but rather to master another physical form.","In simple terms, this stage tested one’s control over a physical body.","As long as he chose a form he could control, he could proceed to the next stage.","Now, his task was to select a physical form and then master it.","If he couldn’t control it, he would need to switch to a weaker form.","There were nine physical forms in a row.","Jian Wushuang didn’t dare to be careless and began testing them one by one, starting from the first.","Mastery didn’t require claiming ownership; he merely needed to try each form to see which one suited him best.","Starting with the first one.","Though called a physical form, it was actually a mass of flesh, into which he could project his soul and freely transform it.","With a flash!","He instantly transformed into his own appearance, with the form’s strength determined by his soul power.","Thus, this physical form now had the strength of a Godly State’s peak form.","However, its life force was 1,000-fold stronger.","It had already reached the level of a Special Life Form.","Ordinary human cultivators couldn’t control it.","Particularly those in the Godly State; they would likely be expelled by the oppressive force above as soon as they entered the body.","No wonder they had created blood mist and a blood-colored passage outside the temple.","Those were set up later. According to what Immortal Jiu Chen mentioned, they were originally created in the Skyfire Domain when Jiu Chen still had his own forces. Back then, his ambition was already showing.","To prevent weaker beings from bothering him, he created the blood mist world and the blood-colored passage.","These were all made from ancient demon blood.","Whether it was the blood of that Flame Emperor, he did not know.","However, the temple’s master, also a Universe Master who followed the path of fire, seemed like a coincidence.","Jian Wushuang burned his Thought power, increasing his soul power a hundredfold. Controlling this form, which had a life force 1,000-fold stronger, was effortless for him. In fact, he accidentally burned his Thought power too intensely, causing the physical form to warp slightly under the pressure.","There was no choice. Without any suppressive force here, he could burn as much Thought power as he wished.","In an unguarded moment, his Thought power surged to around 500-fold. This required a physical form with 5,000-fold life force to withstand such soul power!","Jian Wushuang’s heart stirred as he immediately left that physical body.","Now that there was no more suppression, he could utilize the second layer of the burning secret technique.","Burning his soul power once would return 10-fold the soul power.","The returned power would then be burned again, and the second stage of burning could yield 100-fold the soul power.","For example, if he initially burned 90 percent of his soul power, it would return with 90-fold the soul power. Upon burning it a second time, his soul power would instantly break through to 900-fold its original strength.","And the secret technique for burning thought power had five layers.","This was just the beginning.","Of course, all of this was possible because he continuously replenished his soul with his original body.","It also contained the consciousness of a Realm Beast, which was the most terrifying power of all.","The consciousness of a Realm Beast was equivalent to the consciousness of the Starry Sky.","After all, the Starry Sky was created by Realm Beasts.","Everything within the Starry Sky, including all those so-called innate and acquired beings, no matter how powerful, ultimately derived from the materials of the Realm Beasts themselves.","His thought power contained the will of the Realm Beasts, which was essentially the will of the Starry Sky.","Such a powerful will was not something that could be compared to those Special Life Forms that had been divided into countless layers of existence.","Without even attempting the second body, he directly moved on to the third.","His soul entered, his appearance transformed, and his thought power ignited.","He followed a familiar process, starting to control the physical body.","He performed various techniques with his fists, palms, and legs.","There was no pressure at all.","The life level of this body had reached 9,999-fold.","It was just a sliver away from becoming a perfect Universe-level Special Life Form.","Naturally, he wasn’t satisfied with this body.","He then attempted the fourth body, a perfect Universe-level Special Life Form with a life level of 10,000-fold.","This time, everything felt natural and smooth.","However, when he saw there were still five more bodies remaining, he took a deep breath and suddenly noticed something unusual.","The one who crafted this First Sequence Temple at best matched a Universe God.","It wasn’t surprising that he could obtain a perfect Universe-level Special Life Form, or even create one.","Beyond the Universe-level was the space-time level of Special Life Forms.","These were Special Life Forms with life genes exceeding 10,000-fold, which were not particularly rare and were easy to acquire.","But among the remaining five bodies, could there be a Starry Sky-level Special Life Form?","Driven by curiosity, he decided to try the fifth body.","This time, he pushed the second layer of the burning thought power secret technique to its extreme.","It reached 1,000-fold his soul power.","Yet even changing the physical form seemed to be a struggle.","“The life level of this body has actually reached 30,000-fold!” Jian Wushuang endured the oppressive feeling, barely managing to alter his appearance, but his movements had become stiff.","He knew he couldn’t pass the three-stage assessment.","But he was unwilling to settle for an ordinary Universe-level body.","He increased the burning of his thought power again.","“Third layer of burning, Extinction!”","Buzz!","His thought power instantly soared from 1,000-fold to 5,000-fold.","This time, it wasn’t that he couldn’t control the body, but rather that the body couldn’t withstand him.","However, his soul was starting to feel strained. Although it was constantly replenishing, it was still only at the divine form level.","“It seems I need to improve my realm!”","With a thought, Jian Wushuang created a small opening in the Nine Prison Pagoda, allowing his soul’s original body to return, but keeping his realm at the Primordial Spirit level.","At this level, he had stepped into the realm of laws, similar to when he was a law master in the native world.","In the orthodox division of realms, a law master was already at the peak of the Primordial Spirit level.","Once he suppressed his realm to this level, his soul indeed felt much lighter.","At the Primordial Spirit level, one could sever the divine, and divine thought would become incredibly powerful, naturally capable of enduring more burning.","He no longer felt satisfied with this body either, and his thought power moved directly to another clone.","“Right, I can split my soul power to control the other bodies. How would the inheritance assess that?”","This sudden idea intrigued him.","Moreover, all these bodies were spherical fluids, naturally immortal beings.","Wouldn’t they also be able to merge into one?","Because each body was at the extreme level within its own realm.","Nine extremes.","He suddenly wanted to try the strongest body.","The first body: Life level of 1,000-fold.","The second body: Life level of 5,000-fold.","The third body: Life level of 9,999-fold."]},{"number":6353,"title":"Chapter 6353: Star-Grade Special Life Form","paragraphs":["Chapter 6353: Star-Grade Special Life Form","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The fourth physical body: a life level of 10,000-fold.","If we categorized the first four physical bodies uniformly, they would fall under the universe-level Special Life Form category.","The upper limit of a universe-level physical body was 10,000-fold, and the lower limit was one time.","For ordinary human cultivators, adulthood represented a life level of one time. To increase this required postnatal effort, but no matter how much effort was exerted, raising the life level of the physical body to 10-fold was typically the limit.","Further enhancements mainly relied on treasures.","For instance, the entire body of a Special Life Form was a treasure. The simplest and most straightforward method was to use the blood of a Special Life Form as a reference, dilute it, and merge it with one’s physical body.","There were many such methods. For example, in other races, the life genes of the demon race started at around three times, and refining demon cores could also increase it.","However, there was always a limit to these enhancements.","For instance, absorbing a Special Life Form with a level of a thousand times could elevate one’s physical body to nine hundred and ninety-nine times.","It was impossible to surpass the original life level.","Theoretically, an ordinary human could not achieve a perfect universe-level physical body merely by relying on the Special Life Forms within the universe.","Unless they transcended the universe level and absorbed Spacetime level Special Life Forms, they could not surpass the universe-level physical body.","But physical enhancement was ultimately considered a side path.","Everything was centered around the divine body and divine power.","Back then, his physical body had undergone ten refinements with the help of the Shan Jun at Demon Sound Mountain, perfectly integrating the physical body with the divine body and forging his perfect divine power.","That was the key to enhancing combat strength.","However, to exceed the limits of combat strength, one had to achieve perfection in everything, even in the so-called side path of physical enhancement.","Speaking of Spacetime level Special Life Forms...","The fifth physical body: a life level of 30,000-fold.","He split his soul power, directing it towards the sixth and seventh physical bodies.","These two physical bodies had life levels of 50,000-fold and 80,000-fold, respectively.","His soul level had already burned to the 10,000-fold level, so controlling three Spacetime level Special Life Forms at once was not challenging.","This was because each of his three soul avatars could burn to the 10,000-fold level.","In this way, he could control the perfect Special Life Form with a life level of one hundred thousand times within the Spacetime level.","The eighth physical body: a life level of one hundred thousand times.","This was the pinnacle of the Spacetime level.","He had encountered many perfect Special Life Forms at the Spacetime level, but he had never studied them closely.","Only now did he realize that the perfect Special Life Form at the Spacetime level was nothing less than a beast god.","A life level of one hundred thousand times, with an initial divine power of one hundred thousand times as well.","However, he was currently unable to use divine power.","That was something he had seen in the Qishen Temple.","As for starry sky-level Special Life Forms, he had not encountered any.","Because he had not yet ventured into the starry sky.","At this moment, his gaze fell upon the ninth physical body.","Nine physical bodies forming a sphere, representing the nine layers of the physical body.","The final body was a Special Life Form at the Starry Sky level.","“How could the creature refining this divine palace possess a body of Starry Sky level? At most, it should be a Universe God!” Jian Wushuang couldn’t believe it.","Moreover, this vast world was merely one percent the size of the Realm God Continent.","He could accept that a perfect life form of the time-space level had been nurtured and picked up by a powerful member of the God Eye Clan.","But the presence of a Special Life Form of Starry Sky level was beyond explanation.","Unwilling to believe it, he decided to attempt to take control of the ninth body.","To be safe, he merged his soul clone into his main soul.","His divine power burned to the extreme, and his soul power reached a thousandfold.","With a thought, he guided his soul into the final body.","Buzz!","The moment his soul tried to enter, a terrifying pressure forced him out.","That overwhelming force sent a shiver down his spine.","“That power is so close to that of a Realm Beast; it’s just like my Beast God Weapon!” Jian Wushuang gasped, steadying his soul.","He was all too familiar with that aura.","After devouring the consciousness of a Realm Beast, he had learned much about them, especially since his Beast God Weapon was embedded with a Realm Beast’s eye.","He used that power daily, making it as familiar as his own.","“Could this Starry Sky level Special Life Form have reached the level of a Realm Beast?” He shook his head, dismissing the thought.","That power had not fully reached the level of a Realm Beast, perhaps only a fifth of its strength.","But even so, it was beyond what his current soul could bear.","This body was equivalent to a fifth of a Realm Beast!","One had to know that powerful Realm Beasts like Morosa were capable of shattering the Realm God Continent.","Even Spacetime Gods struggled to break the Realm God Continent; only those who had reached the Starry Sky level could achieve that.","For example, the Star Spirits.","They were capable of killing Realm Beasts because their power was extracted from the essence of countless Realm Beasts, which made them so formidable.","After discovering the secrets of the Starry Sky, Jian Wushuang realized that to progress further in his cultivation, he would have to deal with Realm Beasts.","In his weaker years, he had relied on his Beast God Weapon to rise in power, later utilizing Beast God power combined with the Thousand Ancient Change and the Eternal Change to create the Primeval Change, mastering the power of the Starry Sky ahead of time.","The power contained within was purer than Spacetime power, far more refined.","This was why his strength had become so formidable.","Now, if his body could compare to a Realm Beast, it would be more than just a minor path; it would dramatically enhance his combat power.","No matter what, he had to control this body, even if it meant breaking the divine palace to take it with him.","Although he didn’t know how that God Eye Clan member had acquired this Starry Sky level Special Life Form, he was determined to take it.","Even if he couldn’t take it now, he would attempt to do so and, upon returning, he would kill the clone of Immortal Jiu Chen, seize the Blood Altar, and carry this first-sequence inheritance palace with him.","For now, his goal was to enter this body.","The limit for a Special Life Form at the Universe level was a thousandfold soul power, requiring a hundredfold to control.","For a Special Life Form at the Spacetime level, the limit was 10,000-fold, requiring a thousandfold soul power to control.","Thus, a Special Life Form at the Starry Sky level exceeded the 10,000-fold limit.","His soul power would first need to surpass the thousandfold mark.","But his Thought power had already reached the third level.","Going further wasn’t impossible, but his current level wasn’t sufficient!","“Transcendence, Great Perfection!”","Jian Wushuang’s soul power instantly soared, and his level elevated to the Great Perfection.","This was the final stage before immortality, equivalent to the peak of the Ancestor realm in the native world.","Beyond this was the realm of the immortal Yan Immortal.","Due to the Nine Prison Pagoda, his soul had only just reached the level of Yan Immortal.","In the upper realms, his power might have surged directly to Dao Lord, though reaching the level of Emperor Lord seemed unlikely.","After all, when he entered this world, his clone had only six-star Universe God strength.","At that time, he had divided his soul among countless bodies, so each portion was relatively weak.","Looking back, he regretted it, but without the determination to split his soul into thousands, he wouldn’t have entered this world, nor would he have encountered a Special Life Form body of the Starry Sky level in the God Eye inheritance palace.","Everything had happened for a reason!"]},{"number":6354,"title":"Chapter 6354: Starting From This Moment","paragraphs":["Chapter 6354: Starting From This Moment","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The Origin!","Let it begin now!","Jian Wushuang burned his soul to the fourth layer.","“Soul Annihilation, Silence!”","This was the peak level of burning Thought Power. Any higher, and it would reach the fifth layer of the burning secret technique.","Although he currently maintained his realm at the Great Perfection, burning the fifth layer of the soul secret technique could not be achieved with just the soul at the Immortal level.","Because the power of burning at the fifth layer was far beyond 100,000-fold or even a million-fold.","Even if he could burn at the Great Perfection level, he would need his original soul, and it would have to surpass his own realm by five levels.","Above Great Perfection, in terms of major realms, the levels were Immortal (Yan Immortal), Great Emperor (Emperor), Universe Master, Universe God, and Spacetime God.","This meant that to burn the fifth layer of the secret technique, he needed to use his original soul in the outside world, and it had to be before his soul was divided into thousands of fragments.","This was simply too defiant of the natural order, and he was currently incapable of doing so.","Fortunately, this Special Life Form at the Starry Sky level did not require him to burn to the fifth layer; the fourth layer of Soul Annihilation would be sufficient.","This was also the first time he had burned the fourth layer of Soul Annihilation, as in the outside world, he had never needed to use this level of burning secret technique.","Burning the soul and divine power had their limits.","Previously, he had the power of life to replenish his divine power, allowing him to freely use the secret technique of burning divine power.","Now, with the supplementation of his original soul, he could freely use the secret technique of burning the soul.","These prerequisites all required sufficient strength.","“Burn!”","He gritted his teeth and roared angrily. The original soul within the Nine Prison Pagoda was instantly absorbed entirely, while his Great Perfection clone gained a soul power of up to 180,000-fold.","“This time, it should be enough!” He gazed intently at the Special Life Form of the Starry Sky level.","With a thought, his soul rushed once again into the flesh.","Buzz!","The immense resistance was still there, but it no longer forced him to retreat.","This time, he went all out, passed through layers of obstacles, and completely entered this body.","Power Lock, Soul Lock, Body Lock!","Great Perfection!","Whoosh!","“Transform!”","Jian Wushuang controlled the Starry Sky level body, and it immediately transformed into his own appearance.","However, while controlling the body, the immense pressure it brought made him very uncomfortable.","Moreover, in his mind, an endless stream of oppressive forces kept emerging, as if a Realm Beast was whispering in his ear.","This interference continuously assaulted his will.","Fortunately, his willpower naturally contained the power of the Realm Beast.","Only then could he control this body.","However, the interference and the pressure still prevented him from fully mastering this body.","The life level of this body had already surpassed a million-fold.","“How is this possible? This isn’t a Starry Sky-level Special Life Form; this is practically comparable to the true form of a Realm Beast!” Jian Wushuang gritted his teeth, his very soul beginning to tremble at that moment.","The eerie thing was that the life level of this body continued to increase.","This brought him even greater pressure.","His true soul had already been completely consumed, turning what was once living water into dead water.","“This is bad!”","Jian Wushuang’s expression changed. He clenched his fists, no longer burning his soul power, but instead used his willpower to suppress this body.","Even if this was flesh and blood condensed from a Realm Beast, he had to suppress the interference and rejection from it.","“This is definitely a Realm Beast’s body. That infinitely growing power is terrifying, just like Morosa’s true form back then!” He felt a wave of fear in his heart.","He vividly remembered the oppressive feeling that came from the Realm Beast.","This was a body that no cultivator’s soul power could withstand.","The ninth body was far more terrifying than the previous eight bodies combined.","Moreover, the life level grew with the soul.","This meant that even if Jian Wushuang burned his soul power a million-fold, he still couldn’t bear this oppressive force.","“How could something like this exist within the Divine Fire Palace?!”","Jian Wushuang gritted his teeth, deeply puzzled.","The body of a Realm Beast was not just precious; the key point was that in the few disciplined times when Realm Beasts invaded, very few were actually slain.","He knew of only one instance, where a Realm Beast that could shatter the Realm God Continent was slain.","And this world should have some connection with the Star Field of the Gods.","The Star Field of the Gods was formed because of the shattered Realm God Continent.","Thinking along these lines, there was some connection.","But that was all. This Realm Beast’s body, even if it had been obtained by that Star Spirit who slew it back then, could not have ended up in this world, let alone fallen into the hands of a cultivator barely at the level of a Universe God!","Moreover, this body had been refined into a sphere, likely to suppress the uncontrollable nature of the Realm Beast’s body.","The being capable of refining such a body could not possibly be a Universe God; at the very least, it would need to be a Time-Space God, or even a Starry Sky God.","He would even believe it if someone said that the Star Spirit had refined it.","“No matter, since I’ve encountered it, this is my destiny, and I must seize it!” A thought stirred in his heart, and his soul power began to gradually decrease.","After all, he had now entered the Realm Beast’s body.","Continuously increasing soul power also raised the life level of the body.","It had just surpassed three million-fold.","So, he simply lowered his soul power directly, maintaining it at around 100,000-fold.","The life level of the Realm Beast’s body also decreased slightly.","But then it rebounded. This time, instead of forcibly suppressing it with soul power, he used his consciousness to wear it down.","“I refuse to believe I can’t outlast a Realm Beast’s body that has been dead for who knows how many years!”","He immediately sat down cross-legged, putting everything else out of his mind, and began to wear down the Realm Beast with his consciousness.","The wear and tear on his consciousness was the most painful.","But the ability to grow stronger meant nothing to Jian Wushuang.","“Let’s see who can outlast the other!” He was extremely confident.","The two consciousnesses clashed continuously, even leading to mutual devouring.","Each side wanted to consume the other.","But within Jian Wushuang’s willpower lay Morosa’s willpower.","Morosa’s strength was among the top in the entire Void Realm.","The original owner of this body might not have been weaker than Morosa, but ultimately, they had already fallen.","Now, the only thing left in this body was some residual willpower of the Realm Beast.","This willpower had no consciousness, behaving like a mad demon.","Like an old hen protecting her chicks, it would let no one approach.","But Jian Wushuang, like a cunning weasel, used the same willpower to slowly devour the opponent.","He sat cross-legged for who knows how long, forgetting everything that was happening in the outside world.","Fortunately, the Divine Fire Palace and the Scarlet Eye Realm were not in the same dimensional plane, so he didn’t know how the flow of time worked.","If the time flow was faster than outside, the outside world was basically doomed; if it was slower, then there was still hope.","But none of this hindered his desire to grow stronger.","To protect Jiang Shang, to protect Xiang Yang, and even to save Chen Yuan’s life."]},{"number":6355,"title":"Chapter 6355: Realm Beast Body","paragraphs":["Chapter 6355: Realm Beast Body","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","These were actions he would only take under the condition of absolute certainty.","If it involved someone he cared about, he might take a risk, even to the point of risking his life to save them.","However, all of this had a prerequisite—his growth rate could not be compromised.","More importantly, this Realm Beast’s body was of immense help to his true self in the outside world. It could very well be the key step to passing his divine Tribulation.","Because he needed to walk a different path, he had to forget everything else.","The two intertwined wills seemed to be vying for control over this body.","At times, they attacked each other; at other times, they devoured one another.","Jian Wushuang’s soul power couldn’t suppress the other side, but his willpower remained dominant, continuously eroding the will of the Realm Beast.","He didn’t know how long it lasted, but after a prolonged struggle, he finally managed to completely suppress the other side.","The Realm Beast’s own will had been driven into a corner, shivering in fear.","“It worked!”","He felt a surge of joy in his heart.","His will had completely suppressed the will of the Realm Beast’s body, which meant he would no longer be disturbed.","The only downside was that he couldn’t fully control the body yet, which was part of the test he needed to pass.","The purpose of entering the Qishen Temple was to obtain the Divine Eye inheritance.","Yet, in this very first trial, he encountered the Realm Beast’s body.","What else awaited him afterward?","With this thought in mind, he didn’t rush to the second trial. Instead, he fully familiarized himself with this body.","Suppressing the will didn’t mean it was entirely eradicated.","If he encountered danger and his willpower waned, the other side might retaliate.","Jian Wushuang didn’t want to plant a hidden threat in his own mind.","So, after suppressing the other side, he began to fully engage, simultaneously comprehending the life structure of the body while also imprinting his soul.","He prepared to completely take over this body.","Originally, this was a treasure used to test the inheritor, but now he intended to forcibly take it away.","This was much easier than seizing it from the Realm Beast’s will.","Once the soul recognized him as its master and the body and soul merged perfectly, who could take this body away?","He was slightly concerned—would his body and willpower become those of the Realm Beast, and would he be surrounded by Star Spirits once he left?","But then he thought, his soul was still primarily human, and the Star Spirits were not fools; they would surely be able to tell.","He then devoted himself fully to controlling this body.","At the same time, he continued to eradicate the last vestiges of resistance in the body’s will.","As he devoured the other side’s willpower, the speed at which he took control also accelerated significantly.","The level of life he was comprehending brought him great joy.","Because the Realm Beast’s level of life was extremely high, it reached the upper limits of the Starry Sky.","After all, living in the limitless void, no one knew how much a Realm Beast could grow.","Just the life level of this body alone, which Jian Wushuang maintained at about a million times, was enough for him to comprehend its life structure. He discovered that the Realm Beast’s body could become formless and colorless, allowing it to maintain the highest absorption state for any gathered power.","The most heaven-defying ability, however, was that this body could isolate Spacetime.","In other words, the Realm Beast could create its own Spacetime.","It could devour Spacetime, even the Starry Sky itself.","“Unfortunately, I was born in the Starry Sky!” Jian Wushuang lamented, shaking his head. He quickly dismissed the thought.","If he were to devour the Starry Sky, wouldn’t he be slapped to death?","The 12 Star Spirits were no joke.","There were many powerful Star Gods and Spacetime Gods within the Starry Sky.","Even at his peak, he was merely a Ninth Tribulation Universe God.","He dared not attempt to devour the Starry Sky.","Of course, besides this heaven-defying danger, there were benefits as well.","He discovered that the life level of the Realm Beast could only be suppressed to about a million-fold at the lowest.","Fortunately, the physical body of the Realm Beast wasn’t reliant on soul power, but the threshold to enter the body required soul power.","Controlling and manipulating it required immense willpower.","This was because the Realm Beast was a natural-born destroyer.","It could destroy everything in existence and was also capable of creating divine beings.","The lower limit was a million times that of the human race, while the upper limit was infinite.","His thought power allowed him to control the body at will.","He punched!","The punch hit the air, and there was no fluctuation in the life level.","But when he used a technique and aimed at the void, the life level instantly soared to ten million times.","This startled Jian Wushuang, who quickly steadied himself.","“That’s terrifying. I can’t probe any further. I must first completely take control of this body!”","That strike just now directly increased the willpower of the Realm Beast by tenfold, instantly overpowering his own willpower.","Willpower was something that increased with the level of the physical body.","However, from this, he also realized that the physical body of the Realm Beast could freely exhibit levels beyond its limits.","This was the biggest surprise.","With such a high life level, once he returned, whether he pursued the path of divine power or swordsmanship, it would assist him in reaching the true pinnacle.","“Once I return and regain my original divine power, and merge it once again with this body, even if I haven’t crossed the Divine Tribulation, I won’t fear those Spacetime Gods!”","He felt an immense surge of confidence at this moment, never imagining that one day his physical body would advance so greatly.","Back when he tempered his body in the Magic Sound Mountain, he thought of his body as a bottle.","Divine power was the water.","That was a self-imposed limitation; the bottle had its limits.","Perhaps his physical body could merge with the divine body to break through those limits, but the body born within the Starry Sky was already restricted.","However, the physical body of the Realm Beast had no such limitations.","If expanded upon, the Realm Beast was a naturally born life form from the Void, while the beings of the Starry Sky were all postnatal life forms.","“With this body, what I need to break through is not just the cultivation system!”","He clenched his fist slightly, feeling the power emanating from his body. This newfound confidence made him feel that transcending the Starry Sky would not be a problem in the future.","Both his physical body and soul now had the foundation to transcend.","His soul had advanced because he devoured Morosa, and the gains from that were similar to what he gained now.","Yet, in the Realm God Continent, he had a battle power surpassing even his peak.","And in this small world of the Crimson Eye Realm, he managed to obtain such heaven-defying opportunities. It was unbelievable, almost like a dream.","And this was just the first trial.","Once he fully mastered the Realm Beast’s physical body and merged his soul and life into one, he would prepare to leave here and seek the second lamp.","But just as he was about to leave, a powerful force of restriction suddenly descended.","“Huh?” Jian Wushuang was momentarily stunned but then began to struggle free.","The corners of his mouth curled up in a cold smile as he thought, “A small restriction left by a mere Universe Master, and it wants to restrain me?”","Despite his current state being maintained at the peak of the Great Ascension, with his formidable willpower and physical strength, this restriction left by a Universe Master couldn’t hold him.","With just a slight exertion, he easily broke through the restriction.","The first lamp instantly extinguished.","The entire hall began to tremble, as if the sky was about to collapse."]},{"number":6356,"title":"Chapter 6356: Fragments of Memory","paragraphs":["Chapter 6356: Fragments of Memory","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jiu Chen, who was guarding outside the hall, suddenly felt his spiritual body beginning to contract. He looked towards the hall in horror and exclaimed, “What’s happening? Why is the aura inside the hall fading away?”","At that moment, even the blood-colored altar started to collapse and contract.","Jiu Chen’s avatar, still plotting outside, had not yet noticed.","However, the internal contraction had reached its limit.","Even the wisp of Jiu Chen’s true self inside began to disintegrate due to the contraction of the Divine Fire Hall.","Fortunately, it was just a trace of spiritual consciousness, so it wouldn’t be completely extinguished.","“Impossible! What did he do?” Jiu Chen’s true self was utterly shocked.","Even though Jian Wushuang had previously displayed his immortality, it shouldn’t have caused such a reaction in the Divine Fire Hall.","How could he have known what Jian Wushuang had discovered inside the Divine Fire Hall?","Luckily, due to the declining power of the Divine Fire, Jiu Chen could once again enter the hall and take control.","Swish!","He rushed into the Divine Fire Hall, only to see Jian Wushuang standing unharmed in his original position. Jiu Chen furiously shouted, “What did you do? Why has the power of the Divine Fire declined? The energy is collapsing!”","Jiu Chen’s true self was seething with rage. He had given up his freedom to guard this place, and now Jian Wushuang had caused such chaos. How could he not be furious?","“In this world, there is no eternal existence, only eternal power!” Jian Wushuang slowly turned around, his eyes filled with pity.","How could a mere Zhen Xian know much?","How could he possibly understand the laws of this world?","The Divine Fire Hall had begun to contract and collapse. While Jian Wushuang hadn’t expected this outcome, it wasn’t entirely surprising.","It was because he had taken the body of the Realm Beast.","This body was undoubtedly the most precious thing in the entire Temple of Inheritance.","He was only curious as to why the body of the Realm Beast had ended up here, and even more so about its purpose, which the Universe Master who created this place clearly knew.","For someone to understand the mysterious uses of the Realm Beast’s body and place it here, their identity had to be extraordinary.","A Universe Master in the Ninth Tribulation realm would never have had the opportunity to encounter a Realm Beast.","Of course, that was unless he excluded himself.","But Jian Wushuang didn’t think that the other person could compare to him.","Back then, it was only because of the Realm King Divine Realm that he learned about the Realm Beast’s immense power, but even then, he hadn’t obtained its body!","Perhaps, by accepting the inheritance here, he would finally understand everything.","Once the Divine Fire Hall had stabilized, Jian Wushuang completely ignored Jiu Chen’s true self and prepared to enter the second lamp.","But Jiu Chen’s true self could no longer stand by. He shouted angrily, “If you don’t explain yourself today, don’t even think about accepting the inheritance!”","As he spoke, he activated all the restrictions he could control, trying to block Jian Wushuang.","For someone who could forcibly merge with the Realm Beast’s body and escape the Divine Fire Hall, Jian Wushuang certainly wouldn’t care about a mere Zhen Xian.","He hadn’t destroyed Jiu Chen out of respect for the creator of this place.","After all, he had gained something valuable and saw no need to wreak havoc.","However, when it came to what he deserved, he wouldn’t hesitate.","“Stop!”","Suspended in mid-air, Jian Wushuang pointed with a single finger. Using only the power of his physical body, he instantly shattered the restrictions in this space, simultaneously binding the controller of this space tightly within the rules of destruction.","Jian Wushuang knew that if Immortal Jiu Chen dared to move recklessly again, he would be instantly annihilated by the laws of destruction.","Though he held a certain respect for this place, it didn’t mean he would allow himself to be controlled by others.","He wouldn’t go to extremes, but he would see things through to the end.","After subduing Immortal Jiu Chen’s true body, Jian Wushuang ventured into the second lamp, the second trial.","Trapped within the laws of destruction, Immortal Jiu Chen’s true body looked around in terror at the destructive forces surrounding him, unable to move. His heart was filled with dread.","When he saw Jian Wushuang entering the second lamp, he was momentarily stunned.","“He’s only just reached the second trial?”","He had thought that the great commotion caused by the Godfire Temple was because Jian Wushuang had violated the restrictions within the secret arts of the inheritance. But to his surprise, it was due to the destruction of various restrictions within the Godfire Temple across the three lamps.","“So, everything that just happened was because of the first lamp?”","He turned his gaze to the mural depicting the Heavenly Palace, focusing on the lamp within the image.","“It’s gone dark!”","“The lamp has gone dark...”","Immortal Jiu Chen’s heart was initially filled with astonishment, but suddenly, a powerful consciousness surged into his mind.","However, due to the surrounding laws of destruction, this consciousness was cautious, not daring to be reckless.","But Immortal Jiu Chen’s consciousness was already weak, and as soon as the powerful consciousness invaded, he fell into a deep sleep.","In its place was a new consciousness, one that was gradually weakening, connected to the laws of time.","The controlled Immortal Jiu Chen raised his head to gaze at the mural of the Heavenly Palace, unable to calm his heart.","“How many years has it been... I’ve finally waited for you!” Within Jiu Chen’s eyes, a starry nebula could be seen. Above the nebula, an elderly man sat cross-legged, and in a flash, the image of the Realm God Continent appeared.","...","The second lamp.","This was the place where souls resided.","There were nine in total.","This time, instead of trying them one by one, Jian Wushuang went directly to the ninth golden soul. A crack appeared between his eyebrows, and a powerful force of attraction drew the golden soul directly into his sea of consciousness.","“Hmm!!”","A strong force of interference pushed him back a step.","It appeared to be a soul, but it felt more like a cluster of memories.","Sealed memories, from...","“I’ve seen this place before!” Jian Wushuang’s eyes became vacant as he saw a scene of the heavens and earth collapsing within his mind.","“This is a battlefield!”","But this place didn’t belong to any part of the Starry Sky.","He had seen it before in Morosa’s consciousness as well.","This was the Void Land.","In an instant, time and space felt far, far away from him.","Yet the mighty warriors on the battlefield seemed very close.","He saw a mysterious warrior wearing a mask.","The mask looked familiar, but he couldn’t recall the name.","The masked warrior, with his hands behind his back, fought against three opponents alone.","His adversaries were not Universe Beasts, but three figures emanating an indescribably powerful aura.","The aura was stronger than anything Jian Wushuang had ever encountered, even stronger than the Star Spirits.","It was so overwhelming that he could barely breathe.","Even with his Universe Beast physique, the pressure made his heart race.","It was as if he had encountered a natural enemy.","This power was immense, enough to shake the heavens and the earth.","Yet the mysterious masked warrior could hold off all three, battling them to a standstill.","Their fight caused the chaotic streams on the battlefield to flow in reverse.","The battle moved from the battlefield to a towering divine mountain, where the aura was so intense that Jian Wushuang shuddered, as if he had been there before.","He looked up at the top of the divine mountain, but clouds obscured his view.","Returning his gaze to the battle, he saw that the fight had grown more intense. The mysterious masked warrior seemed to be desperately holding them off, while the three overwhelmingly powerful warriors were trying to destroy the divine mountain.","The masked warrior was overwhelmed, unable to stop them.","In the end, he sacrificed himself to take down two of them.","But one top-tier warrior remained, and he began to attack the divine mountain.","At that moment, another warrior appeared.","This time, Jian Wushuang saw the face clearly.","His eyes widened in shock.","It was him."]},{"number":6357,"title":"Chapter 6357: The Self in Her Memory","paragraphs":["Chapter 6357: The Self in Her Memory","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Carrying the divine sword on his back, Jian Wushuang wore dark red battle armor, his hair flowing in the wind.","Facing a formidable opponent with an overwhelming presence, he silently drew his sword, executing a move he had never seen before.","But that sword strike encompassed the entire Starry Sky.","It was one of his Starry Sky Nine Swords, though he wasn’t sure which one.","With just that one strike, the formidable opponent was instantly gravely injured, clutching his chest in an attempt to escape. Yet, Jian Wushuang didn’t pursue him. He simply stood alone with his sword at the base of the sacred mountain.","The scene shifted again.","It seemed as though there were fragments missing from his memory.","In the next moment, Jian Wushuang was lying amidst a field of corpses, the sacred mountain still standing in the background. He knelt atop a pile of bodies, his breath completely gone.","At that moment, several figures with overwhelming auras brushed past him, heading toward the sacred mountain.","Within the clouds halfway up the mountain, a crack slowly opened, followed by a blinding burst of light.","In an instant, those figures fell from the top of the sacred mountain, and with a thunderous crash, the mountain itself began to collapse.","A sense of hopeless void erupted from that place.","And with that, the memory abruptly ended.","Jian Wushuang’s eyes instantly cleared, and everything that had just happened felt like a dream. He had silently absorbed the golden soul.","Yet, the images in his mind refused to dissipate. Beyond the memory, what lingered most vividly was that one brilliant sword strike.","In that single strike, he had gained many insights.","It was a revelation that could assist him in his own swordsmanship, but now, he had no interest in training. He stood dazed in place for what felt like half a day.","“A mask... the Prophet... the sacred mountain... a formidable opponent with overwhelming aura!”","Jian Wushuang murmured, momentarily unable to distinguish between reality and illusion. It took him a while to regain his composure.","The mysterious figure wearing the mask was the Prophet he had encountered in the Star Field of the Gods. He clearly remembered that his Beast God Weapon had been forged by this Prophet, but in the memory he had absorbed, he could not recall the Prophet at all.","The reason he couldn’t recall the Prophet in that memory was because he himself had appeared within it.","“Could it be... that everything was real?” Jian Wushuang’s heart trembled.","If that was his past life, he wouldn’t have had the Beast God Weapon or the Myriad Tribulation Sword.","What exactly was it?","He wasn’t sure, but the only person he could think of was his teacher, Xuan Yi.","It seemed to be the future, yet in reality, it was the past!","“Is this what Teacher Xuan Yi meant by seeing the future? But how long will I need to train?” he asked himself with a bitter smile, shaking his head.","It had been a very long time since he last met with Teacher Xuan Yi.","After entering the Dayan Realm, Teacher Xuan Yi had met him in the Qishen Temple, gave him the Heaven-Gazing Chessboard, and instructed him to comprehend the mysteries of the myriad paths through its pieces, ultimately choosing the path of endless transformations.","At that time, he had only been a Dao Lord.","But now...","He wasn’t even a Dao Lord anymore. Though all of this might have been a trial and test from Teacher Xuan Yi, intended to help him overcome the divine Tribulation.","However, in the future memories, those formidable presences were existences he couldn’t even begin to imagine.","Thinking of reaching that level, he wondered how many more years of training it would take.","With greater power comes greater responsibility, and though his powerful state of mind remained, he couldn’t help but feel a sense of impatience.","Perhaps it was because he had seen his future failure and desperately wanted to change it!","“Master Xuan Yi, I will work twice as hard until I can stand before you!” Jian Wushuang’s gaze became incredibly resolute at that moment, and his entire aura surged with determination.","The next moment, the surroundings began to darken.","His entire body was transported out, and the second lamp extinguished.","As he emerged, he immediately noticed Immortal Jiu Chen, who was waiting quietly within the law of destruction. Just one glance was enough for him to realize that something seemed different about the other person.","“Who are you?” Jian Wushuang’s eyes narrowed, and the law of destruction instantly swept over Immortal Jiu Chen. If the other party made even the slightest suspicious move, Jian Wushuang could kill him in an instant.","Because in Immortal Jiu Chen’s eyes, he saw a trace of hatred.","Immortal Jiu Chen, still within the law of destruction, saw Jian Wushuang’s serious demeanor and said something that shocked Jian Wushuang. “Uncle-Master, please don’t take action, let me explain!”","“Who are you calling Uncle-Master?” Jian Wushuang was taken aback.","The changed Immortal Jiu Chen helplessly replied, “You!”","Moments later.","Jian Wushuang stroked his chin, furrowing his brow as he spoke, “Your master is called Ghost Eye? That means he’s my senior brother?”","“Yes, yes, that’s correct. However, I’ve never met Master. I only received his inheritance. From his teachings, I learned that Uncle-Master would come to the temple I had set up after countless years!” Immortal Jiu Chen stood there honestly, not daring to hide anything.","This left Jian Wushuang somewhat perplexed.","From what the other person was saying, he suddenly had a senior brother named Ghost Eye, who was once very powerful but had fallen later on. He then passed his inheritance to the Lord of Divine Fire, who was now possessing Immortal Jiu Chen’s spirit, and set up the Divine Fire Temple, waiting for Jian Wushuang to take over the inheritance?","But who was their master?","If he and Ghost Eye were senior brothers, then who was their master?","“Could it be Master Xuan Yi?” Jian Wushuang’s heart stirred.","In the memories he absorbed, he saw a pair of eyes in a rift—could those eyes belong to Ghost Eye?","Although this seemed far-fetched, he was willing to believe it.","Because what was left for him here was the Realm Beast’s body and that memory.","“I’ll believe you for now!” Jian Wushuang’s voice carried authority as he asked, “Tell me, what else did my senior brother leave behind?”","The Lord of Divine Fire took a deep breath and replied, “Master left behind three lamps. Uncle-Master has already passed through the first two, but the third lamp only requires me to confirm your identity, and then I can directly give the contents inside to Uncle-Master!”","“Oh?” Jian Wushuang raised an eyebrow. He understood the implication.","If someone truly extraordinary had extinguished the first two lamps, the remaining one would activate the Lord of Divine Fire to personally verify Jian Wushuang’s identity. If it was indeed Uncle-Master, then the third lamp’s contents would be handed over.","If not, then it would mean that someone lucky had encountered an extraordinary inheritance.","Of course, this was just Jian Wushuang’s speculation.","But he wasn’t wrong—if an extraordinary inheritor had come to the Divine Fire Temple, the Lord of Divine Fire would have benefited even more.","Much more than waiting here for Jian Wushuang.","However, the contents of the third lamp could not be given to the inheritor; they had to be handed to Jian Wushuang personally.","“Uncle-Master, please take a look. Inside the third lamp is a gray jar. Master said that as long as Uncle-Master appeared, the gray jar should be given to Uncle-Master, and once Uncle-Master retrieves an item from within it, the task would be considered complete!” The Lord of Divine Fire spoke with some excitement.","This made Jian Wushuang chuckle slightly as he asked, “And after it’s completed?”","“Well... I can’t say right now. I can only tell you once Uncle-Master succeeds!” The Lord of Divine Fire smiled awkwardly.","Jian Wushuang didn’t mind this. He accepted the gray jar and, using his thought power, attempted to explore it, only to feel a powerful force pulling his body and soul into the jar."]},{"number":6358,"title":"Chapter 6358: Ash Pot","paragraphs":["Chapter 6358: Ash Pot","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“What’s going on?” The Lord of Divine Fire was stunned.","He hadn’t expected the gray jar to swallow Jian Wushuang, because his master hadn’t mentioned anything like that!","Jian Wushuang was also startled, initially thinking he had fallen into a trap. However, once he entered the gray jar, he dismissed that thought.","Inside the gray jar, countless void particles gathered.","These particles, or rather, white dust, each resembled a universe.","The space within the gray jar was vast, and when Jian Wushuang extended his thought power to cover the surrounding million miles, he only then discovered the boundary.","Within this enormous area, it was filled with microscopic universes in the shape of dust particles.","Each particle contained the power of a universe.","“This... this is truly a windfall!” Jian Wushuang gasped. Under his thought power’s coverage, he couldn’t even calculate how much universal power this place contained.","Such a vast amount of power couldn’t even be fully absorbed after transcending a divine Tribulation.","It might even be possible to directly absorb enough power to reach the level of a Universe Master.","The rewards from these three trials had been greater each time.","First was the body of the Realm Beast, which needed no further explanation; possessing this body was the cornerstone for his journey out of the Starry Sky.","Then, there was the memory fragment. It made him realize that stepping out of the Starry Sky was just the foundation; the first step to helping Teacher Xuan Yi was to leave the Starry Sky.","And now there was this gray jar. Although he didn’t know what it was made from, the power inside was so immense that it could probably rival a fully evolved Realm Beast like Morosa.","Once he transcended the divine Tribulation, he could slowly absorb it.","“Wait a minute, Divine Fire told me to take something out. But here, all around me, there are only these microscopic universes. What am I supposed to take out?” He took a deep breath and exclaimed, “Could it be that I’m supposed to take out an entire universe?”","The white dust here was abundant, even forming a thick layer of the cosmic sea on the ground.","But every single speck of dust was a universe!","If he were in his prime, taking one out wouldn’t be a big deal.","But right now, he was just at the peak of the Grand Perfection stage, a state considered transcendent but still just slightly beyond the general Heavenly Dao. Although his strength had already reached a level beyond immortality, he couldn’t possibly carry an entire universe out!","“Do I have to forcibly move it?” He smiled bitterly.","If that were the case, how much strength would he need?","Relying on just the power of his physical body and the will of his soul, he felt almost hopeless.","Even at the Emperor level’s peak, it was nearly impossible to move a universe.","Back in the original universe, when he had grown to the peak, facing the vastness of the original universe, he could at most destroy some high-level worlds or create some high-level worlds.","At his most powerful, he had only been able to move a secret universe, which was only one-tenth the size of a universe.","But back then, he was at the peak, comparable to a Tribulation level being.","And now?","He was just at the peak of the Grand Perfection stage. Even with the body of a Realm Beast, he didn’t dare say he could span several levels to move a universe out!","“Impossible!”","“But that doesn’t mean I won’t succeed!”","After giving himself a pep talk, he reached out to touch the nearest microscopic universe.","“Hmm?”","Jian Wushuang was delighted. The dust was very light, just like real dust, but it couldn’t be destroyed.","He immediately regained his confidence and, holding a speck of dust, flew toward the opening of the gray jar.","As soon as he tried to leave, the microscopic universe emanated an aura more terrifying than his perfected universe. As it left the gray jar, matter and everything else came into being.","As he began to leave, halfway out of the jar, he was suddenly pulled back inside.","This time, it wasn’t the attraction but the weight of the object that dragged him down.","There was no doubt that it was the microscopic universe.","“As expected, it’s not that simple. If it were, it would be strange. Teacher Xuan Yi always gives me tasks that seem impossible, but I always manage to accomplish them!” Jian Wushuang’s lips curled up. He increased the life level of his physical body by five million times, enduring the soul-crushing pain, and once again charged outward with the microscopic universe.","Boom!","Just as half of his body managed to escape, it was completely dragged back again.","However, his greatest strength was his persistence!","Each time he attempted to break free, he was dragged back over and over.","During these attempts, he needed to increase his strength, continuously challenging his limits.","He elevated the level of his physical body to millions of times its original strength.","This was far from the upper limit of his physical body, but it had already surpassed the limit of his soul.","Yet, he gritted his teeth and persevered.","In one of his closest attempts, his ankle nearly broke free, but he still failed.","However, this failure only fueled his courage to keep trying.","He also realized the importance of focusing his mind.","This was practice for him to perfect his control over his physical body.","It was a beneficial process for him.","Through repeatedly lifting the Universe, he gained the experience of controlling his physical body to its extreme limits in the face of failure.","“A strength of fifteen million times the power of the physical body, this power is enough to rival the Tribulation Realm!” Jian Wushuang adjusted his strength and once again lifted the microcosm of the Universe. With a powerful thrust of his legs, he shot up like a divine sword, rushing towards the opening of the gray jar.","Boom!","The moment he burst out of the gray jar, an immense force swept over him once again. But this time, he didn’t fall. Instead, he used every last bit of his strength to fly out of the jar.","Splash!","He nearly collapsed onto the ground from exhaustion but, remembering that his nephew was watching, he composed himself and sat cross-legged on the ground, speaking calmly, “I have already retrieved one item. You may continue with your explanation.”","“Uncle-Master, you are indeed extraordinary. At the peak of the Great Perfection, you managed to extract an entire microcosm of the Universe. It’s truly unprecedented!” The Lord of Divine Fire was visibly excited. He gazed at the floating microcosm with fiery eyes, swallowing hard before returning to the main topic. “Back then, Master said that if you could retrieve an item, I was to give you this token. He mentioned that this token could open the Nine Prison Pagoda!”","With that, he handed over a simple, ancient token.","Jian Wushuang took it, maintaining a calm exterior, but inside, he was overjoyed.","He had long suspected that the Nine Prison Pagoda was no ordinary treasure, and indeed, it was extraordinary.","Especially this token, which was very similar to the one that Master Xuan Yi had left him back then.","However, that token was meant to be used in times of life-threatening danger, while this one was intended to unlock the Nine Prison Pagoda.","Thinking of this, he stored the token in his mind with a thought, and simultaneously went to unlock the Nine Prison Pagoda.","But the token only had the number “one” on it, corresponding to the first level.","He could fully open the first level without any difficulty, but there was nothing inside, meaning there was no gain. He guessed that as he grew stronger, he would gradually unlock the higher levels.","He put this matter to the back of his mind.","“Is there anything else besides this?” Jian Wushuang asked tentatively.","The Lord of Divine Fire reluctantly tore his gaze away from the microcosm, then looked at the stern expression and said, “No, Master instructed that once you have the Nine Prison Pagoda, you can stand tall in all the heavens and have the potential to ascend to the Heavens!”"]},{"number":6359,"title":"Chapter 6359: Microcosmic Universe","paragraphs":["Chapter 6359: Microcosmic Universe","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Again!” Jian Wushuang smiled bitterly in his heart. This presence had appeared countless times, and he was almost speechless. However, he still feigned a calm expression and said indifferently, “I don’t care about these things!”","He could see that the Master of Divine Fire cared deeply about that microcosmic universe, so he asked, “Do you like this universe very much?”","“I wouldn’t dare. This belongs to my master-uncle; I wouldn’t dare to have selfish desires!” The Master of Divine Fire hurriedly shook his head.","Jian Wushuang waved his hand and said, “This is our first meeting, and you keep calling me master-uncle. You’ve also passed along everything that my senior brother entrusted to you. You’ve done well, so I’ll bestow this universe upon you!”","Although the Master of Divine Fire had fallen, Jian Wushuang could tell that a remnant of his consciousness still existed. It wasn’t a mere fragment, which suggested a chance for revival.","Perhaps, when that Senior Brother Ghost Eye left this gray jar and asked him to retrieve something from it before handing the Nine Prison Token to him, it was his intention to give the Master of Divine Fire another opportunity!","A speck of dust, even a perfect universe that transcended limits, was of no concern to him, for he had a jar full of them.","However, this microcosmic universe could enable the Master of Divine Fire to be resurrected and become a Universe Master once again, reaching his peak swiftly.","In the future, he could be a helpful ally, and as a fellow disciple from the same lineage, he was trustworthy and worth helping.","“I can see that you need this universe to be reborn. I believe Senior Brother Ghost Eye also left you many good things. Take this universe as well; consider it my gift to you!” Jian Wushuang waved his hand, and the floating universe drifted toward the Master of Divine Fire.","This gesture left him overwhelmed with emotion.","Ghost Eye had indeed left him many treasures, but none could facilitate a quick revival. However, this microcosmic universe was different.","Once his consciousness entered the microcosmic universe, starting with controlling the stars and gradually mastering a perfect universe, he could return to the level of a Universe Master of the Seventh Tribulation within ten years.","To restore his peak state, comparable to a Universe God, would only take a few centuries.","By then, combined with the treasures left by Ghost Eye, passing the divine tribulation and becoming a Universe God would be a simple matter.","Without this microcosmic universe, who knew when he would revive? Even if he did, he would have to start from scratch, wasting a lot of time and facing the risk of perishing prematurely. If that happened, he would have to begin again.","The most critical aspect was that starting over meant that the opportunities he needed wouldn’t be prepared in advance. Who knew when he would reach his peak again? Moreover, he couldn’t rush it; every foundation had to be built carefully, or he would have to tear it all down and start anew.","Now, things were different. A perfect universe, and a microcosmic one at that, provided him with ample time and opportunities to be reborn and quickly return to his peak.","Such good fortune was something he wouldn’t have dared to dream of in the past, but now he could, and he dreamed big. In the future, he, too, had the hope of ascending to the heavens.","Every cell in his body trembled with excitement. The Master of Divine Fire knelt down, bowing deeply, and said respectfully, “Master-uncle’s kindness, Divine Fire will never forget. Should you ever need anything from me in the future, I will go through fire and water without hesitation. This I swear, with heaven and earth as my witness, the sun and moon as my testimony!”","One could tell from his speech that he had read many books in his mortal days. If it had been Xiang Yang, he would have simply said, “I’m with you too!”","“Alright, alright, you can directly enter this microcosmic universe. You can also take the Divine Fire Palace with you!” Jian Wushuang said with a calm wave of his hand.","He had already taken the important things from the Divine Fire Palace. Initially, he had considered studying the Divine Eye’s legacy, but the token from Senior Brother Ghost Eye contained the ultimate Divine Eye secret technique.","It far surpassed the rumored sequence inheritance.","The sequence inheritance was far too limited, only sufficient for someone at the level of a Universe God to use.","It might be useful for a Universe Master, but that was all.","Burning a bit of divine power probably wasn’t even as potent as his Super Eternal Transformation.","In this aspect, Jian Wushuang had confidence.","The Divine Eye secret technique required burning divine power, while his Super Eternal Transformation amplified divine power.","Of course, he also had a burning secret technique, but it might be slightly inferior to the top-level Divine Eye secret technique.","After dismissing the Master of Divine Fire, Jian Wushuang returned to the blood-red entrance, where Immortal Jiu Chen’s spiritual form floated down.","However, it had already fallen into slumber.","“The master of Qishen Temple has returned. Now it is time for you, the true spirit of Qishen Temple, to return to your original state!” Jian Wushuang pointed a finger, instantly restoring Immortal Jiu Chen’s spiritual body to its peak.","The power that erupted from that spiritual consciousness was comparable to that of a Universe God.","Unfortunately, in the presence of Jian Wushuang, who had reached the pinnacle of Great Realm King, that power from the Universe God lost its luster.","For the Universe God could not move the universe, whereas Jian Wushuang, despite only being at the peak of Great Realm King, could move an entire universe.","And he had moved it out of the gray jar.","Immortal Jiu Chen regained consciousness and found his spiritual body had returned to its peak. But before he could rejoice, he noticed that Qishen Temple had vanished.","“Jian Wushuang, what have you done?” Immortal Jiu Chen was on the verge of collapse.","The last time Qishen Temple had almost collapsed, and now it had completely disappeared.","Jian Wushuang couldn’t be bothered to explain. He didn’t know where the temple had gone, but it was certain that the temple no longer had anything to do with Immortal Jiu Chen. The only reason he kept Immortal Jiu Chen around was because there was still another Jiu Chen outside.","He was curious to see what would happen when the two met.","Would they devour each other, or cooperate?","Both were possible.","Now, he just needed to wait for the right opportunity to go out.","He had already gained transcendent power; neither his strength nor his realm would be suppressed, and everything outside could no longer escape his detection.","Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang were both present, and so was Chen Yuan. His soul had been well-preserved.","It seemed that Li Miao and Immortal Jiu Chen had kept their word and had not killed Chen Yuan.","His Thought power encompassed the entire Star Field of the Gods.","Within it, two of the most powerful auras stood out.","One was from that ancient demon, whose strength was recovering rapidly and had already reached the peak of Divine Soul.","The other was the Ghost Emperor... though he could no longer be called the Ghost Emperor, as he had merged with Immortal Jiu Chen.","The true spirit’s consciousness had fused with what appeared to be a perfect soul. What remained was the blood mist and blood crystals hidden within the blood-colored altar, the essence left behind after the ancient demon’s fall. Although this essence was from the soul lineage, it could still condense into a flesh body with a life level a thousand times stronger.","That would be the body of a Special Life Form, likely the greatest scheme Immortal Jiu Chen had in the Star Field of the Gods.","Using the souls of mortals, he had refined the Ghost Emperor.","And with the blood essence body within the blood-colored altar, he would eventually become a postnatal Special Life Form, embarking on the path of cultivation.","Everything he saw was transmitted to the forefront of his vision through the celestial curtain.","What Jian Wushuang could see, the real Jiu Chen could also see.","Seeing his own avatar creating a perfect soul and realizing that the blood mist and blood crystals were just one step away from merging with the flesh body, his feelings were incredibly complex."]},{"number":6360,"title":"Chapter 6360: Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6360: Emperor","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Because the Qishen Temple was gone, he had no place to return to.","Perhaps the split consciousness from the beginning was correct.","“This avatar of yours has planned everything well. You’re very close to success. Once you succeed, you’ll become a Special Life Form, with the potential to reach the Immortal level in the future. But you will always remain just an Immortal, and an Immortal with no place to return to at that. Are you willing to accept that?” Jian Wushuang stirred the pot, unafraid of causing more trouble.","Immortal Jiu Chen, furious, retorted, “I don’t need you to worry about it! You’ve destroyed the Qishen Temple, so just wait for divine retribution. The master will not let you go!”","Looking at the other party, Jian Wushuang thought to himself, if he knew that the Master of Qishen had knelt before him, he wondered what his reaction would be.","Without further words, he scanned Li Miao with his Thought power.","The first deposed emperor of the Great Tang was currently nestled with a frail woman.","That woman was none other than Consort Yi.","Seeing her delicate and pitiable appearance, Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but feel regretful. She had been killed by the one she loved the most, resurrected by the same person, and then killed again.","What sin had she committed in her past life to encounter such a wretched fate?","Watching everything from behind the scenes, one could truly see the reality of the human world.","This was the most genuine scene.","A living hell.","The Ancient Demon had slaughtered all the mortals of the Seven Southern Nations and had already reached the Eastern Land.","No one could stop him.","But there was someone who dared to try.","That person was not Emperor Li Miao, but the Commander of the Zhanxian Guards, Wei Jiuxian.","Outside the city of Mangshan.","The Ancient Demon swung his eight arms, shattering the canyon outside the city.","Feeling the summons from beneath Mangshan City, the eyes on the Ancient Demon’s chest burned with heat and greed.","But before that, he intended to devour all life in the Eastern Land.","The light emanating from his enormous eyes covered the entire Great Tang of the Eastern Land.","Countless people watched this scene; even the fierce battle within the city came to a halt.","At this moment, only four people were left fighting Immortal Jiu Chen.","Two of them were powerful beings from the Upper Realm, both at the peak of the Divine Power Realm.","The other two were Arhats from Baoguang Temple.","As for the others, they were severely injured and had lost the ability to fight. They all stood on the city wall, watching the ongoing battle.","But now that the Ancient Demon had arrived, even they had stopped fighting.","“Jiu Chen!!!”","Zhen Xian was also panicking, attempting to persuade him, “Even if you become a Special Life Form, with your potential, you’ll never ascend to the Immortal level. Why not assist me? I’ll ask my master to descend and kill the Ancient Demon, giving all his flesh and blood to you!”","“An Upper Realm cultivator, do you think I’m a fool? If you had a way to summon a transcendent being, you could have done it already. Let your master come down and kill the Ancient Demon. That way, you can also become a Special Life Form. We wouldn’t be in conflict!” Immortal Jiu Chen sneered.","He had experienced nine worlds, seen more people than they had meals, and would never be deceived by an Upper Realm cultivator.","Even if it were possible to summon a transcendent being from the Upper Realm, why not just have the powerful being come down and kill the Ancient Demon directly?","It was evident that there were concerns, as the Ancient Demon was an invaluable treasure no matter where it was found.","Zhen Xian and Fu Qing descended to the lower realm precisely for this Ancient Demon.","Unable to kill it while alive, they set their sights on its blood-colored altar.","They, too, desired to elevate their life levels. Such an opportunity would not be easily handed over to others.","Now, having fused his soul with the Ghost Emperor, his soul level had already increased five hundredfold.","Next, he would refine the Ancient Demon’s essence blood and reshape his physical body, elevating his life level to five thousand times.","With such a supreme body, his strength would soar to the pinnacle of the Great Circle.","At that point, he would be just a step away from becoming an Immortal. When that time came, he would seize control of his original body, thereby gaining mastery over the Divine Fire Palace. From within the Divine Fire Palace, he would gradually transport treasures, sufficient for him to break through to Immortality.","Additionally, he sought the primary sequence of the Divine Eye inheritance.","From then on, he would ascend rapidly, with a chance to become a Great Emperor.","This was his ultimate plan, and now it was very close to being realized.","The Ancient Demon was on its way, and soon everyone here would fall. Their essence blood, due to the great formation, would all be integrated into his refining technique.","At that moment, the Death Formation began to transform into a Blood Refining Formation.","The death energy in the sky gradually turned blood red.","It was a blood mist drawn from the blood-colored altar.","This formation was more than sufficient to refine the Ancient Demon.","Therefore, he feared neither the Ancient Demon nor the cultivators within the city.","Even if they had reached the pinnacle of the Divine Appearance Realm, they were no match for him, regardless of their strength.","His soul level had already reached the Primordial Spirit Realm.","Once he fused with his physical body, he would reach the Great Circle’s completion.","The Ancient Demon outside, whose life level had recovered to two thousand times, would also be suppressed under this great formation.","To him, there was no threat in this world.","Thus, he always looked down on Zhen Xian from the Baoguang Temple.","If it weren’t for the opponent’s protective treasure, he would have slapped him to death long ago.","“Fine, very well, this immortal will withdraw now, let’s see how you fend off the Ancient Demon!” Zhen Xian waved his hand, his face dark, and said, “Junior sister, let’s go!”","With that, he transformed into a stream of light and fled the Mangshan County City.","This infuriated the two Luohan, their faces turning crimson. Originally, they were only at the early stage of the Divine Appearance Realm, but with the help of the Old Ancestor of the Tang Dynasty, they could temporarily elevate to the pinnacle of the Divine Appearance Realm, a level where they could easily shatter space and ascend.","Yet now, Zhen Xian had fled.","This was not what they had agreed to!","Back then, the Old Ancestor of the Tang Dynasty promised them a chance to ascend, but they had to protect the Eastern Lands.","Now, their power was nearly exhausted. If they wanted to fulfill their promise, they would surely die this time, with no hope of ascending.","If they chose to ascend, they would have to watch the Eastern Lands fall apart.","For a moment, two conflicting thoughts swirled in their minds. Finally, they exchanged a glance, said nothing, and also transformed into streams of light, fleeing the Mangshan County City.","There was no need to ask; it was clear that they had given up.","They couldn’t abandon the chance to ascend and perish with the Tang Dynasty.","Fortunately, they still had some attachment to the Tang Dynasty, so they didn’t flee immediately. They decided to wait and see. If things really got out of hand, they would shatter space and ascend directly.","Even though space had become more solid now, their strength was still sufficient to break through and leave.","But for Zhen Xian and Fu Qing, those powerful beings from the upper realm, it would take a hundred times more strength to shatter space and escape.","The key was that these two had descended to pursue the inheritance sequence and the Ancient Demon’s essence blood.","Transforming themselves into Special Life Forms was something human cultivators dreamed of.","It was said that the cultivators from the Ancient Domain were far more powerful than those from the outer spacetime. This wasn’t about quantity but quality.","This place was the Tomb of the Gods, and their blood carried traces of divine blood.","Those Special Life Forms that could be nurtured here were even more powerful.","Their life levels were generally very high.","Combined with the inheritance sequence of the Divine Eye Secret Technique, once they became acquired Special Life Forms, both their comprehension and life levels would reach the pinnacle, leading them on the true path of becoming a Great Emperor."]},{"number":6361,"title":"Chapter 6361: Everything for the Great Cause","paragraphs":["Chapter 6361: Everything for the Great Cause","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Who would give up this path?","Everyone who encountered it would fight desperately.","Zhen Xian who had escaped the city hovered above the clouds, glaring at the ancient demon with gritted teeth. He muttered under his breath, “Hmph, I want to see how Jiu Chen plans to stop this!”","“Senior Brother, I think that Blood Coagulation Array is very strange. We should be cautious. If it really becomes too difficult, we should ask Master for help. Opportunities like this are rare in a lifetime. Even if our master takes most of the benefits, we can still request help from him once we return to the sect. After all, we haven’t transcended yet. I would be satisfied if my life level could maintain a thousandfold,” Fu Qing felt that hope was slipping away.","But Zhen Xian didn’t think so; instead, he became unusually resolute.","He knew that once his master descended, all the benefits would be gone.","By the time they returned to the sect, there would be a group of fellow disciples, and he might not be able to compete with them.","The ancient demon’s essence blood was extremely important; his master needed it too. Even if it wasn’t useful to him, it could be exchanged with other powerful beings for treasures he required.","For a transcendent being who had surpassed mortality, their goal was to become an Immortal. How could they abandon their future for the sake of a disciple’s prospects?","Even if he pleaded, it would be useless. Once his master descended, merely rescuing him would clear all debts, and there would be no rewards.","Understanding this reality, Zhen Xian was even more determined not to let his master descend, unless he was on the brink of death. Otherwise, he would never summon his master.","If he had the chance to succeed, the essence blood of the two ancient demons and the mysterious power within the blood-red altar would all be his.","At that time, he could directly break through, shatter the void, and return to the sect. In just a few years, he could transcend and become a Grand Existence. With the inheritance of the Divine Eye and his life level, breaking through to Immortal was only a matter of time.","This was the prize worth fighting for, not summoning his master to descend on the spot.","At this moment, everyone had similar thoughts— the more they knew, the greedier they became.","Those who were already severely injured in the Divine Aspect Realm were about to lose their lives due to their greed.","The Blood Coagulation Array began to madly absorb the essence blood of the cultivators within the city. This essence blood was only the beginning; the bulk of it was in the blood-red altar.","The blood began to gather around Jiu Chen’s towering soul.","With such a massive body, his life level was condensed to five thousandfold. He was the second greediest person present.","The first was the ancient demon.","He intended to turn the entire Crimson Eyes Realm into his own Dao Field, annihilate everyone, and absorb all the essence blood within the blood-red altar.","At this moment, he was absorbing the essence blood of all the mortals in the Eastern Lands.","Anyone caught in the light of his gaze had their flesh instantly shattered, turning into essence blood that flowed into the light and eventually returned to the ancient demon.","Few cared about what the ancient demon was doing.","Everyone had their eyes on the greater treasure.","In fact, they thought the ancient demon was right; once they killed it, they could obtain even more treasures.","In Mangshan County City.","The consciousness of Immortal Jiu Chen appeared in the underwater cave dwelling.","“Now, only the final step remains!” Immortal Jiu Chen stood at the entrance of the cave, not turning back to look at the two figures on the stone bed.","Li Miao gently laid down Lady Yi, stepped back, donned his clothes, and walked to the entrance, his voice trembling slightly as he said, “Immortal Master, I’ve succeeded!”","This statement was somewhat perplexing, even causing Immortal Jiu Chen to pause in confusion before he understood what Li Miao meant.","Upon taking a closer look at Li Miao, he indeed had succeeded.","Li Miao had once been an ordinary cultivator in the Nascent Soul stage, with a very low level of life essence and soul quality. Even his cultivation was merely the result of accumulating the blood essence of mortals.","Given his frail foundation, reaching the Divine Appearance stage was already difficult; and even if he did, shattering the void to ascend was simply impossible.","Yet, as their final plan unfolded, Li Miao’s ambition became evident.","From a mortal emperor, he aspired to walk the path of immortality, a path filled with cruelty.","He had to gradually cleanse his mortal form.","Without Immortal Jiu Chen’s guidance, how could he have known so much?","From his cultivation level to his soul, and now to the point where he had extracted the essence of the Empress, cleansing his mortal body, and acquiring the Pure Human Physique.","This physique was of a high life essence, capable of nurturing the soul.","In fact, compared to a Special Life Form, it wasn’t that special.","However, it could be used as a stepping stone.","A mortal in the Nascent Soul stage trying to become a postnatal Special Life Form was impossible.","It was like a child learning to walk; it needed to be done step by step.","Now, Li Miao could already stand up and walk, and he was walking steadily. So, how far could he be from running?","“All for the grand endeavor, no need to...” Immortal Jiu Chen, feeling gratified as he looked at the current Li Miao, patted his shoulder, wanting to offer some words of comfort but unsure where to start.","Li Miao nodded slightly, understanding Immortal Jiu Chen’s meaning. Forcing a smile, he said, “Immortal Master, rest assured, I know what I want, and I’m clear on the path I will walk. Now that I possess the Pure Physique and have broken through to the peak of the Divine Appearance stage, the only thing left is the Blood Condensation Array. Once it succeeds and two Special Physiques are born, it will be time to ascend!”","“Li Miao, you’ve never disappointed me. Remember, this is just the first step. Our world is vast, and the Ancient Domain is merely one among the myriad worlds!” Immortal Jiu Chen couldn’t help but sigh, recalling the days of old, which were dull and devoid of hope.","Now, when he looked up, the sky was filled with stars, each one a beacon of hope.","Thus, he had the thought of splitting, eventually separating from his original body.","Now, having reached this point, he was finally about to succeed.","Li Miao also felt gratitude in his heart. From a young prince, he had come this far. No one understood him, he was dethroned, but instead of anger, he felt that the world didn’t comprehend him.","Only Immortal Jiu Chen understood his heart.","That was ambition.","The two of them had fulfilled each other.","Back then, the consciousness of Immortal Jiu Chen was very weak, accidentally taken from the Northern Ice Fields by the ancestor of the Tang Dynasty, and later attached to a toy, eventually discovered by Li Miao, leading to their master-disciple bond.","In truth, both of them had risen from the depths of the mundane world, yet they could now ascend to the heavens.","If not for the countless mortals they had slain, it could have been a beautiful tale.","After their reflections, the two returned to the matter at hand.","At this moment, the ancient demon was devouring billions of people from the Eastern Lands.","Once it finished, it would descend upon Mangshan County City.","Within the city was a grand array, with Immortal Jiu Chen present.","There was naturally nothing to fear.","But after years of meticulous planning, they already had a flawless plan.","The ancient demon was not a fixed variable, so they naturally didn’t bet everything on themselves; they had backup plans.","“Let’s go to the city wall!” Immortal Jiu Chen said, and his consciousness vanished.","Li Miao glanced back at the figure on the stone bed, took a deep breath, and walked out of the cave dwelling.","In Mangshan City, atop the northern city wall.","Zhang Xiansheng and the others stood there, staring at the ancient demon, no longer thinking of escape.","Their physical bodies had already been absorbed by the Blood Condensation Array; now, only their souls remained. If not for the Dispersed Death Qi Array, nothing would have been left of them."]},{"number":6362,"title":"Chapter 6362: Take a Gamble?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6362: Take a Gamble?","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","At this moment, the soul form gazed at the ancient demon outside the city, and a cold feeling spread through his heart.","“There’s no hope left. Next up is the battle between the Ghost Emperor and the ancient demon. Those two powerful beings from the upper realms are probably just waiting to reap the benefits. How boring!” Zhang Xiansheng sighed deeply.","Miao Renfeng of the Barbarian Lands tribe couldn’t help but mock himself, saying, “Even that is better than us. At least they still have choices, while we secretly fight among ourselves. In the end, we’re nothing but cannon fodder. After a thousand years of cultivation, our power hasn’t increased, and neither has our wisdom!”","“Hmph, we righteous cultivators...” Hua Xuejian began to speak, but the other two turned their heads away, ignoring him.","There was nothing to discuss between a Divine Aspect cultivator and a Nascent Soul stage cultivator.","As the awkward silence lingered, two figures suddenly appeared on the city wall.","They appeared right next to the three but didn’t pay them any attention, their gaze fixed on the outside of the city.","“You... you’re the Ghost Emperor?” Hua Xuejian was startled and pointed at Immortal Jiu Chen’s consciousness manifestation with a cry of surprise.","He then turned his gaze to the other person, who was Li Miao.","Many people knew of his identity and immediately recognized him as the Emperor of the Great Tang.","“To think you’re the Emperor of the Great Tang! You’ve truly brought shame to your ancestors!” Zhang Xiansheng and Miao Renfeng immediately started berating Li Miao.","But Li Miao didn’t bother responding to them.","If they had known that the ancient demon had been released by his own ancestor, who knows what they would have thought!","Immortal Jiu Chen, however, found the three too noisy and with a wave of his hand, he sent a shockwave that made their souls tremble, finally silencing them.","Staring at the ancient demon, Immortal Jiu Chen asked with some doubt, “Do you think he will make a move?”","“I’m seventy percent sure he will, and the remaining thirty percent is that he’ll come into the city to cause me trouble!” Li Miao answered nonchalantly, seemingly relaxed, as if he didn’t take that person seriously at all.","In his eyes, that person was nothing more than a pawn.","A pawn of his ancestor, and also a pawn of his.","“I calculated multiple scenarios back then, and based on the current progression, there aren’t many variables left. If he turns towards Mangshan City, I will make him one of us!” Immortal Jiu Chen remained equally calm.","Whether it was the ancient demon or those upper realm cultivators, neither were worth his concern.","Even if they all came together, it wouldn’t matter.","If they could watch them all suffer mutual defeat, it would give them enough time to first transform into a Special Life Form, which would be even better.","So at this moment, neither of them entertained the thought of losing; they were only guessing how they would win!","Outside the city.","No one dared to fight.","Everyone watched as the ancient demon wreaked havoc.","They didn’t even have the courage to resist before their deaths; they just stood and watched.","At this moment, they finally understood what it meant to be at the mercy of others, like fish on the chopping block!","Outside the fortress.","“Such insignificant demons, and they’ve scared you all to this extent? Are you so afraid of death that you won’t even make a final stand?” Xiang Yang looked at the group of Immortal Slayers with disdain.","The powerful members of the Immortal Slayers, after having slain the foreign races, had gathered here. Now, as they watched the ancient demon wreak havoc, not a single one of them dared to speak or step forward.","Facing Xiang Yang’s words, few dared to argue.","But there were always those unafraid of death.","Chang Feng was the first to step forward, saying, “Great Commander, the ancient demon has descended, and this world is doomed. Instead of waiting for death, we should fight with everything we have. Even if there’s no chance of winning, we won’t disgrace the strong warriors of the Tang Dynasty!”","“I agree! Since no one else can hold the line, we should step up ourselves!” Yang Xiao also took a step forward. Though he was only a Golden Core stage cultivator, he was full of passion.","Even the Qianzu Saintess and Jiang Shang stood up at that moment.","Yet, they all waited—for Wei Jiuxian to speak.","Wei Jiuxian was the strongest among them.","As long as he led, everyone was willing to die together.","After all, death was inevitable. Since ancient times, who hasn’t died? Leaving an immortal mark on the path to the heavens was the true legacy.","The heavenly path was ruthless, but some could defy it, shattering the Great Heaven’s Way.","“Enough!” Wei Jiuxian removed his cloak and casually tossed it aside. His expression remained impassive as he spoke calmly, “The Divine Phase cultivators of the Tang Dynasty haven’t all perished yet. If someone must hold the line, it should be me. But I don’t know if I can hold it. If I can’t, then you all may do as you please!”","After he spoke, an aura burst skyward.","Without waiting for anyone to respond, his body shot forward, heading straight for the ancient demon.","At that moment, the commander of the Immortal-Slaying Guards, who protected the imperial city, made his move.","On the city wall, Li Miao saw this scene and slightly moved his lips. This was in line with the plan he had arranged and benefited them the most.","Yet, for some reason, he couldn’t bring himself to feel any joy.","Immortal Jiu Chen’s consciousness wasn’t there; he was busy integrating the first body refined from the Blood Condensing Array.","This body, a hundred zhang tall, had a life level five thousand times higher.","Now, it had condensed to three thousand times, and it would take only a stick of incense’s time to reach the perfect five thousand times.","A life level of five thousand times was still slightly less than five thousand times divine power, but it was close.","Once merged, it would be at the peak of the Great Ascension stage, and after breaking through the void and ascending, becoming immortal would be as simple as drinking water.","Coupled with a human soul level five hundred times stronger, his comprehension and physical body would reach perfection in the ancient domain.","Back then, the most powerful ancient demon nurtured by the ancient domain only barely reached a life level of five thousand times.","Now, Jiu Chen would reach that level.","Feeling the aura soaring from outside the city, he suddenly looked over, his heart sinking as he sensed something big was happening.","And this event might backfire.","But now, with only a little time left to condense the perfect body, he had to stay calm. He also sent a voice transmission to Li Miao, telling him to be extremely cautious about the situation outside the city.","Wei Jiuxian was not simple.","Neither was Jian Wushuang, who was deep within the blood-colored altar.","However, he had long discovered the oddity within Wei Jiuxian’s body but had said nothing.","Now that it was revealed, even Jiu Chen’s true self was astonished!","“That aura is the third accumulation. This person has received the perfect inheritance of the third sequence!!!!” Jiu Chen’s true self exclaimed.","Although Jian Wushuang had not yet explored that inheritance, he could sense that the aura bore a slight resemblance to the previous Lord of Divine Fire.","But that was enough.","The third sequence inheritance, and it was a perfect inheritance, meant that all secret arts within had been comprehended to the extreme.","Even in the Divine Phase, burning divine power could unleash power over a thousand times.","Moreover, within his body, there was a seed.","This was a seed of life.","A rare treasure indeed. If taken out, even an immortal would fight for it, as this seed had the potential to become a Dao Lord.","As the perfect inheritor of the third sequence and with this seed of life, Wei Jiuxian would surpass a Dao Lord given time. He was also very young, having lived for less than a hundred years, yet he had perfected the secret arts of the third sequence. He could fully comprehend the divine eye secret arts of the other sequences."]},{"number":6363,"title":"Chapter 6363: Merely Mortal","paragraphs":["Chapter 6363: Merely Mortal","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Combining the two sequences was entirely possible; once achieved, even becoming an Emperor would no longer be a mere fantasy.","The greatest advantage of the Divine Eye Secret Technique was its universality.","It was applicable to all cultivators.","In each sequence, one could find the secret technique that suited them best.","Finally, there was the burning.","This extremely life-consuming secret technique could be entirely offset for a cultivator possessing a Life Seed.","Therefore, this battle was worth watching.","That ancient demon might not necessarily be a match for Wei Jiuxian.","Moreover, judging by Wei Jiuxian’s appearance, he seemed quite composed.","In the sky.","One figure, towering a hundred zhang tall, with nine heads, eight arms, and four legs, seemed like a demon descending upon the world.","It was one of the 108 ancient demons, a Special Life Form unique to the Ancient Realm.","At its peak, its life level could reach five thousand times that of a human.","However, at this moment, it had only reached less than 2,000-fold.","Though in a weakened state, it still posed an insurmountable chasm for the human race.","Fortunately, there was the Divine Eye Secret Technique.","Standing on the other side, Wei Jiuxian, with the faintest glimmer of light, burst forth with a brilliance that overshadowed the sun.","“The legendary ancient demon. This is the Tang Empire of the Eastern Lands. The one who will slay you is named Wei Jiuxian. Remember that!”","As soon as he finished speaking, Wei Jiuxian’s divine power ignited once more, and the area behind him was engulfed in a sea of divine power.","The nine-headed ancient demon let out a cold, eerie laugh, its enormous eyes rotating, causing the heavens and the earth to resonate with a low rumble.","“Mere mortal, dare you slay a god!”","Buzz!","The demon’s eyes trembled, and a scarlet beam of light instantly erupted.","Wei Jiuxian remained where he was, not even attempting to dodge. With a roar, he crossed his arms, and merely by force of will, shattered the scarlet beam.","Then he unleashed a punch, his body leaning back slightly. This punch seemed to embody the very beginning of the world.","A deafening explosion instantly swept across the entire Tang Empire of the Eastern Lands.","The shadows of fists intertwined, and no one knew how many punches were thrown in that brief moment, but from the ancient demon’s body, countless bloody holes could be seen blooming with blood.","Such intense combat made everyone tremble with fear.","Outside the ancient castle.","“This... this is the legendary Divine Eye Secret Technique? It feels even more powerful than the secret techniques I’ve been cultivating!” Xiang Yang was shocked, frozen in place.","At that moment, he wasn’t sure if entering this world was a blessing or a curse.","But after witnessing such a powerful Divine Eye Secret Technique, which elevated a mere mortal to such heights, he made a firm decision: he had to learn it, and he had to learn the best Divine Eye inheritance.","With this secret technique, even a mortal body could rival a Special Life Form.","If one possessed a Special Life Form’s body as well, it would be an absolute kill.","This was why Li Miao and Immortal Jiu Chen spared no expense.","Even the two upper-realm cultivators who were present couldn’t help but gasp.","An indigenous person from a mundane world had surpassed them.","If they had been involved in that intense battle just now, they might have perished.","“It’s the Divine Eye inheritance from the third sequence. He actually cultivated it to perfection, but I’m not sure which kind it is from the third sequence. If my second sequence inheritance could be cultivated to this level, it would definitely be stronger than his!” Zhen Xian was somewhat indignant.","Among the mortals, he admired the Old Ancestor of the Great Tang Dynasty the most.","That person was a true prodigy.","But now, another emerged, Wei Jiuxian.","No matter which one, in the Upper Realm, they would all exist as Dao children.","At this moment, each of them surpassed him, and even his pride in the Second Sequence Inheritance only brought him to the domain level, far from perfection.","The only advantage he had was in the foundation, as the Second Sequence was purer than the Third Sequence, and the burning power was more violent.","On the city wall.","Li Miao watched this scene, feeling equally shaken inside.","He had constantly thought that Wei Jiuxian would be defeated, but he never expected Wei Jiuxian to suppress the Ancient Demon.","His strength far surpassed that of the Ancient Demon.","Such powerful strength was much greater than his own.","Even if he condensed the flesh of a Special Life Form, he might not be a match for Wei Jiuxian.","Because what Wei Jiuxian burned was power, power that surpassed ordinary people by thousands of times.","The multiplier of the life level was just the foundation.","For example, if your body’s level was 10-fold, a punch would be ten times the strength of an ordinary person.","But if the power burned was 10-fold, a punch would not just be ten times stronger because there would be the addition of secret techniques, possibly 30 or 50 times stronger.","So now, although Wei Jiuxian’s life level was low, his strength was immense!","With thousands of times the power, a punch could collapse a vast space.","Ascending to a higher realm was merely a thought away.","Yet he chose to stay and kill the Ancient Demon.","Yes!","Not just to severely wound, not just to repel.","But to kill.","Each of his moves was made with full effort. Though he could suppress the Ancient Demon, killing it was extremely difficult, requiring him to burn more power to sustain the battle.","But this power came from the mortal world, not divine power.","If it were divine power, he could easily kill the Ancient Demon.","This was something Jian Wushuang understood most clearly.","The division of power systems had many paths, such as the Void Universe and the Divine Power Universe.","They followed different paths.","There were different roads between powers, but the path of divine power was not wrong and was also mainstream.","The number of cultivators in other power systems was small for this reason.","Like now, the ordinary power used by the Chimu Realm was not much different from that of the Upper Realm.","The difference lay in the power of immortality versus the power of mortals.","Mortal power was limited and would eventually be exhausted.","For example, now in the Chimu Realm, the power was limited. If they continued burning, the entire world might not be able to sustain it.","Fortunately, the Ancient Demon broke through the Nine Heavens, allowing this world’s power to be enhanced.","In this regard, Wei Jiuxian truly had to thank the Ancient Demon.","As a cultivator with mortals in his heart, Wei Jiuxian deliberately waited for the opponent to break the Nine Heavens before choosing to strike.","Immortal power, on the other hand, was different.","Immortal power was the power of Zhen Xian.","What was immortality?","It was the immortality of the Dao.","So after becoming a Zhen Xian, the power burned and used came from the power of the Dao.","This power would almost never extinguish.","The period when the Divine Eye Secret Technique exploded was this time when immortal power continuously burned, making the Zhen Xian of the Upper Realm extremely formidable.","Once they fought, they could even destroy an ancient domain.","The thirty-six ancient domains shattered back then because of the participation of Zhen Xian in the battle.","The strength of immortal power corresponded to that of heaven-defying power.","Further up was divine power.","This power originated from the universe.","Universe Divine Power!","Divine power was the pinnacle of power, extending to the Universe God, which is why it was called divine power.","Further up were the powers of time and space, and Starry Sky power.","These powers, when used at a weaker stage, were slightly challenging, unless one was like Jian Wushuang, then it didn’t count.","However, even when Jian Wushuang used it, it was because of the effects of the Primordial Transformation.","He never compared divine power to time and space power, but the difference was extreme.","When reaching the Starry Sky, the conversion of power might have to switch to time and space power or Starry Sky power.","Back to Wei Jiuxian, who had burned mortal power to its peak, tearing apart the Ancient Demon’s head with his bare hands, leaving the Ancient Demon powerless to fight back."]},{"number":6364,"title":"Chapter 6364: Shocking Heaven Spear","paragraphs":["Chapter 6364: Shocking Heaven Spear","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The ancient demon, who had been suppressed all this time, began to erupt with fury, determined to reverse the situation. At the very least, he wanted to even the odds!","He roared in defiance, his eight arms wielding his innate divine abilities, continuously blocking the oncoming barrage of fists.","Fortunately, his physical body was strong enough that even when his head was shattered, it could still regenerate.","Although Wei Jiuxian’s body was small, he used the God-Image Technique, known as “Law of Heaven and Earth,” to enlarge his form to a hundred zhang, making him almost equal in size to the ancient demon.","“Damn human! I will tear you limb from limb!” the ancient demon roared, bellowing, “Eight-Armed Space Lock!”","“Suppress!”","With those words, the surroundings trembled as a formidable law and power descended upon Wei Jiuxian’s head.","The sensation was agonizing, causing Wei Jiuxian to weaken by a level, and the speed of his fist shadows slowed down.","Seizing this opportunity, the ancient demon roared once more:","“Kill!”","As soon as the word “kill” was uttered, countless shadows of ancient demons surged towards Wei Jiuxian.","The earlier command to “suppress” had a unique domain quality, allowing it to restrain opponents. But now, the command to “kill” was a deadly force.","A brutal slaughter ensued, closing in swiftly.","Wei Jiuxian abandoned his fist attacks and instead focused on defending against the oncoming shadows of the ancient demon.","“Shocking Heaven Spear!”","With a wave of his massive hand, a long spear descended from the heavens.","The moment the power of the divine spear made contact, a dragon’s roar from the firmament instantly shattered the suppression domain!","The spear swept across, obliterating the shadows of the ancient demons.","“How is this possible? He actually broke through my suppression and killing divine ability just like that!” The enormous eyes of the ancient demon were filled with astonishment.","This was his innate divine ability, a method strong enough to challenge opponents beyond his level, yet he couldn’t defeat a human cultivator of the same level.","For a Special Life Form, this was a tremendous humiliation.","“Suppression and Killing Domain!”","The nine-headed ancient demon roared furiously, and his eight arms exerted simultaneous force. A destructive power surged from the heavens and earth.","He forcefully expanded his domain to cover the entire Eastern Land of the Tang Dynasty.","This was his strongest attack.","At the same time, he summoned the Third Sequence Inheritance Hall, intending to use it to suppress Wei Jiuxian.","No matter what, he couldn’t afford to lose to a human cultivator.","After being suppressed for so many years, only to encounter such a formidable opponent upon his release, his anger had reached its peak.","The domain descended.","Everyone trembled.","The billions of people in the Tang Dynasty all knelt at that moment.","Only a few cultivators struggled to stand.","Even Immortal Jiu Chen and Li Miao, who were within Mangshan County’s city, had complicated feelings.","“Is this a naturally born Special Life Form?” Li Miao was deeply shocked. He had seen so little, only receiving a vague introduction from his immortal master.","He lacked a sense of reverence for true powerhouses.","At this moment, he finally understood the vast difference in the essence of life.","The Nine-Headed Demon had elevated its life level by a full two thousand times. Although it was far from its peak condition, this disparity was enough to make mortals submit and cause cultivators to bow their heads.","“It won’t be long before you become as powerful as he is, perhaps even stronger!”","Li Miao was stunned and turned to look at Immortal Jiu Chen within the Blood Condensation Array, nodding excitedly.","He too would become that powerful. The thought made him suppress his excitement.","Outside the city, the four God Manifestation Realm peak experts, though experienced, were also somewhat unsettled.","One of the two Arhats, the Destruction Arhat, trembled with his lips, speaking in an unwilling tone, “They say the heavens are fair, but how can cultivators compensate for such a disparity? Without the secret technique of the Divine Eye, the human race would likely be suppressed forever!”","“Boundless!” The Extinguishing Arhat clasped his hands together and made no further comment.","Zhen Xian, hearing their conversation, couldn’t help but sneer, “What do you know? The greatest trait of the human race is their comprehension ability. Though the collective might not match Special Life Forms, their top-tier combat strength is not weaker than these ancient demons. Who do you think killed those ancient demons?”","“When they ascend, they will understand. In the Ancient Domain, humans are supreme. No matter how powerful Special Life Forms may be, they cannot overshadow the heavens!” Fu Qing held his divine sword, appearing cold and detached.","Though ancient demons were strong and possessed innate divine abilities, they started at such a high level that they lost the ability to innovate.","Because they could not reproduce.","They lived flamboyantly, or established forces to dominate one region.","Without the desire to advance further, they would be surpassed by others.","For billions of years, ancient demons were born at the pinnacle of the Great Completion, but when they fell, they were still only at the peak of the Great Completion.","They even disdained using treasures and refused to cultivate secret techniques created by the human race or invent their own. They could be said to lack the will to progress.","Moreover, their breakthroughs were thousands of times harder than those of humans, making them more likely to abandon the path of cultivation.","Today’s outcome was inevitable.","Calling them the most perfect life forms was not an exaggeration, but they were not perfect powerhouses.","True powerhouses possess a heart that constantly seeks progress.","Every human cultivator present had such a heart.","No matter how difficult and perilous the road ahead, they would forge ahead.","For example, Li Miao and Immortal Jiu Chen.","One was a human emperor, the other a spiritual entity, yet they had spent decades planning, culminating in today’s imminent peak—this was determination and confidence.","Stripped of their titles, they were merely a mortal and a well-informed spiritual entity.","Yet they both had the heart of a powerhouse, constantly striving forward.","Even two powerful experts from the upper realm, both at the peak of the Primordial Spirit, willingly descended into the mortal world, enduring a millennium of hardship, all for the sake of a heritage temple and the elusive legends of ancient demons.","They had not given up even now.","It was also a heart that continually sought progress.","On a grander scale, Jian Wushuang was no different.","He kept advancing.","After falling from Universe God to mortal, he still climbed back step by step.","He struggled among mortals, steadily returning to the peak.","This process, though seemingly wretched, was nothing.","When he reached the summit again, looking back, he would realize that those moments of bowing his head, retreating, and enduring grievances were mere fleeting hardships, easily brushed aside.","They would not affect his status as a supreme powerhouse.","Being able to pick up and let go, endure and chase—this was the cultivator’s heart of progress.","Everyone had their own perspective, but this was Jian Wushuang’s view.","Just like everyone present who, upon witnessing the power of the ancient demons, felt a pang of bitterness in their hearts.","In contrast, Wei Jiuxian, who truly faced the ancient demons, remained calm.","He felt no awe for the innate perfection of the ancient demons; instead, he harbored a sense of pity.","Suspended in mid-air, Wei Jiuxian gently raised one hand, his expression stern as he shouted angrily, “Citizens of the Great Tang, from this day forward, do not kneel to the strong!”","“Moreover, he is nothing more than a flawed being, without parents, family, or brothers. He is not worthy of your submission!”","With that, he raised his long spear and charged directly at the ancient demon.","At this moment, his battle intent soared to its peak.","“With this spear, I will bring peace!”","The long spear, like a dragon’s roar, emitted a melodious sound, stirring the dragon spirit within the hearts of billions of mortals."]},{"number":6365,"title":"Chapter 6365: The Resistance of Billions of Mortals","paragraphs":["Chapter 6365: The Resistance of Billions of Mortals","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Everyone as a dragon!","“Kill!”","At that moment, all the mortals in the world roared out this single word.","Wei Jiuxian charged toward the Ancient Demon.","Billions of mortals rose up against the powerful beings that had oppressed them.","In that moment, the hearts of the masses united as one.","He, Wei Jiuxian, was the ruler of this world.","His body transformed into the red-eyed realm’s manifestation of the Heavenly Dao, displaying a truly invincible stance.","At that moment, it wasn’t the secret art of the Divine Eye, nor the life seed within him that he relied on.","It was the collective breath of all the people in the world, propelling him toward the Ancient Demon.","Even the Ancient Demon with its nine heads trembled in its heart. Facing this unstoppable spear, its domain shattered in an instant. Despite using its eight arms to unleash divine powers to block the attack, they were swiftly torn apart.","“No!!!!”","With an unwilling roar, the Ancient Demon bellowed. Even in the ancient times, it had never faced death, but now, it was about to fall at the hands of a mere mortal, a native of the Red-Eyed Realm.","The unwillingness and humiliation caused its massive eyes to explode.","In those eyes, the last image it saw was the spear charged with the power of a dragon heading toward it.","In the next moment, the heavens and earth collapsed.","The enormous eyes of the Ancient Demon shattered completely.","At that very moment, its life force crumbled.","Its body disintegrated, and the blood of the Ancient Demon dyed the earth red.","In the sky, with its domain gone, the third sequence’s Hall of Inheritance also fell to the ground.","Only Wei Jiuxian remained standing in mid-air, gripping his long spear like a peerless warrior guarding the gate of heaven. The Ancient Demon’s blood boiled, dancing on the tip of his spear, but in the end, it unwillingly slid down the shaft, falling onto the mortal land below.","The Ancient Demon was slain!","He had done it.","The entire sky was illuminated by Wei Jiuxian’s figure.","“My name is Wei Jiuxian, a mere mortal of the Red-Eyed Realm!”","“Today, I declare that there shall be no more cultivators, no more powerful beings under this sky!”","He swept through the world.","It wasn’t just empty talk—he had truly done it.","Standing on the city walls, Li Miao gazed at Wei Jiuxian in shock. His heart surged with emotion, yet was filled with disappointment.","He had hoped to witness Wei Jiuxian being slain by the Ancient Demon so that he could step forward and be the savior.","Then, he would have looked down at Wei Jiuxian’s corpse and said, “You were wrong.”","This world needed powerful beings to suppress it; only then could it be a paradise.","But today, Wei Jiuxian, with the body of a mortal, had slain the Ancient Demon.","It was a hard slap to Li Miao’s face.","He felt jealousy, resentment, but he also acknowledged it. Wei Jiuxian had said it, and he had done it.","At that moment, he forgot to look behind him at the Blood Condensation Formation.","Immortal Jiu Chen had successfully forged a body with a life force five thousand times stronger, and his spiritual form possessed a soul level five hundred times more powerful. The two had fully merged into one.","“It worked!”","Only Jiu Chen paid no attention to Wei Jiuxian outside.","He was basking in the joy of success. His towering human figure, a hundred feet tall, instantly shrank to normal size, and he donned a black robe, flying straight toward the city walls.","“Immortal Master!” Li Miao saw Jiu Chen approaching, but he wasn’t particularly excited, only responding faintly.","Immortal Jiu Chen looked at the hovering Wei Jiuxian, then glanced at Li Miao and said, “Are you feeling that Wei Jiuxian might be the savior, stealing your spotlight?”","“Yes!” Li Miao was honest, with no need to hide it.","While others marveled at Wei Jiuxian’s strength, he was jealous of his actions.","“Haha, your mortal heart has not yet been extinguished,” Immortal Jiu Chen chuckled softly. He was in a good mood because his success had finally come. With his life force magnified five thousand times, though he hadn’t mastered the Divine Eye technique, his sheer physical and spiritual strength could easily crush everyone present, so he remained so composed.","Upon noticing that Li Miao was feeling down, he offered some comfort, saying, “Showing off in front of mortals isn’t something to be proud of. Once you ascend to the higher realms, you’ll have everything you desire. There’s no need to compete with mortals, understand?”","“I understand!” Li Miao, regaining his composure, nodded firmly.","Now that Immortal Jiu Chen had succeeded, and the ancient demon outside had fallen, all that remained was to retrieve the essence blood. With that, a second physical body could be formed. However, his soul was still lacking, so he needed to perform the death array again to condense the Ghost Emperor.","That could be accomplished using the souls of those cultivators.","In his mind, everything was already within reach.","“I’ll head out and deal with that boy. You stay inside the city and wait!” After speaking, Jiu Chen took a step forward, walking through the air toward Wei Jiuxian.","Seeing how powerful Wei Jiuxian was, both Zhen Xian and Fu Qing realized that this was their chance.","Wei Jiuxian didn’t care about the ancient demon’s corpse, but they did!","The two Arhats, whose mission had been to protect the mortal realm, had completed their task. Both bowed their heads, reciting their mantras in silence, and with the resolution of karma, they ascended in broad daylight.","In the past, the combined ascension of two Arhats would have been a grand event in the cultivation world.","But at that moment, it was overshadowed by Wei Jiuxian’s presence.","So, not many people paid attention.","However, on the city wall, Zhang Xiansheng and others trembled with jealousy.","Watching others ascend while their own souls were about to be refined filled their hearts with immense resentment.","Why wasn’t that them?","Had they known this outcome, they would likely have chosen to align with the Old Ancestor of the Tang Dynasty.","But now, it was too late. All they could do was stand there and watch.","Meanwhile, their focus shifted to the gathering forces outside the city—three factions, four individuals.","They still had hope.","If Jiu Chen and Li Miao failed, they could potentially reconstruct their physical bodies.","An intact ancient demon body was of immeasurable value.","If the ancient demon released all its power, it could reignite the glory of the Red-Eyed Realm from ancient times.","Moreover, the essence blood, skin, and bones could be used to craft a body that would multiply their strength a thousandfold. They didn’t need a large body; a human-sized one would suffice.","It wasn’t mere wishful thinking—this was a real possibility.","In mid-air, Wei Jiuxian gazed coldly at the three people.","Privately, Zhen Xian communicated with him, proposing a partnership.","He also sent a similar message to Jiu Chen.","But Jiu Chen completely ignored the two higher realm cultivators.","If he could rely on others so easily, that would be one thing. But Jiu Chen still believed the Divine Fire Hall was within the altar, so he wasn’t afraid of the higher realm experts. At worst, he would summon the Divine Fire Hall.","With his current power, he could fully absorb his true form. Once that happened, he could control the Divine Fire Hall and suppress the entire Red-Eyed Realm. Even an Immortal wouldn’t be able to enter.","Seeing that Jiu Chen was unwilling to cooperate, Zhen Xian shifted his full attention to Wei Jiuxian.","“Let’s work together!”","“Brother Wei, if we collaborate, I only need thirty percent of the ancient demon. I will help you kill Jiu Chen, and afterward, I’ll leave with my junior sister and never return to the Red-Eyed Realm!”","Though Zhen Xian said this, how could he never return after gaining such a great advantage?","With thirty percent of the ancient demon’s blood and flesh, he could create a life body two thousand times stronger. Although it would be less than a hundred feet tall, it would be enough for him to transcend. After that, he could return to the Red-Eyed Realm, seize the rest of the body, and destroy the entire realm. No one would know of the benefits he had reaped.","As for his junior sister, she was from the same sect. At worst, they could split the gains evenly, which would be enough for both of them to reach the immortal level."]},{"number":6366,"title":"Chapter 6366: Bewitching","paragraphs":["Chapter 6366: Bewitching","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","He couldn’t help but feel a surge of excitement welling up from deep within.","At that moment, Wei Jiuxian responded with a single word.","“Agreed!”","The cooperation was accepted.","Zhen Xian was even more thrilled. Immediately, he pulled his junior sister over to stand beside Wei Jiuxian, speaking righteously, “Jiu Chen, the things you’ve done with Li Miao are utterly despicable. Today, we, the righteous cultivators, will offer you as a sacrifice for the sake of all beings under the heavens!”","“Hahaha!!!”","Jiu Chen, upon hearing this, couldn’t contain his laughter.","He laughed at the other’s hypocrisy and at his ignorance.","“A cultivator from the Upper Realm, here in the Crimson Eyes Realm, ridding it of demons and upholding the Dao? If the common folk knew, they’d probably hang a plaque for you and offer their prayers, wouldn’t they?”","Zhen Xian didn’t flinch, sneering coldly, “That would still be better than being a filthy scoundrel like you!”","Both of them, in truth, knew exactly what kind of people they were dealing with.","But winning was not merely a matter of virtue.","In fact, in terms of virtue, Jiu Chen might even have had a slight edge over Zhen Xian.","“You lot just want the ancient demon’s body. I’ve inherited the God’s Eye, and I know what you’re planning. Stop putting on a show in front of me!” Wei Jiuxian said indifferently.","But his words were a sharp slap in Zhen Xian’s face.","Fortunately, Zhen Xian’s skin was thick enough. If his real name had been known, someone would surely have been pointing at him, cursing.","Jiu Chen shrugged, his expression cold as he said, “It’s good that you know. I’m going to use the ancient demon’s body to help Li Miao refine a second one. If any of you have a problem with that, feel free to attack me at any time. I’ll take you all on!”","He had already convinced himself of his invincibility.","Zhen Xian gritted his teeth in fury. They wanted to take everything for themselves—what were they supposed to do?","It was sheer greed.","“To be honest, I’m not interested in ascending, nor am I interested in the ancient demon’s body. If you want to take it, then take it!” Wei Jiuxian moved aside, pointing at the ancient demon’s corpse, and continued, “However, after you take it, you must leave the Crimson Eyes Realm and swear never to return, never to disturb these mortals again!”","In truth, whether they swore or not didn’t matter. Without treasures, who would even want to come to the mortal realm?","So Wei Jiuxian wasn’t worried about them going back on their word. He just wanted them gone.","Either die by his hand or leave voluntarily.","“Wei, my brother, you may not know the full significance of the ancient demon’s body. It is...” Zhen Xian hurriedly tried to persuade him.","He didn’t want Wei Jiuxian to step back now. Just a moment ago, they had agreed to cooperate—why stop the fight now?","If Wei Jiuxian withdrew, it would be impossible for him to split anything with Jiu Chen peacefully.","At this point, Jiu Chen’s life level was already five thousand times that of an ordinary Special Life Form. How could Zhen Xian stand a chance?","He had to drag Wei Jiuxian into the fight.","Seeing that Wei Jiuxian remained unmoved, Zhen Xian realized this fool truly didn’t care about the ancient demon’s body. So, he attempted to lure him in with the Crimson Eyes Realm:","“Wei, my brother, think carefully. Once Jiu Chen and I start fighting, I’ll surely perish. Afterward, it will be just you. Do you really believe Jiu Chen will keep his promise then?”","Jiu Chen glanced briefly at Mangshan County City in the distance, where the Ghost Emperor had already successfully formed. Thanks to Li Miao using the Empress’s Pure Body, all impurities had been cleansed from the Ghost Emperor, allowing for a swift fusion.","The Blood Condensation Array had also entered its second phase.","He calmly spoke up, “Wei Jiuxian, I’ll admit, I have some respect for you. So, I’ll give you this opportunity. I promise that once I help Li Miao refine his body, I will ascend immediately. After that, I won’t interfere with anything you do in this world!”","Initially, the plan was to kill these people; there was no need to keep them around.","However, the Ghost Emperor had condensed too quickly, so there was no need for their souls anymore.","Another reason was to leave a mark for Li Miao, motivating him to strive for greatness.","Wei Jiuxian was, after all, Li Miao’s inner demon.","When the critical moment arrived, allowing Li Miao to descend might yield unexpected results.","Immortal Jiu Chen, known for his strategic prowess, took one step, considering nine.","At this moment, his words were intended to provoke Zhen Xian and see him lose his composure.","A powerful figure from the upper realm, descending to the lower realm, being schemed against by a group of mortals—whether soft or hard approaches—was unable to defeat them.","This was the truly amusing part.","When Wei Jiuxian heard Jiu Chen’s words, he paid no attention to Zhen Xian and only replied with a single word, “Fine!”","This left Zhen Xian in an awkward position.","Anger, unwillingness, humiliation!","He stood there, afraid to move, afraid to think.","Because he couldn’t defeat Jiu Chen.","But he was a strong figure from the upper realm, at the pinnacle of the Yuan Spirit stage.","Now, he was being ridiculed by a group of mortals.","“Good, very good!” Zhen Xian laughed in embarrassment. He pointed at Wei Jiuxian and Jiu Chen, enunciating each word, “You two are ruthless. Since you’ve forced me into this, then we shall all perish together!”","As he finished speaking, he took out a dark green token. A powerful surge of thought power emanated from it, though the material was quite special. Zhen Xian gently squeezed, and the token shattered instantly.","The powerful surge of thought power dispersed along with it.","Buzz!","In the next moment, the Red Eyes Realm began to tremble.","Space quaked constantly, and even the heavenly laws of this world began to shudder. A powerful pressure forced the heavenly laws to bow.","At that moment, the strength of Zhen Xian and Fu Qing surged dramatically.","Even Jiu Chen’s aura was rising.","His life force was five thousand times stronger, and if not for the suppression of the heavenly laws, he would have already broken through to the Yuan Spirit stage.","Now, with the suppression lifted, he instantly reached the pinnacle of the Yuan Spirit stage.","His aura was even stronger than that of Zhen Xian and Fu Qing.","Only Wei Jiuxian’s aura remained unchanged.","“Is this your trump card?” Wei Jiuxian observed everything, seemingly having anticipated it, and said indifferently, “Lifting the suppression of the heavenly laws to restore your cultivation?”","Zhen Xian let out a cold chuckle, though a bitter smile lingered on his face.","“I don’t need to make a move. You’ll soon understand!”","The heavens and earth trembled.","In the shattered sky, a massive crack appeared.","An overwhelming aura of invincibility radiated from within, making it impossible for anyone to breathe.","“Haha, I’ve been waiting for you!” Jiu Chen was excited.","He had long known about Zhen Xian’s backup plan, which was nothing more than summoning a powerful figure from the upper realm.","Those transcendent beings in the Great Perfection stage were not afraid of this small realm’s heavenly laws.","Therefore, their cultivation would not be suppressed.","This gave Jiu Chen the opportunity to capture a Great Perfection cultivator alive.","He immediately flew back to Mangshan City, retrieved the blood-red altar, and shouted, “Come forth, Temple of Divine Fire!”","...","“Hmm?”","Everyone stared at him like he was a fool.","The Temple of Divine Fire did not appear.","The blood-red altar also shattered in that moment.","“How could this be?” Jiu Chen was shocked!","The altar crumbled, and its final essence of blood had been absorbed by the Blood Condensing Formation.","Nothing was left, not even the aura of his true body.","At this moment, he was utterly bewildered.","In the void.","Jian Wushuang grasped Jiu Chen’s true body, observing everything with a faint smile.","After watching for so long, he had finally understood their plans.","Unfortunately, they had encountered him.","Otherwise, Jiu Chen and Li Miao could indeed have achieved great things.","In the Red Eyes Realm, they were truly being stifled.","Right now, Jian Wushuang didn’t plan to reveal himself because the being in the crack had yet to emerge.","True powerhouses were always the last to take the stage.","Revealing himself too early wouldn’t have the desired effect.","Besides, the Blood Condensing Formation had not yet finished forming a physical body.","Once the physical body had condensed, it wouldn’t be too late to swoop in and take the spoils."]},{"number":6367,"title":"Chapter 6367: True Lord Ye Huo","paragraphs":["Chapter 6367: True Lord Ye Huo","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang concealed Immortal Jiu Chen in the void.","At that moment, in the sky outside Mangshan City, a massive human face emerged.","“Disciple, Wuyan greets Master!” Zhen Xian bowed with an indescribable expression as he faced his master.","He was truly unlucky.","He had stumbled upon such a grand opportunity, yet it happened in the mortal world, causing his master to descend, and now everything was lost.","When Fu Qing saw the newcomer, she also bowed and greeted, “True Lord Ye Huo!”","Although this person wasn’t her master but rather a senior uncle, she still had to address him respectfully in front of outsiders.","Faced with such a powerful presence.","Wei Jiuxian appeared insignificant.","Jiu Chen was utterly at a loss.","He forcefully pulled Li Miao out of the grand formation, urgently saying, “Go, we must leave now!”","Boom!","With Jiu Chen’s current strength, he effortlessly tore open the space, and Li Miao followed suit.","Without the Divine Fire Hall, they were no match for the cultivators at the Great Ascension stage.","Staying would bring no benefit. If the opponent discovered that his life level was five thousand times higher, he would undoubtedly be killed. Escape was the only option!","There was no place to hide in the mortal world, so ascending immediately was their best bet.","After all, the destination after ascension was random, making it difficult for the enemy to track him down.","Although everything was gone, with his life level and what he had witnessed in the past, he could quickly break through to the Great Ascension stage in no time.","By then, he would have the strength to protect himself and continue his journey, which wouldn’t be too much of a failure.","But if he lost his life, everything would truly be over.","Li Miao, although unsure of what had happened, could tell from Jiu Chen’s panic that something big had transpired.","Without hesitation, the two of them shattered the void, attempting to leave this world.","But just as they stepped into the rift, the massive human face, accompanied by flames from True Lord Ye Huo, lightly snorted, sealing the surrounding space.","“Trying to leave?”","“Meeting me without even a greeting? You juniors have no manners!” True Lord Ye Huo manipulated his power, pulling Jiu Chen and Li Miao, who were sealed in space, right in front of him.","With just one glance at this world, he understood everything that had transpired.","This was a being beyond the Heavenly Dao.","An existence so powerful it left everyone breathless.","Zhen Xian remained silent, standing obediently in place, saying nothing and doing nothing.","His master was present, and the more he spoke, the more trouble he would invite upon himself.","Remaining calm might even earn him a reward, perhaps some ancient demon blood, making his millennium of toil not entirely in vain.","Wei Jiuxian stood still, his brilliance concealed, yet he remained upright, expressionless, with no trace of emotion.","It was as though the True Lord posed no threat to him.","Zhen Xian sneered inwardly, mocking Wei Jiuxian for his arrogance.","But what was the outcome of such arrogance?","Everyone was doomed.","True Lord Ye Huo was no righteous figure. The ancient demon blood had already dissipated into the world.","Although only a small amount was lost, it was still a valuable treasure, not something to be wasted.","He might even refine the entire Crimson Eyes Realm to recover the lost blood.","As for the fate of mortals, True Lord Ye Huo cared nothing about their survival.","“What’s the use of arrogance? The path of a cultivator requires fortune, wealth, companions, and land, not arrogance!” Zhen Xian sighed inwardly.","Wei Jiuxian was destined to fail and would pay with his life.","His calm expression now was likely due to the fact that Wei Jiuxian had never encountered such a powerful existence before and was probably scared senseless.","As for himself, although his efforts over the past millennium had been in vain, it was still better than losing his life.","He still had his sect, his master, and his fellow disciples. Upon returning to the Upper Realm, he would still be that Little Zhen Xian.","It was a somewhat derogatory title, but also a sign that his seniors believed in him and thought he had the potential to become immortal.","“Huff!”","Jiu Chen, sealed in space, gazed at True Lord Ye Huo, his eyes brimming with fear and unwillingness.","“Why did the Divine Fire Hall disappear? Why?” His heart roared in agony, but no one answered him.","True Lord Ye Huo glanced at the two of them, finally locking his gaze onto Immortal Jiu Chen.","“You’ve crafted this body quite well. What method did you use?” he asked.","Jiu Chen gritted his teeth, furious. “I know you won’t spare me. Even if I told you, it would still end in death. Do you think I’ll speak?”","In truth, it was possible to search their souls, but both of their souls had reached a level of five hundredfold, which made it impossible for True Lord Ye Huo to perform the search.","This was because his own soul level wasn’t as high as the two before him.","At this moment, Zhen Xian finally spoke, breaking the silence. “Master, they’ve set up a grand array within that city, divided into two formations. One is a Death Qi Formation that can elevate the soul’s level to five hundredfold. The other is a Blood Condensation Formation, which can refine the physical body to five thousandfold. The former requires mortal souls as nourishment, while the latter needs the ancient demon’s essence blood.”","True Lord Ye Huo could clearly see the entanglements of fate among everyone, yet he couldn’t discern what was hidden within the restrictions inside the city.","After all, he hadn’t yet reached the level of an immortal, so there were things he still didn’t understand.","Now, hearing his disciple’s clear explanation, he was momentarily shaken but quickly regained his composure. “It’s quite the clever trick.”","With that, he stopped looking at Jiu Chen, knowing the man was a tough nut to crack. Instead, he turned his attention to Jiu Chen’s companion.","“You possess a body free of evil. Your potential is impressive, so why are you entangled with demonic cultivators?” True Lord Ye Huo asked, feigning curiosity.","At this moment, Li Miao’s heart trembled, both at the immense power of True Lord Ye Huo and his own failure.","Why had he failed?","Even now, he didn’t understand. Nor did he comprehend why such a powerful being had appeared here.","Sensing that True Lord Ye Huo held some favor toward him, Li Miao didn’t know how to respond.","In the past, he might have begged for mercy.","But this time, he chose to maintain the composure of a disciple of the immortals, although deep within, the bitterness of defeat still pulsed.","Given what he knew of himself, he wouldn’t be able to endure this much longer.","True Lord Ye Huo, being who he was, could see through Li Miao’s pretense at a glance. Despite this, he wasn’t angered; rather, he was a little disappointed, like a teacher lamenting a student’s failure to meet expectations. “Do you know how unique your body is? Even in the ancient domain, it’s rarely seen. Once you ascend, many old masters will likely fight to take you as their disciple. With your potential, transcending the ordinary won’t be difficult for you.”","This simple assessment was like dangling an enormous prize before him.","Before, according to what his immortal master had said, he had the potential for immortality. But between his immortal master and True Lord Ye Huo, Li Miao found himself more inclined to trust the latter.","Because his power was undeniable.","Jiu Chen had experienced too much and immediately saw through the ploy. He glanced at Li Miao, and his heart settled on a plan.","Although the two of them had never officially taken on a master-disciple relationship, their bond was deeper than such formalities.","If offering himself as a bargaining chip would allow Li Miao to become the disciple of True Lord Ye Huo, then perhaps this would be Jiu Chen’s final gift to him.","At that moment, True Lord Ye Huo continued, “Young one, would you be willing to take me as your master?”"]},{"number":6368,"title":"Chapter 6368: Accepting Disciple","paragraphs":["Chapter 6368: Accepting Disciple","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Li Miao, this is a heaven-sent opportunity for you! My teacher is a figure who can dominate the Ancient Domain. Once you become his disciple, your path will be much smoother!” Zhen Xian Wuyan chimed in at this moment to help persuade.","However, deep down, Li Miao was utterly unwilling. Ever since his physique had been transformed, he was no weaker than Wuyan, and he might even surpass him.","By then, if he had to deal with someone like Li Miao frequently, it would undoubtedly irritate him.","If it were his ancestor, it would be different. After all, he only respected that Great Tang Ancestor.","Honest and upright!","With someone like that, you would never be at a disadvantage. It was a friendship where you could fully trust the other person to have your back. Who wouldn’t want a junior brother like that?","What he didn’t know was that his master’s real reason for extending the olive branch to Li Miao was because of Immortal Jiu Chen.","The Ancient Demon’s physical body and blood essence weren’t important in the eyes of True Lord of Karma.","Even the formation that could refine the physical body wasn’t important because it required too many treasures. After achieving transcendence, the materials needed to alter his physical body were far too numerous, and it would be impossible to afford the cost.","However, advancement in the level of the soul—now that was different.","The nourishment the formation required was merely the souls of mortals.","The Upper Realm had no shortage of mortals, and there was also an endless supply of cultivators’ souls, all of which could be used as nourishment.","That was what he valued.","Because the Secret Art of the Divine Eye and the Dao that followed immortality required elevation of the soul. The higher the soul level, the greater one’s comprehension.","That was what True Lord of Karma truly valued.","After all, his perspective was different. Most of the people he interacted with were at the Mahayana stage, and some were even Immortal beings.","He understood that the path after immortality was one’s personal Dao.","There were stronger and weaker Daos; some were supreme, while others were mere trifles.","There was even the Ultimate Dao, and special Daos as well.","These were not determined by the level of the physical body but by comprehension.","Though many followed the path of divine power due to the Secret Art of the Divine Eye, that path was far more distant.","At the very least, one had to be at the level of a Great Emperor before coming into contact with divine power.","Moreover, the divine power path still required augmentation from the Dao.","In this interconnected path, the physical body could be improved with hard work later, so there was no rush. But comprehension was different. The sooner it was raised, the more benefits it would bring for the future.","Thus, True Lord of Karma was willing to lower his pride, pretending to be courteous in front of a mere mortal, just to obtain the formation that advanced the soul.","Of course, taking on a disciple with such an innocent physique wasn’t a loss either, as he would gain an ally who might one day become a transcendent powerhouse.","With such a tempting offer, Li Miao hesitated.","He thought he could hold out a little longer, but he hadn’t expected...","His Dao heart was so fragile.","Li Miao trembled as he lowered his head, speaking with respect, “Senior, I am willing to accept you as my master!”","With this one sentence, the bond of master and disciple between him and Immortal Jiu Chen was shattered.","Though Jiu Chen felt deeply helpless in his heart, all he could do was sigh.","He remembered the past.","A young, introverted prince had been playing in the palace when he accidentally stumbled upon a storeroom filled with strange and rare items, where he discovered Jiu Chen’s existence.","At first, Jiu Chen attached himself to the prince. Later, he helped the prince ascend to the throne, and the prince became the Emperor of the Tang Dynasty, aiding this immortal master in reconstructing his physical body.","Scene after scene of memories flashed by, and Jiu Chen’s heart felt as though it was being cut by a knife.","Even though he was heartbroken, he couldn’t bear to see Li Miao perish alongside him.","Perhaps this was a good way for him to find peace.","However, he himself had lost that peace.","Amidst his sorrowful thoughts, Li Miao spoke again. This time, he directly knelt and prostrated himself on the ground, his tone even more respectful as he said:","“Please have mercy, True Lord of Heavenly Fire, spare Immortal Jiu Chen’s life. Your disciple is willing to serve you like a beast of burden, without a word of complaint!”","At these words, the True Lord of Heavenly Fire’s brow furrowed.","Jiu Chen, however, felt a warmth bloom in his heart, and his eyes reddened with a feeling he couldn’t put into words.","It felt as if, after raising a child for so many years and believing the child belonged to someone else, a blood test revealed they were a perfect match.","“How dare you! It is an honor that my master is willing to take you as his disciple, an opportunity for you. And yet, you dare to make demands!” Zhen Xian, without hesitation, seized every opportunity to step on Li Miao.","Preferably, to crush him entirely.","He had no desire to become a fellow disciple with someone like this.","“Little one, do you know the consequences of making demands of me?” The True Lord of Heavenly Fire’s massive, illusory face began to revert to its true form, transforming into a human shape.","His appearance mirrored that of the giant face—tall and imposing. Though his features had frozen in the image of a mortal in their sixties, his body remained incredibly strong.","In short, he appeared to be an elderly man with white hair but with a powerful and robust physique.","In this fully restored form, his presence grew even more oppressive.","The pressure was so overwhelming that even Jiu Chen and Li Miao struggled to breathe.","“Li Miao!” Jiu Chen spoke with great difficulty, “There’s no need to plead on my behalf. I can tell him the secret of the Soul Advancement Formation!”","This information was highly sensitive, and once revealed, the True Lord would surely pursue more of Jiu Chen’s secrets.","However, Jiu Chen had already made up his mind. For Li Miao’s sake, he would rather sink into damnation than face death together.","Li Miao, in his simplicity, genuinely believed that revealing the Soul Advancement Formation would be enough to spare Jiu Chen’s life.","The True Lord of Heavenly Fire waved his hand, and Jiu Chen was absorbed into his ring. The two communicated through thought power, leaving those outside unaware of what was said.","“Very well. I do not intend to take his life!” The True Lord of Heavenly Fire’s mood improved significantly, for he had just learned a shocking secret.","A secret regarding the first sequence of inheritance.","His journey to the lower realm to rescue his disciple had not been in vain.","The benefits he’d gained were greater than what he’d acquired from years of wandering the outside world.","After collecting Jiu Chen, he turned his gaze toward the massive ancient demon’s body and casually stored it within his space ring.","In high spirits, the True Lord of Heavenly Fire smiled and said, “Wu Yan, there is some lingering ancient demon essence in this place. It should not go to waste. Start refining it now, and extract the demon blood from the Crimson Eye Realm. I shall head into the city for a look around!”","“Yes, Master!” Zhen Xian Wu Yan was excited.","To refine the demon blood of the Crimson Eye Realm—that meant the blood would be his!","Although there wasn’t much, it was certainly better than nothing!","Even if only a tenth of the demon blood remained, it would be enough to elevate his life level.","But on second thought, Wu Yan realized it wouldn’t be that simple.","The Crimson Eye Realm still contained billions of mortals. Wouldn’t it be a waste to refine them all?","And now that his master had obtained the Soul Advancement Formation...","At this realization, Zhen Xian Wu Yan understood.","His master intended to make him do all the heavy lifting!","Refining billions of mortals would be no problem for a transcendent powerhouse, but for him, who hadn’t yet transcended, it would incur karma.","However, that karma was nothing compared to the benefits of ancient demon blood.","“Heh, seems like Master wants to leave a good impression on the junior disciple!” Zhen Xian Wu Yan sneered inwardly, but dared not express any dissatisfaction.","He began to refine the entire Crimson Eye Realm.","Ever since the True Lord of Heavenly Fire had descended, Wei Jiuxian had been nothing more than a background figure, standing at the edge of the clouds, completely ignored.","No one bothered with him.","It was as if he had been forgotten entirely."]},{"number":6369,"title":"Chapter 6369: Life Seed, Explode!","paragraphs":["Chapter 6369: Life Seed, Explode!","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Outside the ancient castle, the powerful cultivators of the Zhanxian Tower, along with Xiang Yang and the others, all looked up toward the sky.","The massive face that had just appeared left a huge impact on them.","They had no idea what was happening.","Only Xiang Yang knew—a powerful being from the Upper Realm had descended.","“This is bad! Brother Wushuang still hasn’t appeared. What is he waiting for?” Xiang Yang’s heart was filled with anxiety.","But there was nothing he could do.","In the next moment, the color of the sky changed, and these cultivators began to rise into the air as if an enormous force was pulling them up. It felt like they were being dragged away by a giant suction force.","High in the sky, a giant sun appeared.","Zhen Xian, standing silent, formed a hand seal with one hand and shouted, “Devour the heavens and earth!”","This was a type of condensed divine ability.","Devouring a section of the heavens and earth, then condensing the power within it.","However, this method was cumbersome, and the power gained was minuscule. But if the world being condensed contained the ancient demon’s essence blood, then the harvest would be much greater.","Not only would the world be condensed, but along with it, billions of mortals and countless cultivators would be absorbed as well.","One part would be the ancient demon’s essence blood, and another part would be billions of souls.","“Huh!”","A soft sigh caught Zhen Xian’s attention.","It was Wei Jiuxian.","He exhaled lightly and looked helplessly at Zhen Xian, his tone stiff as he spoke: “Why? Why, after gaining so much, do you still covet these things? Are cultivators truly driven by endless greed?”","“Why do you always disregard mortals as humans? Do you not realize that you yourself once walked the path from mortal to immortal?”","“Why do you always believe that mortals cannot resist?”","“Why...”","“Why so many questions? If you weren’t pretending to be noble, would I have ended up like this?” Zhen Xian sneered, paying no further attention to Wei Jiuxian. After all, they would all soon die in the condensation process.","Li Miao had originally intended to say something, but upon noticing Zhen Xian’s cold indifference toward him, he abandoned the thought.","When he turned to look at Wei Jiuxian, the jealousy and bitterness in his heart had faded, replaced by a sense of pity for the other man.","“Why bother!” Li Miao shook his head slightly.","Wei Jiuxian, standing midair, clenched one hand into a fist, while gripping a spear in the other.","He muttered to himself with his head lowered, then shook his head again, finding his words childish, unable to express them. But when an opposing aura surged toward him, he suddenly raised his head, his eyes full of killing intent, and shouted:","“I ask you—WHY!!!”","The roar startled everyone!","Wei Jiuxian had finally let out the anger he’d been suppressing for so long.","“Hmm?”","True Lord Ye Huo, who had just entered Mangshan City, also paused. He had never taken Wei Jiuxian seriously, but at that moment, after sensing the strange aura around him, he sized him up for the first time.","“Interesting!”","Looking at Wei Jiuxian, True Lord Ye Huo turned to Zhen Xian and said, “Leave this little one alive!”","With that, he paid no further attention to him.","However, just as he was turning away, the aura around Wei Jiuxian plummeted sharply.","“Not good!”","True Lord Ye Huo’s figure flashed, trying to intervene, but it was too late.","In that instant, the seemingly unremarkable Wei Jiuxian had pierced through Zhen Xian’s chest with a spear, shattering his body and even his soul.","“I...” Zhen Xian looked in disbelief at the hole in his chest.","His reaction had been even slower than his master’s.","By now, it was already his final breath.","He had fallen!","Completely fallen, as Wei Jiuxian’s spear had pierced through his chest, leaving him dead beyond any hope of revival.","As Wei Jiuxian struck, the life seed within his body began to erupt.","His entire being surged with energy, his aura rising by several levels.","This was the seed of life that the woman in white had left him back then.","With it, he could protect the Tang Empire of the Eastern Lands and even the Red-Eyed Realm.","“It’s actually a seed of life!” True Lord Ye Huo also sensed the aura at that moment, his face filled with shock.","In the Mortal Realm, to encounter such a treasure...","This was something that even Immortals would fight over!","“My luck is incredible!” At this moment, he felt no sadness over the death of his disciple, only excitement.","Coming to the Mortal Realm, not only had he acquired a soul-advancing formation, but also the complete corpse of an ancient demon.","And now, he had stumbled upon a seed of life.","At this moment, he felt like he was the chosen one of this world.","“Haha, this realm truly is my lucky domain. I almost don’t want to destroy it!” True Lord Ye Huo was ecstatic. He looked at Wei Jiuxian and said excitedly, “Boy, give me that seed inside you, and maybe I’ll spare your life!”","Fu Qing stood silently to the side, glancing at his senior brother’s corpse, then at True Lord Ye Huo, but in the end, he said nothing.","The death of Zhen Xian was worthless in the face of the seed of life.","Li Miao opened his mouth, but it wasn’t because he had anything to say—it was the despair he felt at Wei Jiuxian’s continuous displays of power, each time surpassing his limits by countless folds.","Just what kind of inheritance had he obtained?","Only Wei Jiuxian knew.","Facing True Lord Ye Huo now, he knew he stood no chance, but he was determined to give it his all.","“You’ll take nothing from me but my life!” Wei Jiuxian pulled out the burning seed of life and crushed it with one hand.","The overwhelming power surged through him, nearly tearing his body apart.","It was clear he couldn’t contain such power.","True Lord Ye Huo watched the seed of life being crushed and felt an intense pain in his heart. He raged, “That was a seed of life! What a waste, an absolute waste!”","Even though the seed had been shattered, the power remained, though its value was far less than if it had been intact.","So, Wei Jiuxian had to die.","“Boy, you’ve angered me now!” True Lord Ye Huo flicked his fingers, and two fireballs as bright as the sun formed instantly, hurtling toward Wei Jiuxian.","The scorching heat swept over him, but Wei Jiuxian didn’t dodge. He raised his spear, which shot forward like a dragon, charging straight into the flames.","Hidden in the void, Jian Wushuang watched this scene and shook his head in resignation.","If he hadn’t appeared in this world, it would most likely be doomed.","Still, even with his presence, he wouldn’t act rashly.","At most, he’d wait for one side to win, then step in to clean up the mess, claim the treasure, and leave.","At least Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang weren’t in any mortal danger.","Jiu Chen’s true body was also watching. Earlier, when his clone had revealed the soul-advancing formation to save Li Miao, he had felt a moment of confusion.","Because he had never experienced something like this.","On the ground.","The powerful members of the Zhanxian Tower outside the ancient castle saw their commander displaying such immense strength, and they couldn’t help but cheer.","At that moment, even if they all died in battle, it would be worth it.","Because this was the Tang Empire, where only mighty warriors fell in battle—there were no weaklings who knelt and begged for mercy.","The Emperor of the Tang Empire?","From now on, the Tang Empire would have no emperor, only one name.","Wei Jiuxian!","The Tang Empire could live without an emperor, but it could never live without Wei Jiuxian."]},{"number":6370,"title":"Chapter 6370: Even Mortals Have Strong Beings","paragraphs":["Chapter 6370: Even Mortals Have Strong Beings","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“In the Mortal Realm, there are strong beings too!” Xiang Yang couldn’t help but exclaim in awe.","Jiang Shang, on the other hand, gazed at the stream of green energy, feeling a sense of familiarity.","It was just like what her mother had once left for her.","It was nurturing inside her body—would it eventually grow into something like this?","Curiosity filled her heart, but at this moment, she understood that her mother came from the higher realms and was no longer part of this world.","Within Mangshan County City.","There wasn’t a single living being left, only dried-up pools of blood and shattered remnants of soul power.","A gust of wind blew through, and suddenly, a sky-piercing lotus sprang from the ground.","The power on the lotus was weak, but as a surge of life force descended, it began to grow rapidly.","In the sky.","Wei Jiuxian couldn’t withstand the might of True Lord Ye Huo, his entire body covered in wounds.","At this moment, his power had already reached the extreme of mortal limits.","The pinnacle of the primordial spirit.","There was no way he could become stronger without transcending.","He had been a mortal, relying on external forces to grow stronger, but he could never directly transcend.","Now, he was barely clinging to life, yet he hadn’t let go of the long spear in his hand.","“Boy, you can’t stop me, and yet you waste such precious life force—what a waste!” True Lord Ye Huo cried out anxiously.","He didn’t care at all that he was a transcendent existence.","Because life force was far too valuable to him.","As long as he obtained it, he had the hope of becoming an immortal.","He had been stuck at this level for far too long. With the Soul Ascension Array, he could enhance his soul power, and as his soul power increased, so would his comprehension, allowing him to comprehend his own Dao marks and become eternal.","And life force contained the essence of life itself. If he had a life seed, he could nurture it to a certain point and directly ascend to immortality.","Unfortunately, the seed had been crushed by Wei Jiuxian, leaving only the life force. But even that life force was enough for him to break through to immortality—it would just take a bit longer.","But he could ultimately break through without relying on comprehension.","Now, watching the life force steadily drain away, he felt deeply frustrated, yet he couldn’t take down his opponent.","“There was once a shortcut placed right before me, and I failed to seize it!” True Lord Ye Huo fumed with anger.","Now, all he wanted was to kill Wei Jiuxian out of sheer rage.","“Boy, today I’ll show you the consequences of angering me!”","True Lord Ye Huo unleashed his full power, revealing the strength of a transcendent being.","In an instant, his entire form merged into a sea of fire.","What had once been an ordinary sea of flames now turned into black fire.","“Ye Huo!”","The Ye Huo descended!","The sky was completely scorched and turned into void.","The ground was burned clean in an instant—mountains and cities all vanished.","Everything was obliterated.","However, the destruction was limited, covering only a thousand-mile radius within Mangshan County.","The cultivators who had been outside the ancient castle, merely watching the spectacle, were suddenly pulled into the void the moment they sensed the Ye Huo flames.","Even True Lord Ye Huo himself hadn’t noticed.","Naturally, this was Jian Wushuang’s doing.","He didn’t want to just stand by and watch as Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang were burned alive.","At that moment, in the void, only two figures remained.","One was Wei Jiu Xian, and the other was True Lord Ye Huo.","Standing within the Ye Huo flames, Wei Jiu Xian remained upright.","He gripped his long spear with both hands, struggling to stay afloat in the air. Slowly, with every last bit of strength left in his body, he extended one hand and roared out the final words trapped in his chest.","“Mortal Wei Jiu Xian, invoke the god!”","As the words left his mouth, his entire body collapsed, falling from the flames.","He fell in the direction where Mangshan County had once stood.","Now, this place was shrouded in darkness, hollow and abyss-like, as if no life had ever existed there.","Yet, within that darkness, a single green lotus flower began to expand.","It grew at a speed visible to the naked eye, soon reaching the size of a lotus platform.","Wei Jiu Xian’s body landed on the lotus platform, and he immediately fell unconscious, but his hands still gripped the long spear tightly.","He lay atop the platform as the last traces of his life force were completely drained, turning the entire lotus a blood-red hue.","Witnessing this scene, True Lord Ye Huo was puzzled.","“What is this?”","He couldn’t quite understand the meaning behind the blood-red lotus platform.","But soon, the color shifted back to green.","The vitality of the lotus grew boundlessly, reaching a level that even caused True Lord Ye Huo to tremble in fear.","“This... this is a lotus of life seeds!”","True Lord Ye Huo couldn’t believe what he was seeing.","A single life seed was already a priceless treasure, but here, atop this lotus platform, were countless life seeds.","And the most precious part was the platform itself—it was worth infinitely more than any supreme treasure.","Hidden in the void, Jian Wushuang was also astonished.","This was something he hadn’t expected.","If he hadn’t been lurking in the void, he wouldn’t have seen this unfold.","The Lotus of Life!","It was indeed a super treasure, reminding him of the fabled Flower of the Other Shore.","Absolutely one of the most valuable treasures among the emperors.","Universe Masters didn’t necessarily need it, but they certainly wouldn’t refuse it.","A transcendent cultivator in the Great Perfection stage would undoubtedly be envious!","Not only was True Lord Ye Huo envious, but even Jian Wushuang felt a burning desire for it.","If he had waited before, it was to secure an opportunity for Xiang Yang and Jiang Shang, but now he, too, sought this opportunity for himself.","Fortunately, the lotus was still there!","It couldn’t run away, and he wasn’t worried that True Lord Ye Huo could steal it.","Because Wei Jiu Xian had revived.","The invocation of the god was something Jian Wushuang had never seen before.","And it seemed that the god Wei Jiu Xian had invoked was a true deity.","At this moment, only Wei Jiu Xian’s willpower remained. His physical body and soul had already perished long ago.","Only his willpower drove him to continue.","“True Lord Ye Huo, I will make sure you stay in the Scarlet Eye Realm forever, turn you completely mortal, and imprison you in the Scarlet Eye Realm for eternity, so you can truly experience the joys of being a mortal!”","The first sentence was spoken in Wei Jiu Xian’s voice.","But after that, both the power and movements changed.","From the lotus platform, Wei Jiu Xian hurled the long spear in his hand, transforming it into a streak of rainbow light that pierced through space, heading straight for True Lord Ye Huo.","“No!”","True Lord Ye Huo roared, but it was too late.","The long spear pierced his chest, and like his disciple before him, he died under the spear’s blade.","And there was another unlucky soul—his nephew Fu Qing—who had perished in his own Ye Huo flames.","One could say Fu Qing was the unluckiest of them all.","The moment Wei Jiu Xian threw the spear, his body turned into a statue and fell from the lotus platform.","His last thread of willpower began to fade away.","Seeing this, Jian Wushuang used his thought power to wrap Wei Jiu Xian’s final thread of will in a gentle force.","He condensed a wisp of his soul, imbued with his own thought power, and injected it into Wei Jiu Xian’s remaining will.","However, Wei Jiu Xian had only his will left, and it had fallen into slumber. Reviving him would be incredibly difficult.","But helping him return to the heavenly cycle of reincarnation would be easy.","With a flick of his hand, Jian Wushuang sent his soul into the cycle of reincarnation.","This was the reincarnation of the Scarlet Eye Realm. Wei Jiu Xian would be reborn in the Scarlet Eye Realm, though his memories would be wiped clean.","“It’s over!”"]},{"number":6371,"title":"Chapter 6371: End Means Beginning","paragraphs":["Chapter 6371: End Means Beginning","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang sighed silently.","The cultivators within the Crimson Eye Realm, whether from the Upper Realm or the natives, had all given their best.","They had planned and schemed, only to end up here.","Jian Wushuang led Jiang Shang and the others out of the void. In the dark void, a cloud ignited in the eastern sky.","Only Mangshan County was destroyed; the Eastern Lands had not yet fully descended into darkness.","The sun continued to rise as usual.","“I never expected this to be the ending!” Xiang Yang looked at the lotus platform and sighed.","Yang Xiao gazed at the place where the Chief Commander had disappeared, remaining silent for a long time. Yet deep within, he harbored the resolve to inherit the Chief’s will.","“I can sense it. My clone hasn’t died yet, and neither has Li Miao!” Immortal Jiu Chen’s true form didn’t seem to care about anything else, still preoccupied with his clone.","Jian Wushuang spoke up at this moment, “They carry heavy karma. Do you still want to fuse with your clone?”","He had originally intended to help Jiu Chen return to his full strength, but seeing Jiu Chen’s overwhelming obsession, he felt it wasn’t necessary to proceed with the fusion.","As for Li Miao, while his soul had returned to reincarnation and he wasn’t technically dead, his path of cultivation was lost. He might not even manage to reincarnate, burdened with too much karmic debt, likely to be condemned to the Abyss of Endless Torment.","“Forget it, let him remain in this world forever!” Immortal Jiu Chen’s true form seemed to come to terms with it at that moment.","It seemed like everything had come to an end.","And yet, it also felt as if something was just beginning.","The lotus platform began to wither, but in an instant, a powerful life force blossomed.","The aura was familiar. Jian Wushuang turned his gaze, and a figure appeared on the lotus platform.","He alerted Jiang Shang, who also looked over.","Upon seeing the woman in plain clothes, Jiang Shang froze on the spot, trembling as she stammered, “Mother? Is that you?”","At first, she couldn’t believe it, until the figure extended her hand.","“Ni’er!”","That figure exuded an indescribable affection, but when she called out her daughter’s true name, a powerful force began to isolate her existence.","She became panicked, her face filled with fear, and her voice grew urgent as she shouted at Jiang Shang, “Don’t come, don’t come, don’t come... remember, never come looking for me!”","As she finished speaking, her figure began to vanish along with the lotus platform.","Yet, as she turned for one last look at her daughter, she noticed the figure standing beside her.","Boom!","It was as if lightning struck her mind. Her entire body began trembling, and she frantically shook her head at Jiang Shang, as if to warn her to leave the figure’s side.","The person standing beside Jiang Shang was none other than Jian Wushuang!","That figure was Jiang Shang’s mother, Jiang Shang, and when she saw Jian Wushuang standing beside her daughter, the fear in her eyes surpassed even the force that was cutting her off.","But in the end, she was unable to say anything.","Jian Wushuang, upon seeing Jiang Shang, didn’t quite know how to address her. He wanted to stop the isolating power but realized that it was Origin Source divine power—too strong. With his current strength, there was no way to intervene.","But it would be rude to meet an old acquaintance with a cold face, so he forced a small smile.","It was this smile that filled Jiang Shang’s eyes with terror.","Whoosh!","Jiang Shang’s figure completely disappeared, and at that moment, the lotus platform fully withered. Only a few dozen life seeds remained, which Jian Wushuang carefully gathered.","“Mother!” Jiang Shang finally snapped out of it, rushing forward in a panic.","Standing in the silent void, she couldn’t find a trace of her mother’s presence. In a daze, she stood there, tears streaming down her face, helpless.","Her pitiful state tugged at Jian Wushuang’s heart, and he couldn’t bear to watch. He stepped forward to console her, “What appeared just now was likely a projection of your mother. This means she’s still alive, probably in the Ancient Domain. Once you ascend, you might meet her again soon.”","“But my mother...” Jiang Shang looked up, her eyes bloodshot.","Jian Wushuang understood what she meant. He patted her shoulder and said, “Don’t worry. I’ll help you! I told you, I was friends with your mother. You don’t have to worry.”","Since her mother had previously looked at Jian Wushuang in an unusual way, Jiang Ni naturally had no reason to doubt it.","She even suspected that Jian Wushuang might be her unknown father!","If Jian Wushuang knew about this, he would probably have nightmares!","Fortunately, she wasn’t foolish and could tell that her personality and bloodline bore no resemblance to Jian Wushuang.","The only thing they had in common was their use of swords.","However, her swordsmanship had been taught by her mother, and it had nothing to do with Jian Wushuang.","Her thoughts were a whirlwind of speculation as she wondered, “Perhaps Senior Jian Wushuang once admired my mother?”","This guess wasn’t entirely wrong.","Because Jian Wushuang really had admired her in the past. Back when he first entered the ancient Moon Space-Time, he had admired the Heavenly Maiden.","The Heavenly Maiden was Jiang Ni’s mother, and this indeed counted as admiration.","There had also been a time in the Qishen Temple when Jian Wushuang had become close with Jiang Ni’s mother, which could be considered some sort of friendship.","But that bond was not particularly strong.","Just as Jian Wushuang was comforting Jiang Ni, Xiang Yang walked over at the worst possible time and asked in surprise, “Jiang Ni, why did I hear your mother calling you ‘Ni’er’? Is that your childhood nickname?”","Jian Wushuang rolled his eyes, feeling that this man always fixated on the strangest things.","“I suppose so!” Jiang Ni, now calm, nodded and explained, “My real name is Jiang Ni. After my mother left me in the Jiang Kingdom, I disguised myself as a man and changed my name to Jiang Shang. Later, I met all of you.”","“I see!” Xiang Yang had a sudden look of realization and then said, “So now that you’re back to being a woman, should we call you Jiang Ni?”","Jiang Ni smiled warmly. In that moment, she finally displayed the kind of smile that only a young woman could have.","That smile was also her farewell to the Red-Eye Realm.","The journey of the three had just begun.","This was merely an ordinary mortal world.","Jian Wushuang had gained much here, from the initial despair to eventual peace, even feeling fortunate. All of this had changed him because of this place.","So when he left, he transformed the Red-Eye Realm.","From then on, this world became a true paradise, free from the rampages of the powerful, a place of peace.","He completely filled the void, turning it into a vast plain.","All the traces left by the Northern Region Glacier and the entire cultivation world were erased one by one.","The remaining cultivators, deprived of the power they once absorbed, began to see their cultivation levels decline.","Eventually, they reverted to ordinary martial artists, with lifespans no different from those of mortals.","Of course, he allowed some individuals to retain their power.","For example, Yang Xiao remained a late-stage Golden Core cultivator, still at the peak of his power.","As for Jiu Chen’s clone, Jian Wushuang placed it within the Heavenly Dao, embedding within it a deep sense of duty towards the revival of the human race.","From that moment on, the Red-Eye Realm would be ruled by humans.","After their power was stripped away, the demon beasts could only become wild animals.","Furthermore, Jian Wushuang also rescued Chen Yuan’s soul, and in the process, he brought back Miss Ah Zi’s soul from the cycle of reincarnation, restoring their bodies together."]},{"number":6372,"title":"Chapter 6372: Ancient Domain","paragraphs":["Chapter 6372: Ancient Domain","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","It was indeed a pity for that rough man, Hu San, as he couldn’t revive the woman he loved. However, regenerating his severed arm was not difficult for Jian Wushuang. He also granted him a life of wealth and prosperity, which could be considered as repaying the first kind-hearted person they had encountered.","After doing all of this, he re-consolidated the ancient demon’s essence blood into three fleshy orbs.","He then dropped a single drop of his own essence blood onto the three bodies.","The life level of each of these bodies had reached ten thousand times the norm, and that was just the baseline. How much more they could advance would depend on the strength of the person occupying the body.","Naturally, these three bodies were given to Xiang Yang, Jiang Ni, and Immortal Jiu Chen himself.","As it stood, there was only one Jiu Chen, without the distinction between a true self and a clone.","After completing all of this, he stored the three into the Nine Prison Pagoda.","He had given them the seeds of life, along with all the treasures he had plundered from the Crimson Eye Realm, enough to help them reach the level of Origin Spirit.","There was also a grand soul-advancement formation, with the seeds of life as nourishment.","It was enough for them to master the bodies of the Special Life Forms, and once they emerged from seclusion, they would transcend.","Having done all of this, Jian Wushuang was free of lingering concerns.","Using his form as a sword, he slashed open the space of the Crimson Eye Realm and ascended to the Ancient Domain.","...","In the Upper Realm, within the Ancient Domain.","The Ancient Domain hadn’t been in existence for very long, only a few hundred thousand years.","But within these few hundred thousand years, several brilliant eras had arisen.","The first era saw the rise of the One Hundred and Eight Ancient Domains and the One Hundred and Eight Ancient Demons, unmatched in their might!","This era was long, reigning over the cosmos for a full hundred thousand years.","After a hundred thousand years, the Ancient Demon Era was destroyed by the Human Race’s Ancient Court.","Most of the Ancient Demons fell, while the rest were suppressed, forming countless mortal worlds.","Their essence blood scattered across the realms, sparking the Ascension Era.","During the Ascension Era, the Ancient Domain was entirely ruled by ascendants.","Even the remaining seventy-two Ancient Domains were firmly under the control of the ascendants.","The founder of the Ancient Court, “Yuan Zheng Celestial Venerable,” formally stepped down during this time, passing the title of Lord of the Ancient Court to his disciple, the strongest of all ascendants!","This was “Zhen Xian of the Three Talents!”","This was the age of the ascendants, but it was a brief one, lasting only a few tens of thousands of years.","The power that supported the mortal worlds, derived from the Ancient Demons, was quickly exhausted.","The Ancient Domain entered a new era.","The Era of Divine Eye!","The Divine Eye techniques had existed since the birth of the Ancient Domain, and the strength of the human race was inseparable from the legacy of the Divine Eye.","However, because the ascendants were numerous, and most of them combined Divine Eye techniques with powerful physical bodies, they dominated the Ascension Era.","But as one mortal world after another fell into ruin, new ascendants from the Ancient Domain grew fewer and fewer. The Ascension Era came to a complete end. The Era of Divine Eye that followed was brought forth by one being who fused two different legacies into one.","His emergence not only altered the Ascension Era but also changed the entire power structure of the Ancient Domain.","In the first two eras of the Ancient Domain, the Ancient Court ruled as the hegemon, governing all seventy-two Ancient Domains.","However, with the integration of the two legacies by the Divine Eye inheritor, a Divine Eye Sacred Land was summoned.","The arrival of this Sacred Land shifted the balance of power, breaking the Ancient Court’s dominance.","From that point on, the seventy-two Ancient Domains were split into two major factions.","One was the Ancient Court, and the other was the Divine Eye Sacred Land.","The one who summoned the Sacred Land became known as the “Sacred Lord,” a title akin to the Lord of the Heavenly Court.","The two forces frequently clashed, with each side ruling thirty-six Ancient Domains, both flourishing in their own right.","Of course, there was always a gap between the new and the old factions.","For instance, the old faction represented by the Ancient Court was more conservative and balanced.","Although the Divine Eye Secret Technique was powerful, it was merely a stepping stone on the path of divine power in the future.","Therefore, they did not regard the Divine Eye inheritance as their true path.","The new faction, on the other hand, was more extreme. Not only did they burn their immortal divine power using the Divine Eye inheritance, but they also integrated it into their own path, even to the point of burning their own path for it.","This explosive power surpassed other experts of the same level.","Countless Divine Eye inheritors tried to emulate this, which caused disdain from the old faction. They believed such actions would ruin all cultivators in the Ancient Domain, leading to a split.","The Ancient Court represented balance, while the Holy Land represented extremity.","In truth, neither side was wrong; it was simply a difference in understanding.","Burning one’s path wasn’t inherently problematic, but it depended on how it was done.","To be precise, it needed to be controlled. One couldn’t blindly burn their own path marks just to increase battle power, as this would affect their future path to becoming an Emperor.","If one prematurely overdraws their path’s power, although the strength gained is formidable, once they reach the point of merging with the Dao, problems would arise.","The path after immortality is relatively smooth, with the merge with the Dao being the most challenging checkpoint.","After merging with the Dao, one’s battle power would transform drastically.","One shouldn’t sacrifice their future merge with the Dao just to increase power in the immortal phase.","This was the crux of the conflict between the Ancient Court and the Holy Land.","Burning one’s own Origin Source path would lead to immense glory during the immortal stage, but they would be left dumbfounded when it came time to merge with the Dao.","However, there were exceptions. If not, the Holy Land wouldn’t have risen so quickly.","This was because one particular inheritor who fused two major sequences succeeded in merging with the Dao. Not only did they succeed, but their battle power after merging was so formidable that they could take on a hundred opponents alone.","Even the ancient Yuan Zheng Heavenly Lord and the number one expert among the ascenders, “Zhen Xian of the Three Talents,” were no match for him.","Additionally, due to the Divine Power Secret Technique, he became the absolute strongest in the Seventy-Two Ancient Domains.","Besides him, three other experts from the Holy Land also successfully merged with the Dao. Although their strength wasn’t as overwhelming as that of the Holy Master, they could rival Yuan Zheng Heavenly Lord.","It was rumored that these three, when combined, could challenge two generations of Ancient Court Masters.","However, for most Holy Land experts, succeeding in merging with the Dao was exceedingly difficult. After a hundred thousand years, only four had succeeded.","One of them had fused two major sequences, while the other three had merely perfected two sequences without choosing to merge them into the Dao.","Only four Emperors had emerged in a hundred thousand years. Though each of them was incredibly powerful, the number was too small.","They were far outnumbered by the Ancient Court.","The Ancient Court had the oldest inheritance and prided themselves on taking the correct path.","The strength of one’s path varied, but those who cultivated a powerful Origin Source path would not be weaker than the Holy Land inheritors after merging with the Dao.","Even those with weaker paths had an advantage, as the difficulty of merging with the Dao was reduced.","Thus, the Ancient Court had the most Emperors, with a full hundred Emperors in their ranks.","Among them, the strongest was Zhen Xian of the Three Talents, followed by Yuan Zheng Heavenly Lord, and lastly, the third-generation Master of the Ancient Court.","The strength of these three individuals was also not to be underestimated, which was why the Ancient Court’s development remained the most stable.","They did not have the intense conflicts found in the Thirty-Six Ancient Domains within the Holy Land.","In contrast, they were relatively peaceful.","At present, what Jian Wushuang sought was this very peace.","A hundred years had passed since his ascension.","Now, he stood within the Holy City of the Heaven Altar in the Ancient Domain of the Overturning Sea.","In these hundred years, he had simultaneously studied the Nine Prison Pagoda Token and meditated on his own path.","His current realm remained the same as when he ascended, still at the peak of the Great Perfection stage.","There hadn’t been much progress.","Mainly because, during these hundred years, he hadn’t ventured out in search of treasures to break through his own limits."]},{"number":6373,"title":"Chapter 6373: Bottleneck","paragraphs":["Chapter 6373: Bottleneck","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Even though he was rebuilding, he still faced bottlenecks.","And these bottlenecks weren’t small.","It couldn’t be helped—his current physical foundation was that of a Realm Beast, which had limitless growth potential. His soul, too, carried the will of a Realm Beast, making it incredibly resilient and also limitless in growth.","Therefore, his path had to match this—limitless growth.","He had already mastered the ultimate path and the Extreme Path, so he didn’t need to expend much effort to grasp them again.","Over the years, he had thoroughly explored the entire Ancient Domain.","In particular, he had gained a clear understanding of the Origin Source after reaching the level of the Immortal.","This world was beneath the Realm God Continent, so it was different from spacetime, but it was very similar to the Realm God Continent. The only difference was that the Realm God Continent didn’t have the so-called Divine Eye legacy.","The Divine Eye legacy came from his Senior Brother Ghost Eye.","Since Teacher Xuan Yi had taken him as a disciple, Senior Brother Ghost Eye’s strength likely wasn’t lacking. He might even have been a Universe God, or perhaps even stronger.","The legacy he left behind was undoubtedly powerful.","The Ancient Domain comprised seventy-two universes, larger than the lower-tier Primitive Worlds, but smaller than the medium-tier worlds like the Great Division.","If the thirty-six shattered universes were included, it could barely be considered a medium-tier world.","From this, it could be inferred that other worlds, too, had high-tier and medium-tier worlds.","This realm should be considered a vast universe.","In a hundred years, he had traveled through the entire Ancient Domain and had learned much about matters related to the Heavens.","However, if one wanted to reach the Heavens, they first needed to leave the Ancient Domain.","One had to enter the Boundless Chaos, traverse various alien worlds, and find the legendary Sea of the Universe.","That was a sea that existed within the Boundless Chaos.","Crossing the Sea of the Universe would lead one to the Heavens.","But to find the Sea of the Universe, one needed to be at least at the Heavenly Emperor level, which Jian Wushuang estimated was roughly equivalent to the Absolute Peak level.","As for surviving the journey across the Sea of the Universe, one needed to surpass the Heavenly Emperor level.","That meant reaching the level of a Universe Master.","This was his estimation based on his knowledge.","In truth, just leaving the Ancient Domain alone required someone to be at the Great Completion Peak level. Entering the Boundless Chaos would require at least an Immortal Zhen Xian, as a Zhen Xian had their own path and no longer needed to rely on external forces.","Throughout the history of the Ancient Domain, many Immortal Zhen Xians had left the Ancient Domain to venture into the Boundless Chaos. However, very few returned alive. Those who had journeyed to alien worlds and returned safely were mostly Immortal Pinnacles.","In other words, only those with the power of a Dao Lord could traverse between two worlds.","He calculated his current strength. Even breaking through to the Immortal level was a challenge, so leaving the Ancient Domain wasn’t a suitable choice for him.","Thus, he decided to stay and improve to the Immortal level within the Ancient Domain before making further plans.","At the moment, he was in Tiantan City. Unlike the mortal realm, there were no taverns here. If a cultivator wanted to find a place to seclude themselves, they had to go to a special retreat called the Legacy Mountain.","This place was under the jurisdiction of the Sacred Land. It had no Cloud Pavilions, which were another type of retreat found in the Heavenly Court, but only the Legacy God Mountain of the Sacred Land.","The Divine Mountain loomed high, stretching for thousands of miles, with countless caves dotting its surface.","From the foot of the mountain to the summit, the price of these caves varied significantly.","Tai’an City, located in the heart of the Ancient Sea Domain, was home to the legendary Divine Mountain, which itself stood at the core of the city. Naturally, it wasn’t possible to train here for free; one had to pay for it.","And the currency wasn’t ordinary either—it required Immortal Crystals, treasures formed from the condensed Origin Source of Immortal-level experts. These crystals were considered the hard currency throughout the Ancient Domain and even in foreign worlds.","Jian Wushuang had once obtained only a few dozen Immortal Crystals from True Lord Ye Huo.","But to cultivate on the Divine Mountain, even the price for staying at the foot of the mountain was exorbitant—so high that most cultivators in the Mahayana stage couldn’t afford it.","Fortunately, Jian Wushuang had mastered the Origin Source Dao. Yet, he had not broken through to Immortality because he couldn’t follow the same path anymore. With the physique and will of the Realm Beast, he needed to forge a new path.","Thus, he had yet to make a breakthrough!","After wandering for a hundred years, he had stayed secluded in the Divine Mountain for decades, searching for his way forward.","Even after a hundred years of wandering and several decades of seclusion, he hadn’t found a clear direction.","At that moment, the token in his hand emitted a brilliant light, and the Origin Source power within the cave was instantly drained.","There was no need to panic in situations like this.","It wasn’t that someone was causing trouble; it likely just meant his lease on the cave had expired.","“Friend Wushuang, the time for your lease on Cave A at the foot of the mountain has expired. Would you like to extend it?” A pleasant voice echoed into the cave. If it hadn’t been for the lease expiration, no one would have disturbed him.","Jian Wushuang took a deep breath, inwardly marveling at how absurdly expensive the caves on the Divine Mountain were.","Just staying in a Grade A cave at the foot of the mountain for one sixty-year cycle cost ten Immortal Crystals.","A Grade B cave required five crystals, a Grade C three crystals, and a Grade D one crystal.","If it were a Grade A cave halfway up the mountain, it would cost a hundred Immortal Crystals.","As for the summit, even most Immortal True Sages couldn’t afford to live there.","He touched the ring on his finger and ultimately decided to leave.","As he stepped out of the cave, he saw a female cultivator wearing a purple skirt. She had a graceful demeanor, and her every movement exuded an indescribable charm.","This was the caretaker of the Grade A cave at the foot of the mountain, “Fairy Ziyu.” He had chatted with her a few times when he first arrived, and they were somewhat acquainted.","“I won’t be extending it. After all these years in seclusion, I’ve gained nothing. I might as well go out and explore!” Jian Wushuang wasn’t about to admit he was out of money.","In truth, he still had quite a few treasures on him; he just didn’t plan on selling them. Plus, after secluding himself for one sixty-year cycle, he had gained little, not even fully comprehending the Nine Prison Command. It seemed better to go out and explore, perhaps visit the Ancient Court’s territory.","Fairy Ziyu smiled warmly and said, “Friend Wushuang, you’re already at the peak of the Mahayana stage. Breaking through to become an Immortal True Sage isn’t easy. Why not venture into some dangerous places? You might just find a path suitable for your Origin Source Dao!”","She wasn’t wrong. After all, she was an Immortal Sage herself and had continuously advanced, gaining quite a reputation among Immortal True Sages. Otherwise, she wouldn’t have landed such a lucrative position at the Divine Mountain.","However, she had no idea that Jian Wushuang now possessed two Origin Source Daos, and they were among the strongest.","The Ultimate Sword Dao, a path of slaughter, was so rare that even among countless Immortal experts, only a few had mastered it.","By Jian Wushuang’s estimation, when the Holy Lord of the Sacred Land succeeded in merging with the Dao, his Origin Source Dao’s power was comparable to the Ultimate Dao.","That’s why he was so terrifying.","Among the third-generation experts of the Ancient Court, their Dao mastery was merely at the first rank.","In other words, no one in the entire Ancient Domain had mastered the Ultimate Dao. If it weren’t for the inheritance of the Divine Eye, even if he were thrown into the Original Universe of the Northern Sky, he wouldn’t stand out.","And he, himself, had mastered both the Ultimate Dao and the Extreme Dao.","It wasn’t possible to abandon these two Daos, and forging a new Dao was far from easy.","“Fairy Ziyu, you’ve traveled far and wide, and your friends span the entire Ancient Domain. If you come across any good opportunities, please keep me in mind!” Jian Wushuang exchanged pleasantries with her, his expression calm and collected."]},{"number":6374,"title":"Chapter 6374: Sweet Mouth Won’t Make You Hungry","paragraphs":["Chapter 6374: Sweet Mouth Won’t Make You Hungry","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","To be honest, Ziyu Immortal Fairy did seem to have some interest in him.","A lot of what he knew about the world of the Ancient Domain came from Ziyu Immortal Fairy herself.","In fact, it was at her invitation that he entered Tiantan City. They had met in an ancient place within the Overturning Sea Region. At that time, Jian Wushuang had only been in the region for a short while, but after showcasing a bit of his strength, Ziyu Immortal Fairy began to see him in a different light.","If it had been any other Peak Stage Da Cheng cultivator, they would never have received such respect from a well-known Zhen Xian like her.","“Daoist Wushuang, you flatter me. I’m merely a few years older than you, that’s all. With your talent, once you break through and become an Immortal, I might need to rely on you instead!” Ziyu Immortal Fairy smiled, her almond-shaped eyes narrowing in amusement. She enjoyed this kind of flattery.","Seeing her reaction, Jian Wushuang continued to compliment her, “With your talents and beauty, Immortal Fairy, I’m sure there are plenty more outstanding cultivators pursuing you. Why would you pay attention to an ordinary cultivator like me?”","As soon as he said this, two voices echoed in his mind.","“Shameless! That old hag is at least fifty thousand years old, and you’re still willing to eat up her flattery?”","“Brother Wushuang, don’t listen to that old guy. Fifty thousand years is nothing. Haven’t you heard that being three thousand years older means they’ve already entered the ranks of the Immortals? Besides, I think Ziyu Immortal Fairy looks pretty good, with that figure, those eyes... hehe...”","The first voice was from Immortal Jiu Chen, full of disdain, while the second was encouragement from Xiang Yang.","Immortal Jiu Chen didn’t know Jian Wushuang’s true origins and could only sense from his aura that he was born into this world relatively recently.","About a hundred years ago, which was indeed very short.","Xiang Yang, on the other hand, knew Jian Wushuang’s background—he was a Universe God, and who knew how many epochs he had lived through, maybe even hundreds of cycles.","How could he possibly be considered young?","But Jian Wushuang ignored both of them. He wasn’t flirting with Ziyu Immortal Fairy just for fun.","He had already figured out most of Ziyu Immortal Fairy’s background. She was a smooth operator, skilled at manipulating people. She might be acting interested in him now, but who knew how many others she had been interested in behind the scenes?","She simply saw his potential and wanted to deepen their connection. When he reached the Immortal level, she probably expected him to become a valuable ally.","Ziyu Immortal Fairy smiled flirtatiously as she swayed her graceful body toward Jian Wushuang. Her tone changed slightly as she said, “If you truly see me as an elder sister, I have a great opportunity that requires a few Peak Da Cheng cultivators.”","Upon hearing this, Jian Wushuang immediately cupped his hands and bowed slightly, saying, “If you don’t mind... no, no, if Elder Sister Ziyu doesn’t mind, I am more than willing to regard you as family!”","At that moment, Jian Wushuang’s genuine expression made him seem like an infatuated man.","For a brief moment, Ziyu Immortal Fairy truly felt something. She took his strong arm in her hand, her voice soft and charming, “You sweet talker!”","“As long as Elder Sister is willing, I’ll eat honey every day!” Jian Wushuang teased.","...","Since they were on the sacred mountain, the two couldn’t go too far and soon hurried down to Ziyu Immortal Fairy’s residence within the city.","It was a sprawling mansion that covered ten li of land.","As soon as Jian Wushuang stepped inside, he immediately sensed several powerful presences.","At least four Zhen Xians, along with two Peak Da Cheng cultivators.","It was clear that Ziyu Immortal Fairy had brought him here for serious business.","In the tea hall, six powerful figures sat on two sides.","On one side were the four Zhen Xians, and on the other side were two Peak Da Cheng cultivators.","Jian Wushuang noticed that when the cultivators saw the unfamiliar Nascent Soul stage cultivator arriving with Zi Yu Immortal, they all furrowed their brows. However, none of them questioned it on the spot. Instead, they all nodded politely in greeting.","Zi Yu Immortal held Jian Wushuang’s arm and began introducing the people present.","The first person she introduced had a young appearance, a burly and muscular physique, and a pair of cold eyes. He had an unapproachable aura, and his neatly combed hair added to his solemn demeanor.","“Wushuang, this is Wu Hou Zhenxian of the Lieyang Sect. He’s already one of the Fifth Step powerhouses among the immortals, incredibly strong, and he also serves as an elder of the Lieyang Sect. Not just any elder, but one who holds real authority!” After finishing her introduction, Zi Yu Immortal winked at Wu Hou Zhenxian. He dodged her gaze slightly but did not seem to resist.","Jian Wushuang quickly stepped forward, bowed respectfully, and said, “Greetings, Wu Hou Zhenxian!”","“Hmm.” Wu Hou Zhenxian, in consideration of Zi Yu Immortal, nodded silently and let out a single hum of acknowledgment, which was enough to consider the introduction complete.","To Jian Wushuang, this type of person wasn’t frightening. At the very least, he wasn’t the treacherous kind. After all, people often said that those who wore their emotions on their faces were the simplest to deal with.","Being able to judge a person’s character based on their appearance meant the threat they posed was minimal. The most dangerous were always those whose emotions were inscrutable.","From the first glance, Jian Wushuang developed a good impression of Wu Hou Zhenxian.","Zi Yu Immortal then proceeded to introduce the other three immortals, as well as the two Nascent Soul stage cultivators.","Initially, Jian Wushuang had assumed that Zi Yu Immortal was the leader of the group. However, when she introduced one of the Nascent Soul cultivators, Jian Wushuang realized that the true leader of these people was likely the Nascent Soul cultivator standing before him.","“True Lord Xue Yang!”","This man was at the peak of the Nascent Soul stage, with a life force five thousand times stronger than average and battle strength that was incredibly fierce.","In the realm of immortality, there were roughly nine steps of power.","Each step was a major leap in cultivation.","The Ninth Step represented the peak of immortality. Beyond that, one could condense their Origin Source to become a Dao Lord.","Among the people present, the strongest in terms of raw power were Wu Hou Zhenxian and another immortal named Tian Can Zhenxian.","Both of them were Fifth Step powerhouses.","Within the realm of immortality, they were considered mid-tier in strength. Those stronger than them had likely already founded their own sects and were regarded as top figures in ancient domains.","Wu Hou Zhenxian was not very talkative and had a cold demeanor, which meant he lacked the diplomacy required to lead.","Hence, Jian Wushuang initially believed that the elderly Tian Can Zhenxian was the leader of these people. When Zi Yu Immortal introduced him, Jian Wushuang had shown even more respect.","But it was only when she introduced True Lord Xue Yang that Jian Wushuang realized the truth. Zi Yu Immortal mentioned the two supreme experts within the city, and Jian Wushuang suddenly understood.","However, True Lord Xue Yang was sensitive about his background. The moment Zi Yu Immortal deliberately mentioned his connections, he immediately interrupted her, saying, “Background is just background; it has nothing to do with my strength. There’s no need for anyone to mind that!”","His words brought smiles to everyone’s faces. It was both a gesture of humility and a way to gain some respect from the others.","Jian Wushuang also acknowledged the fact that True Lord Xue Yang had considerable influence. Anyone with connections to the Sun Symbol within the Heavenly Altar held a prestigious status.","Within the Fu Hai Ancient Domain, there were two supreme experts. One of them was the holy disciple of the Sacred Sect, known as the “Two-Faced Buddha.”","This person had a strange personality, often doing things that sent chills down people’s spines. His strength was immense, and though the faction he had founded had no official name and seemed disorganized, every one of his subordinates was just as cruel and erratic as he was.","Merely hearing his name within the city would make anyone shudder.","The other supreme expert was much more normal by comparison. Not only was he normal, but he was also a righteous cultivator, widely respected. His reputation extended not only across the Fu Hai Domain but also throughout the entire Seventy-Two Domains.","Though this was the Sacred Sect’s territory, even the Ancient Court praised this righteous expert. There were even rumors that if this expert ever decided to visit the Ancient Court, he could easily be granted the title of Heavenly King."]},{"number":6375,"title":"Chapter 6375: Yang Talisman Inheritor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6375: Yang Talisman Inheritor","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","It was known that the Ancient Court had a total of four Great Kings. Although none of them held the title of Emperor, each was a supreme powerhouse among the Dao Lords.","Not only did their strength have to be formidable, but they also had to possess a heart for the righteous path.","Both qualities were essential.","“Yang Dingtian, the inheritor of the Yang Talisman from the Sacred Land!”","That was why his nickname was the Yang Talisman Bearer.","This was because, in the entire Ancient Domain, very few had managed to obtain the inheritance of the Yang Talisman.","Even many powerful cultivators who had perfected the sequence of inheritances had not obtained the Yang Talisman.","It was evident how difficult it was to obtain the Yang Talisman.","In fact, this wasn’t the first time he had heard of the Yang Talisman. He had seen it in the Divine Eye Order. The Yang Talisman was considered a type of key, though no one knew what it was meant to unlock, so it was regarded as merely a symbol of strength.","True Lord Xueyang, whose real name was Yang Zhonghuan, was the younger brother of Yang Dingtian.","Despite his older brother’s immense reputation, True Lord Xueyang’s strength during his Mahayana stage was no less impressive. He was a being capable of contending with Immortal Zhen Xian, yet he was much more reserved in nature. He never took advantage of his brother’s fame to act recklessly.","This was what made many respect him.","However, there were also those who grew jealous because of it.","One of the other Mahayana cultivators was particularly displeased.","He was a disciple of the Crippled Elder. Although he appeared amicable and eloquent, the sinister intent in his eyes could not be hidden.","After briefly greeting everyone, Immortal Ziyu arranged for him to sit next to the Crippled Elder’s disciple and then moved on to the main topic.","Immortal Ziyu smiled warmly and said, “True Lord Xueyang, this matter begins with you. I will vouch for you; everyone here can be considered one of our own. You can now speak in detail about that issue!”","Everyone knew this, so they all turned their attention to True Lord Xueyang. They were curious as to why, as the younger brother of Yang Dingtian, he needed external help for his adventures. Why not just rely on his brother’s formidable subordinates, of which there were many?","And to go through Immortal Ziyu for this? It seemed entirely unnecessary.","Although Immortal Ziyu was quite famous within the city of Tian’tan, the number of supreme powerhouses she truly knew was limited. Most only showed her respect for her reputation. Among the four True Immortals present, only two were at the fifth step of Immortality, while the other two were at the fourth step, and their life levels and Immortal power were relatively ordinary.","If it was said that True Lord Xueyang didn’t want to rely on his older brother, that seemed a bit far-fetched. His brother was strong, but he certainly wasn’t a fool!","Now, everyone looked at True Lord Xueyang, eager to hear his reasoning.","True Lord Xueyang noticed their curiosity and began to explain, “The reason I troubled Immortal Ziyu this time is because I didn’t want my brother to know about this matter. Also, the place I discovered is rather peculiar.”","“It requires Mahayana-stage cultivators as well as True Immortal Zhen Xian. While it doesn’t pose a great threat to me, it would be quite troublesome to handle alone, so I called upon all of you to assist me. However, this matter must remain confidential—especially from my brother. He must not find out!”","“Rest assured, True Lord Xueyang,” the Crippled Elder smiled and agreed, “Now that we’re all on the same boat, we’ll prioritize our shared interests above all else!”","The others also nodded in agreement.","Next, True Lord Xue Yang began to explain the details.","It was actually quite simple. He had discovered the palace of an ancient demon from the archaic era.","This ancient demon had already reached the level of immortality, and his power back then was formidable.","Everyone was familiar with his name—it was the same as the name of the ancient region he ruled.","“The Sea-Covering Demon God!”","He was an ancient demon who became immortal during the archaic era.","Among the one hundred and eight ancient demons of that time, only seventy-two had become immortal demons, while the remaining thirty-six were at the peak of the Great Ascension stage.","As a result, thirty-six ancient regions were completely destroyed.","Only seventy-two ancient regions remained.","The Sea-Covering Demon God was one of those seventy-two.","The palace he had once built must still contain many treasures. Ancient demons were known for their greed, and they loved consuming treasures born from the heavens and earth—each one incomparably precious.","During the archaic era, the ancient regions were filled with treasures, most of which had been collected by the ancient demons. They consumed some, but left others behind.","Now, tens of thousands of years had passed, and there must still be undiscovered palaces or ancient lands remaining.","Everyone was extremely excited after hearing this.","An ancient demon’s palace.","It was an ancient demon’s palace!","Even if there were only a few treasures left untouched by the demons, they would be more than enough for them to use.","After all, treasures born from the heavens and earth during the archaic era were now priceless.","Excitement, however, quickly gave way to hesitation.","Zhen Xian Wuhou spoke bluntly, “Xue Yang, don’t take this the wrong way, but since you’ve discovered an ancient demon’s palace, why not tell your elder brother and let him open it? Wouldn’t all the treasures end up being yours? Don’t tell me you don’t want to rely on your brother. Matters related to an ancient demon’s palace aren’t just about pride!”","Although his words were straightforward, they hit the nail on the head.","“That’s very direct!” True Lord Xue Yang wasn’t offended. He responded immediately, “Because this ancient demon’s palace is inside the Dual-Faced God’s Domain!”","“......”","As soon as he said this, everyone froze.","Even Ziyu Fairy’s expression darkened, and she snapped angrily, “Xue Yang, you didn’t mention this earlier! Are you trying to ruin my reputation?”","“An ancient demon’s palace, with such a huge opportunity, and you say I’m ruining your reputation? If you’re too scared, just forget I mentioned it. We can disband right now!” True Lord Xue Yang’s tone was firm. Otherwise, he wouldn’t be the brother of Yang Dingtian.","Old Man Tian Can was the first to snap out of it, quickly stepping in to mediate. “Ziyu, don’t be too angry. This is indeed a huge matter, and I believe Brother Xue Yang didn’t mean any harm. As the saying goes, ‘Fortune favors the bold.’ Once an ancient demon’s palace is discovered, the treasures inside will be worth a fortune. With such a huge opportunity, Brother Xue Yang is willing to take the risk and bring us along, which means the risk must be considerable. If there were no risks, why would he seek our help?”","Although his explanation was weak, everyone couldn’t help but feel tempted.","Of course, they were merely tempted.","No one dared to speak up.","After all, this was the Dual-Faced God’s Domain.","It was the territory of the Dual-Faced Buddha. Forget about them, even Dao Lords wouldn’t dare cause trouble there.","Jian Wushuang had heard of the Dual-Faced Buddha before, and knew of his ruthlessness and explosive temper. However, he hadn’t expected it to unnerve everyone present to this extent.","Ziyu Fairy immediately sent him a message, “Wushuang, I don’t think you should get involved in this mess. I’ll arrange for you to enter a secluded courtyard in my residence. If they do decide to venture into the Dual-Faced God’s Domain, you’ll stay there temporarily. Once everything is over, you’ll be free to leave. I hope you understand!”","Jian Wushuang understood. She wasn’t trying to imprison him—it was just that the situation was too serious. If he didn’t go along, they might even kill him to ensure his silence. Allowing him to stay at her residence was already quite courteous."]},{"number":6376,"title":"Chapter 6376: Ancient Demon Palace","paragraphs":["Chapter 6376: Ancient Demon Palace","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang naturally didn’t get angry, nor did he blame the other party, because he hadn’t planned on refusing.","The reason he got close to Ziyu was to find an opportunity through her to explore the Ancient Domain.","Finding his own path required both risk and luck. Although this place might not be of much help to him, it was still better than nothing.","Moreover, he discovered that his body needed to constantly devour treasures, or it would gradually weaken.","This was one of the major drawbacks of the Realm Beast physique.","It required continuous absorption of energy, and this massive expenditure was something he couldn’t currently afford without treasures.","In the future, when he became an Immortal, the consumption of divine power would also need to be replenished with treasures.","That’s why he came here with her.","Originally, he thought it would be a minor opportunity or adventure, but to his surprise, luck was on his side. True Lord Xueyang had discovered the Ancient Demon Palace—a chance so immense that even Dao Lords would be tempted!","Encountering such a great opportunity was something he, a Nascent Soul stage cultivator, had to treasure.","However, as a Nascent Soul cultivator, it wasn’t appropriate for him to speak out in front of everyone, so he remained silent, though his expression showed his astonishment.","This prompted Ziyu Fairy to send him a concerned voice transmission.","Though he wanted to go, he didn’t want to seem overly eager, so he replied cautiously, “Fairy Ziyu, what do you think about this? If you go, I will go too!”","Jian Wushuang spoke with a serious and solemn tone this time.","Earlier, in Ziyu’s eyes, he had always appeared carefree and unruly, but now, with this demeanor, his words warmed her heart. Still, she continued to advise him, “I can tell your strength isn’t weak, and you must have encountered great opportunities yourself. I understand that you’re stuck at the threshold of immortality, but there’s no need to take unnecessary risks. You’ve cultivated for a short time, so you might not know what kind of place the Dual-Faced God Palace is. It’s a living hell. Even if we aren’t discovered by the strong cultivators of the Dual-Faced God Palace, reaching the Ancient Demon Palace that True Lord Xueyang mentioned is incredibly dangerous. If we’re caught, no one will be able to save us. You’re still young; there’s no need to push yourself so hard. Why not stay at my residence for now? After this, I can introduce you to a super existence among the immortals, and I’m sure you’ll become an Immortal Zhen Xian in no time!”","Her words were spoken with sincerity and responsibility, and Jian Wushuang was moved.","If he were an ordinary person, this would be an incredibly tempting offer. To be introduced to a Seventh or even Eighth-step Immortal Zhen Xian—many Nascent Soul cultivators would dream of such an opportunity but never have the means to attain it. Yet, Ziyu, whom he had only known for a short time, was willing to make that connection for him. She was undoubtedly a benefactor in his life.","But he was Jian Wushuang!","He wasn’t an ordinary person!","“Fairy, there’s no need to persuade me further. I understand the gravity of this situation. If True Lord Xueyang dares to go, I’m not much weaker than him, so I can naturally go as well. If I want to become a super strong cultivator, I can’t afford to be timid!” Jian Wushuang’s tone was firm.","These were words from his heart. To become a super strong cultivator, one couldn’t fear danger.","Even if the road ahead had a ninety-nine percent chance of leading to death, one still had to walk it.","If one succeeded, they would naturally surpass ninety-nine percent of their peers.","Danger and reward were proportional.","His exchange with Ziyu Fairy reflected the feelings of everyone present.","At present, only True Lord Wu Hou expressed his willingness to go.","The others hesitated.","Old Man Tian Can was speaking with a lot of flowery words, but his meaning was clear—he was probing the risks involved and questioning the details of the Ancient Demon Palace.","Just because True Lord Xue Yang said it existed didn’t mean it truly did.","After all, it was the domain of the Two-Faced God Palace, ruled by the Two-Faced Buddha. If the Ancient Demon Palace really existed, how could it be True Lord Xue Yang who discovered it?","How did he discover it, anyway?","If this were an ordinary place, no one would ask, because everyone had secrets!","But this time, it was different. It concerned their very lives.","Once discovered, they would undoubtedly perish.","At that time, no one would be able to save them.","The Two-Faced Buddha was a superpower on par with True Lord Xue Yang’s elder brother.","And the key issue was that this man was notoriously fickle, showing no regard for anyone. Even True Lord Xue Yang would not escape if things went wrong.","“Young friend Xue Yang, I think we need to deliberate more on this matter. It’s too risky. Without substantial reward, I believe entering would be nothing short of courting death!” Old Man Tian Can continued to debate the benefits.","If there were valuable treasures within, he would naturally be willing to take the risk.","For example, if there were an opportunity that could allow him to make five strides forward on the Origin Source path and become a Dao Lord, that would indeed be worth the risk.","Jian Wushuang was also waiting for his response.","The treasures on him weren’t many, and now he had to think about the future. Having just entered the Ancient Territory, he indeed needed to take some risks to gather treasures for security.","Though he had obtained many treasures in the Crimson Eye Realm, few were of immediate use.","Most of True Lord Ye Huo’s treasures had been given to Xiang Yang and the others. As for the Life Seeds, he had consumed only a few, while most had been given to Jiang Ni.","Jiang Ni was the daughter of Jiang Shang, which was an undeniable fact.","Moreover, this Jiang Shang was the Jiang Shang of the Heavenly Maiden Time-Space.","Although their memories were shared, their cultivation abilities were different.","The Jiang Shang of the Heavenly Maiden had also walked the path of life.","This path of life also stemmed from the Divine Willow Tree.","Therefore, Jiang Ni, influenced by her mother on a life level, had gained the most from absorbing the Life Seeds. Naturally, the majority of the Life Seeds were given to her.","Jiu Chen and Xiang Yang were quite ordinary.","Here, “ordinary” referred to their talents.","Fortunately, after Xiang Yang entered the Nascent Soul stage, he recovered the original inheritance from his soul’s consciousness. Now, following his previous path, things were progressing smoothly. He came from a prestigious family, and during his time in the mortal realm, he had access to the finest resources. However, now he seemed to have regressed, not even as strong as he had been during his mortal years.","As for Jiu Chen, he was even worse off. Originally a spirit body, though he now had a physical body, he lacked cultivation experience and relied entirely on Jian Wushuang’s support.","This old fellow, if Jian Wushuang didn’t get him some benefits, even he wouldn’t be able to stand it.","It must be known that Jiu Chen had traveled to nine great worlds.","These worlds weren’t mortal realms but otherworldly dimensions.","The final world was in the Heavenly Fire Domain of the Ancient Territory.","The first eight worlds were all in different dimensions. With Jiu Chen’s experience, Jian Wushuang could later venture into these worlds to gather treasures.","Now, his physical body could unleash a power surge a thousandfold, making it incredibly strong. But it still required treasures for maintenance, or else the life level would degrade.","That would affect his combat strength.","Currently, he relied entirely on his physical combat prowess.","Although his Ultimate Sword Dao had been acknowledged by the Origin Source, it still fell short compared to the body of a Realm Beast, as the Origin Source’s amplification would only come into play after achieving immortality. For now, his combat strength was quite weak.","However, his Extreme Dao remained as formidable as ever, already allowing him to grasp the mysteries of all things and maintain his strength.","What he lacked now were physical treasures. As for improving his Origin Source, he hadn’t even found a new path yet, so there was no rush."]},{"number":6377,"title":"Chapter 6377: Agreed","paragraphs":["Chapter 6377: Agreed","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Extreme Dao, Sword Dao, what will be the next one? Infinity?”","He had a specific direction in mind, but how to take the next step was something he still didn’t know.","This was the bottleneck—knowing exactly what one wanted but not knowing how to strive toward it.","Some people got stuck at this stage for countless years, fighting desperately for ages without finding the answer.","Jian Wushuang’s comprehension had surpassed his peak from the past, several times stronger. Perhaps he would succeed soon, but no one could say for sure.","While pondering over his own matters, he also listened to the conversations of those around him.","Time passed quickly. The group discussed for an entire day and night.","In fact, it was just a few seasoned veterans trying to wear down True Lord Xue Yang until they had coaxed every detail out of him. Only then did they make a decision.","This was expected. True Lord Xue Yang hadn’t wanted to say too much at first, but the chances were the same for everyone going.","Once everything was revealed, his advantage would be gone.","But if he kept quiet, no one would be willing to go with him.","Even his own brother wouldn’t agree to him going to the Twin-Faced God’s Mansion.","That was why he hadn’t told Yang Dingtian about it.","One was righteous, the other was evil—Yang Dingtian and the Twin-Faced Buddha had always been at odds.","For his own brother to go to the Twin-Faced God’s Mansion was, in Yang Dingtian’s eyes, akin to seeking death.","The Ancient Demon Palace was in the Twin-Faced God’s Mansion, and even Yang Dingtian himself couldn’t access it.","Ordinary people could disguise themselves and possibly sneak into the mansion undetected.","But if Yang Dingtian tried, he would surely be discovered.","That was the reason why True Lord Xue Yang hadn’t sought Yang Dingtian’s help.","He was proud, but not to the point of being arrogantly self-delusional.","If the Ancient Demon Palace wasn’t located in the Twin-Faced God’s Mansion, he would have chosen to tell his brother, letting Yang Dingtian go there personally. Then, even if they had to split it fifty-fifty or seventy-thirty, it would still be cooperation, protecting his dignity while helping his brother, earning the latter’s approval.","But the problem was that the Ancient Demon Palace happened to be inside the Twin-Faced God’s Mansion.","When he first discovered this, he had been devastated.","He had, of course, never been to the Twin-Faced God’s Mansion, but he had obtained an Ancient Demon Token—a personal jade pendant of the Sea-Overturning Demon God. It contained a map and the exact location of the Ancient Demon Palace, and with the jade, he could enter.","However, to enter the Ancient Demon Palace, one needed a bloodline imprint.","In other words, the aura had to match.","No one could do this—only Special Life Forms could.","Yet True Lord Xue Yang had found, through various records, that aside from the main entrance, the Ancient Demon Palace had a special passage. This passage had been used by the Ancient Demon’s subordinates for their daily duties and maintenance of the palace.","This passage could accommodate four Zhen Xian and three cultivators at the Mahayana stage.","It did not require a bloodline imprint, nor the Ancient Demon Token.","So his token was effectively useless.","This meant that he no longer held an advantage, and by the time everyone entered through the special passage, the treasures inside would be won purely by individual ability.","Once he had laid everything bare, the crippled elder and Fairy Ziyu also agreed one after the other. The other two Four-Step Zhen Xian decided to agree as well.","After all, the temptation was simply too great.","Even if the Twin-Faced God’s Mansion was hell itself, they still had to venture into it.","“Since everyone is in agreement, let’s each begin our preparations now! But remember, before we leave, we must announce that we’re going into seclusion. For this, we’ll need Fairy Ziyu’s help!” True Lord Xue Yang’s gaze shifted to the main seat.","The Ziyu Immortal Fairy let out a faint smile with her crimson lips, her voice filled with charm as she said, “Rest assured, I will arrange your caves, but when the time comes, you all must send in an avatar. You should do things thoroughly, right?”","“Naturally!” Everyone nodded in agreement without objection.","Once the date was set, Ziyu Immortal Fairy brought out an Oath Stone, and everyone stepped forward to swear their blood oaths one by one.","The oath was simple: they must not reveal this conversation.","Inside the Twin-faced Divine Palace, they must not attack one another.","However, after entering the Ancient Demon Palace, the oath would be lifted.","This oath was relatively lenient, without much restraint.","Once inside the Ancient Demon Palace, everything would depend on one’s own abilities.","This point disadvantaged True Lord Xue Yang the most, but he still accepted it. At the very least, regarding the Ancient Demon Palace, he knew much more than everyone else.","For instance, he knew where certain treasures within the Ancient Demon Palace were stored, how to access some hidden chambers, and other similar information.","But that was the extent of his advantage.","Compared to Tian Can and the others, it wasn’t much of an edge.","Tian Can had brought along his own disciple and was incredibly strong, so his chances were high.","However, among those present, Ziyu Immortal Fairy remained the most secure.","Two Four-step Zhen Xian and Jian Wushuang were on her side.","Ziyu Immortal Fairy herself was only a Four-step Zhen Xian, but she had a vast array of treasures. Her Origin Source Dao was powerful, and her Divine Eye inheritance, obtained from the Second Sequence, had now been cultivated to the fourth level. She was close to perfecting the fifth level, making her strength comparable to that of Tian Can and Wuhou True Immortal.","She was the core figure in this operation.","Whether it was someone as cunning as Old Man Tian Can or someone as cold-hearted as Wuhou True Immortal, they had to tread carefully around this female immortal.","The same was true for True Lord Xue Yang.","Jian Wushuang might have appeared carefree on the surface, but deep down, he wasn’t that concerned.","However, he remembered Ziyu Immortal Fairy’s kindness.","Having been in the world for many years, he had encountered plenty of people.","Many people’s characters and motives could be discerned from a simple conversation.","Take Old Man Tian Can, for example. He was dangerous and had no bottom line. The moment danger struck, he’d be the first to run.","Then there was Wuhou True Immortal. He was rigid and unyielding, which was both his strength and his weakness. Being teamed up with someone like him could easily get one killed, as his actions were not as cunning as Tian Can’s. However, in battle, Wuhou was somewhat reliable.","Finally, there was Ziyu Immortal Fairy, someone who could navigate every situation.","Those who didn’t like her would consider her opportunistic, clinging to power and wealth without any principles.","But those who admired her would see her as loyal and righteous, always genuinely helping those around her.","Moreover, being a female immortal garnered her considerable goodwill among her peers.","This was why True Lord Xue Yang had chosen Ziyu Immortal Fairy to gather the group—he trusted her.","Jian Wushuang had encountered many similar figures.","In the end, actions spoke louder than motives. It wasn’t about what lay in someone’s heart but what they did.","After the gathering, Ziyu Immortal Fairy did not keep her so-called trusted companions, thus avoiding suspicion from both Tian Can and True Lord Xue Yang. This also made her seem open and transparent to her allies.","Jian Wushuang chose not to leave and stayed at the residence.","He didn’t have much to prepare. Being intangible and invisible, he could conceal himself so that no one could find him.","Unless someone sealed the space and launched a wide-range attack.","Moreover, he didn’t bother preparing life-saving items.","If entering the Twin-faced Divine Palace threatened his life, then his Realm Beast’s physical body would be too worthless.","He had never regarded immortals as a real threat.","Back in the Great Division, as a Yan Immortal, he could thrash even a Grand Yan Immortal.","He had even slain a Grand Yan Immortal."]},{"number":6378,"title":"Chapter 6378: Nine Revolutions of Divine Eyes","paragraphs":["Chapter 6378: Nine Revolutions of Divine Eyes","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Based on his strength conversion, a Nine Revolution Grand Yan Immortal was equivalent to a Five-Step True Immortal.","A Nine-Turn Grand Yan Immortal was the same as a Nine-Step True Immortal.","Above that would be a Dao Lord.","However, when he was in the Grand Division of the Da Si Domain, his physical body had been quite ordinary. While it was considered perfect in the mundane universe, it was far less powerful in the Original Universe’s Great Si Region.","Even back then, with just his ultimate swordsmanship, he had managed to defeat opponents above his level.","Now, he possessed not only the Ultimate Sword Dao but also the Extreme Dao.","Additionally, he had the body of a Realm Beast and the willpower of one.","His combat strength had improved tremendously since then.","Even without the Wanjie Sword, he could still easily defeat Immortal True Immortals who were above his level.","Though the Extreme Dao had not fully evolved into the Starry Sky, he could still harness a portion of the power of all things to amplify himself.","Moreover, with the body of a Realm Beast, he could briefly unleash strength up to ten million times its usual power.","The physical strength of his body was that of a ten-million-fold Great Perfection.","Even True Immortals would tremble before him.","Furthermore, his powerful Realm Beast consciousness could combine with the Eye of the Candle Dragon to perform devastating mental attacks.","He didn’t lack trump cards—rather, he had too many, and many of them remained unused.","Naturally, he didn’t need external items for survival.","What he needed now were external resources to strengthen his foundation.","His current foundation was too weak, which made it impossible for him to utilize the micro-universe within the Grey Flask.","Even if he entered the Grey Flask and devoured the energy from a micro-universe furiously, he still wouldn’t be able to shake the Origin Source of the micro-universe.","Otherwise, he wouldn’t have needed to take any risks.","He could have simply sat back and continuously absorbed energy from the Grey Flask without ever exhausting it.","“Nine Prison Command!”","With a thought, he summoned this treasure, which was on par with the Grey Flask in value.","Even with just a slight comprehension of it, he had already become deeply astonished by the Divine Eye secret technique.","The Divine Eye secret technique was even more powerful than his Eternal Transformation.","That senior brother’s strength definitely surpassed his own.","Although his Eternal Transformation had not yet reached its peak, at his strongest, his true body could barely use the ultimate form of Eternal Transformation.","There was still more potential for him to develop, but by then, his need for greater combat strength had diminished. Across the entire Realm God Continent, there was no one who posed a threat to him. So, he had stopped improving his combat strength and shifted his focus elsewhere. He parted ways with Hui Qing and Wu Zuo, embarking on his own path of Tribulation.","Had he continued developing, he might have discovered another path.","But that was a matter for another time.","The unique aspect of the Divine Eye secret technique was that not all of its burning power came from oneself.","Wei Jiu Xian was the perfect example—he could burn through the entire power of the Crimson Eye Realm.","That was the reason for his immense strength. Of course, the life seed left by Jiang Shang was the key factor.","Yet, this couldn’t hide the fact that he was a heaven-defying existence in the Mortal Realm.","When he first heard about the Secret Art of the Divine Eye, he already felt it was extraordinary. Now, having obtained the Nine Prison Medallion left behind by his senior brother from the Divine Fire Hall, what he had comprehended from the complete Secret Art of the Divine Eye far surpassed what he had initially heard.","The Secret Art of the Divine Eye originated before the first fragmentation of the Realm God Continent.","If one were to trace it back, it would even go as far as the Starry Sky.","The legacy that was left behind wasn’t only confined to this world.","There were traces in the Starry Sky as well.","But he had never heard of it, perhaps because it was not very noticeable in the vast Starry Sky.","Or maybe someone had destroyed it.","After all, the Secret Art of the Divine Eye was far too heaven-defying.","It was different from a Universe Master burning their own universe. A Universe Master at their peak could burn the entire space-time continuum to enhance their battle strength, leaving the Starry Sky to recover the lost power.","If the Starry Sky had an owner, they would never allow such a secret art to exist.","This was Jian Wushuang’s true belief.","The complete Secret Art of the Divine Eye was divided into nine phases.","All the sequence inheritances in the Ancient Domain World came from practitioners of this secret art.","Whether it was the First Sequence or the Fifth Sequence, it was all a matter of the practitioner’s strength.","For example, once a practitioner of the Secret Art of the Divine Eye reached the fifth phase, they could leave behind the First Sequence’s inheritance hall.","A practitioner at the first phase could leave behind a Fifth Sequence inheritance after becoming a Monarch.","However, to leave behind a First Sequence inheritance, one would need the strength of a Universe Master and to have reached the fifth phase of the secret art.","This explained why First Sequence inheritances were so rare.","On the other hand, stronger inheritance sanctuaries were entirely different.","These were left behind by the Divine Eye Clan and were far more powerful and complete than sequence inheritances.","Any expert of the Divine Eye Clan who left behind such a sanctuary must have at least reached the sixth phase of the Secret Art, likely having the strength of a Universe God.","A sanctuary left behind by a Universe God carried immense value.","The Ancient Domain World was too small for such a sanctuary to appear. It was no wonder that the Sacred Lord could overthrow the rule of the Ancient Court in such a short time.","However, the Sacred Lord had taken a rather extreme path.","He wasn’t a member of the Divine Eye Clan, yet he wanted to walk their path.","In Jian Wushuang’s eyes, this person was doomed to fail sooner or later.","From what he had heard and seen, there was no evidence that anyone from the Divine Eye Clan still existed.","It was a clear sign that the clan had been wiped out, and that senior brother had also perished.","How could such a powerful clan, with such a heaven-defying secret art, have been wiped out?","Even in the Starry Sky, who had the capability to annihilate so many people without leaving a trace?","Moreover, it was clear that the Secret Art of the Divine Eye had been intentionally placed here.","The world he had entered was likely a large fragment left behind after the Realm God Continent had shattered.","The entire inheritance of the Divine Eye had been concentrated in this world.","And it was no coincidence that Master Xuan Yi had intentionally brought him here, and his senior brother had handed over the complete Secret Art of the Divine Eye. What did all this mean?","“If the Secret Art of the Divine Eye is forbidden in the Starry Sky, then by cultivating the complete version of it, wouldn’t I...”","No doubt, trouble awaited him once he left.","But with the help of the Star Spirits back then, could that relationship protect him?","He pondered deeply on the connection between the Starry Sky, Master Xuan Yi, and his senior brother.","First, the creator of the Starry Sky was still alive, and he was, in fact, a Realm Beast.","He was the most accomplished of all Realm Beasts.","Back when the Starry Sky was created, the power of countless Realm Beasts had been absorbed into it.","The strongest entity in the Starry Sky was undoubtedly the creator himself.","Then came the power that couldn’t be fully absorbed, which had overflowed.","The Twelve Star Spirits!","These individuals maintained the entire Starry Sky. Since the Secret Art of the Divine Eye was forbidden, there was no way he could cultivate it.","His relationship with Vis wasn’t strong enough to allow him to act without consequences.","“Infinite, formless, Realm Beast?” His brows furrowed as he suddenly thought of something.","It was the issue of the limit.","The Void, or the Infinite Lands, had no rules, and one could grow without any boundaries, as long as they had the potential.","That meant they still needed to absorb power.","The power of the Void.","These Realm Beasts were said to have no limits, but even they would reach a peak.","There was also one other thing he hadn’t given much thought to at the time.","The overflow of power from the Starry Sky had created the Twelve Star Spirits.","Logically, if Realm Beasts had no limits, how could there be an overflow of power from the Starry Sky?","Could it be that the creator of the Starry Sky had already reached his limit?","This contradiction left him perplexed.","“The Secret Art of the Divine Eye can burn power that doesn’t belong to you. The Starry Sky has a limit, but Realm Beasts don’t!” he muttered to himself, going over these rules, until his thoughts finally drifted to his own situation."]},{"number":6379,"title":"Chapter 6379: The Foreshadowing of the Past","paragraphs":["Chapter 6379: The Foreshadowing of the Past","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang suddenly opened his eyes, exclaiming excitedly, “I understand!”","His excitement instantly caught the attention of the few people inside the Nine Prison Pagoda.","“What do you understand?”","“Did Senior Wushuang grasp the Origin Source?”","“Heh, how long has he been alive? It’s already heaven-defying that he managed to reach the peak of the Great Perfection stage. Is he planning to prove his Dao and ascend to immortality right on the spot?”","Now that everything became clear to him, Jian Wushuang had no interest in explaining. He immediately closed his eyes, shutting himself off from everything around him.","At the same time, he also sealed the Nine Prison Pagoda, preventing those inside from hearing anything else he had to say.","He had spoken out of sheer excitement just moments earlier. Thankfully, he hadn’t revealed what he had realized.","Because at that moment, it became crystal clear to him what Teacher Xuan Yi’s true intentions were when he entered this world.","The groundwork laid on the Realm God Continent had prepared him to enter the Realm King Divine World and absorb the majority of Morosa’s power.","This was due to his extraordinarily powerful consciousness. But why was it so strong?","“The Skysight Heavenly Chessboard!”","Back then, he had absorbed all the Origin Source contained within the Skysight Heavenly Chessboard. These Origins were rich in soul essence, which strengthened his own soul.","With a powerful soul came a powerful consciousness. As a result, within the Realm King Divine World, his combat strength had already surpassed the Nine-Star Universe Gods.","On top of that, he had absorbed such an immense amount of Morosa’ power.","Shortly after leaving the Realm King Divine World, he had entered this new world.","Through the will of the Realm Beast, he had fused with the Realm Beast’s body.","Finally, he had acquired the secret technique of the Divine Eye Clan.","All of these things had been carefully arranged in advance. He should have realized this much earlier.","Everything had been preparing him for the cultivation of the Divine Eye secret technique, or perhaps it was all meant to break through his limits.","In the Starry Sky, what did it matter how strong you were?","Why was it that only Star Spirits dared to venture out?","Because Star Spirits, in essence, weren’t all that different from Realm Beasts. Or rather, due to some issue with the Starry Sky, Star Spirits couldn’t stay away for too long.","But he was different. Now, all that was left was for him to obtain an Origin Source similar to the Realm Beast’s.","Once he succeeded, he would be just like the Realm Beasts, able to survive and even cultivate in the Void.","This had all been guided by Teacher Xuan Yi. From that memory fragment, it was clear to him that the place where the battles were fought wasn’t in the Starry Sky but in the Void.","“I should have realized this sooner!” He sighed internally.","Indeed, thinking about it now, it felt somewhat like an afterthought.","But it wasn’t too late.","He hadn’t given up on the Divine Eye Secret Technique, and he still had to cultivate it. However, whether or not he could use it in the Starry Sky, he had to be cautious.","After all, the Divine Eye clan had perished. Senior Brother Ghost Eye might still be alive, but the likelihood was that he wasn’t in the Starry Sky.","It was more probable he was in the Void.","Back then, being able to participate in that battle indicated that they were on a path similar to his current one — the path of disorder.","Void and disorder!","“If the large-scale burning of the Divine Eye Secret Technique is used in the land of disorder, I can’t even begin to imagine the consequences. During that battle, I didn’t see anyone else using the Divine Eye technique. Now that I’ve started cultivating it, perhaps it’s a method that could change the future!”","He hadn’t thought about it much before, which led to his delayed realization. This time, he dared to think boldly.","Perhaps in this lifetime, he had been reborn, and his return was meant to cultivate the powerful Divine Eye Secret Technique.","The others might also cultivate it.","By then, their strength would increase significantly.","But that wasn’t enough. He couldn’t rely solely on the Divine Eye technique. After all, it was a technique created by someone else. He needed to create his own pinnacle secret technique.","It all depended on how far the Eternal Transformation could take him. If the path of divine power couldn’t be traveled for long, he would switch to another.","He couldn’t forget that memory of how he had fallen.","Failure wasn’t an option!","With that thought, he seized every moment and began delving into the Divine Eye Secret Technique.","The first rotation corresponded to the first level of the Nine Prison Pagoda.","At present, he had only mastered the third layer of the first rotation.","This was roughly equivalent to half of the fifth sequence.","However, this was the complete secret technique of the Divine Eye clan.","The inheritance of the fifth sequence could help a cultivator achieve the effect of the First Eye, but there were varying degrees of strength.","His one rotation was worth a hundred of others’.","While comprehending the Divine Eye Secret Technique, he also probed the Nine Prison Pagoda.","As of now, he hadn’t fully grasped the pagoda’s specific function.","“It has the word ‘prison’ in its name. Could there be some terrifying beings imprisoned within this tower?”","He pondered for a moment. It was a possibility, but since there was nothing on the first level, and no threats, it didn’t matter. When he opened the second level, even if there were terrifying entities imprisoned, he could just kill them.","If he could open the second level, he would be capable of killing whatever was inside.","For a whole month, he focused entirely on cultivating the Divine Eye Secret Technique.","During this time, he didn’t pay much attention to the matters of the Origin Source, as they wouldn’t be useful in the short term. He concentrated on the Divine Eye Secret Technique, and his First Eye had reached the perfect stage.","He wasn’t sure if his speed was considered fast or slow.","He also found himself jumping between comprehending the third, fifth, and even the ninth rotations.","Although he could understand them, they weren’t useful at his current realm.","This explained why some could directly comprehend the first sequence, which corresponded to the fifth rotation.","Those inheritors, after all, had only grasped a small part.","If he had started learning the Divine Eye Secret Technique in the Inheritance Holy Land, he would have avoided many detours.","The Holy Master who had drawn the Inheritance Holy Land to him had merged two sequences, meaning he had cultivated two of the first five rotations.","These two rotations were likely very close to each other.","This created a massive resonance, drawing an Inheritance Holy Land.","The descent of the Holy Land signified that within this part of the world, there was a high possibility someone would cultivate to the sixth rotation.","Although the Divine Eye Secret Technique could be cultivated in jumps, the first five rotations were simple and not particularly difficult. In fact, there wasn’t much of a threshold.","But merging them all was extremely challenging, much harder than becoming a Universe God.","Thus, in the ancient domain, the strongest local experts at most merged two sequences, meaning they had cultivated two of the first five rotations.","If one could merge three rotations, they could then proceed to cultivate the sixth.","In this way, out of the nine rotations, four would have been mastered.","There would be hope to open a Holy Land and become a Universe God.","Moreover, their strength would be exceedingly formidable.","If one wished to cultivate to the seventh rotation, they would need to master four of the first five rotations.","To reach the eighth, perfect mastery of the first seven rotations was required.","This difficulty surpassed becoming a Universe God by a wide margin.","There was also a key factor: the bloodline of the Divine Eye clan. Only by altering one’s bloodline could one cultivate to the eighth rotation.","Jian Wushuang, however, didn’t face this requirement. He had the formless and invisible body of a Realm Beast, allowing him to transform into any race at will.","Naturally, he didn’t need to worry about his bloodline.","As for the ninth rotation, he wasn’t sure of the difficulty because not even the Divine Eye clan’s cultivators could achieve it.","This was because Senior Brother Ghost Eye had left no inheritance for the ninth rotation.","That token was something Ghost Eye had specifically left for him.","Perhaps he had also left it for others — those chosen by Teacher Xuan Yi.","After all, with Ghost Eye around, there were bound to be other senior brothers, senior sisters, junior brothers, and junior sisters, and perhaps even a teacher’s wife."]},{"number":6380,"title":"Chapter 6380: Controlling the Nine Prison Pagoda","paragraphs":["Chapter 6380: Controlling the Nine Prison Pagoda","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","On the sacred mountain in his memory, there were many powerful auras.","He guarded the base of the mountain. Although he had slain many strong intruders, his own strength might not have been the greatest, or perhaps, among Xuan Yi’s many disciples, he was not that noticeable?","“This won’t do!”","Deep down, he had always believed he was Xuan Yi’s only disciple, and thus naturally the strongest.","Now, however, he realized that Xuan Yi had more than just one disciple, and that he wasn’t even the strongest among his peers. A hint of jealousy arose in his heart.","“This old man! He secretly took on more disciples behind my back, and it seems like there’s quite a few of them too. No way, I must become the most outstanding one among them!” he swore silently to himself.","At the same time, he began to wonder about the identity of the Prophet. Could the Prophet also be one of his master’s disciples?","In his memories, the Prophet’s combat power wasn’t particularly overwhelming, yet the Prophet gave off the most mysterious vibe.","Perhaps they weren’t in a master-disciple relationship.","At first, the Prophet somewhat resembled Xuan Yi, as both shared a similarly mysterious aura, but later in his memory, he realized that the Prophet had also been blocking those top-tier experts at the foot of the mountain, confirming they were not the same person.","But their auras were strikingly similar—perhaps they were brothers, or fellow disciples. Of course, it was also possible that the Prophet was Xuan Yi’s illegitimate child.","While his mind raced with wild guesses, a voice suddenly came from inside the Nine Prison Pagoda, sounding anxious.","“Jian Wushuang, are you trying to murder us?”","“I can’t feel my breath anymore!!!”","“Senior Wushuang...!”","Jian Wushuang was startled by these words and quickly opened the Nine Prison Pagoda, rushing in at once.","It was only then that he noticed the first layer of the Nine Prison Pagoda had completely transformed.","What used to be a pale, barren world now featured mountains and rivers, resembling a black-and-white landscape painting.","However, the aura had also changed.","Originally, the flow of time inside the pagoda had been the same as the outside world, as Jian Wushuang hadn’t yet figured out how to manipulate time. The energy within had also matched the external world, since he could infuse divine power into the pagoda.","Thus, people like Xiang Yang could cultivate inside.","But now, the energy within had rapidly depleted. It was no longer a paradise for cultivation, but more like a prison.","After all, the Nine Prison Pagoda was originally a prison, so this wasn’t entirely surprising.","He glanced at the three people inside. While they were unharmed, they could no longer train here.","“I’ve only just gained control of this place and am not quite familiar with it yet. Did I scare you, little Jiang Ni?” Jian Wushuang said kindly, his demeanor that of an elder.","Jiang Ni felt a bit embarrassed, her cheeks flushing slightly, as she softly replied, “No, it’s just that the sudden change took me by surprise. I didn’t expect Senior to have such extraordinary abilities!”","“Just a small trick!” Jian Wushuang said, his hands behind his back, pretending not to care.","Xiang Yang and Immortal Jiu Chen didn’t refute him, instead asking about the purpose of the Nine Prison Pagoda.","It couldn’t be that the pagoda was just for admiring the scenery, could it?","Jian Wushuang then realized he hadn’t yet fully activated the pagoda. With a thought, he entered the core of the Nine Prison Pagoda, where an ancient aura immediately surged toward him.","In his mind, a giant eye appeared.","The eye was filled with countless colors, and what surprised him most was that it had ten pupils.","In the central pupil, it seemed as if there was an entire starry sky.","Surrounding it were nine smaller pupils, giving off an incredibly mysterious vibe.","But that wasn’t the most astonishing part—the key was that from the eye, he felt a trace of the Star Spirit’s power.","He didn’t even think twice before his consciousness manifested in the mental world, where he respectfully bowed and said, “Junior Jian Wushuang greets the Star Spirit!”","“Little one, your reaction is quick!” The voice from the enormous eye had no form or color, yet it resonated in his mind.","It carried an aura of invincibility across the Starry Sky.","Jian Wushuang lowered his head, not daring to look up, but he could tell that the other party bore no ill intent. He cautiously asked, “Star Spirit, may I ask if you’ve come for the Nine Prison Pagoda?”","He had encountered the Star Spirit before. Back then, Weiss had stayed in his Origin Source Universe for a while. Otherwise, the first time he saw such an existence, his consciousness would likely have struggled to adapt. After all, the being was on a much higher level than him.","Fortunately, he now had a Realm Beast body and the will of a Realm Beast. With his newfound understanding of the Origin Source of the Realm Beast, he would one day be of the same lineage as the Star Spirit. When that time came, this sense of distance would disappear.","Even now, however, meeting the Star Spirit gave him the feeling of being in a completely different world.","“Do you know who crafted this Nine Prison Pagoda back in the day?”","Jian Wushuang froze for a moment before replying without hesitation, “It was Senior Brother Ghost Eye!”","In the presence of the Star Spirit, there was no room for deception. This was the stark difference between being on different levels.","“Correct, but not entirely,” the massive eye pondered before saying, “Indeed, your senior brother forged the Nine Prison Pagoda to seal all the Gods, but later, he softened his stance.”","“To suppress the God Eye Clan?” Jian Wushuang was stunned.","Senior Brother Ghost Eye was himself a powerful figure of the God Eye Clan. How could he suppress his own people?","A thousand questions swirled in Jian Wushuang’s mind, but he didn’t dare ask them directly.","It was as though the enormous eye could see through his thoughts. “You may wonder why Ghost Eye would suppress his own clan. The truth is, deep down, you already know the answer. The power of the Starry Sky is finite. In time, even a Universe God would have to leave once reaching the Ninth Tribulation. The Realm God Continent is no different. Once someone becomes a Time and Space Lord, they too must leave and enter the Starry Sky. The Starry Sky follows the same principle: it doesn’t reject Star Gods but rejects those who burn the Starry Sky.”","“But do you know why these worlds have become so fragile?” The Star Spirit asked pointedly.","Jian Wushuang was momentarily at a loss for words, so he ventured a guess, “Could it be because they’ve been burned?”","“Yes, exactly. They were burned, but it happened a long time ago. Back then, the Realm God Continent had not yet been shattered. Your senior brother once fought a Time and Space God on the Realm God Continent, and he burned the Realm God Continent along with the four major Time and Space regions. Eventually, this drew the attention of the Realm Gods, leading to a sneak attack. At that time, the Realm God Continent was fragile, easily shattered by the Realm Beasts, which then invaded the Starry Sky!” As the Star Spirit spoke, its enormous eye flickered with a hint of sorrow and regret.","Jian Wushuang felt the same, realizing just how powerful his senior brother must have been back then, burning both the Realm God Continent and the four major Time and Space regions.","It was likely that during that era, the Realm God Continent was still able to house Time and Space Gods, marking its peak.","But the energy had been consumed, and the power that Ghost Eye Senior had used would never return to the Starry Sky. As a result, the Realm God Continent and the four major Time and Space regions were left weakened, never to recover.","It was then that the Realm Beasts attacked. Since the Realm God Continent had been burned, the Time and Space Gods couldn’t remain, and they all moved to the Starry Sky, leaving the Realm God Continent defenseless. Even its protective forces had been consumed, and the Realm Beasts shattered both the Realm God Continent and the four major Time and Space regions in one fell swoop."]},{"number":6381,"title":"Chapter 6381: Giant God Star Spirit","paragraphs":["Chapter 6381: Giant God Star Spirit","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang entered the Starry Sky.","“How many people must have died?” Jian Wushuang took a deep breath. Even he couldn’t begin to imagine.","One space-time dimension contained countless universes. A single continent was equivalent to countless space-times. But in an instant, everything was shattered.","One could only imagine the immense responsibility Ghost Eye Senior Brother had shouldered.","“Back then, he was just like you—full of ambition. He once encountered great fortune and never regarded the Realm God Continent as important, nor did he see the Starry Sky as the end. In the end, he made a terrible mistake, and the Divine Eye Clan was dragged down with him. But... they are all my children...”","At this point, the voice of the enormous Star Spirit trembled slightly.","Jian Wushuang was astonished and asked, “Your children?”","“I forgot to introduce myself. I come from the Starry Sky. I am the master of the Giant God Peak, one of the twelve star districts. The Divine Eye Clan is a race I created. Your Ghost Eye Senior Brother and every member of the Divine Eye Clan are my children!”","After hearing the introduction, Jian Wushuang first thought the other was being too polite. But then his eyes suddenly narrowed as he recalled what Weiss had once told him.","The Giant God!","The ancestor of the Giant God Clan was also a Star Spirit.","Giant God Peak was the ancestral land of the Giant God Clan.","And this enormous eye before him belonged to none other than that legendary Giant God Star Spirit?","Jian Wushuang was dumbfounded. This was the ancestor of the first clan of the Starry Sky—the Giant God Star Spirit!","Even the Divine Eye Clan was a creation of this being. The weight of this revelation hit him hard.","“You... you’re actually the Giant God Star Spirit? Forgive my lack of discernment, I failed to recognize your esteemed presence!” Jian Wushuang’s tone became even more respectful.","After all, he had grown up hearing stories about the Giant God Clan.","He had always been curious about what kind of figure the ancestor of the Giant God Clan was, and now he had seen it firsthand.","Humble, reserved, gentle, and approachable.","Not like Weiss, who loved to act all superior!","Though to be fair, Weiss was a master in his own right.","“Haha, no need to be so formal. In fact, I’ve seen you before. Back then, you even looked after my Giant God Clan members. This time, I hope you can take care of my Divine Eye Clan children as well!” There was a pleading glint in the Giant God Star Spirit’s eye.","Jian Wushuang, understanding the implications, felt uneasy.","His true form had only reached the peak of Universe God, and even as a Space-Time God, what could he do?","Yet here was a Star Spirit, asking for his help?","He hurriedly replied, “Star Spirit Lord, just tell me directly. Whether you want me to release the Divine Eye Clan members trapped in the Nine Prison Pagoda or the ones imprisoned in this world, I will not hesitate!”","In his view, if a Star Spirit was being so polite to him—especially one who was the ancestor of his Ghost Eye Senior Brother—he had to show respect.","Besides, he and Ghost Eye Senior Brother were fellow disciples under Master Xuan Yi, so naturally, they had to look out for one another.","Even if the Giant God Star Spirit hadn’t asked, he wouldn’t have harmed the Divine Eye Clan experts within the Pagoda. If it wasn’t too unreasonable, he had already planned to release them.","“If your Ghost Eye Senior Brother hadn’t softened, then indeed, all the Divine Eye Clan members should have been sealed inside the Nine Prison Pagoda. But alas, he was too soft-hearted. There isn’t a single Divine Eye Clan member in any of the nine levels of the Pagoda!” The Giant God Star Spirit’s voice carried regret.","It seemed as if he was both lamenting and blaming Ghost Eye for not following his advice—to suppress the Divine Eye Clan members in the Nine Prison Pagoda. At least then, they would have survived!","For a moment, Jian Wushuang couldn’t comprehend and asked in surprise, “Ghost Eye Senior Brother softened? Then where did the Divine Eye Clan go?”","A thousand thoughts raced through his mind. Could it be that Ghost Eye Senior Brother led the Divine Eye Clan in a rebellion?","Did they all escape the Starry Sky?","It was possible. Ghost Eye Senior Brother was strong enough in the chaotic region to protect his clan.","Moreover, the Divine Eye secret technique was perfectly suited for the chaotic region, allowing them to burn energy freely, as no one cared. Besides, the power in the chaotic region was infinite.","He had initially thought the downfall of the Divine Eye Clan was tied to the Nine Prison Pagoda, but now it seemed he had misunderstood.","However, the Giant God Star Spirit’s next words shattered all his assumptions.","“Dead!”","“I personally destroyed the Divine Eye Clan!”","The voice of the Great Divine Spirit trembled. He had destroyed his own children with his own hands.","He had slaughtered all the cultivators of the Divine Eye Clan.","Ghost Eye had severed all ties with him after that and left the Starry Sky.","When Jian Wushuang heard this explanation, he was utterly stunned.","He found it hard to believe and didn’t want to accept it.","The large eyeball in front of him, who always looked like a kind old man, had committed such a ruthless act?","Jian Wushuang took a deep breath, realizing he didn’t dare speak at this moment.","He was afraid the Great Divine Spirit might destroy him as well.","As the Great Divine Spirit recalled the event, his tone turned sorrowful. “But the Divine Eye Clan has revived in this world, relying on the Myriad Willow Divine Tree. They will soon make a comeback. This time, I hope you can give them a chance, let them enter the Nine Prison Pagoda, rather than killing them all!”","“What?”","Jian Wushuang wasn’t shocked about the revival of the Divine Eye Clan but rather about the Myriad Willow Divine Tree.","Hadn’t it been taken away by Weiss?","How had it appeared in this world again?","Seeing his confusion, the Great Divine Spirit patiently explained, “Young one, don’t you understand yet? You were chosen as a powerful warrior. The path ahead of you has long been laid out. On this path, you have Weiss helping you, your senior brother Ghost Eye, and even that mysterious Prophet. They are all aiding you!”","Jian Wushuang wasn’t foolish and quickly pieced everything together.","“Lord Spirit, was it you who slew that Realm Beast back then?” Jian Wushuang asked, pointing at his own body.","The Great Divine Spirit blinked his enormous eyes, silently confirming it.","Everything was just as the Great Divine Spirit had said.","His entry into this world had been arranged by the Prophet.","This world had been part of a plan devised by his senior brother Ghost Eye and Weiss.","The Myriad Willow Divine Tree had been thrown into this world, reviving the Divine Eye Clan. Ghost Eye had granted him the Realm Beast’s body and the Nine Prison Pagoda.","The implication was clear: even without the Great Divine Spirit, his task would still have been to suppress all the experts of the Divine Eye Clan.","And all of this had been premeditated by Ghost Eye and Weiss long ago.","The Prophet had merely been responsible for bringing him in.","The road was indeed paved for him, but if he hadn’t claimed the Realm Beast’s body back then, would he have ever had the chance to meet Master Xuan Yi again?","“Lord Spirit, I’m curious. Why was I chosen to suppress the revived Divine Eye Clan? If they were to be suppressed, why let them revive in the first place?”","This was his final question.","At the same time, a vague answer had already formed in his heart.","Just after he had mastered the first level of the Nine Prison Pagoda, the Great Divine Spirit had arrived, likely to clear his doubts.","“It’s simple. The revival of the Divine Eye Clan was to allow you to quickly master the complete Divine Eye secret technique. And the Ninth Turn Divine Eye Secret Technique, since your senior brother created it, no one has been able to successfully cultivate it. Even with your remarkable talent, it would be difficult to do so on your own.”","“Even if you had the potential, your mysterious master wouldn’t have the time to wait. He teaches his disciples with one goal: speed. He provides the best opportunities and the best treasures. I’ve seen it countless times before and am very familiar with his teaching methods. However, he hasn’t appeared in the Starry Sky for a long time, so your senior brother was sent to assist you. As for Weiss, he was likely following the orders of the Divine King to help you!” the Great Divine Spirit mused."]},{"number":6382,"title":"Chapter 6382: Star Spirit’s Request","paragraphs":["Chapter 6382: Star Spirit’s Request","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang trembled slightly upon hearing the title “God King.”","That being was none other than the founder of the Starry Sky.","Even he had shown such respect toward Master Xuan Yi. It seemed Jian Wushuang had underestimated his master.","But the core issue lay with the Divine Eye Clan.","Senior Brother Ghost Eye had chosen the method of sacrifice, allowing him to quickly master the Divine Eye Secret Technique. Wasn’t this method a bit too cruel?","However, compared to the extinction of the race created by Giant God Star Spirit, this was already quite kind.","“Since it’s about suppression, what does Lord Star Spirit mean?” Jian Wushuang asked anxiously.","With a sorrowful tone, Giant God Star Spirit replied, “I hope you do not devour their power.”","“This... you must be overthinking it. I, Jian Wushuang, would never do something so disgraceful!” Jian Wushuang patted his chest and assured confidently.","However, the eyes of Giant God Star Spirit told him otherwise—the spirit did not trust him.","Recalling that Giant God Star Spirit had said they had met before, and it was a long time ago, Jian Wushuang suddenly understood.","Giant God Star Spirit must have felt a connection between their kind and him back when the Qishen Temple had dealings with Giant God Star Clan. That glance must have revealed the sacrificial act he had performed on behalf of King Bai.","Now, the spirit was worried that Jian Wushuang might sacrifice the Divine Eye Clan again, and had come specifically to plead with him.","Such humility was almost embarrassing.","Jian Wushuang, feeling a bit awkward, quickly promised, “Rest assured, Lord Star Spirit, I will not trouble the Divine Eye Clan. When the time comes, I will place them all within the Nine Prison Pagoda. Once I’ve perfected the Divine Eye Secret Technique, I will certainly offer the Nine Prison Pagoda to you. I’m sure my Senior Brother Ghost Eye would also want you and your clan to receive the understanding of your ancestor.”","The real reason for the Star Spirit’s courteous behavior was likely due to the influence of Ghost Eye.","Ghost Eye was strong, and Giant God Star Spirit was naturally proud. Otherwise, the spirit would not have spared Ghost Eye when the entire Divine Eye Clan had been wiped out. It was clear the spirit had not wanted to harm him.","As expected, when Jian Wushuang mentioned Ghost Eye, Giant God Star Spirit became visibly happier.","The spirit’s thoughts about Ghost Eye were quite evident.","“You are truly a formidable individual, chosen by that great figure. Your future achievements will certainly not fall short of those of your Senior Brother Ghost Eye. I have high hopes for you. As for the Nine Prison Pagoda, there will be someone else in need of it once your Divine Eye Secret Technique is complete. I won’t say who it is, but when the time is right, you will naturally understand.” Giant God Star Spirit gazed at Jian Wushuang more favorably now, sighing internally. If only Ghost Eye had been as clever, perhaps the entire Divine Eye Clan wouldn’t have been annihilated by the spirit’s own hand.","Jian Wushuang licked his lips. He wasn’t one to flatter people without reason, but this Colossal Star Spirit was not just any being—it was a Star Spirit, and the ancestor of Giant God Star Clan. Surely, the spirit had many treasures. Being so respectful and clever, and as Ghost Eye’s junior brother, shouldn’t he receive a small token of appreciation to deepen their bond?","Giant God Star Spirit glanced at Jian Wushuang and, after a brief pause, said, “I came here in a rush and didn’t prepare anything worthy as a gift. I shall give you a special treasure instead—this is a leaf I took from the ancient texts of the Starry Sky.”","With that, a blue leaf, crisscrossed with a hundred intricate veins, appeared in the Star Spirit’s eyes. Though it was only the size of a palm, it contained endless mysteries.","Jian Wushuang gazed at the leaf, swallowing hard, and quickly replied, “Lord Star Spirit, you are too kind. It’s an honor just to meet you. How could I possibly accept such a gift?”","He didn’t reach out to take it, but the leaf floated to him nonetheless.","“Young one, may your future path be as optimistic as your character.”","With those words, the enormous eyes of Giant God Star Spirit faded from Jian Wushuang’s mind.","All that remained was the blue leaf, brimming with the power of the Starry Sky.","“Safe travels!” Jian Wushuang bowed deeply.","Rising again, he eagerly reached for the leaf.","As soon as he held it in his hand, he felt a surge of comfort.","“The leaf itself contained a unique space-time. Even a Space-Time God would be envious! As expected of a Star Spirit; anything it produces is extraordinary. But I wonder what use this item has for me right now?” Jian Wushuang pondered, his thoughts drifting to the Starry Sky Tree mentioned by the Giant Star Spirit.","Back then, Weiss had also spoken of an ancient tree as old as the Starry Sky itself.","Legend had it that the Starry Sky had been created in this very place because that ancient tree had taken root here.","Thinking of this, Jian Wushuang became even more excited and immediately used his Thought power to probe the leaf.","In an instant, a terrifying will surged into his soul.","If it weren’t for the will of the Realm Beast protecting him, this single strike would have been fatal.","“It’s too powerful. Unless I’m at my peak strength, my Thought power can’t penetrate it!” He was both thrilled and slightly disappointed.","The leaf, like the gray jar he possessed, was currently unusable, something he could only look at without converting it into combat power immediately.","While he was grappling with both excitement and frustration, he noticed that the leaf could freely transform, remaining both formless and colorless.","The transformations followed his very thoughts.","“Change!” With a thought, Jian Wushuang willed the leaf to turn into armor.","A blue set of armor appeared before his eyes.","“Change again!”","Swish!","In an instant, the leaf transformed into a blue divine sword.","The sword, brimming with the power of the Starry Sky, wasn’t as powerful as his nurtured Myriad Tribulations Sword, but it was still stronger than ordinary space-time treasures.","“I’ve hit the jackpot!” Jian Wushuang exclaimed in excitement.","This leaf could change according to his will, not only transforming into armor to protect him but also into a weapon.","“Wait a second, I haven’t even used a drop of blood to claim it as mine. How am I able to control the leaf?” He paused, then quickly realized.","It must have been the Giant Star Spirit that had helped him accomplish this.","Otherwise, even if he tried the most primitive method of using blood to recognize the leaf as his, it wouldn’t have worked. Not to mention using his will to do so.","After all, his Thought power couldn’t even penetrate the leaf’s interior.","After thinking it over, he gave a command: “Relax your consciousness, don’t resist!”","Once again, his Thought power cautiously probed the leaf.","As expected, the same thing happened as before—the leaf repelled him, sending him flying out of its core.","The leaf circled around him once as if to mock him, saying, “Don’t waste your energy. Even if I let you hit me, you’d never succeed.”","Jian Wushuang sighed in resignation, giving up entirely. He could only make simple use of this leaf from the Starry Sky Tree.","“Transform into the vine of the Myriad Willow Divine Wood!”","Whoosh!","The leaf, which had taken the form of armor, instantly extended a vine that began waving freely.","“Stop!!”","Jian Wushuang hurriedly commanded it to stop, feeling like his brain had been drained in the process.","He immediately left his consciousness world, bringing the leaf with him.","Back in the real world, inside the Nine Prison Pagoda, Xiang Yang and the others looked at him with curious expressions.","Jian Wushuang glanced down and noticed the blue armor on his body.","With a thought, the armor retreated into his body, leaving him in his usual white robe."]},{"number":6383,"title":"Chapter 6383: Set Off","paragraphs":["Chapter 6383: Set Off","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Brother Wushuang, did you just have an epiphany?” Xiang Yang asked curiously.","In fact, the epiphany lasted for a short time, and none of them dared to disturb him. They simply waited. In the time it took for one stick of incense to burn, Jian Wushuang regained consciousness.","“Yes, something like that,” Jian Wushuang replied vaguely, then continued, “There’s something else I need to inform you. If you feel your strength is sufficient, you can leave now. But if you’d prefer to continue cultivating here, I can open up a small cave-heaven for you where the energy won’t be isolated.”","After completely mastering the Nine Prison Pagoda, he could manipulate the first layer of its world at will. Naturally, he could create a separate space suitable for cultivation. Though the space was relatively small, it was just enough for the three of them to stretch their legs. The length and width extended roughly 100,000 miles each.","Moreover, this small world had mountains, rivers, and even some ordinary animals he had casually created. It was far better than the previous barren white landscape.","Upon entering the small world, Xiang Yang nodded with satisfaction and said, “Not bad, much easier on the eyes than before. I’m quite close to reaching the Great Perfection stage now. I estimate it will take about thirty more years. Once I’ve reached that stage, I’ll come out and help you!”","“You should just focus on your cultivation,” Jian Wushuang said helplessly.","These three people would likely be of little help to him. Especially Immortal Jiu Chen—he was practically useless. If it weren’t for the fact that Jian Wushuang had gained so many benefits from the Divine Fire Temple and Jiu Chen’s unwavering loyalty to the temple, he would have discarded him long ago.","For now, Jian Wushuang decided to keep him around and elevate his strength to the Undying level. If he encountered the Temple Master of the Divine Fire Temple in the future, he would return Jiu Chen to him. If not, he would find a place to discard Jiu Chen.","And then there was Xiang Yang.","Jian Wushuang’s future was bright, like a dragon ready to soar with the wind. In this universe, there were certainly experts above the level of Universe Masters, and Xiang Yang wouldn’t be able to help him at all. In fact, following him could be dangerous. As for Xing Luo, he no longer cared about her. She was either in the Supreme Time-Space or had become a major figure in some other universe.","Once his strength had recovered to a certain level, he would capture her and make her Xiang Yang’s wife.","Then there was Jiang Ni, who was the most important of all.","She was the daughter of Jiang Shang, and her mother was Hui Qing. He had to ensure her safety and get her out.","Although she was born from a clone, her bloodline was real!","He had to bring her to Hui Qing, so she needed to stay close to him to prevent any accidents. If something happened, there would be no time to regret it, and it would be impossible to explain once they left.","He certainly didn’t want Hui Qing to misunderstand again.","Finally, there was Jiang Shang. According to what she had told him, he seemed to be trapped somewhere or had offended some powerful figure.","He had to find a way to rescue them and deliver them to Huiqing.","This was a tremendous favor, enough to atone for the mistake he made in the past.","Thinking of this, he couldn’t help but smile.","“Alright, all of you go and cultivate on your own. If you need any treasures, just send me a message. I’ll prepare a Sky Screen for you later. Don’t use thought power to observe the outside world randomly anymore. The place I’m going to this time is extremely dangerous. If I get exposed, you can contact me through the Sky Screen. If you want to see the outside world, use the screen to watch.”","With a single motion of his hand, he condensed a Sky Screen that allowed them to observe the outside world.","However, its range was limited.","Centered around him, they could only see within a ten-mile radius.","“Great! I’ve been wanting to take a look at the Ancient Demon Palace!”","Xiang Yang and Immortal Jiu Chen were thrilled.","But Jiang Ni wore a troubled expression. She was worried about Jian Wushuang and felt that this burden shouldn’t be placed on the shoulders of an elder who admired her mother.","She had to work twice as hard so as not to disappoint the care and cultivation Jian Wushuang had provided.","The thought of Jian Wushuang risking his life outside to find treasures for them filled her with guilt. In her heart, she silently swore that no matter what happened to Jian Wushuang in the future, she would repay him, even if it meant taking care of him in his old age.","If Jian Wushuang knew what she was thinking, he would certainly be pleased.","At that moment, a transmission from the outside world pulled Jian Wushuang back from the Nine Prison Pagoda.","“Wushuang, it’s time to leave!”","The pleasant voice of Fairy Ziyu came through, and Jian Wushuang quickly rose and walked out of the room.","In the same tea room as before, everyone had already gathered.","It seemed that over the past month, these people had swapped out all their equipment.","Some had even sold valuable treasures in exchange for many hidden cards. Their eyes no longer held fear but instead sparkled with eagerness.","“Daoist Wuhou, I heard you even sold a permanent cave mansion on Divine Mountain. I have to say, I admire your resolve!” The elderly Tian Can sighed in admiration.","But unexpectedly, Immortal Wuhou quipped, “No matter how hard I push myself, I can’t compare to you. You even sold your concubine. My cave mansion is nothing in comparison!”","Tian Can didn’t take offense, only chuckling, “It’s all just worldly possessions!”","Indeed, at this point, Jian Wushuang wouldn’t have been surprised if Tian Can sold his own father.","However, Wuhou Immortal selling his permanent cave mansion on Divine Mountain was truly impressive.","Although it was only a mid-mountain cave mansion, it was still permanent.","If unused, it could be rented out, generating a steady stream of income over the years.","Even a mid-mountain “Ding-class” cave mansion could fetch a sky-high price of a million immortal crystals.","More importantly, such permanent cave mansions were hard to come by. Once sold, buying them back was next to impossible.","This clearly showed that Wuhou Immortal was the key figure in their group, with a million immortal crystals to buy strong defensive measures.","After all, a typical Five-step True Immortal’s wealth hovered around that figure. Some were even poorer, lacking a million immortal crystals, while the wealthier ones had no limit.","Take, for instance, True Lord Xue Yang. A Grand Completion in the Transcendence Stage, he was likely the wealthiest among them.","Rumor had it that he possessed a supreme treasure.","A treasure coveted even by immortal beings!","It undoubtedly came from his elder brother, Yang Dingtian.","With just this treasure, True Lord Xue Yang could stand firm among immortals.","In fact, none of them were weak.","Two of the Four-step True Immortals were top-tier experts, practicing Six-level Origin Dao and cultivating the Third Sequence up to the fifth stage. Their combat power was on par with an average Five-step True Immortal!","And as for Tian Can, there was no need to elaborate. He even sold his concubine, fully prepared for this journey. Despite his shameless exterior, he had deep foundations and formidable combat strength. His aptitude was stronger than Wuhou Immortal’s, as he practiced Four-level Origin Dao, with unmatched divine power.","In fact, on paper, Tian Can was the strongest immortal in their group.","Fairy Ziyu, like Wuhou Immortal, practiced Five-level Origin Dao. She had a high net worth and extensive connections, having acquired plenty of life-saving treasures for this journey.","Among the True Immortals and True Lord Xue Yang, each had their preparations in place. Another Grand Completion stage cultivator, Tian Can’s disciple, stood nearby. But as they looked around, it was clear Jian Wushuang hadn’t made any preparations at all."]},{"number":6384,"title":"Chapter 6384: Swirl God Sect","paragraphs":["Chapter 6384: Swirl God Sect","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","But no one noticed him.","“Alright everyone, let’s stick to the original plan: first register at the Divine Mountain, then we’ll take action under the cover of night and leave Tiantan City.”","“Got it!”","The group stood up together, leaving one by one through the back door of Fairy Ziyu’s residence.","At the Divine Mountain, Fairy Ziyu had already arranged for a friend to handle their registration, and they intentionally left a message for her friend, claiming they were going into seclusion.","The earlier transaction for the treasures was also done for the purpose of going into seclusion.","This explanation made sense now.","After the registration, they quietly left one by one during the deep hours of the night.","Of course, their departure wasn’t officially recorded.","At the city gates, Fairy Ziyu had already taken care of everything.","They boarded a flying boat and easily passed through the city gates.","Once they left Tiantan City, they advanced at full speed, rushing toward the direction of the Bifaced God’s Palace.","Inside the flying boat, Fairy Ziyu pointed toward a swirling nebula ahead and said, “Look, up ahead is the Swirl God Sect. Once we pass it, we’ll have to abandon the flying boat and proceed slowly on foot!”","“The Swirl God Sect, I’ve been here a few times before. Speaking of which, it’s quite bold of them to establish a sect so close to the Bifaced God’s Palace!” The old man Tian Can sighed.","By now, they had traveled far from Tiantan City, entering the northern region of the Ancient Sea Domain.","Not all forces and powerful figures resided in Tiantan City.","Aside from the Sacred City, the Ancient Domain was home to many powerful individuals and factions.","For instance, the northern region of the Ancient Sea Domain housed many prominent forces.","Even the base of the formidable Bifaced Buddha was located here.","The Bifaced God’s Palace was vast, occupying a third of the northern region, which equated to about a tenth of the entire Ancient Sea Domain.","Only someone as arrogant as the Bifaced Buddha could command such a large territory.","True Lord Xue Yang’s older brother, Yang Dingtian, who was rumored to be the strongest in the Ancient Sea Domain, merely owned a mansion the size of a battlefield a thousand miles wide within Tiantan City. He used it to recruit powerful figures and cultivate his personal retainers.","Yang Dingtian’s forces were considered elite, so having a large territory wasn’t necessary for him. However, he had many ways to amass wealth, and many of the sects outside the city had connections with him.","But Yang Dingtian had never been able to extend his influence into the northern region.","Apart from the Bifaced God’s Palace, there were six major powers in the northern region. Though these powers had no direct connection to the Bifaced God’s Palace, establishing a sect in the northern region required forming some sort of relationship with them. Even though the Bifaced Buddha was known for his erratic personality and disdain for socializing, his subordinates were different.","Take, for instance, the Swirl God Sect they passed by, which was one of the six major forces in the northern region outside of the Bifaced God’s Palace, with a Dao Lord-level expert overseeing the sect.","There were hundreds of Zhen Xian (True Immortals) within its ranks.","Across the entire Ancient Sea Demon Domain, it was considered a notable power.","At this point, Wu Hou True Lord spoke up, “I have a friend in the Swirl God Sect who holds a fairly high position. He once told me that the reason the Swirl God Sect managed to secure a foothold in the northern region is because their Holy Maiden has a relationship with Qifeng, one of the four Guardians of the Bifaced God’s Palace.”","“I didn’t expect you, Brother Wu Hou, to be so well-informed about such matters!” Tian Can Old Man teased.","Everyone else was already used to it.","Fairy Ziyu, upon hearing this, couldn’t help but sigh, “I know that Swirl Holy Maiden. She was once a maidservant in the City Lord’s Mansion, and we both became sworn daughters to Old Lady Yinhua. But she took a more extreme path, and not long after, she was expelled. The next thing I heard, she had become the Holy Maiden of the Swirl Sect and had already advanced to the level of a Seven-Step True Immortal, leaving me far behind.”","“I never thought that the Holy Maiden had such a history!” True Lord Xue Yang remarked in surprise.","The City Lord’s Mansion was a unique existence. Although the City Lord’s strength wasn’t on par with Yang Dingtian’s, he was a person sent by the Sacred Land, someone with considerable backing, and even Yang Dingtian wouldn’t dare offend him easily.","Thus, anyone who came from the City Lord’s Mansion would be treated with respect.","Moreover, this maidservant had, like Fairy Ziyu, become a sworn daughter of Old Lady Yinhua, indicating that she had considerable talent.","Old Lady Yinhua belonged to the top echelon of experts. In Tiantan City, she ranked within the top ten, and in the entire Ancient Sea Domain, she was among the top twenty. She had countless disciples.","Only the most outstanding, or those recommended by others, could become her sworn daughters.","Of course, it was merely an honorary title.","Like Fairy Ziyu, who had already become a Four-Step True Immortal, there was no longer a need to rely on Old Lady Yinhua for survival. However, she would still regularly visit Old Lady Yinhua, bring rare treasures as offerings, and pay her respects.","This was how relationships were maintained.","Although the Ancient Sea Domain was vast, the circles of the powerful were interconnected, unlike the more isolated Red Eye Realm.","After passing the Swirl God Sect, Fairy Ziyu retracted the flying boat and began low-altitude flying.","She took out a small incense burner, from which an indistinct wisp of thought power floated. She said, “I have a treasure that can block off any aura. Everyone, make sure to stay within a hundred feet of me.”","“Ziqi Donglai?” Tian Can Old Man’s expression changed.","He recognized the treasure—it was incredibly valuable, and even Five-Step True Immortals rarely possessed one. Usually, only Seven-Step True Immortals could afford to own such a treasure.","It was a top-grade immortal artifact that could isolate their aura.","Moreover, it had a wide range of isolation, capable of isolating an area within a hundred zhang around the Purple Furnace.","Once isolated, even a Dao Lord would need to be within a hundred li of them to detect anything.","Below the level of a Seven-Step Zhen Xian, unless they used a supreme treasure, it would be impossible for anyone to discover them.","For those above the Seven-Step Zhen Xian level, they would need to be within a thousand li and use Thought power to cover the area in order to sense anything unusual.","Such a treasure was undoubtedly a life-saving tool.","“I never expected that Fairy Ziyu had such a treasure prepared. Unfortunately, I couldn’t find any item that could conceal our aura like Xiang Yang!” True Lord Xueyang remarked, feeling a bit regretful.","Fairy Ziyu responded calmly, “It was something I obtained by chance back in the day. I’ve never had the opportunity to use it over the years, but it’s come in handy now!”","“With the Purple Furnace concealing us, half of our mission is already complete!” Zhen Xian Wuhou said with a rare smile.","The tense atmosphere had eased considerably.","Because they were flying at a low altitude, their speed wasn’t particularly fast.","True Lord Xueyang took out an ancient demonic token, examined the route, and said, “Fairy Ziyu, head southwest. After traveling three hundred million li, we will encounter a red Blood River. We need to follow the Blood River at that point.”","“Blood River?” Fairy Ziyu frowned. She had previously researched the Dual-Faced God’s Mansion and knew about the Blood River.","Originally, that river wasn’t red. It had been turned that way when the Dual-Faced Buddha opened this place, exterminating an entire tribe and dyeing the river red with their blood. Even after ten thousand years, the river still flowed with that same blood-red color.","One could only imagine how many powerful beings had been slaughtered there.","“The river Xueyang mentioned should be within the Blood Demon’s territory inside the Dual-Faced God’s Mansion. He is a Seven-Step Zhen Xian, so we’ll need to be cautious around him. However, along the path ahead, there shouldn’t be any particularly powerful Zhen Xians!” The Elder Tian Can shared the information he knew as well."]},{"number":6385,"title":"Chapter 6385: Two-Faced God’s Mansion","paragraphs":["Chapter 6385: Two-Faced God’s Mansion","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Ziyu Immortal nodded and increased her speed considerably.","After traveling for a day, the group finally entered the Two-Faced God’s Mansion.","Although it was called a mansion, it actually resembled a vast, ancient territory.","This place had not been developed by any sect, and some demons still lived here. However, their strength was very weak and posed no threat to the group.","The only worry was encountering a Zhen Xian within the Two-Faced God’s Mansion.","If they were discovered, it would trigger a chain reaction.","On their way to the Blood River, they had already passed several Zhen Xian abodes.","These were the obvious Zhen Xian abodes, but some Zhen Xian had eccentric personalities, much like the Two-Faced Buddha, and likely no one even knew where their abodes were.","The group was most afraid of this scenario. If they stumbled upon an eccentric Dao Master who had opened a hidden abode near the outskirts of the Two-Faced God’s Mansion, and disguised their identity, they would all be doomed once discovered.","The powerful beings following the Two-Faced Buddha were hardly normal.","Especially his four Guardians, each of whom was a top-tier Dao Master with countless killings under their belt. Some had even provoked Emperors, which is why they sought refuge with the Two-Faced Buddha—both for protection and because they shared the same twisted nature.","If they ran into these people, even the cultivators within the Two-Faced God’s Mansion could be doomed.","Not to mention the fact that they were strong beings from Tiantan City, combined with True Lord Xue Yang’s unique identity, they probably wouldn’t even know how they died.","So, throughout the journey, they were on edge, not daring to let their guard down.","They even intentionally avoided the sacred mountains, flying only in the low skies above the plains.","Most powerful beings preferred to open abodes in mountain ranges.","Very few chose to open abodes on the plains.","But it wasn’t completely unheard of.","However, the chances were much lower, which reduced the risk of encountering powerful beings.","Ziyu Immortal led the way, considering every possibility. She made sure to be as cautious as possible. If they still encountered a Dao Master in the outskirts, it could only be attributed to bad luck.","After flying for a full day, they finally completed most of the journey. The Blood River was now close, and they could already sense the stench of blood emanating from it.","There were also more beasts in this area, particularly bloodthirsty ones.","“There’s a swarm of bloodthirsty bats ahead. If we take a detour, we’ll need to travel an additional thirty million miles, and that area is mountainous, which carries higher risks!” Ziyu Immortal explained, seeking the group’s input.","The old man Tian Can raised his brow slightly and asked, “What’s the strength of the bat swarm?”","“The Bat King is a Zhen Xian, probably not a Second Step Zhen Xian, while the others are in the Great Ascension stage, with a few at the Nascent Soul stage. There are roughly thirty thousand of them. Within a seventy-thousand-mile radius, there are only two other Zhen Xian-level beasts, and no cultivators,” Ziyu Immortal reported on the surrounding situation.","At that moment, True Lord Wuhou spoke, “Let’s walk through and leave the low skies to them.”","The group had been flying in the low skies, where the bats were also flying. Even though their aura was being concealed, they could still be seen with the naked eye. Moreover, bats had strong sensory abilities and could easily detect them.","So, they had no choice but to walk on land.","Although it would slow their pace, it was still better than engaging in a fight.","True Lord Xue Yang was getting anxious, as the slow speed meant they had not yet reached the Blood River. The slower they moved, the higher the risk became.","He immediately spoke up, “Let’s just fly at low altitude. If we encounter them, we’ll kill them directly. There’s no need to waste time. We’re very close to the Blood River, and beasts often fight here. The strong smell of blood can completely mask us from those bats. Even if cultivators notice, they won’t care!”","“Agreed!” the Old Man Tian Can said.","Fairy Ziyu nodded and replied, “Alright, Tian Can, you’ll handle it later!”","“No problem!”","The Old Man Tian Can was confident. Dealing with a group of weak bat monsters posed no challenge for him.","The reason he was chosen to act was because of a special immortal artifact he possessed.","Before long, they approached the bat swarm.","At that moment, the Old Man Tian Can took out a black gourd, casually pulling out the stopper. Instantly, a searing flame surged forth.","The flame contained no immortal power, making it more subtle and secure.","However, its potency was overwhelming. In a mere instant, the black flames shot out, incinerating the entire swarm of bats into ashes.","The entire space seemed significantly less oppressive.","Having dealt with the obstacle, the Old Man Tian Can shouted urgently, “Move!”","Fairy Ziyu immediately picked up speed, and the others followed closely behind.","Dealing with the bat swarm was merely a minor episode.","As they continued to travel millions of miles ahead, the number of monster groups they encountered increased.","They even encountered a few Zhen Xian, who commanded legions of monsters. Although their individual strength was that of a Five-Step Zhen Xian, when commanding their beast armies, their combat prowess could rival a Six-Step or even Seven-Step Zhen Xian.","“Damn it! How are there so many people from the Beast Control Sect in the Twin-Faced God’s Palace?” Old Man Tian Can cursed in a low voice.","Fairy Ziyu frowned deeply and shook her head. “I don’t know, but their presence likely has something to do with an important figure inside the Twin-Faced God’s Palace. That figure might be nearby. Everyone, stay alert!”","“Yes!!!” the group responded in unison.","Jian Wushuang, however, remained unfazed. His perception extended far beyond the range of Fairy Ziyu’s purple furnace.","He could sense all the powerful auras within billions of miles around him, including every expert within the Twin-Faced God’s Palace.","Unless the opponent was a Universe Master, they couldn’t block his detection.","Universe Masters had already created their own universes, controlling their own space.","This self-contained law of isolation was beyond Jian Wushuang’s current ability to probe.","But once he mastered an Origin Source similar to that of a Realm Beast, even those self-contained universes wouldn’t be able to block his Thought power.","For now, though, there were no Universe Masters in the Ancient Domain World, so his Thought power sufficed.","He was just too weak at the moment. Even though he wasn’t afraid of those Zhen Xian, his current level was only in the Grand Accomplishment stage, so it was wiser to stay low-key.","Throughout the journey, he remained silent.","He followed quietly behind Fairy Ziyu, walking wherever she led.","If he had mentioned that, during the bat extermination, a Seven-Step Zhen Xian was actually hidden below, it would’ve likely shocked everyone.","However, that Zhen Xian seemed to be in seclusion and had no interest in bothering them.","It could be considered their good fortune.","But now, things were different.","Many powerful presences lurked within the Blood River, and as they had to follow the river, they were bound to come close to some Zhen Xian. Fortunately, the distance wasn’t enough for those experts to notice them.","“Three thousand miles ahead, there’s an Eight-Step Zhen Xian!” Jian Wushuang’s heart stirred.","Beside that Zhen Xian were dozens of Seven-Step Zhen Xian-level monsters, likely belonging to a Beast Control Sect expert.","Ten thousand miles away, there was even a Nine-Step Zhen Xian.","Not only could Jian Wushuang detect their locations, but he could also overhear their conversations."]},{"number":6386,"title":"Chapter 6386: Blood River Ancestor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6386: Blood River Ancestor","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Ancestor of the Blood River?”","This was a name he hadn’t heard before. Earlier, he’d heard them mention that the Blood Demon was a supreme powerhouse stationed at the Blood River.","But how was there also an Ancestor of the Blood River?","However, through further investigation, he found out that this Blood River Ancestor was the being stationed at the source of the Blood River, and he was known as the Ancestor of the Blood River.","He was also one of the top ten Zhen Xian under the command of the Dual-Faced Buddha.","His status was high, and his strength formidable. He practiced the Second-tier Origin Source Dao and had cultivated the Divine Eye secret technique, which was a Second-sequence inheritance.","Moreover, he had already cultivated it to perfection.","The battle prowess of the Blood River Ancestor could already rival that of a Dao Lord.","However, his mastery of the Origin Source Dao had not yet reached perfection.","Once perfected, he would be among the top-tier Dao Lords.","And he was just one of the top ten Zhen Xian under the command of the Dual-Faced Buddha, with nine others as strong as him.","The fact that the Blood River Ancestor had appeared in this place was not something he had mentioned. Naturally, the others were unaware.","If they had known, the pressure would likely have been enough to drive them all to despair.","“Whoosh!”","In the distance, a river of blood began to emerge, and everyone let out a sigh of relief.","But this was only the beginning.","“Finally here. Brother Xue Yang, how much farther do we have to go?” Old Man Tianchan asked.","True Lord Xue Yang’s expression remained grim as he replied in a cold tone, “Not far now. From here, we just follow the Blood River, and we’ll reach Yunhai Mountain, the residence of the Dual-Faced God’s palace. The Ancient Demon Hall is located there!”","“Roughly a billion miles left. From here, our pace will only slow down. It’ll probably take at least half a month!” Fairy Ziyu calculated.","In truth, this wasn’t a particularly long time. The real concern was that the deeper they went, the greater the number of powerful beings they would encounter.","This was what they feared.","“Yunhai Mountain is the territory of Yunshan Guardian, one of the Four Great Guardians. And we’ll have to pass through the source of the Blood River, which is the domain of the Blood River Ancestor. Is there no way to take a detour?” Old Man Tianchan asked anxiously.","The Blood River Ancestor was one of the top ten Zhen Xian under the command of the Dual-Faced Buddha and ranked within the top hundred Zhen Xian in the entire Canghai Ancient Domain.","Furthermore, he was known for his love of slaughter, his very existence a living battlefield.","He was an even more terrifying figure than the Yunshan Guardian.","Fairy Ziyu noticed the anxiety among the group and reassured them, “There isn’t much room for deviation. The source of the Blood River is very close to the core of the Dual-Faced God’s palace, and the area around it is filled with the residences of powerful beings. It’s dangerous no matter which way we go. Although the Blood River Ancestor is violent, he’s also arrogant and prideful. He won’t bother scanning the area with Thought Power. Besides, even though he’s strong, he’s not a Dao Lord. As long as we don’t get within a thousand miles of him, he won’t sense us!”","“Alright then,” Old Man Tianchan nodded.","True Lord Xue Yang spoke up, “Now that the route is decided, let’s hurry. I have a bad feeling that danger is lurking nearby. We should leave as soon as possible.”","“Understood!” Fairy Ziyu smiled softly and continued forward along the Blood River. The group followed closely behind.","Jian Wushuang glanced meaningfully at True Lord Xue Yang.","This guy could actually sense danger. It must have something to do with the Blood River Ancestor and that Eight-Step Zhen Xian from the Beast-Taming Sect.","He was in the Great Vehicle Stage, yet he could sense the aura of such a powerful existence. The supreme treasure on him was likely more than just a simple item.","Among Zhen Xian, those who possessed a supreme treasure were usually backed by significant powers. It was exceedingly rare for a genius like True Lord Xue Yang, who was in the Great Vehicle Stage, to have a supreme treasure.","After all, supreme treasures were typically used by Emperors.","Of course, Emperors generally wielded high-level or even top-tier supreme treasures.","Dao Lords used regular supreme treasures, while beings as powerful as the two-faced jester and Yang Dingtian undoubtedly had high-level or top-tier supreme treasures.","Within the Holy Lands, Emperors were few in number and mostly trained within the Holy Lands themselves.","Thus, there were no Emperor-level powerhouses in the ancient regions.","However, they were never afraid of the Emperors from the ancient courts invading.","This was because, within every ancient region, the Holy Lands had assigned top-tier Dao Lords to oversee it.","The two-faced Buddha was actually a holy disciple of the Holy Lands. He had come to oversee the Fu Hai Ancient Region, as it was located very close to the thirty-six ancient regions of the ancient court.","His strength was incredibly formidable, capable of directly confronting an Emperor.","When he burned his divine power, he could even suppress an Emperor.","Although he hadn’t yet fused the two sequences, he had trained both sequences to perfection.","Among Dao Lords, his power was considered first-class.","The truly top-tier Dao Lords were those who had already fused two sequences and were on the verge of merging with the Dao.","However, such beings wouldn’t waste their time overseeing ancient regions. They chose to cultivate in the Holy Lands instead.","They were the future of the Holy Lands, and even the Holy Master wouldn’t force them to do anything.","After all, there were far too few Emperors in the Holy Lands.","As for Dao Lords like Yang Dingtian, who wasn’t originally from the Holy Lands, although he had perfected both sequences, he had not attempted to fuse them.","He understood that once the two sequences were fused, there would be no turning back, and the chance of merging with the Dao would become incredibly slim.","Ultimately, he lacked the determination.","After all, becoming an Emperor didn’t require fusing two sequences.","One could break through without doing so, and the process would be much simpler.","One could also follow the path of the Origin Source or the divine power route.","This way, the power might be slightly weaker, but the cultivation speed would be much faster. As long as one had enough talent, they wouldn’t be weaker than those Emperors who fused two sequences.","However, talent was always limited.","Otherwise, no one would have surpassed the Holy Master after all these years.","The cultivation system of the ancient regions was simply too scarce and too extreme.","If one went down the wrong path, it would take a long time to correct it.","Just like the current struggle for the Dao inheritance.","The ancient court and the Holy Lands were both unwilling to back down.","Yet, some cultivators had already started to retreat.","Sooner or later, a battle for the Dao would erupt!","Jian Wushuang had seen far too many such battles. In a world that had been newly established, he understood both the advantages and the disadvantages.","When that time came, how many of the people before him would survive?","He glanced at the crowd.","Zhen Xian seemed eternal, but in this world, there were no eternal Zhen Xians, only eternal powerhouses.","Otherwise, after so many years since the Starry Sky was established, everyone would have become Zhen Xian by now.","All would have achieved eternal life, and there wouldn’t be any mortals left.","But throughout the history of the Starry Sky, too many powerhouses had fallen, even the gods of the Starry Sky.","Mie Sheng, as a god of the Starry Sky, had already fallen along the timeline.","Even the God of Reincarnation, whom Mie Sheng had longed to become, had left that position vacant.","Wasn’t it because of some reason that he too had fallen?","Otherwise, why would Mie Sheng covet that position?","Therefore, there was no such thing as eternal existence in this world—only eternal powerhouses.","Only powerhouses could achieve eternity.","In the Starry Sky, if you were a powerhouse, you could attain eternity.","In the world of the ancient regions, if you were a powerhouse, you could also achieve eternity.","Of course, there were always risks from external forces.","The world of the ancient regions had been established for only a short time and had not yet had much contact with other worlds. But in the future, changes were bound to come."]},{"number":6387,"title":"Chapter 6387: Wu Taidou","paragraphs":["Chapter 6387: Wu Taidou","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Everything now did not belong to those eternal beings, but was merely entrusted to them for safekeeping.","After undergoing reconstruction, Jian Wushuang had gained a great deal of insight.","During the journey, since he had nothing else to do, he continuously meditated on the path of the Origin Source.","He contemplated his ultimate swordsmanship and the Extreme Path.","These two paths, which he had already mastered, were subjects he continued to explore.","He sought to find common ground between them, hoping to carve out a new path of the Origin Source.","Time passed day by day, and ten days later, they reached the end of the Blood River without incident.","They had passed through the territory of the Blood Demon True Immortal, and along the way, they encountered several Seventh Step True Immortal, all of whom they successfully avoided, smoothly continuing on their journey.","They now stood at the end of the Blood River, and from here onward, it was the domain of the Blood River Ancestor.","Moreover, within the territory of the Blood River Ancestor’s domain, many mortals lived.","Their numbers were vast, numbering in the billions, a million times greater than the population of the entire Red Eye Realm.","These mortals lived on an ancient continent on the northern shore.","On the southern shore, however, lay a battlefield of carnage.","While the northern shore was stable, they did not dare travel through it.","This was because the peace of the northern shore was maintained by several True Immortal, along with the Blood Demon Guards under the command of the Blood River Ancestor.","The Blood Demon True Immortal whose territory they had previously passed through was, in fact, one of the descendants of the Blood River Ancestor. Although separated by many generations, they still shared the same bloodline.","Moreover, this Blood Demon True Immortal was the strongest among the countless descendants of the Blood River Ancestor. His talents were exceptional, and he was deeply favored by the Blood River Ancestor, who entrusted him with the strongest of his Blood Demon Guards.","This was how the title of Blood Demon True Immortal came to be.","The general of the Blood Demon Guard was Blood Demon True Immortal, but he was not the strongest.","There were also three deputy generals, each of whom was an Eighth Step True Immortal.","Any one of them was not someone they could afford to provoke.","Naturally, they dared not pass through the Blood Demon Guard-patrolled northern shore.","They could only sneak along the southern shore.","Halfway through their journey, Old Man Tian Can couldn’t help but curse, “Damn it, our luck is terrible. The southern shore is currently undergoing a Blood Demon Trial. There are probably some Blood Demon Guard experts stationed here. We have to be extra cautious!”","“Check what level of Blood Demon Trial it is!” True Lord Xue Yang asked anxiously.","He was well-versed in this matter. The Blood Demon Trials were divided into three tiers. If it was the weakest trial, it might end in just a few days. However, if it was the strongest type, not only would it last longer, but the number of participants would also be vast. Naturally, this meant many Blood Demon Guards would be present.","There was even a chance that two of the three deputy generals might arrive.","And those were Eighth Step True Immortal.","Ziyu was at the front, carefully scouting the area. After a while, she returned and said, “I didn’t detect any Blood Demon Guard experts, but I did discover someone from the Beast Taming Sect, and he’s quite powerful!”","“Who?” True Lord Wu Hou raised an eyebrow and asked.","“Eighth Step True Immortal, Wu Taidou!” Ziyu Immortal answered, a trace of excitement flickering in her eyes.","Because True Lord Wu Hou’s clan belonged to the Beast Controlling Sect.","However, True Lord Wu Hou wasn’t suited to controlling beasts, so from a young age, he entered Tiantan City and apprenticed under a powerful True Immortal. Yet, he never severed ties with the Beast Controlling Sect.","The senior they encountered from Wu Hou’s clan might be able to show some leniency.","For a moment, everyone turned to look at Wu Hou True Immortal.","“It’s him!” Wu Hou True Immortal’s brows furrowed with anger. Upon realizing everyone was looking at him, he immediately said, “Don’t even think about it. I already have a grudge against Wu Taidou. If he discovers I’m here, he will undoubtedly seize the opportunity to eliminate me!”","The Old Man Tian Can was surprised, “That shouldn’t be the case. I heard your clan is quite united. Even if you’re not part of the Beast Controlling Sect, they wouldn’t take action against you, would they?”","His question wasn’t without reason, but Wu Hou True Immortal clearly didn’t want to make things more complicated, nor did he need to explain further.","Fairy Ziyu quickly interrupted Old Man Tian Can’s questioning and changed the subject, saying, “You’ve all seen the situation ahead. I believe the trial hasn’t started yet, so now is our chance to pass through this area. While there’s an Eight-Step True Immortal guarding it, we only need to avoid him for one day to cross the Southern Shore of the Asura Field!”","“Let’s proceed with what Friend Ziyu suggested!” Old Man Tian Can was slightly dissatisfied but understood the importance of unity at this moment.","Wu Hou True Immortal didn’t offer any further explanation and silently pressed on.","From his expression alone, it was clear that there was indeed a deep grudge between him and Wu Taidou from the Beast Controlling Sect, one so severe that it was irreconcilable.","In such situations, someone would typically intervene within the clan. After all, Wu Taidou was an Eight-Step True Immortal with high standing in the Beast Controlling Sect, and Wu Hou True Immortal’s strength was not insignificant either. As a fifth-grade Origin Source Dao cultivator, his God-Eye Secret Technique had already reached the pinnacle, and he was still young. He was expected to reach the level of Seven-Step or even Nine-Step True Immortal in the future.","One was the clan’s current top combat force, while the other was its future pillar.","For such figures to harbor irreconcilable hatred—there had to be a compelling reason behind it.","Since Wu Hou True Immortal wasn’t talking, the others refrained from probing further. Besides, they were in a hurry, so no one gave it more thought.","As they carefully crossed the Southern Shore of the Asura Field, tens of thousands of flying ships appeared above the Northern Shore.","Each flying ship carried ten thousand people.","Tens of thousands of flying ships amounted to millions of individuals.","The flying ships bore the insignia of the Blood Demon Guard. There was no need to ask; these were the Blood Demon Guard’s ships.","The people inside shared similar auras. The majority were Nascent Souls, and a portion were cultivators in the Mahayana Stage.","Millions of them.","Such vast numbers meant that nearly all the strong individuals from that ancient continent on the Northern Shore had been swept up.","At the top of the flying ships—","“Captain, all seventeen Nascent Soul cultivators from the Seventh Ascension Formation have been gathered!”","“The cultivators from the Fourteenth Ascension Formation have also been collected—four thousand Mahayana Stage cultivators, far more than in previous sessions!”","The leader, a red-robed True Immortal, nodded arrogantly and said coldly, “Good. Once the rest of the team returns, we’ll head to the Asura Field on the Southern Shore and inform those fools about the trial!”","“Understood!!”","The Blood Demon Guards saluted in unison.","Immediately, a stern voice echoed throughout the flying ships.","“To all strong cultivators from the ancient continent, you’re just one step away from ascending to prove your Dao...”","This entire conversation was detected by Jian Wushuang, who couldn’t help but sneer internally.","“This Blood River Patriarch is quite interesting. The Asura Field he’s constructed is decent. It’s a pity the trial is too short, and the rewards too few!” Jian Wushuang mused to himself.","This trial was essentially a demonic path trial.","In fact, when Qishen Temple once conducted a massive hunt for Grand Yan Immortals, it wasn’t much different from the Blood Demon trial.","So many Grand Yan Immortals had fallen back then, and after all that, only a handful of inheritors had been selected from the trial.","However, those few inheritors had brought immense growth to Qishen Temple.","It was because of that trial that they later won the decisive battle against Miesheng.","Of course, as a bystander now, Jian Wushuang viewed the Blood Demon trial as nothing more than a demonic endeavor."]},{"number":6388,"title":"Chapter 6388: Blood Demon Trial","paragraphs":["Chapter 6388: Blood Demon Trial","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","When Jian Wushuang was in the Qishen Temple, he hadn’t fully realized the gravity of the situation.","But now, watching those cultivators at the Great Ascension Stage about to undergo the Shura Trial, he knew that perhaps not even one out of a hundred would survive.","After all, the trial was incredibly brutal.","“If the Blood River Ancestor had a powerful inheritance, maybe he could really make it happen!”","Unfortunately, the Blood River Ancestor was merely a successor of the Divine Eye secret technique.","Even after generations of harvesting cultivators from the Ancient Continent, he was only able to gather a group of Blood Demon Guards to serve him.","The cultivators of the Ancient World were in a very different situation compared to Jian Wushuang’s own trial back in the Qishen Temple.","These people still believed they were ascending, but in reality, they were like birds in a cage, kept in the dark by the Blood River Ancestor.","Unless they could become Dao Lords, there was no escaping his control.","But under the Blood River Ancestor’s command, becoming a Dao Lord was nearly impossible.","The Blood Demon Guards selected through the trial were merely tools for the Blood River Ancestor. Most of the treasures they obtained had to be handed over to him.","Otherwise, death awaited them.","Without treasures or a powerful inheritance, the thought of surpassing the Blood River Ancestor and breaking free was nothing short of delusional.","Thus, the Blood Demon Guards never even considered rebellion.","Perhaps at first, they had thoughts of resisting, but those thoughts were eventually ground down.","Now was not the time to pity them.","Because they had their own troubles to deal with.","The Blood Demon Trial was about to begin, and it was the highest level of Blood Demon Trial.","Hundreds of Yuanshen and Great Ascension Stage cultivators were about to be thrown into the Shura Grounds on the southern shore.","At that point, every cultivator would be closely monitored.","Even if their aura was concealed, with so many cultivators, they would surely be spotted by the naked eye.","“To deal with the ordinary folk, an illusion technique would be sufficient. But when a large number of Blood Demon Guards arrive, I fear we’ll be hard-pressed to move!” Zi Yu Immortal worried aloud.","Everyone was anxious at that moment.","But there were no good solutions.","Suddenly, one of Tian Can Elder’s disciples blurted out a foolish question.","“If we can’t cross by land, why not fly over the Blood River?”","Tian Can Elder shot a glare at his disciple and snapped, “You idiot! Do you think the Blood River Ancestor got his name for nothing?”","“The reason he’s called the Blood River Ancestor is because he controls the Blood River. Even a fly flying over it would not escape his notice. While crossing briefly might go unnoticed, if you fly along the river for any length of time, you’re bound to be detected!” True Immortal Wuhou explained calmly before continuing, “I do have a plan to get us across the Shura Grounds on the southern shore.”","Zi Yu Immortal and Tian Can Elder’s eyes lit up as they eagerly asked, “What plan?”","“Fight our way out!”","True Immortal Wuhou answered seriously, but his words caused both Tian Can Elder and Zi Yu Immortal’s faces to darken.","Fight their way out?","That plan was even more foolish than what Tian Can Elder’s disciple had suggested.","The Blood Demon Trial was an important event, and several powerful True Immortal would definitely be stationed there.","If they were discovered, there would be no chance of escape.","“Perhaps you misunderstood my intention. I’m not suggesting that we reveal our identities and fight our way out. Instead, we should disguise ourselves as trial participants and fight our way to the edge of the Asura Arena. Do you understand now?” True True Immortal Wuhou chuckled, feeling that these people were thinking too slowly.","It was also possible that, due to the constant tension over the past few days, their minds had become somewhat sluggish from the lack of relaxation.","Especially Elder Tian Can, who took a deep breath before asking, “And what do we do when we reach the border?”","At that moment, Fairy Ziyu finally caught on, exclaiming in surprise, “Once we reach the border, of course, we run!”","The others were stunned for a moment, then quickly understood.","The logic was actually quite simple.","In the Blood Demon Trial, the strongest participants were only at the pinnacle of the Mahayana stage. Those who oversaw the trial were aided by a grand formation, and the outer perimeter was guarded by ordinary Blood Demon guards—at best, at the level of the three-step formation.","The core area, however, was home to several vice commanders, all of whom were at the level of eight-step True Immortals. Why would they bother with such trivial matters?","It was likely that their main responsibility was to observe promising trial participants with exceptional talent.","Among millions of cultivators, a few extra individuals wouldn’t be noticed.","Once they reached the border, using a supreme treasure to conceal their aura and slip through the formation to evade the guards would be relatively easy.","Upon realizing this, they immediately decided to adopt True Lord Wuhou’s method.","...","“All units, hear my command! Begin deploying the trial participants from the flying boats. Ensure they are scattered across different regions of the Asura Arena!”","“Yes!”","Hundreds of Blood Demon guards—all of whom were True Immortals, with some as strong as five-step True Immortals, and others at the more common level of three-step True Immortals—moved into action.","As for the stronger figures, they resided within the Blood Demon Hall in the sky. They wouldn’t bother with such mundane tasks, delegating everything to their subordinates.","At this moment, inside the hall, three True Immortals were present.","Two of them were vice commanders of the Blood Demon Hall, and the third was Wu Taidou, a member of the same clan as True True Immortal Wuhou.","These three were all eight-step True Immortals, possessing formidable strength.","“Taidou, my friend, it’s been a while, hasn’t it? The last time we ventured into the Vortex Domain was three hundred years ago!” said a young alien with azure scales covering his body and curved horns on his head. He raised his wine cup in a hearty gesture. “Come, let’s have a drink first!”","Wu Taidou smiled warmly and responded, “Indeed, it has been many years!”","The three had once adventured together and had become life-and-death companions.","This time, Blood River Patriarch had a collaboration with the Beast Taming Sect, and Wu Taidou had been sent, giving the three of them a rare opportunity to sit down and share a drink.","“By the way, I heard this trial is of the highest level, and it’s being presided over by Brother Jiye. Looks like he’ll be gaining quite a few talented subordinates this time!” Wu Taidou said enviously.","Though Wu Taidou was a strong member of the Beast Taming Sect, naturally gifted in beast control and now an eight-step True Immortal, commanding several seven-step True Immortal demonic beasts, he still couldn’t compare to the vice commanders of the Blood Demon guards. While he might have more subordinates than them, their quality was far inferior.","The most critical issue was that maintaining these beasts consumed vast amounts of resources. Every day, feeding his legion of demonic beasts was an immense expense.","It was nothing like being a Blood Demon, where they had their own territories and could venture out for battles and adventures. Whatever treasures they obtained, they would merely hand over to the more powerful figures.","It was a dream setup.","The azure-scaled warrior laughed at Wu Taidou’s words, pointing at the handsome young man with a pale blue face across from him. “Jiye, since Brother Taidou is here, you should show some generosity. You’ve had a stroke of good fortune lately!”","“Please, don’t tease me,” Jiye True Immortal responded humbly. “While the talents from the trial may be under my command, they ultimately serve as the patriarch’s guards. How could I dare to benefit from it?”","Though he was modest, Jiye’s exceptional talent and strength were undeniable. He had emerged from the Asura Arena and, in less than a millennium, had already reached the eight-step True Immortal level.","He was highly gifted, incredibly powerful, and greatly favored by the Blood River Patriarch.","He was also one of the patriarch’s closest confidants and was regarded as the most likely candidate to ascend to Dao Lord in the future."]},{"number":6389,"title":"Chapter 6389: Divine Beast Flood Dragon","paragraphs":["Chapter 6389: Divine Beast Flood Dragon","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Once someone stepped into the Dao Master realm, they would soar to great heights. At that point, they wouldn’t need to remain with the Blood Demon Guards anymore. They could stand on equal footing with the Ancestor and serve the Two-faced Buddha directly.","“You sure know how to talk! No wonder the Ancestor values you!” teased the Azure Scale expert.","The three of them chatted casually as they drank.","Before long, the conversation turned to the current collaboration with the Beast-taming Sect.","“I’m not too sure about the specific details, but when I came, the Sect Master actually lent me their prized divine beast!” Wu Taidou revealed with a mysterious glint in his eyes.","The Azure Scale expert exclaimed in surprise, “Brother Taidou, don’t fool me! A divine beast is comparable to a Dao Master. Would your Sect Master really lend it to you?”","“I’ve heard that the Beast-taming Sect currently has four divine beasts, each in the hands of True Immortals at the forty-nine step level. However, the soul imprint belongs to the Sect Master, so it’s not unusual for them to lend them out,” Ji Ye True Immortal nodded faintly.","A divine beast was a treasure wherever it was.","It could be considered a Special Life Form among the demon race.","Its life level alone was a thousand times higher than that of a normal being.","Back in the Crimson Eyes Realm, it wasn’t unusual for life levels to reach five thousand times higher, but that was because of Immortal Jiu Chen’s presence.","His knowledge was vast. As the True Spirit of the Divine Fire Hall, he controlled many of the formations and inheritances left behind by previous masters of divine fire.","That’s how he was able to create a heaven-defying soul-advancement grand formation.","However, in the Ancient Domain World, increasing one’s life level was extremely difficult.","First, one needed Ancient Demon blood.","And not just a small amount—massive quantities of Ancient Demon blood were necessary. The higher the life level, the larger the physical body, just like the divine body.","Back when Jian Wushuang had a divine power of one billion, his divine body was as massive as a universe.","His physical body was similar in size, and if he reached one billion times the life level, it would also rival the size of a universe.","One time the normal size was around nine feet tall. Ten times meant fifty feet, and a thousand times could reach five hundred feet.","It could get even bigger.","Thus, more blood was needed.","In the Ancient Domain World, there were very few beings whose life levels surpassed a thousand times.","After all, there were only so many Ancient Demons.","Most of them had been captured by the Ancient Court. The strong experts with higher life levels were also mostly in the Ancient Court.","Aside from those early experts, there were very few ways to increase one’s life level now, and even then, the limit was usually around a thousand times.","However, divine beasts were born with a thousand-times life level, which made them immensely powerful.","In the Beast-taming Sect, they were considered treasures on par with supreme artifacts and rarely revealed.","That Wu Taidou had managed to bring one out this time was truly astonishing.","“Brother Taidou, why don’t you show us that divine beast and let us take a closer look? Honestly, I’ve rarely seen one before, and even then, it was always from a distance!” Qinglin’s eyes gleamed with excitement.","Wu Taidou chuckled and waved his hand, revealing a cloth bag in his grasp.","It was a Beast Bag.","Inside was a space like a pocket dimension, capable of storing lifeforms.","Not only that, but the bag also contained a beast nest. Wu Taidou had spent a fortune having it custom-made by a specialist.","After careful management, he eventually developed it into a sizeable beast nest.","The divine beast resided within.","“Come out, Mo Jiao!” Wu Taidou commanded, and from the bag flew out a massive dark green flood dragon as thick as a barrel.","Its life force was overwhelmingly powerful, and its immortal strength had reached the Ninth Tribulation True Immortal level. However, being a divine beast, its combat power was likely comparable to a Dao Lord.","It could even rival the Blood River Patriarch.","As Qinglin and the True Immortal Ji Ye observed it up close, they both felt a tremendous pressure.","Swish!","After giving them a brief look, Wu Taidou quickly retracted the beast.","After all, the divine beast wasn’t his own; it was borrowed, so he couldn’t summon it at will. He was only permitted to use it in battle.","Showing it to these two was a matter of friendship.","“A flood dragon! Its life level must be at least 1,500 times higher!” Qinglin exclaimed in astonishment.","Since the flood dragon bore the character “dragon,” it was much stronger than ordinary divine beasts.","If it had been a true dragon, it would have rivaled Special Life Forms.","Wu Taidou proudly replied, “Of course, Mo Jiao carries the bloodline of a true dragon, giving it a higher and purer life level!”","He then changed the topic, “Speaking of which, I’m really curious about this. The sect master not only lent us a divine beast, but specifically Mo Jiao. What exactly is our Beast Master Sect’s deal with the Blood River Patriarch?”","“You don’t know?” Qinglin looked surprised.","Wu Taidou shook his head in confusion.","At this moment, True Immortal Ji Ye lowered his voice and said, “The Patriarch didn’t provide specifics, but it’s related to the Ancient Demons. A divine beast with a higher life level is required, though the exact purpose wasn’t explained.”","“What? It’s related to the Ancient Demons?” Wu Taidou’s eyes widened in disbelief.","He hadn’t expected such a collaboration.","He had assumed they were heading to some dangerous land for an adventure!","The Dual-Faced Divine Mansion often hosted such excursions, inviting strong cultivators to venture into perilous areas.","Typically, these ventures were done in cooperation with the local experts of the Dual-Faced Divine Mansion, and outsiders like him were just there to catch any benefits that came their way.","But this time, the mission was connected to the Ancient Demons.","What shocked Wu Taidou even more was that their sect master hadn’t even hinted at it.","The three fell silent as they broached the topic.","Just then, a command came from the Blood River Patriarch.","He summoned them to the Blood River Hall.","This hall was located at the source of the Blood River.","“Let’s go. Since the Patriarch has summoned us personally, it might be related to this matter!” Qinglin called out.","Wu Taidou nodded, and the three of them left the Blood Demon Hall together, flying toward the source of the Blood River.","Meanwhile, below them, a massive battle involving hundreds of cultivators suddenly erupted in the Asura Field.","The disturbance was significant enough to catch their attention.","They scanned the area with their thought power.","In just a moment, True Immortal Ji Ye sensed that something was amiss.","Qinglin and Wu Taidou didn’t pay much attention, only giving it a casual glance. But True Immortal Ji Ye noticed something unusual.","“Wait!” True Immortal Ji Ye stopped the other two, his eyes sharpening.","Though young, he was both bold and cautious.","He pointed toward the battle below and said, “Several of them don’t bear the mark of the Ascension Array. They’re likely powerful outsiders. Let me deal with it. You two go ahead to the Blood River Hall.”","“Alright, but make it quick!” Qinglin responded casually, waving his hand as he and Wu Taidou continued on their way.","After all, it was the Blood River Patriarch himself who had summoned them. They couldn’t wait for Ji Ye.","True Immortal Ji Ye’s eyes gleamed with killing intent as he looked down at the Asura Field.","This was his territory, and the cultivators in the field were all potential subordinates once they ascended.","Now, some outsiders had infiltrated, insulting him to his face.","“Fools courting death!”","True Immortal Ji Ye sneered as his figure descended into the Asura Field.","Within the battlefield below, a few powerhouses had been fighting absentmindedly, retreating as they battled.","Their retreat led them toward the edge of the Asura Realm.","This group of people was none other than Jian Wushuang and his companions.","To be honest, their luck had been quite good at the start."]},{"number":6390,"title":"Chapter 6390: Discovered","paragraphs":["Chapter 6390: Discovered","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Upon entering the Asura Field, they encountered several fierce battles. Taking advantage of the chaos, they frantically made their way towards the border.","When they reached the border, they found themselves in the middle of a chaotic battle involving hundreds of people. It provided the perfect opportunity to escape the Asura Field amidst the confusion.","At the same time, the three True Immortals of Blood Demon Hall had received an order from the Blood River Ancestor, directing them to head toward the source of the Blood River. This left them no time to bother with the trial takers in the area.","However, as luck would have it, Jian Wushuang was noticed by the True Immortal Ji Ye.","Feeling Ji Ye’s aura descend upon them, Jian Wushuang sighed. It seemed inevitable that they would cross paths.","Buzz!","A sudden, powerful aura appeared and instantly crushed the entire battlefield.","The trial takers, still in their Great Vehicle stage, were instantly killed without a single survivor, leaving only Jian Wushuang and his group standing at the edge.","It was at this moment that Ziyu Immortal finally woke up from her shock.","“We’ve been exposed!” True Immortal Wuhou’s heart sank.","“It’s Ji Ye, an Eight-Step True Immortal!” Elder Tianchan’s expression changed drastically.","“An Eight-Step True Immortal!” True Lord Xueyang gasped.","The other two Four-Step True Immortals, along with Elder Tianchan’s disciple, also turned pale.","It was over.","There was no doubt about it—this time, they were truly in trouble.","Among them, some had powerful backgrounds, and others had strong cultivation and deep foundations. Against ordinary Six-Step or even Seven-Step True Immortals, they wouldn’t be afraid.","But they had run into an Eight-Step True Immortal.","There was no hope of resisting—only escape.","“Run!”","Everyone was left with one thought—escape as quickly as possible.","They needed to run as far as they could.","Resisting was tantamount to courting death.","Swoosh!","The first to move was Elder Tianchan’s disciple.","He was only in the Great Vehicle stage, surrounded by others of the same stage, and could easily blend in.","Besides, he was just a minor figure, unlikely to draw any attention.","It was a reasonable thought, but unfortunately, he acted too hastily.","It wasn’t that his reaction was quick; it was that he was overly clever, thinking that running earlier would give him a better chance to escape.","However, he hadn’t considered why the other Great Vehicle stage cultivators had died so quickly just moments before.","Ji Ye, as a True Immortal, didn’t even need to lift a finger to kill a Great Vehicle stage cultivator. The mere shockwaves of his immortal power were enough to shred them to pieces in an instant.","The only reason this disciple had survived earlier was because of Ziyu Immortal’s protection.","But now that he had moved beyond the range of her protection, he was instantly caught in the invisible shockwave of immortal power, torn apart in midair. His body didn’t even remain intact; it was reduced to a mist of blood.","The Elder Tian Can didn’t have time to grieve. He flipped his hand, pulling out the black gourd and shouted angrily, “Scatter and flee!”","As he finished, he yanked out the cork.","Boom!","Terrifying black flames erupted, instantly engulfing the surrounding area for a thousand miles.","As long as they could escape the range, each had a treasure capable of concealing their presence. Once outside, they’d be able to avoid Ji Ye True Immortal’s pursuit.","In this critical moment, the elder’s mind remained sharp.","Previously, they hadn’t fled immediately because the first to run would be the first to be hunted down.","His foolish disciple, who had always stayed close by, never experienced being chased and didn’t understand this. Now he was dead, and it was a pointless death.","The black flames spread, instantly consuming the nearby space.","The chaotic space caused everyone to begin scattering.","Before Ziyu Immortal escaped, she didn’t forget to grab Jian Wushuang, but as for the two Four-Step True Immortals, she was genuinely powerless to help them. Bringing a Universe Master along didn’t weigh on her too much, as it wouldn’t consume much of her strength.","“Stay close to me. As long as we make it out of this thousand-mile range, we’ll have a chance to survive!”","Jian Wushuang felt a warmth in his heart. He hadn’t expected Ziyu Immortal to still be willing to bring him, a mere Universe Master, along to escape at a time like this. He immediately followed her.","As for the others, he merely glanced at them, but he kept his Thought power locked on True Lord Xue Yang.","If True Lord Xue Yang couldn’t escape, this whole trip would be for nothing, so he couldn’t let him die.","The others, however, were not his concern.","Wu Hou True Immortal, with his solid background from a prestigious family, wasn’t doing too badly either. When he fled, a shield appeared under his feet, instantly accelerating his speed beyond that of even the Seven-Step True Immortals.","Even Ji Ye True Immortal would have a hard time catching up to him.","Elder Tian Can wasn’t far behind either. Using some unknown runes, he managed to enter a dimensional shield, slipping through the cracks of space to escape.","True Lord Xue Yang was even more outrageous. He directly activated the supreme treasure within his body, transforming into a streak of blood-red light. Those with experience could instantly recognize it as the Blood Shield, and his speed became the fastest among them.","But no matter how fast they fled, they were all awaiting judgment.","If Ji Ye True Immortal seriously chased after anyone, the one being pursued would almost certainly die.","“Each of them has a treasure? It seems their intentions are far from simple!” Ji Ye True Immortal’s lips curled into a twisted smile. He didn’t chase anyone but simply watched the escaping figures coldly.","After briefly scanning them, he recognized who they were.","After all, the powerful figures from Tian Tan City were mostly well-known.","“Ziyu, Tian Can, Wu Hou?”","He had identified the three strongest True Immortals.","When he spotted Wu Hou True Immortal, his brow twitched. He had just been drinking with Wu Doutu, and now he encountered a member of his clan.","Out of respect for him, Ji Ye True Immortal decided to spare Wu Hou True Immortal’s life. But trespassing into the Blood River Domain of the Shura Realm still called for some punishment.","“A Universe Master?”","Yet Wu Hou wasn’t the one who surprised him the most. What truly caught his attention was True Lord Xue Yang.","Because Xue Yang had always kept a low profile, very few people knew his appearance, but his treasure was anything but low-key.","A Universe Master with a speed comparable to an Eight-Step True Immortal?","Ji Ye felt a thrill in his heart and thought to himself, “This guy must be carrying a supreme treasure. My luck is really good. The Patriarch just rewarded me with a supreme treasure, and now I encounter another Universe Master with a treasure of his own. But for a Universe Master to carry such a treasure and use it so well, his background must be extraordinary!”","Of course, he didn’t plan to hold back. Even if he killed him, it wouldn’t matter.","This was, after all, the domain of the Twin-Faced God. His superior was the Blood River Patriarch, one of the ten True Immortals under the Twin-Faced Buddha.","If anything went wrong, the Patriarch would shield him, and even the Twin-Faced Buddha would step in if needed.","This was the Twin-Faced God’s domain.","No matter how strong their background, killing them was nothing to worry about.","“None of you will leave.”","Ji Ye muttered darkly.","“Ji Ye Origin Source!”","Hum!","The world instantly dimmed.","The bright sky plunged into darkness.","This was no ordinary darkness; even Thought power began to weaken.","Ji Ye not only obscured their sight but also their Thought power.","The fleeing group suddenly became blind.","They couldn’t even figure out which direction to flee.","At that moment, Ji Ye True Immortal made his move, starting with the two slowest Four-Step True Immortals.","“Two weaklings, no need to leave them alive!”","Killing intent surged in Ji Ye’s eyes. Darkness enveloped the two Four-Step True Immortals, and within a single breath, they were swallowed by the night. Their life force completely vanished in the next moment, leaving behind only two storage rings."]},{"number":6391,"title":"Chapter 6391: Death of Ji Ye","paragraphs":["Chapter 6391: Death of Ji Ye","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Ji Ye casually caught it in his hand.","Next up was Fairy Ziyu.","At this moment, Fairy Ziyu, who was fleeing frantically with Jian Wushuang, started to panic. Within the Ji Ye Origin Source, everything around them was engulfed in darkness. Nothing was visible to the naked eye, and even their thought power couldn’t perceive anything.","“No wonder Ji Ye wasn’t worried. He let us run while holding such a trump card!” Despite her fear, Fairy Ziyu didn’t lose her composure.","At this critical moment, she crushed a small green bottle, releasing a green mist that instantly washed over her eyes.","The darkness before her slowly receded.","Sensing the powerful presence approaching from behind, she immediately took out a talisman.","“Freeze!”","Buzz!","Within the Ji Ye Origin Source, time suddenly came to a halt.","Only Fairy Ziyu and Jian Wushuang could move.","“Let’s go!”","Fairy Ziyu grabbed Jian Wushuang, and another talisman appeared in her hand.","“Ten Thousand Miles Teleportation!”","Swoosh!","In a flash, the two vanished, reappearing ten thousand miles away, outside the battlefield.","However, they hadn’t completely escaped the Ji Ye Origin Source yet. Despite this, by using the Ziluo furnace to block their aura, the two instantly vanished from any detection.","Fairy Ziyu didn’t dare to relax. After flying tens of thousands of miles at low altitude with Jian Wushuang, she finally dared to stop.","They found a crevice along the shore and hid inside.","As soon as they entered, they sensed a massive disturbance erupting from a distance of ten thousand miles.","“Did the fight break out?” Fairy Ziyu sighed and said, “I wonder if Daoist Xue Yang will manage to escape safely.”","Jian Wushuang’s thought power had been focused on True Lord Xue Yang the entire time. He knew best whether the latter had a chance to escape.","After he and Fairy Ziyu fled, Ji Ye was deeply shocked. Fairy Ziyu was merely a Fourth-step True Immortal, yet she possessed a talisman capable of freezing space.","And it was done within his own domain.","That talisman was, at the very least, refined by a top-tier Dao Lord.","Recalling Fairy Ziyu’s background, Ji Ye quickly understood—it had to have been crafted by Grandma Yinhua.","Otherwise, Fairy Ziyu couldn’t possibly afford such a precious talisman.","Seeing the two of them escape, Ji Ye didn’t dare be careless any longer. He immediately pursued True Lord Xue Yang.","Though True Lord Xue Yang was incredibly fast, already at the level of an Eighth-step True Immortal, Ji Ye himself was an Eighth-step True Immortal—and one of the top-tier at that.","Before long, he caught up with True Lord Xue Yang, expecting to easily capture the Great Immortal.","But to his surprise, just as he caught up with the Great Immortal, Xue Yang took out a terrifying Dao Talisman.","This wasn’t just any talisman—it was a Dao Talisman, containing the attack of a Dao Lord’s might.","True Lord Xue Yang, without hesitation, crushed the Dao Talisman. A wave of violent energy swept through the Ji Ye Origin Source.","In an instant, it shredded the Eighth-step True Immortal to pieces.","The immense power surged in all directions. Even True Immortal Wuhou and the Elder of Heaven’s Remnants were affected. Fortunately, they were far enough away, and the attack was aimed solely at Ji Ye, so neither of them was harmed.","As for True Lord Xue Yang himself, he was protected by a golden light. The power of the Dao Talisman couldn’t harm him in the slightest.","Despite having annihilated Ji Ye, True Lord Xue Yang couldn’t feel any joy.","After sending a message to the Elder of Heaven’s Remnants and True Immortal Wuhou, the three regrouped and left the battlefield together.","Meanwhile, Jian Wushuang and Fairy Ziyu, hidden in the crevice within the distant mountains, were still waiting.","Once Jian Wushuang realized they were safe, he was considering how to remind Fairy Ziyu that they should regroup with the others.","But before he could speak, Fairy Ziyu already knew.","“They escaped. Let’s go find them and regroup!” After Fairy Ziyu finished speaking, she immediately took him away from the hidden crevice.","Jian Wushuang’s heart stirred. He sensed a peculiar presence of thought power, which likely came from the others who shared the same thought power tokens, enabling them to communicate through transmission.","...","At the core of the Twin-Faced God’s mansion stood Twin-Faced Mountain!","Within the majestic hall atop the clouds, nebulae swirled, and a misty Origin Source aura filled the air.","In the center, a figure sat cross-legged.","No matter from which angle one looked, both sides of the person’s face were visible.","He was the Twin-Faced Buddha.","One side joyful, the other sorrowful.","“The aura of Yang Dingtian?”","The Twin-Faced Buddha, still sitting cross-legged, suddenly opened his eyes. His lips curled into a constant smile—it was his joyful face.","“Why would his aura appear in my domain? Could that fellow be planning to betray the Holy Land?”","He abruptly rose to his feet, and his thought power instantly reached the Blood River Domain.","Yet the aura vanished.","However, from the lingering traces, he discerned that it wasn’t Yang Dingtian himself who had acted but the power of a talisman. This realization calmed him.","With a thought, a plump figure walked into the hall from outside.","“Master!” The plump man spoke respectfully.","The Twin-Faced Buddha sat back down cross-legged, lifting his eyelids slightly. He instructed, “Go to the Blood River Domain and see what happened.”","“Yes!” The plump man was a bit curious, but he quickly agreed and left the hall.","...","Meanwhile, inside the Blood River Hall.","Sensing the overwhelming aura, Xue He Ancestor immediately stood up. As soon as he stepped out of the hall, he encountered the approaching Qing Lin and Wu Taidou.","Once the aura spread, the two of them realized that something had happened to Ji Ye.","“Ancestor!” Qing Lin quickly explained, “Earlier, Ji Ye mentioned that he had found several outsiders, but their strength didn’t seem that formidable, so he intended to deal with them alone. But unexpectedly...”","Xue He Ancestor frowned and said coldly, “Enough! Let’s go see what happened.”","Originally, he had summoned them to discuss this cooperation with the Beast-Taming Sect. Unexpectedly, such an incident occurred on his territory at this time.","Enveloping the two with his aura, his figure flashed, and they arrived at the Asura Field in an instant.","At that moment, much of the Asura Field had been destroyed.","Nearly ninety percent of the cultivators in the Mahayana stage had perished.","Only a few thousand remained, some of them Nascent Soul stage cultivators who had survived by sheer luck.","Looking at the shattered sky, even Xue He Ancestor couldn’t help but gasp. Even he would have been severely injured if he had been hit by that strike.","“What a terrifying aura!” Wu Taidou felt a sense of relief in his heart.","Luckily, they had left earlier. Otherwise, he too might have fallen.","At the same time, he was astonished by who could have caused such a massive disturbance.","Xue He Ancestor held onto a wisp of lingering aura. After carefully probing it with his thought power, he concluded, “It’s indeed the power of a talisman. It seems that whoever acted is no ordinary person!”","“Ancestor, you’re saying the person who struck used a talisman?” Qing Lin asked in surprise.","Xue He Ancestor shot him a glance without answering.","If it weren’t for the talisman’s power, would he have come?","Would he have dared to come?","If it hadn’t been a talisman but rather a top-level Dao Lord, would he have dared to investigate?","Even though it was a talisman, he had come cautiously. If the person hadn’t left and hit him with another strike, it would have been a disaster."]},{"number":6392,"title":"Chapter 6392: Guardian Qifeng","paragraphs":["Chapter 6392: Guardian Qifeng","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Alright, you two return to the Blood River Hall. Without my orders, you are not to leave!” The Blood River Patriarch suddenly commanded, ordering the two to head to Blood River Hall and stay there.","Wu Taidou and Qinglin immediately bowed and obeyed, leaving the area.","Not long after they departed, a powerful presence suddenly descended.","It was a fat man from the Twin-faced Divine Mountain.","Upon his arrival, he saw the Blood River Patriarch waiting for him.","The Blood River Patriarch’s expression changed when he saw the man. He hadn’t expected this person to come in person, so he immediately greeted him with respect. “Guardian Qifeng!”","“Blood River, what exactly happened here to alarm the Prefecture Lord?” The fat man, without wasting time, directly questioned.","As a Guardian who had already reached the Dao Lord level, and a powerful one at that, he naturally didn’t regard the Blood River Patriarch highly. From the start, he came with a stern interrogation.","This was partly because the other man was one of the top ten True Immortals in the Twin-faced Divine Prefecture, holding a somewhat special position.","Otherwise, the questioning wouldn’t have been so mild.","The Blood River Patriarch frowned but didn’t dare to show anger. With a slightly respectful tone, he replied, “I just arrived as well. Someone used a Dao Talisman here earlier, and then they vanished!”","“Hmph!” Guardian Qifeng snorted coldly, his voice filled with fury. “You oversee the Blood River, and a stranger appeared on your territory, and you say you don’t know? You don’t even know who it was, and you let them escape? Do you realize this is negligence on your part?”","Inwardly, Blood River cursed this man for making things difficult.","There was no helping it, as they weren’t from the same faction.","His relationship with the Four Guardians was mediocre at best, but the ten True Immortals stuck together like glue. Normally, even the Four Guardians wouldn’t dare to give them a hard time.","But now, seeing him alone, they wanted to intimidate him.","If it weren’t for the important matters at hand, he would have already called his brothers for backup.","Among the top ten True Immortals, there were those powerful enough to suppress even Dao Lords.","That’s why they didn’t fear the Four Guardians.","“I will give the Prefecture Lord an explanation for this!” Blood River suppressed the fury burning inside and answered stiffly.","Guardian Qifeng narrowed his eyes, feeling a bit surprised. He knew Blood River was famous for pulling strings, yet this time he hadn’t called his brothers for support, which was unusual.","Initially, he had planned to take the opportunity to humiliate Blood River, but now he was curious about what Blood River was holding back.","“An explanation alone won’t suffice. This incident alarmed the Prefecture Lord. I will need to stay here and investigate for a while. As for you... this negligence won’t go unpunished. You’ll be sent to Centipede Mountain to kill three Centipede Kings. Hand their corpses over to me afterward!” Guardian Qifeng’s tone softened.","In truth, this punishment wasn’t severe.","The Centipede Kings were merely at the Ninth Tribulation True Immortal level, but their combat abilities were weak. With Blood River Patriarch’s strength, slaying three Centipede Kings posed no threat to his life. It would only require some time, and he’d have to mobilize the Blood Demon Guards for assistance.","But at this moment, he had important matters to attend to and wasn’t willing to go to Centipede Mountain to hunt the Centipede Kings.","Since the punishment was determined by Guardian Qifeng, it could be changed.","The Blood River Patriarch took a deep breath and retrieved a mustard seed-sized object, smiling as he offered it. “Thank you, Guardian, for your leniency. It’s true I, Blood River, have failed in my duties this time. Not only did I alarm the Prefecture Lord, but I also caused you to personally come here. In this mustard seed, I’ve placed a small token of apology for you, Guardian.”","“Blood River, I’ve noticed you’ve become quite polite lately!” Guardian Qifeng casually accepted the mustard seed bag and, after probing it with his thought power, widened his eyes.","Inside were two peak-grade immortal weapons, almost comparable to a supreme-grade immortal weapon.","For a Ninth Tribulation True Immortal, this was no small fortune; these could be sold for millions of immortal crystals.","Although Dao Lords already possessed supreme treasures and had no need for immortal weapons, who would ever complain about having more treasures?","With a smile, Guardian Qifeng accepted the gift and said with a faint grin, “Since you’re showing such a good attitude in admitting your mistakes, I’ll let this punishment slide for now. But remember, the Blood River Domain doesn’t belong to you; it belongs to the Twin-Faced Divine Palace. The Twin-Faced Divine Palace is the Domain Master’s residence. You and I are merely servants of this place. Know your place and don’t disrupt the Domain Master’s household because of your cultivation!”","“Yes, yes, Guardian, you’re absolutely right!” Blood River Ancestor quickly nodded in agreement.","What he didn’t realize was that his strange behavior had already aroused Guardian Qifeng’s suspicion.","“Alright, you’re dismissed for now. Once I finish investigating, I’ll report back to the Domain Master!” Guardian Qifeng feigned indifference.","This, however, made Blood River Ancestor secretly delighted.","As long as he could get Guardian Qifeng out of the way, he could proceed with his own plans.","“Thank you for your hard work, Guardian!” After a few more flattering words, Blood River Ancestor eagerly left the Asura Field.","Guardian Qifeng, still watching Blood River Ancestor’s retreating figure, smirked coldly.","After scanning the area, Guardian Qifeng soon discovered the fallen body of a True Immortal of the Eighth Tribulation—none other than Immortal Ji Ye.","True Immortals of the Eighth Tribulation were rare in the Twin-Faced Divine Palace.","Moreover, Immortal Ji Ye was a formidable fighter with remarkable talent. Guardian Qifeng had once been envious of Blood River Ancestor for having such a skilled subordinate.","Blood River Ancestor often took Immortal Ji Ye with him to the Twin-Faced Divine Mountain, clearly grooming him as a trusted confidant.","Yet now, Immortal Ji Ye had fallen, and Blood River Ancestor hadn’t even mentioned it, seeming completely distracted. This only deepened Guardian Qifeng’s doubts.","“Tsk tsk, I’ll have to see what kind of tricks you’re up to!”","With a sneer, Guardian Qifeng left the Blood River Domain in a flash of light.","But his departure was a ruse—he stayed behind, hidden.","Blood River Ancestor, however, was too careless.","Believing that Guardian Qifeng had truly left, Blood River Ancestor returned to the Blood River Hall to begin his plan.","Seated on the main throne, Blood River Ancestor commanded, “Notify Blood Demon to come to the Blood River Hall to hold his position. The two of you, come with me to Yunhai Mountain!”","“Now?” Qinglin was visibly surprised.","After all, Immortal Ji Ye had just fallen. Wouldn’t they need to investigate the incident?","Blood River Ancestor, unwilling to explain, angrily rebuked, “Do I need to explain my actions to you?”","“I wouldn’t dare!” Qinglin quickly bowed and obeyed.","Meanwhile, Jian Wushuang and his companions were also heading toward Yunhai Mountain.","At this point, after fleeing for some time, Yunhai Mountain was within sight.","The group remained silent along the way, until Fairy Ziyu finally broke the silence. “Daoist Xueyang, where is the secret passage you mentioned?”","She wisely refrained from bringing up the battle that had just occurred, instead getting straight to the point.","“I’ll lead the way from here,” True Lord Xueyang said, without disclosing the exact location.","He feared that someone might leak the information.","Hearing his words, no one objected, and they followed True Lord Xueyang into Yunhai Mountain.","Unbeknownst to them, another group of three had also arrived at Yunhai Mountain.","It was none other than Blood River Ancestor and his companions.","Qinglin and Wutai followed behind, silently questioning why the Blood River Ancestor had chosen to come to Yunhai Mountain."]},{"number":6393,"title":"Chapter 6393: Gathering in One Place","paragraphs":["Chapter 6393: Gathering in One Place","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","This place was rather unusual, and it was guarded by Guardian Yunhai.","He was a powerful Dao Lord.","Entering this place without warning and concealing their presence clearly indicated they had no intention of greeting the other party.","“Follow me!” Ancestor Xue He transmitted his voice.","He immediately led the two into the thick clouds.","After flying for a short while, they arrived at the Yunhai behind Yunhai Mountain.","Below the sea of clouds was a vast, endless ocean.","Swoosh!","The three descended, and ripples spread instantly across the surface of the sea.","“I’ve brought the divine beast this time. If it still doesn’t work, we’ll have no choice but to take the other path!” Ancestor Xue He took a deep breath and led the two of them into the sea.","They dove deep into the ocean, descending ten thousand feet until they reached the seabed.","The depths were not only silent but pitch black, with no signs of life around them.","After traveling tens of thousands of miles along the seabed, Ancestor Xue He finally stopped, turning to Wutai Dou. “Release the Black Flood Dragon.”","“Understood!” Wutai Dou did not hesitate and immediately released the Black Flood Dragon.","This was because the sect master had instructed them to follow Ancestor Xue He’s orders in everything.","Upon seeing the Black Flood Dragon, Ancestor Xue He’s tense expression softened with a trace of joy.","His tone towards the two also became much more relaxed, saying, “Wait here. Do not move around recklessly, and be sure not to reveal your presence!”","“Understood!” Qinglin obediently agreed this time.","Wutai Dou also nodded obediently.","Satisfied, Ancestor Xue He glanced at the two before leaving.","Though he said he was leaving, he merely entered a nearby underwater canyon.","He continued to descend for several thousand more feet, and the pressure of the deep sea had already reached the point where it could crush a cultivator in the Great Ascension stage. It was only then that Ancestor Xue He stopped.","He began to feel around the rock walls of the crevice.","Before long, his hand found a movable stone.","With a gentle twist, a stone door appeared on the wall.","Creak!","The stone door automatically opened.","A passage was revealed.","After glancing around, Ancestor Xue He entered the passage with the Black Flood Dragon.","What he didn’t realize was that just before he entered, a mysterious figure had already slipped ahead of him.","Ancestor Xue He remained completely unaware. His strength had already reached the peak of the Ninth Tribulation True Immortal, just a step away from becoming a Dao Lord. For someone to stand right in front of him without being noticed, there were probably no more than three people in the entire Ancient Sea Domain capable of such a feat.","Whoosh!","Inside the passage, the seawater was kept out, and the surrounding walls were covered in moss that thrived from the moisture, giving the entire passage a greenish hue.","Ancestor Xue He cautiously advanced. Before long, a massive beast head came into view.","The beast head had fangs and enormous eyes, giving it a terrifyingly fierce appearance.","Standing before it, Ancestor Xue He swallowed nervously before saying to the Black Flood Dragon at his side, “Drip a drop of your essence blood on it!”","“Roar!” The Black Flood Dragon resisted at first, but its life imprint began to glow, leaving it no choice but to obediently drip its blood onto the beast head.","As soon as the dark green blood touched the beast head, a golden light burst forth.","Ancestor Xue He quickly took out a small bottle, uncorked it, and dripped several drops of golden blood onto the beast head.","Buzz!","The seabed began to tremble instantly.","The sudden movement startled Ancestor Xue He.","The beast head before him seemed to emit a furious response.","However, after glowing briefly, it quickly fell silent once more.","“Sigh, still a failure!” Ancestor Xue He muttered with a hint of reluctance.","Jian Wushuang had gone to great lengths to open the door. He had even obtained a considerable amount of ancient demon blood and promised the Beastmaster Sect’s leader certain benefits, borrowing a divine beast to assist him.","But in the end, he still failed.","“It seems the only way forward is that passage,” he muttered, shaking his head. With a slight nod, he led the black flood dragon away from the passage.","Unbeknownst to him, his movements had already attracted someone’s attention.","Just as Jian Wushuang emerged from the passage, a stout and powerful figure blocked his path.","“Brother Xue He, why didn’t you think of me when there were benefits to be had?” Guardian Qifeng said with a sly grin, the corners of his mouth curving up mischievously.","Old Ancestor Xue He was startled, silently blaming himself for being too careless.","Meanwhile, deep beneath the sea, another group was steadily making their way toward this location.","“How much further, Blood Sun?”","“Soon, don’t be impatient at this point!” True Lord Blood Sun could barely contain his excitement now that they had safely arrived.","He was so thrilled that he found it difficult to keep his composure.","Originally, he had intended to check out the main entrance, but his impatience got the better of him, and he headed straight for the secret passage.","Splash!","After crossing the rushing underwater whirlpools, the group arrived at a vast undersea canyon.","Descending further into the depths, they followed Blood Sun into a narrow crevice in the canyon.","Once they passed through the tight space, they entered a flat area nestled within the mountain range, a valley within a valley.","“We’re here!” True Lord Blood Sun’s voice trembled with excitement.","He quickly advanced and located the passage marked on the jade pendant.","However, the passage was blocked by some rubble. Using thought power, he easily moved the stones aside, revealing a dark tunnel before them.","Just as they were about to enter, a voice made them break out in a cold sweat.","“Haha, Brother Xue He, it looks like you’re not the only one who knows about this place!” A rough voice echoed, and everyone was taken aback.","Immortal Ziyu’s pupils contracted sharply, as if she had seen a demon.","“Guardian Qifeng... Old Ancestor Xue He, True Immortal Qinglin, Master Wu Taidou!”","Four figures descended from above, the weakest of them being at the Eighth Step of True Immortal.","The old man Tian Can nearly collapsed from shock.","It was over.","This time, they were truly done for.","True Lord Blood Sun felt the same way. Though he still had a trump card, his opponents were Dao Masters!","And not just any Dao Master—these were powerful ones.","He had heard his elder brother mention Guardian Qifeng’s strength, which was formidable enough to rank among the top fifty in the Ancient Sea Domain.","His own trump card would likely appear as a mere trinket in the eyes of such an opponent, hardly posing any real threat.","“What should I do? What am I supposed to do now?” True Lord Blood Sun’s mind screamed in panic.","At that moment, another powerful aura descended upon them, accompanied by a voice filled with authority. “Qifeng, this is my territory. You dare bring Xue He here without notifying me? Do you no longer respect my authority?”","The next moment, a figure engulfed in blue flames appeared in their midst.","At the sight of this figure, the old man Tian Can nearly fainted.","“Brother Murong, no need to be so angry!” Old Ancestor Xue He cast a meaningful glance at the blue-flamed figure before him.","The name Murong caused everyone’s expressions to shift.","It was Murong Yunhai, one of the four great Guardians, also known as Guardian Yunhai in the outside world.","He was extraordinarily powerful, rumored to be the strongest among the four Guardians.","Even Guardian Qifeng was no match for him.","His arrival instantly drew everyone’s attention, halting Guardian Qifeng’s intended assault.","“Xue He, I know you’re involved in this. Speak!” Guardian Yunhai ignored Qifeng entirely, turning his gaze directly toward Old Ancestor Xue He."]},{"number":6394,"title":"Chapter 6394: News of the Outside Realm Expert?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6394: News of the Outside Realm Expert?","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","At this moment, Xue He Patriarch found himself caught in a dilemma, knowing full well that he couldn’t afford to offend anyone.","Moreover, the situation at the Ancient Demon Palace could no longer be kept hidden.","He had no choice but to reveal everything.","Only then did the crowd, including Immortal Ziyu, understand why they had been discovered. It turned out that Xue He Patriarch had also obtained a token from the Ancient Demon Palace.","True Lord Xue Yang could hardly believe it, exclaiming in shock, “This is impossible! The Ancient Demon Token was something the Ancient Demon carried with his jade pendant. How could there be two of them?”","His words caused both guardians and Xue He Patriarch to glance his way.","“So that’s who it is! You’re the younger brother of Yang Dingtian!” Yunhai Guardian smiled faintly and continued, “Kid, I bet you didn’t tell Yang Dingtian about the Ancient Demon Token. If he knew, he would have told you that there are many such tokens. Each craftsman involved in building the Ancient Demon Palace had one!”","“What?” Xue Yang gasped in surprise. Losing his balance, he fell heavily to the ground.","This time, he had been too full of himself.","Trying to prove himself behind his elder brother’s back had only resulted in disaster.","Xue He sneered coldly, “What an idiot. How could Yang Dingtian have such a foolish younger brother?”","“I heard they have the same parents, but the difference between them is huge!” Qifeng Guardian smirked wickedly.","Whether or not they could enter the Ancient Demon Palace didn’t matter anymore. Even if they failed to enter, capturing Yang Dingtian’s younger brother would still be a great achievement.","After all, the Double-Faced God Mansion had always been mortal enemies with Yang Dingtian.","Now that they had captured his younger brother, it would undoubtedly give Yang Dingtian a serious headache.","True Lord Xue Yang sat on the ground, looking utterly defeated.","Compared to his elder brother, he appeared no better than a clown.","“I cannot let them capture me!” True Lord Xue Yang roared in his heart.","However, the trump cards he carried were only effective against Ninth Step True Immortals, and they were useless against Dao Lords.","Moreover, there were two Dao Lords. Even if he could disrupt them for a moment, the next second, they’d capture him with their own hands.","Once captured alive, he would become a laughingstock throughout the entire Overturning Sea Ancient Region.","He had always been proud, refusing to burden his elder brother with trouble. Even while wandering outside, he never used his brother’s name to elevate himself.","True Lord Xue Yang was extremely proud and had a strong sense of self-respect.","At this moment, he had already made the worst decision possible.","Self-destruction!","If he died, at least he wouldn’t allow himself to be captured alive, which would save his elder brother from trouble.","“Stop teasing this brat. Let’s kill the others first!” Yunhai Guardian said calmly.","Xue He Patriarch didn’t hesitate either. He immediately stepped forward, preparing to strike.","Suddenly, Tian Can Elder, who had been frozen with fear, dashed out and shouted loudly, “Please, sirs, spare my life! I possess great fortune that I can offer to all of you!”","Tian Can feared death more than anything, and now he was trembling uncontrollably, his face pale.","With such a fear of death, it was impossible for him to just wait for it. He would do anything to survive.","“Old fool, do you think I’m a child?” Xue He scoffed as he struck without hesitation.","A blood-red column shot out instantly, aimed directly at the quivering Tian Can.","Yunhai Protector seemed to sense something familiar from Tian Can. His brow furrowed. “Hm?”","In the next moment, a sudden explosion echoed.","Tian Can dropped to his knees, covering his face with both hands, screaming, “No!!! I have a secret! I know where a powerful outsider is hiding!!”","Boom!","A moment later, Tian Can, panting heavily, opened his eyes and realized he wasn’t dead. In front of him stood a figure with his back turned.","It was Yunhai Protector!","He was gripping the blood column with one hand, crushing it effortlessly. The terrifying power from the act pushed Xue He backward.","The overwhelming divine power caused Xue He’s chest to resonate painfully, and he nearly spat out a mouthful of blood. But he forced it down, glaring angrily at Tian Can. His voice was filled with dissatisfaction as he asked, “Yunhai Protector, what are you doing? Do you seriously believe the words of a cowardly True Immortal?”","“Yunhai, you’re going too far! Xue He was just being kind, cleaning up the trash. Why are you defending it? Is Tian Can your illegitimate child or something?” Qifeng Protector sneered.","Yunhai Protector, having crushed the blood column, ignored the complaints of both men. Slowly, he turned to Tian Can and, without warning, crushed Tian Can’s arm with a single grasp.","A ring that had been on Tian Can’s finger floated in mid-air. Yunhai Protector grabbed it and, with a slight use of his thought power, inspected it. A smile crept across his lips.","“This ring is your ticket to survival.” Yunhai Protector casually tossed the ring back to Tian Can.","Tian Can, who had been on the brink of death, let out a long breath of relief and hurriedly knelt down to express his gratitude.","Both Qifeng Protector and Xue He were extremely curious now. What had Yunhai Protector discovered?","They weren’t the only ones.","Even Lady Ziyu and True Immortal Wuhou were taken aback. The two of them had thought today would be their end, but unexpectedly, Tian Can had found a way to survive.","Initially, there was some comfort in all of them facing death together, but now that Tian Can had a way out, the expressions of the two became even more unsightly.","Comparisons always create disparities.","Seeing Tian Can survive also ignited the survival instinct in both of them, making them eager to beg for mercy.","However, the three powerhouses of the Twin-Faced Divine Mansion ignored them entirely.","Though Wuhou True Immortal was a rigid man, faced with death, he couldn’t help but lower his head. He transmitted a message to Tian Can secretly, “Brother Tian Can, could you speak a word for me? If I survive, I will give you all my treasures.”","Tian Can, who had just recovered, grinned and completely ignored Wuhou’s message. Instead, he glanced at Lady Ziyu. Surprised that she hadn’t sent him a message, he raised an eyebrow but remained silent.","Meanwhile, True Monarch Xueyang, who had initially been surprised by Tian Can’s luck, began to waver. His survival instinct flared up too. But then he thought about how his begging would be seen by others. Even if he survived, he would be shamed for life. His heart hardened.","Jian Wushuang, however, remained the most unnoticed figure in the entire scene. He hadn’t spoken a word, nor had he shown any signs of fear. He simply stood alone in a corner, his gaze somewhat dim.","The others assumed he had been scared senseless.","Swoosh!","Xue He and Qifeng Protector landed on the ground, walking up to Yunhai Protector. Curious, they asked, “Yunhai Protector, what did you discover? If you don’t share it with us and try to keep it all to yourself, I’ll kill that old man!”","Qifeng Protector, shameless as ever, clearly coveted whatever had caught Yunhai Protector’s attention. If it could move Yunhai Protector, it certainly had to be something incredible!","Moreover, he had heard Tian Can mention a powerful outsider. The implications of this were even greater.","After all, only True Immortals could traverse the chaotic flows of the Starry Sky. Those capable of crossing worlds were elite among the True Immortals—most were Dao Lords or even Emperors."]},{"number":6395,"title":"Chapter 6395: Why?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6395: Why?","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Guardian Yunhai looked coldly at Guardian Qifeng, who was threatening him with a mischievous grin, and said in a stern voice, “If you want to kill, go ahead and do it. As long as you’re prepared to bear the consequences, I won’t say a word!”","“Brother Yunhai, there’s no need for this,” Guardian Qifeng replied, still unaware of the gravity of the situation, his tone agitated. “We’re all working under the same Lord. We see each other all the time. Why let it come to this? Just tell me what’s going on, give me a chance, and I’d be grateful!”","Xue He, the Old Ancestor, had no opportunity to speak. Even though he was a Ninth Tribulation True Immortal and could match an ordinary Dao Lord, he still fell far short compared to the two Protectors.","Yet today, since he had the chance to hear about this matter, he knew he wouldn’t walk away without some benefit.","Yunhai Protector glanced at the two of them before saying in a heavy tone, “First, we should investigate the Ancient Demon’s Palace. I’ll personally report this matter to the Lord. When the time comes, the three of us will go together. Don’t think I’ll take all the credit for myself!”","“Huh?” Xue He, the Old Ancestor, was startled. “Does such a small matter really require the Lord’s personal involvement?”","Guardian Qifeng was equally surprised. Though the outsider was powerful, most of them were Dao Lords, not significant enough to draw the Lord’s attention.","After all, the Lord was currently merging with the Sequence Legacy.","Once the merge was complete, he would undoubtedly become the strongest in the entire Overturning Sea Ancient Domain. At that point, there would be no need to remain in this desolate place. He could directly head to the Sacred Land for cultivation.","He was preparing to harmonize with the Dao. If he succeeded in doing so, the Dao Lord, having merged two great Sequences, would be as powerful as a Saint Lord!","In their eyes, the Lord was extraordinarily gifted and truly stood a chance.","Naturally, a mere outsider would be of little interest to him.","Unless, of course, this outsider was an Emperor Lord. But in that case, the Lord might not even be a match.","Seeing their curious expressions, Yunhai Protector lowered his voice and said, “The outsider Tian Can mentioned is the mysterious cultivator who injured the Lord earlier. The Lord has been searching for this person ever since. That cultivator was poisoned by an ancient toxin and doesn’t have much time left. Perhaps by now, they’ve already perished. So, what do you think? Does the Lord care or not?”","These words left Xue He, the Old Ancestor, and Guardian Qifeng frozen in place.","Earlier, when the Twin-faced Buddha was injured, they had both thought it was Yang Dingtian’s doing. They hadn’t expected it to be an outsider.","This was an internal secret of Twin-faced Palace, something no outsider knew about.","Only a few people were privy to the truth, and Yunhai Protector was one of them.","He had been by the side of the Dual-faced Buddha when they encountered that mysterious expert from another world. Within Elder Tian Can’s ring, Yunhai Protector could feel the lingering aura left behind by that individual, confirming that Elder Tian Can had not lied.","When they presented Elder Tian Can to the Palace Master, it would certainly count as a significant achievement.","Understanding the situation, Guardian Qifeng and Xue He Patriarch both smiled and looked at Elder Tian Can with much kinder expressions.","“Brother Yunhai, the reason you discovered our whereabouts, was it because of Elder Tian Can?” Guardian Qifeng speculated.","Yunhai Protector did not deny it and nodded in response.","The group shared their reasons clearly among themselves.","Jian Wushuang, who stood nearby, heard every word.","The others, however, were kept in the dark.","After all, such secrets were not meant for everyone to know.","Yet Jian Wushuang’s powerful thought power made it impossible to exclude him from the conversation.","“Alright, let’s continue exploring this Ancient Demon Palace. Xue He has one token, and that useless brother of Yang Dingtian has another. Each token allows three people to enter. Including Elder Tian Can, we have four people, leaving us with two more spots. I’ll take one. You two have no objections, right?” Yunhai Protector said.","Xue He Patriarch and Guardian Qifeng both shook their heads.","Although Xue He Patriarch had brought along two subordinates, he wouldn’t dare fight with Yunhai Protector over it.","Guardian Qifeng had come alone, and there was no need to return for anyone else.","Besides, Yunhai Protector had the upper hand this time, and they would need to rely on him later, so they naturally had to show him respect.","Seeing no objections from the two, Yunhai Protector immediately took out his token and notified his two subordinates.","While waiting for them to arrive, it was time to deal with the small fry.","“Tian Can, I’ll give you an opportunity. Follow me into the Ancient Demon Palace. After we’ve finished exploring, I’ll take you to meet the Palace Master. As long as you behave, once everything is over, the Palace Master will reward you!” Guardian Qifeng played the role of the good guy for now, since they would still need Elder Tian Can later.","Once they were done with him, giving him some benefits wouldn’t hurt. If necessary, they could always silence him.","Although Elder Tian Can harbored some doubts, he still put on a submissive smile and thanked them profusely.","“Good!” Guardian Qifeng turned to the others and suddenly opened his mouth wide. A powerful suction force instantly drew True Immortal Wuhou toward him.","Buzz!","True Immortal Wuhou’s expression changed dramatically. He wanted to resist but couldn’t fight the overwhelming suction. In the next moment, he was swallowed whole by Guardian Qifeng.","His fate, needless to say, was sealed.","The rumors about Guardian Qifeng’s taste for human flesh turned out to be true.","Witnessing this, Fairy Ziyu turned pale with fear.","The look Guardian Qifeng gave her made her legs tremble uncontrollably.","As his gaze traveled down her body, lingering on her snow-white legs, Guardian Qifeng smirked wickedly. “Such tender skin, you must taste even better!”","Just as he was about to act, Fairy Ziyu hastily pulled out a token and pleaded, “Spare me, Guardian Qifeng! I am the goddaughter of Silver Flower Madam!”","“Oh?” Guardian Qifeng raised an eyebrow in surprise. “So, that’s why you reek of that old hag. You’re her goddaughter, huh? That makes me even more excited!”","Xue He Patriarch couldn’t help but chime in, “That old witch Silver Flower has gifted plenty of beautiful women to many powerful figures, yet she never offered any to our Dual-faced God Palace. Her influence won’t help here!”","Elder Tian Can stood to the side, watching coldly, feeling disdain toward Fairy Ziyu’s attempts to use her connections.","In the entire Overturning Sea Ancient Domain, the Dual-faced Buddha ranked alongside Yang Dingtian at the top.","The Dual-faced Buddha, being a powerful figure from the Holy Land, had little fear of offending others.","Pulling strings like this was pointless; it would be better if she begged for mercy from him.","Elder Tian Can’s eyes gleamed with greed. He had long coveted Fairy Ziyu, but outside, his status was too low, and although his strength was considered top-tier among his peers, he lacked the background and connections that Fairy Ziyu had. Hence, he never dared make a move.","But now, things were different. The secrets he possessed were enough to make the three powerhouses in front of him envious. If he pleaded for her, they would surely show him face.","However, Fairy Ziyu stubbornly refused to ask him for help.","“We’ll see how long you can hold out,” Elder Tian Can sneered internally.","Realizing that Silver Flower Madam’s influence held no weight, Fairy Ziyu took out another token, this one dark and foreboding, and cried out, “I have the identity token of the City Lord of Tianshen City! I beg the three elders to spare my life for the sake of the City Lord.”","When she presented the City Lord’s token, Guardian Qifeng was momentarily stunned."]},{"number":6396,"title":"Chapter 6396: Fairy Ziyu’s Connections","paragraphs":["Chapter 6396: Fairy Ziyu’s Connections","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The City Lord of Tiantan, though his strength wasn’t particularly impressive—only slightly stronger than theirs—was still ranked around the thirtieth in the entire Fuhai Ancient Domain.","But his background was exceptional.","No one in the Fuhai Ancient Domain dared to touch him because he hailed from a Holy Land.","Moreover, his connections within the Holy Land were quite strong, which was why, despite his mediocre strength, he could still secure such a lucrative position.","“It’s definitely the Tiantan guy’s token!” Yunhai Protector reminded with a hint of caution.","Guardian Qifeng sneered, “So what if it is? Do you think he’d actually dare to mess with our Dual-Faced God Palace?”","Though the Tiantan City Lord had a decent background and connections, he was still leagues away from the true powerhouses of the Holy Land.","And Purple Feather Fairy was at best a mere plaything for the Tiantan City Lord.","Could he really fall out with the Dual-Faced God Palace over a mere plaything?","“Brother Yunhai, you’ve already given the other two spots to your own people. If you want to give face to Tiantan, you’ll have to bring one less person inside!” Guardian Qifeng chuckled nastily.","In fact, it wasn’t necessary to take Purple Feather Fairy inside. Just having someone escort her out would suffice.","But Qifeng deliberately said that to dissuade Yunhai Protector from worrying about giving face to the Tiantan City Lord.","He had no face to give the Tiantan City Lord!","Besides, if he killed her here, Tiantan City Lord wouldn’t even know it was his doing.","And considering Purple Feather Fairy and her group snuck into the Dual-Faced God Palace, the logic was on his side.","“Tsk tsk, so you’ve got that guy’s personal token, huh? Seems like you’ve got something going on with him!” Qifeng licked his lips, a wicked smile appearing on his face.","Seeing that her connections couldn’t get her out of this situation, Purple Feather Fairy was completely desperate.","Guardian Qifeng reached out with his greasy hand, gently caressing her smooth, jade-like neck. His dark tongue slithered out as he was about to take a bite when someone stopped him.","This time, his expression changed immediately.","He had been interrupted time and again—if he didn’t get angry, the onlookers would be furious for him.","“Lord Qifeng, could you spare Purple Feather Daoist’s life? She... she is my Dao partner!” Elder Tian Can pleaded cautiously, afraid of provoking the other party.","A Dao partner?","Guardian Qifeng clearly didn’t believe it.","Why didn’t he say so earlier?","Moreover, Purple Feather Fairy had presented the City Lord’s token, clearly marking her as a kept woman of the City Lord’s mansion—likely someone the Tiantan City Lord had already grown tired of.","Elder Tian Can knew this well. However, just moments ago, Purple Feather Fairy had transmitted a message to him, promising that if he pleaded for her, she would belong to him from now on.","This made Elder Tian Can tempted. Despite his fear of death, the allure of Purple Feather Fairy was no small thing.","“Tian Can, you’re a True Immortal of the Five Steps with impressive battle prowess. How could you be interested in her? A woman already worn out by another!” Guardian Qifeng mocked.","Elder Tian Can smiled obsequiously and replied, “You’re absolutely right, Lord. It’s my lack of discernment that caused me to fall for this woman. But it was still some sort of bond, after all. If you want to take action, you don’t have to consider my face at all!”","Yunhai Protector took a deep breath and shook his head, impatiently saying, “Enough, it’s just a woman. Spare her life. My people have arrived; let’s get on with the exploration. Once this is done, there are more important things to attend to.”","This was a reminder to Guardian Qifeng not to let minor matters delay the bigger task at hand.","“Fine, I’ll give you face this time!” Guardian Qifeng squeezed Purple Feather Fairy’s soft body before tossing her to Elder Tian Can like a discarded item.","Only two people remained on the field.","Two Universe Masters.","This time, there were no unexpected events.","“Xue He can’t be killed either. Leave him alive so we can deal with Yang Dingtian later!” Protector Yunhai specifically instructed.","Protector Qifeng sneered sinisterly, “I’m not that stupid!”","With that, he approached Xue He.","“Little one, don’t be afraid. I won’t kill you. As long as you cooperate and tell me all your elder brother’s secrets, and have him send over a supreme treasure, I promise you’ll live more comfortably in the Double-Faced God’s Mansion than out there!” Protector Qifeng approached step by step.","Xue He’s pupils shrank bit by bit.","The supreme treasure hidden on his body began to operate wildly.","Just as Protector Qifeng got close, Xue He suddenly stood up and shouted with a tearing voice, “You!!! You will never catch me!!!”","*Buzz!*","Xue He suddenly exploded into action, and a terrifying burst of divine power began to spread.","In the distance, Protector Yunhai’s expression changed. The divine power immediately enveloped both the elderly Tian Can and Zi Yu Immortal, who had been watching the spectacle, pulling them to his side.","He warned, “Be careful, Qifeng! This kid has a supreme treasure on him!”","Hearing the words “supreme treasure,” a trace of greed flashed in the old man Tian Can’s eyes.","Who wouldn’t covet a supreme treasure?","Unfortunately, he didn’t have the strength to fight for it. He had once had the opportunity for such a treasure, but to stay alive, he had already surrendered everything.","Even if there was a treasure, it would belong to the Double-Faced Buddha.","Next to him, however, Zi Yu Immortal felt a deep sorrow.","She had thought she was doomed to perish, but in the end, Tian Can saved her.","Not out of kindness—she had paid a tremendous price.","If she survived and got out of here, she would be forced to serve Tian Can for the rest of her life.","The days ahead would likely be even harder than those in the City Lord’s mansion.","Greed.","It was the cause of all of this.","It had all started when Xue He found her to plot against the Ancient Demon Palace, and this was the result.","They hadn’t even entered the palace, and already half of them were dead or wounded.","At this moment, she glanced at Jian Wushuang, the young man whose sweet talk had caught her attention. Now, he was scared stiff.","Standing motionless in the corner, his appearance stirred a moment of pity in her.","But there was no saving him!","She was now nothing more than a plaything for Tian Can.","She had no right to negotiate.","Tian Can seemed to have noticed her earlier gaze. He snorted coldly, “What? You still want to save that boy?”","“Tian Can, you’ve misunderstood. I only feel like I’ve let everyone down!” Zi Yu Immortal quickly shook her head.","This was indeed the truth, but ever since Tian Can had narrowly escaped death, his true nature had been revealed—jealous and mad.","Even a single glance from Zi Yu Immortal could ignite his anger. He raised his hand and slapped her hard, knocking her to the ground.","“You really are a b***h. I saved your life; I am your god. You will revere me for the rest of your life. From now on, your eyes can only see me, understand?” Tian Can said viciously.","Zi Yu Immortal, lying on the ground, nodded silently, offering no resistance.","This was the price she had to pay.","At this moment, she almost envied Xue He, who was fighting back.","He was actually managing to hold off Protector Qifeng with the help of his supreme treasure.","“This is... the supreme treasure, Ling Nian Bead!” Old Ancestor Xue He exclaimed in surprise. “Yang Dingtian really treasures his younger brother, giving such a high-level supreme treasure to a mere Universe Master!”","Protector Yunhai was also surprised, frowning as he said, “Comparing oneself to others is frustrating. Back when I was a Universe Master, I didn’t even have an Immortal artifact, only a top-grade Origin tool, which I used all the way until I became a True Immortal!”"]},{"number":6397,"title":"Chapter 6397: If You Have a Backstory, You Have to Use It","paragraphs":["Chapter 6397: If You Have a Backstory, You Have to Use It","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Back then, we were all about the same. But after encountering the Palace Master, each of the Four Guardians received a high-grade treasure set. Even someone like me, a Ninth Step True Immortal, managed to get one piece of high-grade treasure!” Xue He Ancestor sighed with emotion.","This wasn’t mere flattery; it was simply the truth.","With the backing of a super powerhouse, one naturally acquired more treasures.","Of course, one’s own strength had to be sufficient as well.","However, for someone like True Lord Xueyang, whose elder brother was a super powerhouse, it didn’t matter whether he was strong or not. Even if he did nothing but laze around, he could be pushed to the level of immortality.","“Why don’t I have a big brother like Yang Dingtian?”","This was the thought everyone had.","They didn’t need to work hard, yet could still obtain such powerful treasures.","Their treasures had been bestowed by the Two-Faced Buddha, but they had risked their lives countless times to exchange for them from his hands.","Even so, there were still many who envied them.","This was the gap.","“This kid’s physical body level has probably already reached five thousand times. What a freak. If his Origin Source Dao and Divine Eye techniques get any stronger, when he becomes an Immortal True Immortal, he might surpass us in no time!” Xue He Ancestor exclaimed.","Guardian Yunhai didn’t disagree.","That was indeed the case. Although True Lord Xueyang was still in the Mahayana stage, his foundation was incredibly deep. The only reason he was stuck at that level was likely because he hadn’t yet comprehended an Origin Source Dao that satisfied him.","You could see it just from the way he acted.","True Lord Xueyang had taken the path of the Space Dao, which included both the Wind and Water Daos.","He was simultaneously comprehending two Daos.","Moreover, both of these Daos were at least Third Grade Origin Sources. If they fused into the Wind and Rain Origin, it would become a top-tier Second Grade Dao.","At that point, if he comprehended a Second Grade Thunder Origin, he could ascend to a First Grade Origin.","This was True Lord Xueyang’s ambition.","A First Grade Origin Dao, combined with his cultivation of the Divine Eye technique, was of the highest rank.","Even if he didn’t merge with a sequence inheritance later, he could still walk the Origin path, or specialize in the Dao of Divine Power through his physical body.","Integration would become much easier.","Becoming an Emperor Lord would be even more attainable.","This flawless cultivation path was clearly designed by Yang Dingtian himself.","Unfortunately, True Lord Xueyang was too arrogant.","He foolishly brought people into the Two-Faced God’s Mansion to explore an ancient demon’s palace.","Watching the desperate True Lord Xueyang, Guardian Yunhai and Xue He Ancestor’s eyes were filled with disdain.","Not using your background? How foolish!","This was not something worthy of respect.","If you wanted others to admire you, you should make full use of your resources for cultivation. Once your strength was close to your elder brother’s, then you could act all aloof.","By then, at least you could stand shoulder to shoulder with your elder brother.","But True Lord Xueyang, at this point, was just a small Mahayana stage cultivator, yet he wanted to free himself from his brother’s influence.","Did he think he could become a super powerhouse on his own?","What a dream.","Naive!","Not only did Xue He Ancestor and Guardian Yunhai think this way.","Even Fairy Ziyu and Old Man Tiancan shared the same view.","The flattery they offered back then was nothing more than a means to curry favor.","If they were to speak honestly, True Lord Xueyang had no sense of timing.","Jian Wushuang thought the same, but it was a common problem among cultivators.","Some geniuses with powerful backgrounds were overly proud, to the point of arrogance.","Others, with similarly powerful backgrounds, were too reliant, eventually ruined by the overindulgence of their families.","Both were extremes.","What one truly needed was to remain neither arrogant nor impatient, and also to face some setbacks.","As with the current situation involving Xueyang True Lord, if he could escape, he might have a chance to walk the path of a powerful warrior in the future.","Unfortunately, this time, no one could save him.","Boom!","Guardian Qifeng blocked the treasure Xueyang True Lord had just unleashed with just one hand.","“This treasure is not bad, capable of stabilizing the soul and focusing thought power. But in your hands, it hasn’t shown its true potential!” Guardian Qifeng smiled lightly.","He had a reason for being so eager to act—he had known that Xueyang True Lord carried a treasure, so he rushed to make a move.","This way, the treasure would be his.","Initially, he thought it was just an ordinary treasure, at best a middle-grade one.","To his surprise, the treasure within Xueyang’s body was actually a high-grade treasure!","And it was a high-grade soul-stabilizing treasure.","Such an item could be exchanged for two or three high-grade offensive treasures.","Even if he entered the Ancient Demon Palace, he might not gain such a significant reward.","“Haha, this treasure is mine!”","Guardian Qifeng wasted no time, his figure bypassing the attacks and rushing straight toward Xueyang True Lord.","He had no choice. The treasure’s power was too strong, and although Xueyang True Lord hadn’t fully unleashed it, breaking through would still take time.","After all, the treasure had been refined by Yang Dingtian and had completely fused with Xueyang True Lord. Otherwise, how could a mere Great Ascension stage cultivator like Xueyang True Lord possibly wield a high-grade treasure?","Seeing Guardian Qifeng charging at him, Xueyang True Lord’s mouth bled. His eyes were filled with reluctance, but an even stronger will urged him to make one final stand.","“All of you, die!” Xueyang True Lord suddenly raised both hands, and his entire body exploded. A burst of white light flashed, and a massive light gate appeared.","No!","That wasn’t a light gate!","Guardian Yunhai, who had a clear view of the situation, suddenly shouted in fury, “Everyone, fall back! Do not approach!”","He immediately retreated himself as he spoke.","Tian Can and Purple Feather Immortal swiftly escaped at full power.","The so-called light gate wasn’t actually a gate but a spatial rift.","This wasn’t a void rift.","This was a spatial rift.","It came from the ancient domain world.","A grand world was incredibly stable.","Only an Emperor could tear it open.","But now, with Xueyang True Lord’s body exploding, he had managed to summon a spatial rift, clearly revealing his final trump card.","Guardian Qifeng was startled. He wanted to retreat, but it was too late.","The now transparent Xueyang True Lord grinned. “It’s over!”","“Infinite Wind!”","Whoosh!","As soon as he finished speaking, a white wind gust emerged from the spatial rift, instantly shattering Xueyang True Lord’s soul, and the high-grade treasure he carried was swept away by the Infinite Wind into the spatial rift.","But the remaining gusts of Infinite Wind continued to rush toward Guardian Qifeng.","Guardian Qifeng was a cultivator of the Origin Source of Wind.","The Third-grade Origin Source Path was the weakest form of the Wind Origin Source.","The Second-grade Wind Origin Source contained both wind and rain paths.","The First-grade Wind Origin Source combined wind, thunder, and rain paths.","Yet none of these origin sources could create the Infinite Wind.","Only a stronger Ultimate Origin Source could summon the Infinite Wind.","The Ultimate Wind Origin Source!","It contained all the minor paths of wind and merged them into the most powerful Wind Origin Source.","As a cultivator of the Wind Origin Source, Guardian Qifeng knew well that if the Infinite Wind touched him, he would be finished.","“How is this possible? How could that kid summon the Infinite Wind? There isn’t a single Dao Emperor with the Ultimate Wind Origin Source in the entire ancient domain world. How did he manage this?” Guardian Qifeng was full of curiosity, but he still had to evade."]},{"number":6398,"title":"Chapter 6398: Entering Together","paragraphs":["Chapter 6398: Entering Together","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","He couldn’t afford to fall at the hands of a cultivator in the Daluo Golden Immortal stage.","If he did, he would die full of regret.","“Feng Yin!”","Guardian Qifeng quickly formed a seal with his hands, revealing his Origin Source. Both the power of his Origin Source and divine power ignited simultaneously.","This was a heavy burden on him. If too much was consumed, it would be a huge issue for his future attempts to merge with the Dao.","Although his current situation was already troublesome, he didn’t want to make things worse.","After burning through a portion, he used Feng Yin to send the Infinite Wind away.","This technique could have eradicated all attacks, but faced with Infinite Wind, it was impossible to hide it.","The only option was to redirect it.","The vast, overwhelming Infinite Wind instantly destroyed the underwater canyon, and the surrounding waters surged into towering waves that reached the height of city walls.","Everyone originally at the seabed could now see the sky outside.","“That damn Guardian Qifeng!” Xue He cursed inwardly as he saw the Infinite Wind blowing toward him. He swiftly dodged out of the way.","Fortunately, it was still quite a distance away, so it was easy to avoid.","However, the same could not be said for Wu Taidou and the Green Scale powerhouse with him. They lacked the speed to escape and were torn to pieces by the Infinite Wind, leaving not even a trace behind.","Their immortal weapons were shattered as well.","Only higher-level treasures could survive, as even ordinary ones couldn’t withstand an attack of this magnitude.","It wasn’t just the two of them who were unlucky. The two True Immortals summoned by Guardian Yunhai were also caught in the disaster.","One of them was a Nine-Step True Immortal, slightly weaker than Xue He, and the other was a top-tier Eight-Step True Immortal, stronger even than Ji Ye True Immortal.","When the Infinite Wind swept through, they didn’t even sense its power before being torn to powder by the white tempest.","Some were unlucky, but others were fortunate.","Neither Fairy Ziyu nor Elder Tian Can needed to dodge, and likely wouldn’t have had the ability to. The wind happened to blow in the opposite direction, allowing them to pause and catch their breath.","As they gazed at the immense, overwhelming white tempest, they couldn’t help but break into a cold sweat.","“It’s too strong. If even a hint of that had touched me, I would’ve perished!” Elder Tian Can thought, his heart still pounding with fear.","He hadn’t died at the hands of Guardian Qifeng, but if he had been killed by the white tempest conjured by Lord Xue Yang, that would have been a truly unlucky end.","Fairy Ziyu’s eyes were focused on the corner where Jian Wushuang had once stood, which had now been shredded by the Infinite Wind. His fate was clear without needing further thought.","This battle had ended in devastating defeat.","Carefully entering, boldly perishing.","The sorrow of the weak, while unworthy of praise, still stirred a tinge of sadness.","As the wind gradually subsided, everyone regrouped once more.","After all, the Infinite Wind was not truly infinite.","Its power was eventually exhausted, and the sea returned to calm.","When they reached their previous position, a passage had appeared.","Guardian Yunhai and Xue He both wore grim expressions.","The losses this time were significant—all their subordinates had perished.","Seeing their expressions, Guardian Qifeng snapped angrily, “Why are you giving me that look? I just consumed a tenth of my divine power and Origin Source! Do you have any idea how many treasures it’ll take to replenish that?”","“Enough!” Guardian Yunhai forcefully suppressed his anger. Only after seeing that Elder Tian Can was unharmed did his expression finally ease.","Guardian Qifeng also understood that at this point, it was pointless to argue about the extent of the losses.","The most important thing right now was to hurry into the Ancient Demon Palace.","The commotion here had been significant, and it was possible that other powerful beings would arrive soon.","Let’s not forget, the Twin-faced Divine Mansion had four major guardians and ten True Immortals.","If they all showed up, it would be a huge problem.","Moreover, the Mansion Lord had a few formidable fighters by his side, whose strength even surpassed the guardians.","“Let’s go in together!”","Guardian Yunhai glanced at Elder Tian Can and Fairy Ziyu.","He didn’t feel comfortable leaving the two outside, so he figured it was better to bring them along.","After all, the Ancient Demon Palace didn’t pose much danger. There was no record of any Dao Lords perishing there, so bringing them in shouldn’t be an issue.","With so many losses already, they couldn’t afford another accident.","Thus, the two guardians, along with Patriarch Xue He, led Fairy Ziyu and Elder Tian Can into the Ancient Demon Palace.","True Lord Xue Yang and True Immortal Wuhou had both perished.","...","In a secluded meditation hall within a mountain villa in Tian Tan City, a middle-aged man with streaks of white in his hair suddenly opened his eyes. A trace of sorrow flickered in his gaze, and his chest throbbed with a dull ache.","It was the tearing pain of a blood bond.","“Xue Yang!!!”","He abruptly stood up and rushed out of the meditation hall.","With a flash, he appeared in a hidden ancestral shrine within the villa.","The soul lamp that had once belonged to True Lord Xue Yang had gone out!","“No!!”","The tall and imposing man roared toward the heavens, his chest wracked with stabbing pain.","He was none other than Yang Dingtian, the number one powerhouse in the ancient domain of Fu Hai.","His strength was overwhelming, and his talent unparalleled.","Though he wasn’t a cultivator who had emerged from the Holy Land, the Holy Land had long been trying to recruit him, and even the Ancient Court had extended offers.","After all, he was very likely to become the fifth Emperor in the Holy Land’s domain.","But now, his younger brother had fallen.","The tall figure dropped to his knees with a thud before the ancestral tablet in the shrine. His eyes were bloodshot, and his voice cracked as he spoke, “Mother, I have failed you. I didn’t protect my brother!”","The shrine was vast, but only one tablet was enshrined within it.","“Yang Qianxue!”","This was the name of Yang Dingtian and True Lord Xue Yang’s mother.","The two brothers had been raised by their mother since childhood. As for their father?","Their mother had never spoken of him, not even revealing his name.","Thus, the only name enshrined in the ancestral shrine was their mother’s.","When she passed away, she had entrusted her younger son to Yang Dingtian. Now that Xue Yang had fallen, how could he not be heartbroken?","This was his last remaining family member in the world!","After bowing reverently three times, Yang Dingtian, his eyes still bloodshot, made a vow before his mother’s spirit tablet, “Mother, rest assured, I will avenge Xue Yang!”","With that, he rose to his feet and retrieved a token, on which the karmic thread of Xue Yang was still visible.","Mount Shen!","Following the trail of karma, Yang Dingtian sent a message directly to the chief of Mount Shen.","After all, Mount Shen was under the jurisdiction of the Holy Land, and he couldn’t act recklessly.","Whoosh!","A figure appeared before Yang Dingtian. Upon seeing the newcomer, Yang Dingtian’s face turned cold, and he demanded, “Take me to Xue Yang’s cave!”","“Ah?” The chief of Mount Shen hesitated, perplexed. “Brother Yang, that would go against the rules!”","Yang Dingtian’s eyes narrowed, his gaze sharp as he glared at the chief of Mount Shen. He spoke each word slowly, “Did you not hear what I said? Either you take me, or I go myself!”","This made the chief of Mount Shen take a deep breath. He had already sensed something was off with Yang Dingtian earlier and didn’t dare bring up the rules again.","Although Yang Dingtian was a righteous figure, his strength was undeniable, and in his current fury, who would dare stand in his way? If he decided to kill him, where could he go to seek justice?","After all, in this world, strength was the ultimate law.","“No one?”","The chief of Mount Shen led Yang Dingtian to the cave where Xue Yang had previously resided, but it was empty!","Yang Dingtian, enraged, roared, “So this is your so-called rule?”","No one was there, yet the records showed Xue Yang had been present, and the karmic thread of Xue Yang still lingered here."]},{"number":6399,"title":"Chapter 6399: Yang Dingtian’s Fury","paragraphs":["Chapter 6399: Yang Dingtian’s Fury","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Brother Xue Yang, I’ll get to the bottom of this right away!” The head of Qishen Temple was drenched in sweat.","At the same time, he was puzzled as to why Yang Dingtian was so furious today.","It seemed like no one had provoked him!","As he recalled that they were searching for True Lord Xue He, a chilling thought crept into his heart.","Before long, they discovered that it was all orchestrated by Fairy Ziyu.","Those who had disguised their identities included Elder Tian Can, True Lord Wuhou, and others.","“Scoundrels! Do you think Qishen Temple is your playground? You do whatever you want?” The temple head roared at his subordinates, “Arrest everyone involved and make sure to find out Ziyu’s motive!”","However, Yang Dingtian didn’t have time to vent his anger on them. With a cold expression, he soared into the sky and left.","That day, he pulled every string and used all his connections to search for the whereabouts of True Lord Xue He.","Eventually, he didn’t hesitate to reverse the very laws of causality, paying a steep price to find Xue He’s location.","“Double-faced Deity’s Manor?” A murderous gleam flashed in Yang Dingtian’s eyes.","Meanwhile, in the villa, the numerous guests had already gathered. Upon hearing that their young master had perished in the Double-faced Deity’s Manor, they clenched their fists, eager for revenge.","As the second-in-command of the villa, “Rain Lord Huatian” approached the heartbroken Yang Dingtian. Bowing slightly, she stepped forward to console him, “Brother Yang, this matter is no small affair. If we act rashly, it will trigger the greatest conflict in the entire Overturning Sea Ancient Region. The Ancient Court will mock us, and once you provoke one person from the Holy Land, many more will come after.”","“Xue He is my only brother. If I don’t avenge this, I will never achieve unity with the Dao!” Yang Dingtian’s words shocked everyone!","They all knew how much Yang Dingtian cherished his younger brother.","But no one had expected that the death of his brother would affect his path to Dao fusion.","This battle was inevitable.","With a flourish of his robe, Yang Dingtian turned and addressed the crowd, “This matter is my personal affair. I don’t want any of you involved. I will make arrangements for you to leave the Overturning Sea Ancient Region shortly. I’m going to Double-faced Deity’s Manor alone. No matter who killed my brother, I will have my revenge!”","“Brother Yang is going for vengeance, and we’re just supposed to leave? How would people look at me afterward? It’s only the Double-faced Deity—I’ve wanted to meet him for a long time. I’ll accompany Brother Yang!”","Rain Lord Huatian, who had long harbored feelings for Yang Dingtian, couldn’t bear to leave him. She stepped forward immediately and said, “Brother Yang, I once said that if you did not accept me, I would follow you forever!”","Yang Dingtian was momentarily moved, but remembering his unresolved hatred, his gaze hardened again.","The rest of the group began to shout, “Count me in!”","In the hall stood hundreds of True Immortals, the weakest of whom had reached the seventh step. Not one of them backed down; all were willing to follow Yang Dingtian to the Double-faced Deity’s Manor for revenge.","“The Overturning Sea Region will face a battle sooner or later. Why not let it be today?”","Someone shouted, and for a moment, everyone was stunned. Then, excitement lit up their faces as they said, “That’s right! Let’s settle this today. We’ll help Brother Yang avenge his brother and wipe out the entire Double-faced Deity’s Manor in one go. After all, this is an internal conflict within the Overturning Sea Region. The Holy Land won’t be able to intervene!”","“If that’s the case, we should prepare ourselves properly...”","In just an hour within Tiantan City, they devised a plan that would alter the fate of the entire Overturning Sea Ancient Region.","In comparison to Xue Yang True Lord’s petty schemes, they were utterly insignificant.","At this moment, the Double-Faced Divine Mansion remained completely unaware of the situation.","Even Guardian Qifeng, who had entered the Ancient Demon Palace, had not anticipated that his actions would trigger a war that would sweep through the entire Overturning Sea Ancient Territory.","Inside the Ancient Demon Palace.","The few who had entered had already scoured the entire palace, searching every corner meticulously.","Yet, they hadn’t found a single thing.","Not even a single Immortal herb or an Immortal artifact.","“How is this possible? The Ancient Demon Palace shouldn’t have been explored yet!” Guardian Yunhai exclaimed in disbelief. “Could it be that someone looted this place before the Double-Faced Divine Mansion was established?”","Guardian Qifeng shook his head and replied, “No, the treasures here were likely taken recently. I can sense the lingering essence of an Immortal herb in the air.”","Indeed, there was still a strong herbal scent within the palace.","If the treasures had been taken millennia ago, the scent would have long dissipated.","The two Guardians simultaneously turned their gaze towards Xue He, the old ancestor.","Two tokens had been obtained, one by Xue Yang True Lord, but he had never entered this place before his death. The other token had been obtained by Xue He.","And he had been here before!","“Don’t look at me like that! We all entered together. How could I have taken the treasures right under your noses?” Xue He felt uneasy under their stares and hurriedly explained.","Guardian Qifeng scoffed, “Xue He, don’t fool yourself into thinking you’re a good person. Back when the Swirling God Sect’s treasure emerged, you killed many of your fellow Divine Mansion disciples for it. Do you think you hid it well?”","Hearing this, Guardian Yunhai said nothing, but stood by and watched the drama unfold.","Everyone knew there were two ways to enter the Ancient Demon Palace.","Entering through the main gate allowed access to the Ancient Demon’s hidden sleeping chambers, something even the craftsmen couldn’t replicate.","However, entering through this path meant they couldn’t reach the hidden chambers.","The one who acquired the first token had a chance to enter, but only if they possessed Ancient Demon blood.","It wasn’t something one could bypass by having a high enough level of life force.","Ancient Demon blood had long disappeared from the world.","Although the Ancient Demon left behind descendants among various races, their bloodlines had diluted to the point of insignificance by now.","Even if someone with such blood existed, they wouldn’t dare reveal themselves.","After all, the Ancient Demon’s entire body was a treasure, and its descendants were no less valuable.","Thus, the possibility of entering through the main gate was nearly zero, especially since Guardian Qifeng had been keeping an eye on Xue He the entire time. Xue He had never gone through the main gate.","Otherwise, he wouldn’t have tried using the bloodline of a Divine Beast.","Now, Guardian Qifeng was making things difficult for Xue He, clearly trying to help his mistress vent her frustrations.","It was said that many had died at Xue He’s hands when the Swirling God Sect’s treasure emerged, including several strong figures from the Double-Faced Divine Mansion.","However, Xue He had covered it up well, killing everyone involved and blaming it on the Swirling God Sect.","Guardian Qifeng had close ties with the Swirling God Sect, so naturally, Xue He had made an enemy of him.","Now, it was clear that Guardian Qifeng was looking for trouble, openly trying to ruin him.","Within a single day, Xue He had lost two of his most important subordinates, including Ji Ye True Immortal, whom he valued the most. Then, Qinglin had fallen as well.","To make matters worse, Wutai Dou had died, and along with him, the Divine Beast in the Beast Nest had perished as well.","He had wagered a precious treasure with the Beast Taming Sect, but now the treasure was gone, and he had offended the Beast Taming Sect in the process. A Divine Beast was far more valuable than a precious treasure, and unless he was willing to offer compensation, there was no way to smooth things over.","Yet, their harvest from entering the Ancient Demon Palace was zero."]},{"number":6400,"title":"Chapter 6400: How to Split?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6400: How to Split?","Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“What could he possibly use to compensate?”","“He couldn’t possibly use his own precious treasure as compensation, could he?”","Holding back a stomach full of anger was already difficult, but now he was being picked on by Guardian Qifeng. Even though the other party was a Guardian, at this moment, Xue He couldn’t stand the insult any longer.","“I told you, I didn’t take it, so I didn’t take it. If you don’t believe me, there’s nothing I can do about it. Since there’s no treasure here, I’ll be leaving now!” Xue He scowled, turned around, and prepared to leave.","But Guardian Qifeng, having finally found an opportunity, wasn’t about to let it go so easily. He blocked the path and sneered, “What, you think you can just leave after taking the treasure? I don’t think it’s that simple!”","“Qifeng, don’t push me too far. Just because you’re a Dao Master doesn’t mean you can oppress me, Xue He. If you really think I took the treasure, I can call my brother to prove it!” Xue He was thoroughly enraged, directly bringing up his backup.","At the mention of his brother, Guardian Qifeng’s lips twitched, but he wasn’t willing to back down either. “What? Trying to use Chuxiong to pressure me? A Nine-Step True Immortal is still a Nine-Step True Immortal. As long as he doesn’t become a Dao Master, he can’t scare me!”","Chuxiong!","The leader of the top ten True Immortals in the Dual-Faced Divine Palace.","Though his Origin Source had not yet reached perfection, the Origin Source he cultivated was the first-grade Thunderstorm Origin Source. Its power was extremely fierce, and combined with his thunderstorm body, the immortal power he condensed was even stronger than that of an average Dao Master.","Crucially, he had also perfected the inheritance of the Divine Eye. Cultivating two sequences simultaneously, both had reached perfection.","The Dual-Faced Buddha had said that once Chuxiong took that final step and his Origin Source reached perfection, becoming a Dao Master, he would be able to rival the Buddha himself.","He was also destined to become the second leader of the Dual-Faced Divine Palace.","Such a figure held a position higher than the Four Guardians.","However, Chuxiong had been in seclusion for a long time and rarely ventured out, so his influence wasn’t particularly widespread.","Otherwise, Qifeng wouldn’t have dared to completely disregard him and still press down on Xue He.","On the side, Guardian Yunhai couldn’t take it anymore. The two biggest losers in this situation were himself and Xue He.","Initially, he had wanted to sit back and watch, letting Qifeng play the bad guy while he played the good guy, hoping to coax some treasures out of Xue He.","Make him cough up some blood, so to speak.","But now, Xue He had already brought up his backer, and if things kept going this way, there would be a real fight soon.","That wouldn’t benefit anyone. After all, they were all part of the same force.","“Qifeng, Xue He, both of you, say no more. Now is not the time for infighting. Let’s not make ourselves a laughingstock for these youngsters!” Guardian Yunhai gave both of them a way out.","At the same time, it hinted that Qi Feng couldn’t continue this way.","Xue He Patriarch glanced over, cursed under his breath, and said nothing more.","Guardian Qi Feng was the same.","Seeing the two of them stop arguing, Guardian Yunhai continued, “This is more like it. We’re all on the same side, and this time we’ve all suffered considerable losses. If we leave like this, wouldn’t that be a waste? Why don’t we work together to break open this palace? We might even find some treasures!”","The Ancient Demon’s palace was, after all, just a palace, not the Ancient Demon’s lair.","Although the Ancient Demon was a special life form with decent talent, his comprehension was lacking. But he wasn’t foolish and had set up many formations in his lair.","Breaking through those formations would require an Emperor-level figure.","However, this was just a palace. If a few Dao Lords couldn’t break it from the outside, they could certainly break it from the inside.","Guardian Qi Feng’s frown gradually eased, and a smile appeared on his face. He said, “Brother Yunhai always has a way. I almost forgot that our current realms are no different from before. It’s just that our power is inferior to the Ancient Demon’s. Since this is just a palace, if the three of us join forces, we can break through from the inside. Who knows? There might be hidden chambers!”","“There’s no other choice now!” Xue He Patriarch also agreed.","In truth, Guardian Qi Feng had suffered the least losses.","He had merely lost some immortal power and Origin Source.","But even that required treasures to replenish.","None of them wanted to give up on this place.","Even though they had Tian Can to ensure some returns, who wouldn’t want to obtain a bit more treasure?","Having made up their minds, the three of them began gathering their strength.","The three of them attacked together!","“Don’t burn your power just yet. Let’s try opening it first. If it doesn’t work, we’ll burn our immortal power!” Guardian Yunhai reminded them.","This clearly benefited Xue He Patriarch the most.","Guardian Qi Feng had initially wanted to say something, but thinking they had to cooperate, he held back.","“Let’s move!” Guardian Yunhai commanded.","Boom!","The three attacked simultaneously, each using their signature techniques.","Their attacks converged on a single point—the compass formation on the ground.","Although it was a compass formation, it wasn’t the strongest part of this place.","The entire Ancient Demon’s palace was refined from special materials.","If they could dismantle it and sell it, it would fetch a price exceeding a billion immortal crystals.","This palace was comparable to the lairs of some top Dao Lords.","In the era of the Ancient Demons, they had no natural enemies.","The number of powerful figures was few, and most of the treasures had been taken by the Ancient Demons. They were the wealthiest among the strong.","However, that era had its downside—there were no supreme treasures.","Supreme treasures were the key to raising the overall power of the human race.","No one in the Ancient Domain World could forge a supreme treasure.","The supreme treasures they had were all found in the Chaos.","They weren’t innate supreme treasures but were forged later. Why so many supreme treasures drifted into the Chaos remained a mystery.","As it stood, the Ancient Domain World couldn’t produce supreme treasures. Only in the inheritances left behind by fallen experts might one find a supreme treasure obtained from the Chaos.","With the appearance of supreme treasures, the dangerous places within the Ancient Domain World became insignificant.","Unless they were treasures left from the Ancient Demon era, few experts were willing to take risks. Most preferred to venture into the Chaos Void.","After all, one could find supreme treasures there as long as they were at the True Immortal level.","Of course, the risks were great as well.","Often, the dangers hidden in the opportunities for supreme treasures surpassed the True Immortal level, and many Dao Lords perished as a result.","During the peak of the Ascension Era, all the Dao Lords in the Ancient Domain World rushed into the Chaos Void. At first, almost everyone possessed a supreme treasure, but as more people went in, supreme treasures became scarcer.","Until now, only a few supreme treasures remained in the Chaos Void, with an average of one appearing every hundred years.","Thus, most supreme treasures still circulated within the Ancient Domain World. Ninety-nine percent of them were traded.","The chances of acquiring a supreme treasure through adventure in the Ancient Domain World were slim to none.","At this time, the battles were for orthodoxy, and treasures seemed insignificant. There weren’t many, and most Dao Lords and True Immortals still pursued the path of Origin and the Divine Eye Inheritance.","Aside from these, there were treasures within the Holy Land as well. However, the treasures there weren’t supreme treasures but rare wonders. The strong in the Holy Land referred to them as holy artifacts."]}]);
